window.AKK_MATRIARCH_MANUAL_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_MATRIARCH_MANUAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":201,"title":"Chapter 201: Let's Bet Bigger","paragraphs":["The new concubine Xian Si's residence, the Jade Brocade Courtyard, had a termite problem.","This was a serious matter. A young maidservant came rushing to find Cheng Zhao early in the morning.","\"...Termites were found at the base of the wall, and the concubine and her maids are all terrified. We don't know how much of the house has been damaged.\" Nanny Li told Cheng Zhao, \"Young Madam, what should we do about this?\"","Zhou Yuanshen sat in quiet contemplation. Some matters fell within Cheng Zhao's authority, and he could not overstep. He had to wait for Cheng Zhao to make the decision.","Cheng Zhao frowned. \"Where exactly have they eaten through?\"","\"One of the doors and windows in the storeroom shows signs of gnawing. They haven't reached the roof beams yet,\" Nanny Li said.","\"The entire Jade Brocade Courtyard needs to be inspected and treated for pests,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"First, move them to the back garden—there are a few secluded residences over there.\"","\"Should you ask the Dowager Madame first?\" Nanny Li asked.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"I'll go after I've eaten. Since termites have appeared, every part of the household needs to be checked. If it becomes an infestation, all the buildings will be in danger.\"","She then added, puzzled, \"Not to mention the Duke of Chen's mansion—even wealthy households use camphor or cypress wood for construction. At the very least, if good wood isn't available, they would coat everything in layers of tung oil to prevent pests and moisture. Nothing like termites has ever been reported elsewhere in the house. And the Jade Brocade Courtyard isn't even near the back garden—so where did the termites come from?\"","As she spoke, she looked at Zhou Yuanshen.","Zhou Yuanshen returned her glance.","Cheng Zhao understood. After the Mid-Autumn Festival, she had anticipated shadows and storms; these termites were but the tip of the wave—someone had done this deliberately.","Who was behind it and what their purpose was, Cheng Zhao could not yet guess.","\"I told you, there would be trouble after the festival. We can't just sit and wait for the storm to fall on our heads,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Cheng Zhao had only just begun laying her plans when the termites appeared—others were faster than she was.","Nanny Li was also shaken. \"Your gamble this time, I'd say it was the right bet.\"","Zhou Yuanshen then said, \"If we're going to gamble, then let's gamble bigger. See if we can close the net within the next couple of days, so you don't have to keep suffering through this.\"","Nanny Li was confused but afraid Zhou Yuanshen might be displeased, so she dared not speak.","Cheng Zhao, however, understood and nodded slightly. \"Very well, let's gamble bigger.\"","After the midday meal, Cheng Zhao went to the Hall of Longevity.","The Dowager Madame had not yet fallen asleep and was speaking with Huan Qingtang.","Huan Qingtang had not obeyed orders at Mid-Autumn Festival, but the Dowager Madame indeed lacked people to use, so she had not treated her harshly.","When Cheng Zhao arrived, Huan Qingtang was in the inner chamber, helping the Dowager Madame lie down.","\"Let her in,\" the Dowager Madame said. \"Since she's come at this hour, there must be something urgent.\"","Her voice was not low, and both Cheng Zhao and the servants waiting behind the curtain heard it.","Cheng Zhao sometimes thought that the Dowager Madame also had many constraints—for instance, the mask of kindness and tolerance she wore, which she had to keep on even in great pain.","At this moment, she must be hating Cheng Zhao to the bone, wishing she could beat her soundly.","Nanny Qin from the main kitchen had been dismissed—not only had that wounded the Dowager Madame's authority, it had also wounded her heart.","While the wound in her heart was still bleeding and unhealed, she had to muster her spirits and put on the dignified air of a \"grandmother\" at every turn.","It was so difficult.","\"I sometimes demand perfection a bit too much,\" Cheng Zhao suddenly thought.","Was this trait of hers not somewhat similar to the Dowager Madame's?","If this continued, one day she too would end up wearing a mask.","Over time, she might find it impossible to take it off, unable to face her true self. If she could not face things with equanimity, how could she call herself a matriarch?","Cheng Zhao took this as a caution to herself and entered the inner chamber.","The Dowager Madame's inner chamber had a faint incense—a pleasant blend of sandalwood and pine.","\"Grandmother, the Jade Brocade Courtyard is infested with termites. It is close to the Morning Radiance Courtyard and the Beautiful View Courtyard. Every part of the house needs to be inspected, lest it becomes a major disaster. We must dig out the ant colony,\" Cheng Zhao said.","The Dowager Madame sat up in surprise.","Huan Qingtang's expression also turned grave.","Most of the mansion's structures were made of wood, so termites were a very serious matter.","\"Where is the steward in charge of this property?\" the Dowager Madame asked. \"He should be inspecting on a regular basis.\"","Not just the buildings, but also the grounds. Large households had dedicated people responsible for wood-boring insects and pests.","\"Checks are done daily and monthly—this incident was unexpected,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"It's just that the matter is urgent, and we need to find the ant colony quickly, which is why I'm disturbing Grandmother's afternoon rest.\"","The Dowager Madame said, \"Handle urgent matters first. Send people to the Jade Brocade Courtyard immediately and dig out the ant colony.\"","Cheng Zhao asked, \"And what about the rest of the house? His Grace's opinion is to start with the Jade Brocade Courtyard. If we find the colony and know how to seal it off, we can leave the rest of the house alone for now. If we can't find it, then every part of the house will need to be thoroughly examined and searched, and it might get chaotic for a while. I was worried it would disturb Grandmother.\"","Huan Qingtang frowned.","The Dowager Madame said, \"Follow His Grace's method—start with the Jade Brocade Courtyard.\"","Cheng Zhao acknowledged with a \"Yes.\"","The Dowager Madame asked, \"And that concubine in the Jade Brocade Courtyard—move her somewhere else to stay.\"","\"There's nowhere to put her easily for the moment. I'll have her move to the Bright Flower Courtyard for a few days—fortunately, we've just prepared the side rooms,\" Cheng Zhao said.","The Dowager Madame and Huan Qingtang both fixed their gazes on her face.","Cheng Zhao added, \"This is also His Grace's wish. She was bestowed by the Emperor, after all, and His Grace said we may show her some leniency. The Emperor even asked His Grace about her—whether she was obedient, whether she respected the principal wife, or whether she tended to be frivolous.\"","The Dowager Madame smiled faintly.","Huan Qingtang lowered her gaze.","So the Emperor had raised the matter—Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen had no choice but to put on a sincere show. Moving Xian Si into the Bright Flower Courtyard, whether or not His Grace favored her, was embarrassing for Cheng Zhao.","And on top of that, the termites.","\"The Emperor reprimanded His Grace?\" the Dowager Madame asked.","Cheng Zhao said, \"His Grace said it was nothing. He said, with Grandmother's face in consideration, the Emperor would show some leniency.\"","\"The Emperor is worried about His Grace's heirs. Ah Jiang miscarried, and you haven't shown any signs yet,\" the Dowager Madame said. \"The Zhou family's bloodline is far too thin.\"","Then she added, \"Since you are being so virtuous and magnanimous, I am at ease leaving the concubine in your hands.\"","Cheng Zhao said, \"Yes.\"","Having said her piece, Cheng Zhao went out to get to work—she needed to visit the Jade Brocade Courtyard that afternoon.","Huan Qingtang was silent, watching her retreating figure.","The Dowager Madame smiled and looked at her. \"What, do you think she's being too easygoing this time?\"","\"Grandmother, I feel like she's plotting something,\" Huan Qingtang said.","\"She's a clever little thing, quick-witted, and you're no match for her. But sometimes, she's a bit too competitive,\" the Dowager Madame said with a laugh.","Huan Qingtang replied, \"Yes, I am not her equal.\"","\"As women, we must be steady and composed. It doesn't matter if you're not her match—it's of no consequence,\" the Dowager Madame said.","Huan Qingtang again said, \"Yes.\"","Cheng Zhao went to the Jade Brocade Courtyard.","There, she met Xian Si again.","Xian Si was a singsong girl—the first time Cheng Zhao had seen her, in the hunting grounds, she was dressed in lavish attire, dancing around a bonfire.","Now she wore ordinary clothes, with her hair combed into a low married woman's bun.","An apricot-colored short jacket and a white silk pleated skirt, almost without any patterns, yet they made her look utterly pitiable; her hair ornaments were of silver.","Her silver ornaments were quite beautiful—they gleamed three times more brightly than others', and their craftsmanship was exquisite, looking anything but cheap.","It made her appear like a fully bloomed white lotus—pure, delicate, yet bewitchingly seductive.","She raised her eyes to look at Cheng Zhao, then performed a greeting. \"This humble one greets the Duchess.\"","Cheng Zhao stood still, a smile hanging at the corners of her lips. \"What is your surname?\"","Since Xian Si had entered the household, everyone had addressed her as \"the new concubine\" or referred to her as \"the one from the Jade Brocade Courtyard.\"","When Cheng Zhao stood before her, she found herself unsure of what to call her.","\"I have no surname. I was raised in the rear gardens of the imperial hunting lodge,\" Xian Si said.","The hunting lodge at the imperial enclosure kept a large troupe of singing girls and dancing girls. They were there solely for the emperor's amusement during his hunting excursions.","Sometimes the emperor would bring a few back to the palace; other times, he would privately bestow them upon his ministers.","Each year, new ones were selected, better ones.","Xian Si had been bought and sold multiple times over the years and could no longer remember her original family name.","\"Dowager Madame, please grant me a surname,\" Xian Si said, sinking into a graceful bow.","Cheng Zhao: \"...\""]},{"number":202,"title":"Chapter 202: Entering the Hall","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao did not rashly bestow a surname upon Xian Si. She had the maids call Xian Si \"Second Aunt.\"","Because the Duke still had Mu Jiang ahead of her.","\"...Second Aunt will bring her two personal maids and move into Nonghua Courtyard for a few days. The rest will stay temporarily in the courtyard at the back garden. That courtyard is crude, close to the servants' quarters and the storeroom, and near the back street—it may be noisy.\" Cheng Zhao said.","The entire room was shocked.","But no one dared show any sign of surprise; they respectfully acknowledged the order.","The household servants all knew that the Duchess was a formidable woman, and her authority was known from top to bottom.","Xian Si was stunned for a moment, then her eyes welled with tears: \"Thank you for your generosity, Madam. But would this be too much of an imposition? I could share quarters with Lady Concubine.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"Lijing Courtyard also needs to be inspected, and I fear the termites might tunnel through the ground—they could come to your place, and also to hers.\"","She added, \"Lady Concubine recently made a mistake, and the Grand Madam punished her. She was beaten. Her welts have not yet healed, and she can hardly withstand the disturbance of your presence.\"","Upon hearing this, Xian Si lowered her head and said, \"Yes, I will follow all of Madam's instructions.\"","And so it was done. Xian Si, with her two maids, packed two large bundles containing her change of clothes and cosmetics, and moved into Nonghua Courtyard.","Within half an hour, this matter had spread throughout the Duke's mansion.","Strictly speaking, Cheng Zhao's arrangement was not wrong—a concubine staying in the mistress's courtyard to serve the mistress and the Duke was within the rules.","Some mistresses bullied their concubines, using them like night-duty maids.","But the Duke's household did not torment people that way.","Cheng Zhao was also a young wife, not quite able to put aside her pride.","She was willing to take Xian Si in—regardless of how people privately speculated about her motives, publicly they had to praise her as \"virtuous.\"","After arranging for Xian Si's accommodation, Cheng Zhao proceeded to inspect the termite nests in Yujin Courtyard.","As she left Yujin Courtyard with Suyue and Qiubai, she passed by Lijing Courtyard and encountered Mu Jiang.","Mu Jiang's face was sallow. She wore only her inner garments and trousers, with a thin robe draped over her shoulders, her hair scattered.","She stared quietly at Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao also noticed her, as well as the maid and the stewardess who were supporting her on either side.","\"Third Young Madam.\"","The maid and stewardess bowed to Cheng Zhao.","Mu Jiang only glared hatefully at Cheng Zhao, filled with both pain and rage.","Cheng Zhao ignored her, addressing only the servants who had greeted her: \"Why is Lady Concubine standing in the draft?\"","Then she asked, \"Is Lady Concubine in poor spirits, that she cannot speak?\"","Mu Jiang whirled at her: \"Are you cursing me?\"","\"So she can speak. I thought she had been beaten so hard that her throat was injured.\" Cheng Zhao said.","\"Cheng Zhao, you—\"","She was about to charge forward, but the maid and stewardess behind her had already swiftly flanked her and grabbed her arms.","Mu Jiang struggled furiously: \"Let go!\"","Her eyes bulged, her arms flailed, and she kicked at those restraining her. With no way out, she spat at them.","She was utterly disheveled.","Many servants passing by gathered around.","Someone blocked in front of Cheng Zhao, trying to curry favor, saying: \"Third Young Madam, be careful—don't let her spit on you.\"","Others scolded Mu Jiang's maid: \"Take her back at once. For such dereliction of duty, the Grand Madam and the Duke will not spare you. Don't think that just because Third Young Madam has a good temper, you can take things lightly.\"","\"Shut up! Cheng Zhao! Cheng Zhao!\" Mu Jiang screamed instead, \"Cheng Zhao, if you don't save me, one day you will be me! You'll come to no good end either, Cheng Zhao!\"","Everyone was speechless.","Cheng Zhao looked at her.","Mu Jiang's mouth had already been covered.","She glared at Cheng Zhao with a fierce, venomous gaze.","After Mu Jiang was taken away, Cheng Zhao slowly walked back.","She didn't take the small cart but strolled back to Nonghua Court on foot.","She was thinking about Mu Jiang.","Those frantic movements, those twisted expressions—Cheng Zhao had been baffled at first, then gradually came to understand.","Mu Jiang had deliberately come out of the courtyard, intending to beg for help.","But when she saw Cheng Zhao, her first instinct was hatred.","Hatred that Cheng Zhao looked polished, hatred that she looked respectable.","Hatred that Cheng Zhao had everything Mu Jiang wanted.","The instinctive jealousy and resentment were so overwhelming that Mu Jiang couldn't lower herself to say soft words. She simply stared at Cheng Zhao, waiting for Cheng Zhao to ask her.","Waiting for Cheng Zhao to offer her a way down.","At the same time, she didn't trust her own judgment or decisions.","Whether Cheng Zhao could save her—she had no confidence.","It wasn't until she was seized and about to be taken back that she realized it would be hard to run into Cheng Zhao in the future, and she wanted to cling to her last shred of opportunity.","Still, she didn't beg Cheng Zhao.","She threatened Cheng Zhao.","Threatening that Cheng Zhao had to save her, because it was also Cheng Zhao's self-rescue.","Cheng Zhao sorted out Mu Jiang's mindset and gave a faint shake of her head.","Suyue and Qiubai were walking beside Cheng Zhao. Thinking Cheng Zhao had been angered by Mu Jiang, they both tried to console her: \"Young Madam, don't lower yourself to her level.\"","Cheng Zhao gave a slight nod. \"Alright, I won't lower myself to her level.\"","Then she added, \"Suyue, Qiubai—back when we were in Fengzhou, whenever we went to the seaside, my mother always told us that if we saw someone drowning, we should run far away and never reach out to pull them in.\"","When a person falls into water, no matter how pitiful or innocent she may be, the one who approaches to save her could very well become her substitute death. A person flailing and fighting for survival will trample all kindness underfoot in exchange for their own chance to live.","Mu Jiang didn't just fail to beg Cheng Zhao—even if she had wept bitterly and shown deep regret, Cheng Zhao still wouldn't have reached out a hand.","This was the karma between Mu Jiang and the Zhou family, their own entanglement of sin.","\"Yes, the lady always taught us that,\" Qiubai said. \"But we've never actually encountered someone drowning.\"","Cheng Zhao hummed in acknowledgment.","They returned to Nonghua Court, where Nurse Li had already settled Xian Si in.","Xian Si was staying in the west wing; the furnishings there were relatively new.","\"Second concubine, you'll only be staying a few days. Once the ant nest in the house is found, dug out, and the pests eliminated, you can go back,\" Nurse Li reassured her repeatedly.","Xian Si softly murmured her agreement.","After returning, Cheng Zhao first changed into casual clothes, intending to head to Jiangyun Court for the evening meal, when the Second Madam arrived.","The Second Madam came alone, hurrying into Nonghua Court.","\"Mother, why are you—\"","As Cheng Zhao spoke, her eyes darted toward the side rooms.","The Second Madam followed her gaze, shocked and incredulous: \"You brought the woman from Yujin Court here?\"","\"Yes.\"","The Second Madam: \"...Are you out of your mind with anger, Zhao Zhao?\"","\"Just two days, Mother. Termite inspections are quick—they wouldn't dare delay,\" Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","\"Even so, she can't stay in your courtyard,\" the Second Madam said.","\"If she stays in my courtyard, it's actually the most proper arrangement. If I were short on maidservants, she'd have to remain here indefinitely, serving me,\" Cheng Zhao said.","The Second Madam: \"...\"","She took Cheng Zhao's hand.","Cheng Zhao chuckled lightly: \"Don't worry, Mother. I've already come to an agreement with the Duke—we won't be staying here for the next two nights.\"","The Second Madam gradually relaxed a little: \"Where will you go?\"","\"The General's Mansion,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam: “......”","Cheng Zhao lowered his voice again, smiling. “Mother, during the Dragon Boat Festival when we went to the General’s Manor, you said something.”","“I said countless things. Which one?”","“You said, next time you want to scare Grandmother, we could move to the General’s Manor for a stay.” Cheng Zhao grinned.","Second Madam: “......”","She remembered now.","Back then, Cheng Zhao had also said that if anything really happened, they could first move to the General’s Manor for a temporary stay. If the Grand Lady wanted her to move back, she would have to vacate Chengming Hall.","That statement Second Madam recalled.","She shot Cheng Zhao a puzzled look.","“Her moving over—the Duke also agreed to it,” Cheng Zhao added.","That was what Zhou Yuanshen meant by “betting bigger.”","As the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law were talking, Nanny Fan arrived.","Nanny Fan said to them, “The Duke has gone to the Jiangyun Courtyard. The Second Master and the Fifth Young Master have also returned. They await you both for dinner.”","Cheng Zhao and Second Madam then left together.","After dinner, Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen went out, using the excuse of browsing the night market, and went to stay at the General’s Manor.","Ever since Xian Si moved into Nonghua Courtyard, Zhou Yuanshen had not set foot there again."]},{"number":203,"title":"Chapter 203: Divine Will","paragraphs":["The inner courtyard of the General's residence had been tidied up in advance.","The inner courtyard was not large—one main courtyard with three rooms, two side courtyards, and a small rear garden; behind the garden stood a row of low buildings that blocked out the noise of the back street.","The main courtyard had been scented with incense for several days, and since it was golden autumn, there was no chill dampness or musty smell.","“...You’ll have to make do for now,” Zhou Yuanshen said to Cheng Zhao. “Tomorrow we’ll have your maidservant brought over.”","Cheng Zhao: “Everything is already provided. Where’s the hardship? It’s very nice.”","Only two women were in the courtyard—wives of deputy generals who usually managed the main courtyard’s affairs. They weren’t accustomed to serving others and looked very nervous when they saw Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen.","Everything had been prepared in full, all conveniences at hand.","The bedchamber was rather small, with no screen before the bed; a layer of bed curtains hung above, and within that another layer of gauze netting, layered thick and heavy, enough to block out the light.","After washing up, Cheng Zhao let her hair down herself and sat before the dressing table to comb it.","Her black tresses were soft and smooth; she swept them to the right and combed slowly.","“This comb is very good for combing—better than the ones we use,” Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen picked it up and glanced at it: “The steward picked it up at the market. It’s not as fine as the ones you use.”","“A comb is for combing hair—what use is fineness? This one works very well,” Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen: “Take it with you. Have the steward buy more.”","“Alright.”","He caught Cheng Zhao’s hand.","Cheng Zhao looked at him in the mirror, catching the emotion in his eyes, and whispered: “I have to get up early tomorrow.”","Zhou Yuanshen bent down and kissed her hair: “Then let’s be quick.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","He lifted her into his arms.","Cheng Zhao wasn’t prepared; the comb slipped onto the corner of the dressing table, and she was seated upon it in his embrace, her black hair cascading down, cool and silky, brushing across the back of his hand.","Zhou Yuanshen’s breath hitched, his throat bobbing.","He pressed close and kissed her.","One of Cheng Zhao’s hands braced against the tabletop, the other clung to his shoulder, but she still couldn’t steady herself. She was like a small boat in wind and waves.","“Cheng Zhao,” Zhou Yuanshen murmured close to her ear, “Cheng Zhao, are you happy?”","Cheng Zhao had no leisure to answer, because he hadn’t stopped.","She bit her lip.","“Cheng Zhao, am I a husband who pleases you?” he asked again, his lips brushing her cheek.","Cheng Zhao glared at him: “You...”","“Do you need me to try harder?” he asked.","Clearly up to no good.","Cheng Zhao cupped his face in both hands, losing her support—her back pressed against the bronze mirror. She kissed him with force.","Then she bit his lip, neither hard nor soft.","Oil poured onto a raging fire—Zhou Yuanshen could no longer bother teasing her.","The comb on the corner of the table fell with a clatter to the blue brick floor—a clean, crisp sound, like a silver vase shattering.","Zhou Yuanshen wrapped his arms tightly around Cheng Zhao. Cheng Zhao did the same. The couple was rarely so close, their breaths seeming to merge into one.","He buried his face into her hair, breathing in her fragrance, and for a moment Zhou Yuanshen had the illusion of having wandered into a fairy realm.","After a long while, the room grew quiet, and Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen gradually cooled down.","After washing, the bed curtains were drawn, and within the darkness was complete.","Zhou Yuanshen held Cheng Zhao in his arms.","Cheng Zhao said: “The comb broke.”","“Buy another.”","“Alright.”","The next day, the steward delivered a new comb.","Zhou Yuanshen was to go to court; Cheng Zhao was to return to the Marquis’ residence.","The road to the imperial city and the Marquis’ residence was the same, so the couple shared one carriage.","When they reached the gates of the Chen Marquis residence, a deputy general lowered the mounting stool. Zhou Yuanshen got down first and helped Cheng Zhao by the hand.","The gatekeeper’s page and the steward all saw it.","The steward came forward to greet them.","“The Marquis is almost late, isn’t he? You go on ahead,” Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen: “I may not be back for midday meal. Eat on your own.”","“Yes,” Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","Another deputy general had a horse ready, waiting by the gate.","Zhou Yuanshen did not continue in the carriage—he mounted the horse and rode toward the imperial city.","Cheng Zhao stepped through the gates of the Marquis’ residence.","“Third Young Madam—why are you returning from outside?” When Cheng Zhao arrived at the Chenming Hall to handle affairs, a bold and curious steward asked her with a smile.","Cheng Zhao: “Yesterday His Lordship and I went out to the night market, and it got too late, so we stayed at the General’s residence.”","The stewards were taken aback.","Huan Qingtang heard this and briefly lifted her eyes toward Cheng Zhao.","Everyone in the Marquis’ household knew that the Xiansi courtyard had termites, and the Marchioness had moved her to her own courtyard.","But no one expected the Marquis and his wife to stop staying at the Nonghua courtyard.","It seemed unreasonable—which made it all the more fitting.","At midday, Cheng Zhao went to the Chenhui courtyard for her meal. Suyue and Qiubai had been waiting for a long time; the page Nanfeng was there too.","“How is the situation?” Cheng Zhao asked Suyue.","Suyue: “Second Concubine is very proper—give her anything and she uses it, no complaints. But she rose at dawn to pay respects to you and the Marquis.”","“Doesn’t she know we didn’t stay in the main courtyard last night?” Cheng Zhao asked.","Suyue: “She blew out the lamp and went to bed early.”","“She seems quite well-behaved,” Cheng Zhao said.","Suyue: “We’re all watching her, and it’s the Nonghua courtyard—a clever person should know to keep quiet.”","Cheng Zhao smiled: “Then she counts as a clever one.”","Suyue was a little worried: “Clever people aren’t easy to deal with either, Young Madam.”","“No matter—success or failure is up to heaven,” Cheng Zhao said.","Suyue: “...”","Cheng Zhao asked again: “And the matter I ordered—how has it been handled?”","Suyue: “Nanny Li has already arranged things. The fastest way news travels in this household is through the main kitchen. The kitchen will speak on your behalf.”","Cheng Zhao nodded.","Suyue sighed in admiration again: “Young Madam, you are truly formidable. It was the Grand Matriarch who put the main kitchen in your hands, yet it’s helped you stand firm.”","The main kitchen was a good place.","Not just because of the generous pickings.","The entire household’s gossip and talk revolved around the main kitchen. If a matter didn’t first spread from the kitchen, it often carried little weight.","When Cheng Zhao married into the family, she hadn’t such great ambitions as to take over the kitchen first.","It was Madam Song and the Grand Matriarch’s people battling in the kitchen, and the Grand Matriarch needed a third party to stir the pot.","She sent Cheng Zhao to the main kitchen.","Cheng Zhao not only went—she first pushed out Madam Song’s people; then she drove away Nanny Qin, casting out the Grand Matriarch’s trusted confidante.","That was how she firmly took hold of the main kitchen.","Today, if she wanted to spread a message, without this territory of the kitchen it would take twice the effort.","Suyue couldn’t help but admire her mistress’s cleverness.","“You see—success or failure is up to heaven,” Cheng Zhao said again.","Suyue mulled it over, then smiled and nodded: “This servant worried too much. You’re right—success and failure are not in one’s own hands.”","Cheng Zhao smiled and nodded.","Because victory and defeat never lie in the hands of the schemer—Cheng Zhao did not get proud when she won, nor dejected when she lost.","That attitude, in fact, made everything go smoothly for her.","Within half a day, the entire Marquis’ household knew that the Marquis and his wife had not slept at home the night before.","The Shou’an courtyard heard of it as well.","The Grand Matriarch frowned: “Why did they go stay at the General’s residence?”","Nanny Sun said: “They say they were out too late last night and couldn’t make it back in time.”","“They just moved in a concubine, and now they don’t stay in the Nonghua courtyard. This Marchioness’s behavior is truly hypocritical—not in the style of the Cheng family,” said the Grand Matriarch.","Then she asked, “What do the servants say?”","Nanny Sun: “They all praise the young couple for being so devoted to each other.”","\"The servants' words are deliberately spread by someone. It seems Madam Cheng had planned this all along,\" the Grand Lady said.","Nanny Sun agreed.","Every step Cheng Zhao took was followed by another trap—she calculated every move. She even had the servants spread rumors first, seizing control of public opinion.","\"Cheng Zhao is truly troublesome, Grand Lady,\" Nanny Sun said. \"She must be dealt with.\"","The Grand Lady fell silent for a long time.","Removing Cheng Zhao was easy; defeating Zhou Yuanshen was the hard part.","And standing behind Cheng Zhao was precisely Zhou Yuanshen—he was her greatest shield and support.","This unremarkable grandson had grown far too powerful in too short a time.","The Grand Lady could no longer control him.","She even suspected that, given time, even the Emperor would be unable to restrain him."]},{"number":204,"title":"Chapter 204: Running Water","paragraphs":["The Duke’s residence was bustling with activity.","Huan Qingtang had also heard about Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen moving into the General’s residence.","Huan Qingtang sat before her writing desk, copying a Buddhist sutra.","Cheng Zhao had mentioned to the Dowager Madame that she wanted to enshrine the Child-Giving Guanyin, and asked Huan Qingtang to transcribe a sutra for her as well; Huan Qingtang agreed.","“What is Cheng Zhao trying to do?”","In Huan Qingtang’s view, Cheng Zhao’s goal this time was to move into Chengming Hall.","But was Cheng Zhao really aiming for something so blatant and undisguised?","It was too obvious.","“What’s her plan?” Huan Qingtang wondered again.","She sorted through Cheng Zhao’s reasoning: stir up the termite problem, bring Xian Si to Nonghua Court, then use Xian Si to create an incident and move out of Nonghua Court?","Wasn’t she afraid of gaining a reputation for jealousy?","Or did she have some other purpose?","Huan Qingtang felt she might be overthinking and missing the key point.","She finished copying a scroll of the sutra and sent her maid: “Deliver this to Nonghua Court, and take a look at what’s going on there.”","Her closest maid said, “I’ll go personally.”","Huan Qingtang nodded.","The maid was gone for quite a while. After all, the walk from Cuiyun Court to Nonghua Court was a long one. Nonghua Court was in a very remote corner.","“Cheng Shi isn’t in the courtyard,” the maid reported.","The day’s work finished in the afternoon, and Cheng Zhao had already returned.","“Her maids said she was at Jiangyun Court,” the maid added.","“It seems Cheng Shi goes to Jiangyun Court every day to wait on her in-laws during the morning and evening meals,” the maid said further.","At that, the maid’s tone carried a hint of schadenfreude.","Being a daughter-in-law was hard; standing attendance on one’s parents-in-law was grueling. Fortunately, her own mistress didn’t have to serve her mother-in-law.","“She’s very good at this kind of hollow show. When the servants talk about her, they inevitably praise her filial piety. Word will spread, and it will do wonders for her reputation,” Huan Qingtang said.","“Young Madam, I’ve truly never seen such a disagreeable person,” the maid spat.","Huan Qingtang: “The Cheng family has always been like this—excellent reputations. She was raised on it, and has known since childhood how to play these hypocritical games.”","The maid once again heaped contempt on Cheng Zhao and the Cheng family.","“...So she’s not at Nonghua Court? What about that new concubine?” Huan Qingtang asked again.","The maid: “I asked out of curiosity. Her maids said she was in the side chamber doing needlework.”","“This new concubine is rather interesting,” Huan Qingtang remarked.","“She’s truly patient. Compared to the secondary wife, this new concubine has far more skill,” the maid said. “And she’s beautiful—delicate and alluring. No man could resist her.”","“If she can stay steady, she’ll have good days ahead,” Huan Qingtang said.","She found herself thinking of her own situation.","She was also beautiful.","All she needed to do was do nothing, maintain her noble elegance, and in time she would get what she wanted.","Men always tired of the old and craved the new.","So why couldn’t she stay steady herself? What was she so anxious about?","Was she worse off than a singing girl?","“Young Madam, is there anything we need to do?” the maid asked.","Huan Qingtang: “Let’s wait too for now.”","The maid looked as though she wanted to say something but held back.","“What do you want to say?”","“Young Madam, staying steady is all well and good—winning through patience. But Cheng Shi keeps nibbling away bit by bit. For us, staying steady means falling behind,” the maid said.","The calm surface of Huan Qingtang’s heart rippled once again.","Yes, Cheng Zhao’s offensive was too fierce.","If both sides remained quiet and dutiful, Huan Qingtang could just wait, wait for the perfect moment.","But Cheng Zhao would not.","She chose to cut through brambles, charging forward boldly. She never waited passively for anything; whatever she wanted, she schemed to obtain.","Ever since Cheng Zhao married into this household, nothing she had gained had come from waiting.","Everything had been actively fought for by Cheng Zhao.","And in the process, Cheng Zhao had even made sacrifices.","Take, for example, the honorary title of “Duchess”—the highest-ranking noble title. She had seized a misstep from Mu Jiang and, at the cost of some of her own reputation, secured it.","Time had passed; who still remembered how cornered Cheng Zhao had been by Mu Jiang back then, or the incident of her rushing to Lijing Court to snatch someone away? Even if they did, it no longer stained Cheng Zhao’s name.","People never see flaws in the successful. At least, not in the eyes of the world, nor in the eyes of the servants.","Take the main kitchen, for another example.","Next would probably be the gatekeeper’s post.","And perhaps before long, Chengming Hall would welcome a new mistress.","At that thought, Huan Qingtang’s heart ached sharply.","She, too, had exhausted her wits to marry into the Zhou family; she had endured more than a few grievances since arriving.","Was she, at this point, to see it all slip away and remain a widow forever?","Was there no other path for her?","Then Huan Qingtang thought of Mu Jiang.","The thought came abruptly.","“Perhaps Grandmother has already planned a way out for me?” Huan Qingtang mused.","She kept that thought to herself.","If making a sacrifice could win her everything she desired, she was willing—just as Cheng Zhao had done.","She let out a soft sigh.","Meanwhile, Cheng Zhao was at Jiangyun Court, admiring the new spear that Second Madam had acquired.","“...Your father-in-law bought it,” Second Madam showed her.","Cheng Zhao knew a bit about spears and was skilled at praising them, though she couldn’t wield one well herself.","She praised everything from the shaft to the spearhead, making Second Madam beam with delight.","“Mother, you and Father clearly have a wonderful relationship,” Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam: “One day, you and Ah Shen will be the same. He’s quiet, but he dotes on his wife just the same.”","Cheng Zhao smiled.","Then Second Master and Zhou Yuanqi came back.","Zhou Yuanqi spotted the spear and said, “Mother, a spear isn’t as pricey as a ruby headdress—Father was being cheap.”","Second Madam rapped him on the head: “Stirring up trouble, and with no taste to boot. What use is having a son like you?”","Zhou Yuanqi refused to back down: “What use is a broken spear anyway?”","“More uses than you can count,” Second Madam said.","Second Master added, “Your mother’s title as First-Rank Pacifying Lady came from a spear. It may prove useful for even bigger things later.”","Zhou Yuanqi: “...”","He was about to say more when Zhou Yuanshen walked in.","Cheng Zhao shot him a smile.","Zhou Yuanshen carried a few bundles of pastries.","“Where did these come from?”","“Not bought. Tried them at the Eastern Palace, found them quite good, so I asked the Crown Prince for some,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","He handed them to Nanny Fan, who took them away to be arranged on plates.","Before the evening meal, the family sat together for tea and snacks.","Zhou Yuanshen asked Cheng Zhao, “How did things go at the mansion?”","“Word has been spread—everyone is praising how in love we are,” Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam and Second Master: “...”","Zhou Yuanqi: “You have no shame.”","“What’s there to be ashamed of?” Cheng Zhao laughed. “I wrote the script myself and had the main kitchen circulate it.”","Second Madam couldn’t help but chuckle.","She said Cheng Zhao was refreshingly unpretentious.","Zhou Yuanshen picked up a piece of date-paste pastry and offered it to her.","Sweet without being cloying, easy to swallow—Cheng Zhao nodded repeatedly, saying it was even better than what you could buy outside.","Zhou Yuanqi tried one too, adored it, and wolfed down three or four in a row.","Second Madam told him to eat fewer or he’d be too full for dinner.","The evening meal finished early.","Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen left the house again, heading for the General’s residence.","Word of this reached the Dowager Madame and Huan Qingtang.","That very night, something happened at Nonghua Court.","The small Buddhist shrine where Cheng Zhao kept her Child-Giving Guanyin caught fire, blazing with flames that lit up the sky.","When Second Madam heard the news, she threw on her robes in alarm and rushed out to see rolling black smoke.","Terrified, she quickly changed and went with Second Master to Nonghua Court.","Everyone from Nonghua Court stood outside the courtyard walls, while Nanny Li directed the coarse laborers to haul buckets of water to put out the fire.","“What’s going on?” Second Madam asked urgently."]},{"number":205,"title":"Chapter 205: Talk Back","paragraphs":["Fire broke out in Nonghua Courtyard.","Second Madam stared at the thick smoke, badly frightened, clutching Nanny Li's hand and asking what was happening.","Nanny Li knew what she was thinking and squeezed her hand back. \"Don't be afraid, madam. Everyone is safe. No one got hurt.\"","She added, \"The small shrine held many sutras. Perhaps they were stacked too tightly. Or perhaps someone tampered with the sutras, and that caused the fire.\"","Second Madam caught the implication and paused. \"Tampered with?\"","\"Fires don't just start for no reason,\" Nanny Li said.","She shot Second Madam a meaningful look.","Second Madam, never quick-witted in her life, understood Nanny Li's intent with unusual clarity.","Whatever the cause of the fire, since the small shrine contained sutras sent by others, they would insist someone had sabotaged them!","And Second Madam was famous throughout the marquis manor for having no guile.","Certain words were best spoken by her!","That night, the entire marquis manor was roused, including the servants quarters in the back. Fearing another fire, the head steward ordered the inner gates unlocked so people could move about freely—either to flee or to fight the fire.","The Dowager arrived at Nonghua Courtyard, accompanied by Huan Qingtang. Madam Song, the eldest madam, arrived shortly after.","The smoke refused to dissipate, so the crowd kept their distance, standing behind the pavilion to talk.","A single palace lantern sat in the pavilion, its light dim. There was no moon that night, and every face seemed veiled in shadow, hard to make out clearly.","\"Did everyone get out?\" Huan Qingtang asked with concern.","Nanny Li answered promptly: \"Everyone is out. Someone is on duty every night, and tonight it was me. I saw the flames and first woke everyone staying in the courtyard, then went to fight the fire.\"","Huan Qingtang nodded slightly. \"Very good. Lives come first.\"","She asked again, \"What caught fire?\"","\"The east side room,\" Nanny Li said. \"The two main rooms beside it also caught fire, but fortunately the inner bedchamber was spared.\"","Nanny Li turned to the Dowager. \"Luckily the Duke and the young madam were not in residence tonight. If anything had happened to them, we would deserve death.\"","The Dowager expression was unreadable.","Second Madam spoke up: \"Someone must have tampered with things. Our house hasn't had a fire in years.\"","Huan Qingtang said, \"Second Aunt, this needs to be investigated carefully.\"","\"The sutras are the problem. They caught fire all of a sudden, out of nowhere,\" Second Madam said.","Huan Qingtang fell silent.","Madam Song then said, \"Sister-in-law, what's wrong with the sutras? Don't be quick to blame others.\"","\"You sent sutras for offering, and then a fire broke out,\" Second Madam said.","Madam Song was furious: \"Absurd! We sent them to pray for her to bear children, and now we're the guilty ones? Your words make no sense. You don't know gratitude when you see it!\"","\"Could it be you have a guilty conscience?\" Second Madam shot back.","Madam Song opened her mouth, too stunned to respond, and merely gave a heavy snort.","The Dowager, who had been silent for a long time, finally spoke: \"Second son, control your wife. Don't let her fling wild accusations. She's not a barking dog.\"","Second Master had been standing in the shadows, not saying a word, unnoticed by everyone.","Until the Dowager spoke.","\"Mother, what Madam Fan says has some merit. The courtyard only gained those sutras and then caught fire. She's not making things up.","I don't understand the tricks of the inner quarters, but you should know them better than I do. Why not let your daughter-in-law speak?\" Second Master said.","Huan Qingtang and Madam Song looked at him in surprise.","They hadn't expected Second Master to dare defy the Dowager.","Zhou Yuanshen and Cheng Zhao were disobedient, Second Madam had learned to speak with barbed irony, and now even Second Master had grown a spine.","The second branch of the family was in rebellion.","The Dowager stared hard at Second Master.","He did not meet her eyes. His gaze dropped, and he bent slightly at the waist: \"Of course, household matters aren't about right and wrong. If Mother says don't investigate, don't speak of it, then we'll treat it as if it never happened.\"","He turned to Second Madam. \"Apologize to Mother. From now on, keep the truth bottled up inside. You're a mother-in-law yourself now—you should have learned some discretion by now.\"","His words, crisp and deliberate, reached everyone's ears.","The Dowager said, \"So it's my fault, then? Fine. If you want an investigation, if you want someone held responsible, then investigate thoroughly.\"","She extended her hand.","Huan Qingtang steadied her.","The Dowager said nothing more. She turned and, supported by Huan Qingtang, boarded a small carriage and returned to Shou'an Courtyard.","Shou'an Courtyard was brightly lit.","The Dowager sat down, her face dark, all traces of her usual softness gone. Her glance was like a blade, sharp with a thirst for blood.","\"Grandmother, please calm down,\" Huan Qingtang said, offering her tea in a gentle voice.","\"That little weasel Cheng Zhao—this time she's openly scheming against us,\" the Dowager said.","\"Grandmother, what burned was the statue of the Child-Giving Guanyin. Sister-in-law wasn't just scheming against the family—she also offended the Bodhisattva.\" Huan Qingtang's brow furrowed with worry. \"Pray she doesn't bring misfortune down on the rest of us.\"","The Dowager's eyelid twitched.","She was a devout believer. She would never have done anything sacrilegious in her own shrine.","She hadn't anticipated Cheng Zhao pulling such a trick.","How dare Cheng Zhao!","So brazen as to defile even a sacred image—was she not afraid of divine retribution?","At the thought, the Dowager was nearly choking with rage.","\"Send someone to the General's mansion. Tell them to come home at once!\" the Dowager ordered.","Huan Qingtang was surprised. \"At this hour?\"","\"Tell them to return immediately,\" the Dowager said.","Nanny Sun went to give the order.","Before leaving, she glanced at Huan Qingtang with considerable displeasure.","Huan Qingtang had done nothing to soothe the Dowager—in fact, she had only provoked her into even greater fury with a few words.","Nanny Sun frowned, thinking Huan Qingtang was no saint either.","The Dowager closed her eyes. She didn't drink the tea, just turned her prayer beads in her hand, trying to calm herself.","Beneath her aged, drooping eyelids, her eyes darted rapidly.","Huan Qingtang sat silently beside her, occasionally glancing at the Dowager, her own thoughts restless.","After a long while, the steward sent to the Pingxi General's mansion returned.","There was no curfew in the capital, but the streets were empty at night, and riding was quick. The steward had made the round trip with fair speed.","\"...Great Dowager, I didn't see the Duke. The deputy general on duty was fierce. If I hadn't left, he would have shot me with an arrow.\" The steward lifted his sleeve to show the Dowager.","His sleeve had a hole in it.","That was from the arrow shot by the gatekeeper deputy general at the General's mansion. The deputy had said that if he didn't leave at once, the next arrow would go through his head.","The steward had no choice but to come back.","The Dowager asked, \"Didn't you announce who you were?\"","\"I did. The deputy wouldn't listen,\" the steward said.","The Dowager was silent.","Huan Qingtang felt the Dowager might suffocate from sheer fury.","That night, Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen didn't return to the mansion.","Nonghua Courtyard suffered considerable damage—two main rooms burned down.","But Cheng Zhao's losses were minimal. The fire hadn't reached her inner bedchamber or her storeroom. Her dowry maids and servants, her clothing and jewelry, her silver and valuables—all were unharmed.","The next day, she still didn't return.","The Dowager sent someone to find her again.","This time, the steward returned and knelt at the Dowager's feet: \"The Third Young Madam has gone back to the Cheng family. A servant at the General's mansion said she left a message: someone tried to kill her by setting fire to her courtyard. She's very frightened and has gone back to her mother's house to take shelter.\"","The Dowager's anger had cooled. She said coldly, \"There's no need to fetch her again.\"","If she didn't want to come back, fine—she could stay away forever.","But the Dowager's defiant words could not reach Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao, meanwhile, had gone to the palace.","She went to pour out her grievances to the Empress.","Soon, the entire capital would know that Cheng Zhao, the Duchess of the State of Chen, had been relegated to a remote corner of the duke's residence. Yet even so, some would not let her be, and sought to burn her to death.","Who was behind it? Speculation ran rife.","The Grand Lady, who had always prized her dignity and kept family shame buried within the walls, was nearly driven mad by the sudden flood of gossip."]},{"number":206,"title":"Chapter 206: Too Beloved","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao did not return to the Cheng family home.","After going to the palace to lodge her complaint, she continued to stay at the Peace Calming General's residence.","\"...If we don't respond, Grandmother will fly into a rage. Will she ask the Emperor to intervene?\" Cheng Zhao asked Zhou Yuanshen.","Zhou Yuanshen was set to leave for the Capital Garrison camp the next day, and he was making arrangements to ensure Cheng Zhao's safety.","He had even enlisted Fan Xiao's help.","Hearing her question, he looked up and said, \"If the Emperor steps in, it works to your advantage.\"","Cheng Zhao thought about this and found it deeply sensible.","If the Emperor mediated, then for the sake of his own prestige, even if he applied pressure, it would be coercion disguised as favor, not something done blatantly.","If he truly dared to threaten Cheng Zhao, her grandfather would band together with the censors and denounce the Emperor for moral failure.","If it came to the Emperor mediating, the Dowager Madame would be utterly defeated.","Cheng Zhao didn't think it would go that far.","\"I'll be at the Capital Garrison camp for eight days and then return to the city. You can stay safely at the General's residence,\" Zhou Yuanshen said. \"And don't do anything rash.\"","Everything should be handled slowly; acting hastily often backfires.","\"Alright,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"During the day, I'll go home and relax. It's a rare chance to rest.\"","She added, \"The people in the Duke's residence are mine. They won't betray me anytime soon. And anyone with eyes can see I have the upper hand.\"","Cheng Zhao could also use this opportunity to test the loyalty and character of the stewards she trusted.","It would serve multiple purposes at once.","Zhou Yuanshen pulled her into his arms. \"When you move into the Hall of Inherited Brilliance, will you be afraid?\"","\"Is it because someone died there? I'm not afraid of that,\" Cheng Zhao said.","A physician had died in the Hall of Inherited Brilliance.","Zhou Yuanshen said, \"No, it's about bearing greater responsibility. Will you be afraid?\"","\"No,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"I'm young, but my mother and my eldest sister have seen the world. Whatever comes up, I have people to ask.\"","Her mother and eldest sister would teach her everything in detail.","Cheng Zhao wasn't afraid of managing the household; she could handle it. Even if she encountered setbacks, she could find people to help. She had great confidence in herself.","\"Cheng Zhao, once you get what you want, can you spare some thought for other things?\" Zhou Yuanshen asked her.","Cheng Zhao looked at him, puzzled. \"About having children? I think about that every day.\"","\"I mean about the two of us,\" he said. \"Cheng Zhao, what kind of husband do you want, and what kind of wife do you want to be? Setting aside the titles of Lord Duke and Duchess—just the two of us.\"","Cheng Zhao lowered her gaze slightly.","Zhou Yuanshen gently kissed her. \"This matter—ask your mother and eldest sister about it too, alright?\"","Cheng Zhao remained silent.","Zhou Yuanshen lightly lifted her chin. \"Cheng Zhao?\"","She looked into his eyes.","She saw fervor there.","Passion is so hard to sustain. Like the peony—it blooms with such intensity, but soon withers, leaving crimson petals scattered on the ground.","Better to be like the pine and cypress, forever green and plain, mild as plain water.","Cheng Zhao claimed she feared nothing, but she did fear some things.","Seeing Mu Jiang, Huan Qingtang, or even that delicate, flirtatious Xian Si—her heart would stir with unease.","Not fear of Zhou Yuanshen, but fear that she herself might change.","The road ahead was muddy. If Cheng Zhao became less resolute, how could she reach the shore she longed for?","\"I promise you, I will ask,\" Cheng Zhao said, sinking into the depths of his gaze, finally relenting.","Zhou Yuanshen gathered her into his lap.","Cheng Zhao's fingers lightly brushed his cheek, then traced his jaw, and further down, her fingertips stroked his Adam's apple.","Zhou Yuanshen's hands clasped her waist, then tightened suddenly, drawing her close as he kissed her fiercely.","He pressed too tightly; Cheng Zhao couldn't breathe.","She gasped and pounded his shoulder, and he finally loosened his hold.","That night, the two of them didn't sleep until well past midnight.","The next day, Zhou Yuanshen left for the Capital Garrison camp, and Cheng Zhao slept until the sun was high in the sky.","She had Suyue, Qiubai, and another attendant skilled at hair-styling brought over to the General's residence, where she enjoyed a little idle time.","In the morning, with nothing else to do, Cheng Zhao returned to her parents’ home.","Her second sister-in-law immediately sent word, summoning both her eldest and third sisters back.","The four women played mahjong together, and Cheng Zhao had the best luck.","\"...Using the fire to publicly reveal your situation in the Duke's residence—letting people know that the Duchess who already runs half the household lives in such a remote place—is a clever move,\" her second sister-in-law laughed.","Her eldest sister said, \"The strategy is sound, and things worked out well. It just so happened that the new concubine moved into that residence and then a fire broke out—no one would suspect you.\"","Cheng Zhao said, \"I originally only planned to use the 'scriptures' as a ploy, but then termites showed up. The more chaos, the murkier the waters—better for me.\"","Her third sister said, \"Using force against force—this time, Zhao Zhao might just achieve what she wants.\"","\"I hope so.\"","Her eldest sister said with a smile, \"Mother will probably nag you. Scheming in front of a shrine like that—it's disrespectful.\"","Cheng Zhao said, \"That deity isn't all that efficacious. I offered so much incense, and it still didn't help me conceive.\"","\"Hush, that's even more irreverent,\" her eldest sister said.","Cheng Zhao's faith was shallow, and her second sister-in-law and third sister felt the same way.","Perhaps because they were young and had experienced little, they had less fear of the unknown.","Her eldest sister smiled, though when she mentioned the shrine, a trace of unease flickered in her expression.","While they were chatting, the head maid from their mother's quarters arrived.","\"Mother requests the Fifth Lady's presence,\" the maid said.","Cheng Zhao recognized this head maid and spoke to her politely. \"Sister Yu Zan, is my mother angry?\"","\"The lady hasn't heard the full story yet. She heard the Duke's residence had a fire and was just sending people to inquire. She's not angry,\" said the maid named Yu Zan.","Her eldest sister teased Cheng Zhao: \"Aren't you the one who said you're not afraid?\"","\"Know your enemy and know yourself. If Mother is vexed, I'll have to shed a few tears and play the pitiful one,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Her eldest sister called her mischievous.","Cheng Zhao went before her mother.","She told her the whole story.","\"...I had someone light the scriptures and set the fire myself. With the scriptures given by the Dowager Madame, the First Madam, and Huan Qingtang as an excuse, and with the new concubine moving into my courtyard...\" Cheng Zhao said.","Her mother's face darkened.","\"Mother, with such a dangerous thing as termites happening, you can see some people are even more impatient than I am. If I don't act first, I'll just get schemed against again, and gain nothing in the end,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She was stirring things up, but others were faster and crueler.","\"Who released the termites?\" her mother asked.","Cheng Zhao thought for a moment. \"Very likely my aunt, the First Madam. She managed the Duke's household for years and wants to move back to the Hall of Inherited Brilliance. She's taking a risky gamble.\"","\"That's also a wicked scheme. If the termites got out of control, all the buildings in that residence would be destroyed, and they might even spread to the whole street,\" her mother said.","Cheng Zhao said, \"Yes. If the Hall of Inherited Brilliance stays empty, things like this will keep happening.\"","Her mother sighed.","\"Still, you were too reckless. You shouldn't have schemed before the statue of Guanyin,\" her mother insisted.","Cheng Zhao said, \"Mother, it's just a jade carving. If it weren't carved as Guanyin, it would just be a piece of jade.\"","\"That's even more improper talk!\"","Cheng Zhao fell silent.","Her mother scolded her for a while, then offered her advice anyway.","Cheng Zhao staying hidden and not responding to the Dowager Madame's \"inquiries\"—her mother also thought that was the best course for now.","When she returned to her second brother's courtyard, her fourth brother Cheng Chao had also arrived.","\"Did you get scolded?\" Cheng Chao asked her.","Cheng Zhao said, \"Mother couldn't bear to scold me. She even praised me for doing well.\"","Cheng Chao: “...”","Setting fire in his own courtyard and being praised for it—unbelievable.","Why had he never received such doting indulgence and leniency?"]},{"number":207,"title":"Chapter 207: Playing Hard to Get, Refusing to Return Home","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao was visiting her family home that day.","Her fourth brother had even reserved a restaurant, and the brothers and sisters went out to have some drinks together.","In the evening, Cheng Zhao brought her eldest sister back to the General's residence for a short stay.","The next day, the two sisters strolled around the General's residence.","\"It's a bit small,\" her eldest sister said. \"Even smaller than my courtyard.\"","\"Fine for a short visit, but not for a long stay,\" Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","Her eldest sister added, \"It's elegant and tranquil, and Yuanshen earned it himself. This place is very good.\"","\"He loves it here,\" Cheng Zhao said.","As she spoke, her ears grew slightly warm.","She felt that Zhou Yuanshen here was more bold and reckless in his behavior, three parts more unrestrained than when he was in the Duke's mansion, as if all the restraints on him had scattered.","\"Looks like you quite enjoy it too,\" her eldest sister teased, her words carrying a double meaning.","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","In the afternoon, the sisters sat idly in the small rear garden pavilion of the General's residence.","The osmanthus blossoms had not yet all fallen, and a faint floral fragrance drifted through the garden; a few plates of delicate pastries were laid out, exquisite and delicious.","On the stone table in the pavilion sat a small tea stove, and her eldest sister personally boiled water to brew tea. Tea sets were arranged nearby.","Cheng Zhao hesitated several times, as if about to speak.","\"What do you want to ask?\" her eldest sister encouraged her with a smile. \"It's fine—whatever we say here, I won't tell anyone.\"","Cheng Zhao hesitated a few more times before finally telling her eldest sister what Zhou Yuanshen had asked of her.","\"Zhaozhao, you really should consider this matter,\" her eldest sister said with a smile. \"You are husband and wife, not just the Duke of Chen and the Duchess.\"","\"Being the Duchess is easy; being a wife is hard,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She added, \"Wouldn't plain and simple be better, eldest sister? Some trees never bloom their whole lives, yet still tower into the clouds.\"","\"If your aspiration is to be a tree that never blooms, that's all well and good. But I'm afraid that as time goes on, your heart will harbor regrets,\" her eldest sister said.","Cheng Zhao did not answer.","Her eldest sister continued, \"Yuanshen's words have shaken you, which shows your resolve is not so firm either.\"","She also said, \"A tree that blooms is not necessarily one that cannot grow tall.\"","Cheng Zhao let out a soft sigh.","\"The water is boiling,\" her eldest sister said.","The water on the small tea stove was bubbling, and white steam drifted out from the spout.","Cheng Zhao took out the tea leaves and handed them to her eldest sister.","Her eldest sister poured in the hot water and began brewing the tea. Her tea-making skill was excellent, her movements fluid, and Cheng Zhao watched without blinking.","After a moment, the fragrant tea was poured into a teacup, and she handed it to Cheng Zhao.","\"Not hot anymore—so fragrant,\" Cheng Zhao said.","As she spoke, she suddenly paused.","She looked at the teacup.","\"What's wrong, does it taste off?\" her eldest sister asked.","\"I was just thinking—the water for brewing tea must be boiled; but it's best to drink it once it's cooled slightly,\" Cheng Zhao said.","\"Yes, who can drink boiling-hot tea?\"","\"What I've always feared is the boiling tea, eldest sister,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She was afraid of having too deep a bond with Zhou Yuanshen—like bringing her emotions to a boil, steaming and bubbling, fervent and intense.","At that point, she would lose her rationality.","She would become jealous and greedy.","But if the water never boils, the tea leaves won't release their fragrance, and the tea will have no flavor.","Cheng Zhao wanted to become the revered old matriarch; she needed a more harmonious and stable family, a more solid marital relationship.","If she never brought the water of her marriage with Zhou Yuanshen to a boil, what kind of good tea could she brew?","This wasn't about trees blooming or not blooming—it was a cup of tea.","She hadn't experienced it yet. In another ten or twenty years, could she still drink tea brewed with lukewarm water, bland and astringent?","How could she refuse to bring this pot of water to a rolling boil?","When it boils, there is inevitably the risk of scalding, but it is also essential for brewing tea.","\"...It seems you've had an epiphany,\" her eldest sister said, observing her expression and smiling.","Cheng Zhao nodded. \"An awakening.\"","\"Good, as long as you can see it clearly,\" her eldest sister said. \"You're growing up day by day, Zhaozhao. Time really flies.\"","She added, \"Back then you were so small—Mother carried you over... from the wet nurse. All wrinkled, I was a bit scared to look at you. But within a few months you blossomed, so beautiful, I wished I could be by your side every day.\"","\"You were still a child yourself then.\"","\"I was already twelve,\" her eldest sister said with a laugh. \"Think about when you were twelve—you had such strong opinions.\"","Cheng Zhao still remembered her twelfth year clearly; she had felt she was practically an adult.","Her eldest sister then recounted some amusing stories from Cheng Zhao's childhood.","Cheng Zhao had been unusually perceptive from a young age; by four or five, her intellect was already remarkable.","The two sisters always enjoyed each other's company, and before she knew it, her eldest sister had stayed at Cheng Zhao's place for two days.","She had to return home—she still had three children to look after. Though each had their own wet nurse, her eldest sister couldn't stay away from them for long.","She told Cheng Zhao not to be afraid: \"Your grandmother-in-law is more anxious than you.\"","Cheng Zhao nodded.","She prepared several gifts for her eldest sister to take back for her niece Heng'er.","Another three days passed, around the time Zhou Yuanshen was due back from the capital garrison, when the Zhou family once again sent someone to the General's residence.","This time, it was actually Nanny Sun who came in person.","\"...Young Madam, do you wish to see her?\" Suyue asked.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"I have to see her. If she appears in person, it's as good as the Dowager Madame appearing herself.\"","Since Nanny Sun had come, the Dowager Madame must have calmed down and started thinking about the real matters at hand.","Cheng Zhao received Nanny Sun in the front hall of the General's residence.","Nanny Sun was always stern, and this time was no different.","\"Young Madam, the Dowager Madame requests that you return to the mansion to stay. The restoration of Ronghua Courtyard requires your own input,\" Nanny Sun said.","Her face was stiff and proper as she looked calmly at Cheng Zhao, her gaze sharp.","Cheng Zhao spoke in a gentle and composed manner: \"When Ronghua Courtyard caught fire, someone tried to burn me to death. I was frightened.\"","She added, \"I heard the termite inspection is finished—they found the nest in Second Aunt's courtyard, and she's moved back; my dowry staff have moved to the servants' quarters, and Ronghua Courtyard is empty awaiting repairs?\"","\"Young Madam certainly has far-reaching connections—even from the General's residence, you know everything about the Duke's mansion,\" Nanny Sun said.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"I am, after all, the Duchess.\"","\"The Dowager Madame said the Duchess may temporarily stay at Chengming Hall,\" Nanny Sun said.","Cheng Zhao looked rather surprised. \"Then has the arsonist been caught?\"","\"It was the First Madam,\" Nanny Sun said.","Cheng Zhao said, \"Aunt?\"","Nanny Sun said, \"The First Madam confessed herself. She placed a fire-accelerating powder inside the Buddhist scriptures. When a spark from the incense fell onto the scriptures by accident, it would ignite within half an hour.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","So there had been an unexpected windfall.","Cheng Zhao's idea of having someone set the fire had actually originated from her aunt.","That time, her aunt had looked at Cheng Zhao with a venomous expression and offered to embroider scriptures for her—that had given Cheng Zhao the idea of starting a fire in the small prayer hall.","She just hadn't known how her aunt would do it or plan it.","Cheng Zhao had followed that path and done it first.","In the end, it really was the scriptures that were the problem.","Her aunt was simply too impatient.","She had experienced little in her life, her horizons confined to the inner quarters, and she had never faced much hardship before Cheng Zhao married in—she was far too rash.","\"I never imagined she would try to burn me to death,\" Cheng Zhao said, pressing a hand to her chest.","\"You may return and ask her yourself,\" Nanny Sun said.","Cheng Zhao said, \"I don't think this was my aunt's idea. Perhaps someone misled her into believing that killing me would let her return to Chengming Hall.\"","Nanny Sun seemed about to say something, but held back.","She knew whom Cheng Zhao was referring to.","Cheng Zhao: \"Mother, please go back. I’ll wait for Lord Duke to return to the city, and then we’ll go home together.\"","Nanny Sun: \"Young Madam, you must go and pay your respects to the Dowager Madame. She is waiting for you.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"Grandmother would not be so harsh as to torment a bird startled by the mere twang of a bowstring. With Lord Duke away from home, I am afraid. I was nearly burned to death.\"","Nanny Sun: \"...\"","You weren’t even there the day of the fire—how were you nearly burned to death?"]},{"number":208,"title":"Chapter 208: The Beauty Trap","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao was a slippery eel that no one could catch.","Nanny Sun tried to deal with her and nearly had a heart attack from frustration.","Compared to the First Madam and the Second Madam, Cheng Zhao was far bolder. She didn't even fear the Dowager Madame, let alone Nanny Sun.","Nanny Sun's authority was utterly useless against her.","When it was time to be firm, Cheng Zhao was clear in her stance; when it was time to play weak, she looked utterly pitiful.","Nanny Sun talked for a long while, her face turning uglier by the minute, yet she still failed to drag Cheng Zhao back.","Her first mission was a failure.","The Dowager Madame naturally assumed that since Nanny Sun had gone in her stead, it was as good as going herself, and Cheng Zhao would surely return.","But only Nanny Sun came back.","\"...You were right, that Cheng Shi is simply out of her mind!\" Nanny Sun said. \"Dowager Madame, this old servant couldn't do a thing with her.\"","The Dowager Madame pondered for a moment: \"Help me change my clothes. I'll pay a visit to the palace.\"","Nanny Sun: \"You wish to have the Emperor intervene?\"","\"That Cheng Shi was married into this family by imperial decree from the Empress, so she has backing, which is why she dares to act so brazenly. She shows no respect to her elders. I ought to voice a complaint or two,\" the Dowager Madame said.","Nanny Sun acknowledged the order.","The Dowager Madame did not need to request an audience in advance; she could always visit the Emperor whenever she pleased.","The Emperor was always happy to see her.","But to her surprise, in the imperial study, she ran into Zhou Yuanshen.","The Emperor was nowhere to be found.","\"Grandmother, His Majesty has a bit of a headache. He went for a stroll in the imperial garden. Consort Wu is with him,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Consort Wu was the Emperor's newly acquired consort and greatly favored by him.","Last time the Emperor went out, he even had Consort Wu dress as a young eunuch to accompany him. It had been many years since the Emperor had doted so heavily on any consort.","This Consort Wu had entered the palace in the fifth month, and her rise to favor was only in the last two months. The official who selected and sent Consort Wu into the palace was rumored to be a close aide of Zhou Yuanshen's.","— Only rumored, though; the Dowager Madame wasn't certain.","She had sent people to investigate, but they had found nothing.","\"Aren't you stationed at the capital's garrison?\" the Dowager Madame asked, all affability.","\"His Majesty issued a special decree to summon me back. He had a nightmare last night and was restless, so he called me to keep him company.","He had originally planned to visit the Zhou residence, as Grandmother's pastries soothe him. But with me back, he had someone to talk to, and naturally he recovered,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","He spoke slowly.","His gaze was calm and steady, seemingly devoid of emotion.","But every single word struck at the Dowager Madame's heart.","She looked at him: \"Yuanshen, what are you doing?\"","\"Exactly what a minister should do: loyalty, duty, and outstanding ability,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","The Dowager Madame's smile was almost impossible to maintain.","Moments later, the Emperor and Consort Wu returned.","Consort Wu was eighteen or nineteen, with a delicate, seductive beauty, and her manner was somehow familiar.","The Dowager Madame knew of this consort but had never seen her before. She was exquisite and graceful, exuding a gentle charm that strongly resembled Xian Si, the singing girl the Emperor had once bestowed upon Zhou Yuanshen.","Seeing the Dowager Madame, Consort Wu was warm and reverent: \"The Dowager Madame indeed has remarkable bearing, like a bodhisattva. This humble consort feels at peace just looking at you.\"","Then she turned to the Emperor: \"Your Majesty, even worshipping Buddha would not give me the same comfort as meeting the Dowager Madame.\"","The Emperor's face unconsciously broke into a smile: \"You certainly have good taste.\"","The Dowager Madame smiled modestly: \"Your Highness flatters me too much.\"","\"This must be fate between this humble consort and the Dowager Madame. I hear Your Ladyship also recites Buddhist scriptures. Allow me to embroider nine volumes of sutras for you,\" Consort Wu said cheerfully and breezily.","The Dowager Madame hastily declined, saying it was too much honor.","But the Emperor said, \"Let her do it, Mother-in-law. Consort Wu has plenty of spare time, with youth and energy to spare—it is her filial devotion.\"","The Dowager Madame could only consent.","A few words from Consort Wu, and the frown lines on the Emperor's brow smoothed away.","The Dowager Madame lowered her gaze.","Zhou Yuanshen stood nearby, silent.","The Emperor asked the Dowager Madame why she had come.","\"...I saw sparrows feeding their young under the eaves this morning and found myself thinking of Your Majesty,\" the Dowager Madame said with a smile.","The Emperor was even more pleased: \"I did suffer nightmares last night and barely slept. Since Mother-in-law is here, and Yuanshen too, let us have lunch together.\"","The Dowager Madame and Zhou Yuanshen acknowledged.","At lunch, the Dowager Madame shared the table with the Emperor, Zhou Yuanshen sat at a lower seat, and Consort Wu stood to the side, tasting dishes and serving the Emperor.","She performed all this with perfect skill.","After the meal, the grandmother and grandson of the Zhou family left the palace together.","Nanny Sun was waiting at the palace gate. Seeing Zhou Yuanshen, she too was startled; then she looked at the Dowager Madame's face.","The Dowager Madame's expression showed nothing unusual—her smile remained as amiable as ever.","Once in the carriage, the Dowager Madame unclenched her tightly held hand; the palm was wet with sweat, and fine beads of perspiration stood on her temples.","\"...Yuanshen used 'an eye for an eye.' He sent the Emperor a woman,\" the Dowager Madame said.","Nanny Sun was taken aback: \"You mean the consort the Emperor recently promoted above rank?\"","\"Yes, her,\" the Dowager Madame said. \"What beauty, what cleverness—she has the Emperor completely figured out.\"","Consort Wu's deference toward the Dowager Madame had been so abject, so utterly humble, that even she had been startled.","And the Emperor, without a doubt, was thoroughly pleased. When he looked at Consort Wu, his eyes held an added layer of tenderness.","Even the Empress had never shown the Dowager Madame such reverence before the Emperor. And Zhou Yuanshen excelled at reading the Emperor's mind—this was almost certainly his design.","\"Will she work against you?\" Nanny Sun asked.","The Dowager Madame: \"She is Yuanshen's woman. Of course she works against me.\"","With Consort Wu in the palace, if the Dowager Madame wanted to deal with her, she would have to do it through the Emperor.","But right now, the Emperor's heart was entirely with that consort.","Observing closely, the Dowager Madame felt that the Emperor was showing off in front of Consort Wu—but he was the Emperor. What did he need to flaunt?","Unless it was courtship.","No matter a man's age, in front of a woman he truly fancied, he could not resist displaying himself.","\"Did you bring up matters at home?\" Nanny Sun asked.","The Dowager Madame shook her head.","She said nothing more, silent for the entire ride home.","Once back at the ducal mansion, the Dowager Madame immediately summoned the household steward and ordered him to have the family possessions moved to the main quarters of the Chenming Hall.","\"Tell the Duke and the Duchess to return and take up residence,\" she said to the steward.","The steward was stunned: \"Move into Chenming Hall?\"","\"The Duke has inherited the title; it is only right that he resides in Chenming Hall,\" the Dowager Madame said.","Then she added, \"But first, go ask the second branch: does Madam Fan wish to reside there too?\"","The steward: \"...\"","To have the Duchess move into Chenming Hall and then ask the Second Madam about it—was that not fanning discord?","But since the Dowager Madame ordered it, the steward had no choice but to comply.","He went personally to the Jiangyun Courtyard.","Upon hearing this, the Second Madam was blank for a moment, then said: \"Go and fetch the Duke and the Third Young Madam back home. I know of this matter; we will discuss it later.\"","The steward acknowledged and took his leave.","After he was gone, the Second Madam couldn't help but laugh.","\"...Sending such clumsy tricks toward me. How shamelessly transparent!\" the Second Madam said. \"Zhaozhao has what she wanted—she can live in Chenming Hall.\"","Nanny Fan said: \"They wanted you to fight for it.\"","\"Am I mad, to fight over that? If my son and daughter-in-law live in Chenming Hall, that is even more secure than if I lived there myself,\" the Second Madam said.","Then she let out another cold laugh: \"What filthy thoughts. They want to drive a wedge in this family. The old lady really does judge others by herself.\""]},{"number":209,"title":"Chapter 209: His Grace Dotes on the Young Lady","paragraphs":["At dusk, the courtyard was lit with lanterns when Zhou Yuanshen finally returned to the General's Mansion. After leaving the palace, he had stopped by the Fan residence for a brief meeting with Fan Xiao.","The main courtyard of the mansion was bright, light spilling through the lattice windows. A lively scene awaited, for his mother and his fifth brother had come to visit Cheng Zhao.","\"...If you move like that, you'll lose in no time,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","\"The chess manual says this move is allowed,\" said Cheng Zhao.","\"I'm going to take your chariot,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Cheng Zhao retorted, \"Your chess manual is misleading me. Give it back—I still need that chariot.\"","\"Give it back to your sister-in-law. What nonsense is this? Why aren't you following the manual?\" said the Second Madam.","Zhou Yuanqi fumed, shouting in frustration, \"Don't touch my board! Who plays chess by following the manual move for move?\"","Zhou Yuanshen: \"...\"","Cheng Zhao caught sight of him first, casually shoving aside her nearly losing match as she rose: \"Lord Duke has returned.\"","The Second Madam and Zhou Yuanqi turned around.","\"Where are you coming from?\" The Second Madam looked him over.","Whenever he returned from the Jingyi camp, he wore light armor.","Today, however, he was in official robes.","\"I came back mid-morning and went to the palace. Had lunch with His Majesty, then met briefly with Uncle Fan,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","\"Two days earlier than expected,\" Cheng Zhao noted.","Zhou Yuanshen then relayed how the emperor had called him back to the city ahead of schedule.","\"Grandmother has gone to the palace,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","The Second Madam said, \"Your grandmother sent word for Zhaozhao to go back and stay in Chengming Hall.\"","She then recounted how the head steward had come to stir up trouble before the Second Madam.","\"Those people are simply ridiculous,\" said the Second Madam.","Cheng Zhao responded, \"Mother, you could go stay at Chengming Hall.\"","\"I won't,\" said the Second Madam. \"Every day the stewards come to report, and the place is bursting with people. I couldn't even practice my spear at dawn without it becoming the talk of the house.\"","She'd be driven to distraction.","She added, \"It's not that I ever yearned to live at Chengming Hall—I just couldn't stand them looking down on us, trampling on us. Now that you can stay there, we've gotten what was due to us. Why would I hold any grudge? You and I don't need to be so precise with each other—I know your heart.\"","Cheng Zhao said nothing more, only clasped her hand: \"Thank you, Mother.\"","The Second Madam smiled with warmth.","She then asked Zhou Yuanshen, \"When are you two heading back?\"","\"There's still much to settle with Grandmother. I'll go back tomorrow, and Cheng Zhao can wait,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao nodded: \"I'll follow Lord Duke's arrangements.\"","They exchanged a few more words.","The hour growing late, Suyue came in to ask Cheng Zhao when dinner should be served.","\"Let's eat first,\" said the Second Madam. \"We still need to head home.\"","\"Mother and Fifth Brother can stay the night here,\" Zeng Zhao offered.","The Second Madam: \"The old lady is already simmering with anger. If we stayed out, we'd give her an excuse to make a scene. Better to go back.\"","Cheng Zhao smiled: \"Mother thinks of everything.\"","After dinner, Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen escorted the Second Madam and Zhou Yuanqi to the main gate.","Zhou Yuanqi said to Zeng Zhao, \"Practice your chess properly—I'll come challenge you next time.\"","\"Alright.\"","Once they had left, Zhou Yuanshen and Cheng Zhao walked back together, and he took her hand.","His palm was scorching hot.","The late-autumn night breeze was biting, and Cheng Zhao's hands were cold, so he gripped hers all the tighter.","\"...Would you like me to teach you chess?\" he asked.","Cheng Zhao: \"No need—Fifth Brother will teach me. He puts on a grumpy face, but he's very patient when he explains.\"","Having something to do with Zhou Yuanqi would pass the time.","Zhou Yuanshen said nothing in reply.","When they returned to the main courtyard, Qiubai and Suyue had the bath barrel ready.","Zhou Yuanshen said, \"All of you, withdraw. We won't need anyone on night duty.\"","The maids all departed.","In the courtyard only the couple remained.","Cheng Zhao's heart inexplicably burned. She turned, meaning to say something, but Zhou Yuanshen silenced her with a kiss.","That night, Cheng Zhao was nearly taken apart limb by limb.","She grew reluctant later on.","\"...Cheng Zhao, I brought you a gift,\" he coaxed her. \"Put in a little effort—your return gift is all I ask.\"","Cheng Zhao wrapped her arms around his neck: \"You give a gift and then expect one back?\"","She could barely catch her breath.","Zhou Yuanshen wore her down, gently teasing and pressing.","By the end, the water had gone cold, so they only made a hasty toweling-off. Cheng Zhao, held in his arms, drifted toward sleep with a haze.","She felt a bit sore.","A light ache, nothing serious—even a pleasant soreness after such fullness—that only made her sleepier.","Zhou Yuanshen's hand moved soothingly over her back as he murmured to her, and she only hummed in response.","She slept until late morning light filled the room.","When she woke, Zhou Yuanshen was no longer in bed—he had gone to court.","Suyue came in and lowered her voice: \"Young Madam, would you like to bathe? Lord Duke asked us to have hot water prepared for you.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","She did end up taking a bath.","The night had been cold, but the carrying-on had worked up a light sweat, and by the time she could wash, the water in the barrel had gone completely cold—so she'd deferred.","After dressing, Cheng Zhao sat down to a belated breakfast.","Half the morning had gone by.","\"Start packing—we'll be heading back within a day or two,\" Cheng Zhao told Suyue and Qiubai.","\"We'll be staying at Chengming Hall, I presume?\" Suyue smile.","Cheng Zhao: \"I should think so—the head steward came by to tell us so.\"","\"Young Madam, why don't you wait a while? Let Nanny Li have Chengming Hall arranged first, then you can go,\" Suyue suggested.","Cheng Zhao: \"Let's not provoke the Grand Dowager further.\"","\"One should not,\" Cheng Zhao remarked with a slight smile, \"taunt a cornered beast. It's not fear—just sensibility.\"","Suyue saw the logic in that.","Just then Qiubai entered carrying a long, narrow case.","\"Lord Duke brought this over this morning—said it's a gift for you,\" Qiubai said.","Cheng Zhao recalled now: Zhou Yuanshen had mentioned a gift.","She opened it to reveal a black, cylindrical tube.","\"What is that?\" Suyue and Qiubai crouched around, unable to tell.","Cheng Zhao, however, recognized it—she'd seen one before at her second sister-in-law's.","\"This is an import—it's called a kaleidoscope. The inside is quite amusing,\" Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","She pried off the lid and set it against her eye.","As she rotated it, images unfolded like paintings before her—foreign landscapes, vividly colorful and utterly novel. Delightful, she found it.","Cheng Zhao was rather taken with it.","\"I'll take it over later to show Fifth Brother and show it off to him,\" Cheng Zhao declared.","She then passed it around to Suyue and Qiubai for a look.","Both were mesmerized.","\"It feels like it pokes me straight in the eyeball,\" Suyue observed.","Cheng Zhao laughed at that.","Qiubai likewise found it miraculous.","The trio lingered over the kaleidoscope for quite a while.","\"Lord Duke is truly thoughtful,\" Qiubai remarked.","Cheng Zhao hummed in agreement.","\"Have we got anything nice to give him back?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","Suyue and Qiubai began to inventory their lady's dowry—everything the Cheng household owned of note seemed to appeal to civil scholars.","For a man of letters, one might offer rare manuscripts, calligraphy rubbings, a fine inkstone—treasures every student adores. The Cheng family could easily produce such things.","But as for a general's manly tastes, they had no idea. Nor, alas, any item.","\"Perhaps you should ask him what he likes next time,\" said Qiubai.","Suyue interjected: \"Need you ask? He likes our young lady Cheng Zhao.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","Shortly before midday, Zeng Zhao arrived back at the Duke Chen’s mansion and presented herself at the Grand Dowager’s Shou'an Hall.","Upon hearing of her arrival, the Grand Dowager wiped her face into a smile, sliding the mask of benevolence back into place.","Cheng Zhao bowed respectfully.","\"You look somewhat thinner than a few days ago,\" the Grand Dowager observed, gesturing for Cheng Zhao to take the chair beside her.","Seating herself, Cheng Zhao prepared to play her role."]},{"number":210,"title":"Chapter 210: The Madam Is Out","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao's attitude was extremely cooperative.","She first apologized to the Grand Lady: \"These past days have made Grandmother worry. You sent two groups of people to check on me, and I am deeply grateful in my heart.\"","Nanny Sun, listening nearby, could hardly stop herself from rolling her eyes.","When it came to putting on a performance, few could match Cheng Zhao's skill.","It was almost as if it were real.","\"It's just that the fire at Nonghua Court truly frightened me. Once the Duke returned to the city, I felt I had someone to rely on, and only then did I dare come back to apologize to Grandmother,\" Cheng Zhao continued.","The Grand Lady smiled and said, \"You truly are a bit timid.\"","With that, she sighed, and her smile faded. \"Your Eldest Aunt was foolish, committing such a disgraceful act. A physician was called to take her pulse—she is genuinely ill. She has been moved to the country estate to recuperate.\"","She added, \"You may not know yet—her natal family has run afoul of the law, and their title may be stripped. That is what drove her to lose her wits.\"","Cheng Zhao looked at the Grand Lady.","The Grand Lady looked back at Cheng Zhao.","And Cheng Zhao understood—the Eldest Madam Song's natal family, the Marquis of Changling, was finished.","Not immediately, of course.","First, Song would be moved out; after a period of time, word of her death would be announced, and then the Marquis of Changling would be destroyed.","Punishing Eldest Madam Song was also a warning to Cheng Zhao and the others—a lesson in knowing their place, a lesson that they must not casually betray the Grand Lady.","The Grand Lady wasn't even afraid to tell Cheng Zhao in advance. This was already a settled matter; even Zhou Yuanshen could not save the Song family.","Cheng Zhao put on a timid and shocked expression: \"So that's what happened. Eldest Aunt is pitiable in her own way.\"","\"She should never have schemed against you—you had no grievance with her,\" the Grand Lady said.","Cheng Zhao sighed along with her.","The Grand Lady then asked, \"Now that you're back, would you be willing to move into Chenming Hall?\"","Cheng Zhao: \"If Grandmother shows me such favor, I would never dare let it go to waste. Only, Chenming Hall is the main residence's chief quarters—it rightfully belongs to Grandmother.\"","Since Eldest Madam Song had been sent away, aside from the Grand Lady, only Cheng Zhao and her mother-in-law had the standing to live there. Huan Qingtang had once been the Heir's Wife, but she held no noble title, and her husband had passed away—she could not occupy it.","\"I'm old, where would I find the energy to live in Chenming Hall?\" the Grand Lady laughed. \"Better that you live there. From now on, this household relies on you and your eldest sister-in-law.\"","She had brought up Huan Qingtang.","But Cheng Zhao did not take the bait—didn't even offer a polite word.","She only said: \"Granddaughter-in-law thanks Grandmother!\"","She stood up and bowed with utmost respect.","The Grand Lady smiled faintly.","Cheng Zhao left Shou'an Court and took a small carriage back to Nonghua Court.","Nonghua Court looked bedraggled—the main chamber had been more than half burned, black smoke stains drifting from the window frames, leaving the eaves darkened and the place in disrepair.","The plants in the courtyard had gone days without care, and because it was deep autumn, they had all withered and died.","As if the entire place had lost its vitality overnight.","Cheng Zhao had never before seen a courtyard \"die\" like this, and she was rather taken aback.","\"...It's only been a few days—how did it come to this?\" The one who voiced this was Suyue.","Cheng Zhao nodded: \"Not many days.\"","Nanny Li had also come, trailing behind them, and said with a smile: \"Because winter is approaching. In winter, all things wither—that's why it seems so barren.\"","Cheng Zhao felt a wave of melancholy.","Knowing something and seeing it with your own eyes were two different things; she still couldn't help but be taken aback.","After surveying Nonghua Court, Cheng Zhao went to the Second Madam's Crimson Cloud Court.","The Second Madam had Nanny Fan relay to Cheng Zhao everything that had happened in the household these past days.","\"...Eldest Madam was moved out the night before last. They say she tried to hang herself—she hung for a good while before being cut down, injuring her throat. When she left, she still had white gauze wrapped around her neck and couldn't speak.\" Nanny Fan said.","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","Seeing Cheng Zhao silent, the Second Madam said, \"Child, why are you so much like me? Are you feeling soft-hearted? I only heard this morning, and I felt awful myself.\"","Cheng Zhao snapped back to the moment and gave her mother-in-law a gentle smile.","Her mother-in-law was indeed a kind and soft-hearted woman. Eldest Madam had always targeted her over the years, and yet upon hearing of her downfall, there was no gloating—only sorrow.","Cheng Zhao felt no pity. She had only been silent because she was wondering: who was silencing a witness?","If it were Huan Qingtang, she would certainly have placed people around Eldest Madam. These past few years, Huan Qingtang had not been idle—only meticulous in her work, so no one could see it.","If it were the Grand Lady, then Eldest Madam was doomed. The rescue was only because Eldest Madam was not meant to die in the house.","The hanging attempt was an omen—a message to be spread, letting people know that Eldest Madam Song had made an attempt on her own life.","By the time the next announcement of her death came, no one in the Duke's household would be surprised.","\"Mother, we are all daughters-in-law here. To feel the grief of one's own kind is only human,\" Cheng Zhao said.","The Second Madam: \"Don't worry, I won't meddle in anything. She got what she deserved.\"","Then, abruptly, she added, \"And someday, the old lady will get hers as well.\"","Cheng Zhao smiled, offering no response.","The Second Madam, having said it, also felt the remark was inappropriate and changed the subject: \"Will you move into Chenming Hall tonight?\"","\"Yesterday the Duke said he still had some matters to settle with Grandmother. He should be returning to the residence as well. I'll wait for his news,\" Cheng Zhao said.","The Second Madam: \"Very well.\"","Soon, the Second Master and Zhou Yuanqi returned.","Crimson Cloud Court hadn't been this lively in a long time.","The Second Madam deliberately sent money to the main kitchen to add a few extra dishes.","The woman in charge of the main kitchen was one of Cheng Zhao's trusted people, and she carried the dinner hamper over personally. She also stopped by Crimson Cloud Court to pay her respects to Cheng Zhao.","\"...When Nonghua Court caught fire, we old servants were frightened out of our wits. But everyone in the main kitchen felt for the Third Young Madam, and each of them did their duty without a single slip. The Young Madam can rest easy,\" the head stewardess said.","Cheng Zhao nodded: \"You've all been cautious. I know what I'm doing.\"","A few words, and the mistress and servant understood each other perfectly.","After the stewardess left, Mingyu, the maid from Zhou Yuanshen's outer study, arrived at Crimson Cloud Court.","\"...The Duke had intended to return for dinner, but the Grand Lady sent people to wait at the main gate and had him go to Shou'an Court. The Duke said not to save him any dinner—he'll eat there,\" Mingyu said.","\"We'll eat first, then,\" the Second Madam said.","The senior maid escorted Mingyu out; Nanny Fan led several maids in arranging the chopsticks and serving the dishes.","After the meal, the family gathered in the eastern side room to talk.","The Second Master mentioned something surprising: \"Princess Qing'an's consort has been released from prison—it was the Prince of Andong who went to retrieve him.\"","Zhou Yuanqi lifted his head sharply, staring at the Second Master.","Cheng Zhao and the Second Madam turned to Zhou Yuanqi in confusion.","\"Why are you so worked up?\" the Second Madam asked.","Zhou Yuanqi's small face scrunched up. \"Why did he save Princess Qing'an's husband?\"","\"They're all of the imperial clan—kin,\" the Second Master said.","Cheng Zhao: \"Princess Qing'an has some influence. The late Emperor was very fond of her. She has a good relationship with the Jingnan Prince's household.\"","\"How disgusting,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Looking quite disappointed.","The others were baffled.","Cheng Zhao said, \"You seem to like him a lot? What caught your eye about him? His scholarship is quite mediocre.\"","Zhou Yuanqi muttered something under his breath, but Cheng Zhao couldn't make it out.","When she pressed him again, he refused to say.","\"Helian Xuan is a man of no small ability,\" the Second Master said. \"And seemingly, also of no small ambition.\"","Cheng Zhao disliked the man intensely.","She had no wish to listen.","Fortunately, the Second Master also disliked discussing court politics and soon changed the subject.","The night deepened. Zhou Yuanqi yawned several times, and still Zhou Yuanshen had not returned.","Second Madam said, \"Zhao Zhao, don't go to the General's Mansion tonight. Stay in the east wing instead.\"","As she was speaking, Zhou Yuanshen arrived."]},{"number":211,"title":"Chapter 211: Moving into Chengming Hall","paragraphs":["Zhou Yuanshen came in, and Second Madam immediately asked urgently, “What did you talk about with your grandmother?”","Zhou Yuanqi’s drowsiness was now completely gone.","Second Master also looked at his son.","Cheng Zhao moved aside and gave her chair to Zhou Yuanshen.","Zhou Yuanshen sat down before saying, “I told her that Cheng Zhao and I don’t want to live in Chenming Hall. We plan to stay at the General’s mansion long-term.”","Everyone was taken aback.","Second Madam nearly lost her seat: “Why not stay? That place is rightfully yours.”","“Making Cheng Zhao a chief steward isn’t very meaningful,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao understood what he meant.","If the rent income from the hereditary estate never passed through Cheng Zhao’s hands, then no matter how hard she worked in the household, she would just be a manager.","She’d have status, but no money.","Second Master stayed silent.","Zhou Yuanqi then said, “Don’t be greedy. What if grandmother goes mad and has us all killed? I’m still young.”","The little scholar, who was always afraid of being caught up in the fallout, valued his life dearly.","Second Madam shot him a dissatisfied glance.","Cheng Zhao couldn’t help but smile.","Zhou Yuanshen told him, “You can practice the spear or sword to protect yourself.”","“That would be beneath my scholarly dignity.”","Zhou Yuanshen replied, “‘The gentleman hides his tools upon his person.’ You constantly cultivate virtue and learning, so surely your dignity is harder than blade and spear. No need to worry—you won’t die.”","Zhou Yuanqi: “...”","Cheng Zhao’s smile was almost impossible to suppress.","Before she could laugh, Second Madam burst out laughing, which made Zhou Yuanqi very unhappy: “Mother!”","“Alright, alright,” Second Master said, stepping in to smooth things over. “Stop derailing. Let Yuan Shen continue.”","Turning to Zhou Yuanshen, he asked, “You’re not really going to give up the residence, are you? Not at this point. What did your grandmother say? Did the two of you come to an agreement?”","“Grandmother is still alive. If we asked for the accounts of the hereditary estate now, it wouldn’t sound good to outsiders,” Zhou Yuanshen said. “Grandmother also doesn’t want to be harsh to the younger generation. She said she would give each household fifty thousand taels a year.”","Second Madam was stunned again, hardly believing it: “Fifty thousand taels?”","That much?","Second Master asked, “By ‘each household,’ which ones?”","“Jiangyun Courtyard, Cuiyun Courtyard, and Chenming Hall,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","That covered Second Madam’s side, Cheng Zhao, and Huan Qingtang.","If Huan Qingtang had money in her hands, she would likely stir up trouble again.","The Dowager Madame was giving her capital to contend with Cheng Zhao, wasn’t she?","At that thought, Cheng Zhao said nothing.","“Paying out a hundred fifty thousand taels a year—where would the old lady get all that silver? How many years could she sustain it?” Second Madam asked.","Everyone fell silent.","Zhou Yuanqi was blunt: “Mother, the yearly rent income is far more than a hundred fifty thousand taels, let alone whatever’s been saved up before.”","Second Madam: “The estate produces that much?”","“If it didn’t, they wouldn’t be holding on to it,” Zhou Yuanqi said.","Second Madam: “...”","She truly had no idea.","She simply clung to the title of “Duke’s Manor” because she refused to leave and couldn’t swallow that humiliation.","She rarely calculated the estate’s income.","The Fan family had made up for her dowry lands and shops, her mother occasionally slipped her some money, and Second Master had his own private assets. Second Madam had never been strapped for cash, so she never paid much attention to wealth.","Thinking it over more carefully, Second Madam was startled: “The emperor really did gift the Zhou family a great deal!”","“Mother, please say less. Third brother hasn’t gotten me killed yet—you’ll do it first,” Zhou Yuanqi said.","Second Madam: “...”","Zhou Yuanqi and Second Madam kept interrupting, and the conversation kept drifting off track. It was Second Master who kept pulling it back.","He asked many questions.","All of them were things Cheng Zhao wanted to ask.","Zhou Yuanshen gave detailed answers to everything. He spoke to Second Master, but he was also speaking to Cheng Zhao.","\"Since we've come to an agreement, when will you move into Chengming Hall?\" asked the Second Master.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, \"Let's pick an auspicious day.\"","\"We should choose a good day. But it needs to be soon,\" said the Second Master. \"Only once you're settled in can we rest easy.\"","He glanced meaningfully at Zhou Yuanshen. “The Song family, your aunt’s family on your eldest uncle’s wife’s side, has gotten into trouble. The case is about to go to trial.”","Zhou Yuanshen uttered a soft \"Mm.\"","The Second Madam asked, \"What happened to the Song family?\"","\"No arrests have been made yet; it's just rumors at this point,\" said the Second Master. \"Once the Court of Judicial Review hands down a verdict, I'll tell you.\"","The Second Madam said, \"My sister-in-law just went out of town to recuperate, and now her natal family has run into trouble. Could it be that the Old Lady...\"","She stopped mid-sentence and covered her mouth.","No more could be said.","The conversation was nearly wrapped up. Zhou Yuanshen rose to his feet. \"Father and Mother, please retire early. We'll go rest as well.\"","\"Are you two heading back to the General's residence?\"","\"We'll stay at Chenhui Courtyard for now,\" said Zhou Yuanshen. \"The side rooms are a bit simple, but they're perfectly livable.\"","The Second Madam wanted to persuade them to stay. But then she thought about how the household was full of prying eyes and wagging tongues, and how the Dowager Madame and Huan Qingtang were still watching with hawk-like vigilance. It really wouldn't be proper for the young daughter-in-law to sleep in her in-laws' courtyard.","It wasn't as if they were guests staying over.","\"If you need anything, just take it from Jiangyun Courtyard,\" said the Second Madam.","\"We lack for nothing, Mother. I take my midday rests at Chenhui Courtyard, so everything's within reach there,\" said Cheng Zhao.","The Second Madam gave a slight nod.","That night, the Second Madam barely slept. She kept the Second Master up, talking.","\"...I've often said, I've been married into the Zhou family for over twenty years. When I think about it carefully, in the decade or so since we returned to the capital, we've known nothing about what goes on in this ducal manor. We've been blind, deaf,\" said the Second Madam.","The Second Master replied, \"There's no need to know, either. We have no say in these matters, so why trouble ourselves?\"","\"What secrets does this manor actually hold? And how much wealth? Not just farmland—shops, properties, all of it,\" said the Second Madam.","The Second Master said, \"I'm not really sure either.\"","\"Of course you're not. The Old Lady never favored you, so why would she tell you anything?\" said the Second Madam.","She rambled on and on, and gradually fell asleep.","The Second Master, however, barely slept at all.","On the seventeenth day of the ninth month, Cheng Zhao moved into Chengming Hall.","In the days leading up to it, the five main rooms of Chengming Hall had been completely redone.","The bed was custom-made by the Xu family workshop—they made the finest beds around. The screen was rush-made by the Hu family workshop, with a huanghuali wood base.","Every table, every chair had its provenance. Every detail was exquisite.","Most of it had been brought back by Zhou Yuanshen; some pieces came from the Zhou family storerooms; and the antique ornaments on the decorative shelves were part of Cheng Zhao's dowry.","Early in the morning, Zhou Yuanshen went to court as usual, and Cheng Zhao rose early to wash and dress.","The Second Madam made a special trip over to take a look.","\"Ah Shen must have made preparations a long time ago to have you stay in Chengming Hall,\" said the Second Madam after inspecting the place.","Otherwise, that great bed in the inner chamber would have taken months of work to finish—how could it possibly have been ready in such a short time?","\"I had no idea either,\" said Cheng Zhao. \"I thought the Lord Duke was too busy to bother with household trifles.\"","\"He takes after his father in that regard. Your father-in-law—when he gets meticulous, he's utterly fussy. There are times I find it quite trying,\" said the Second Madam.","\"Mother is blessed in her marriage.\"","\"You're not doing badly yourself,\" said the Second Madam, beaming with pleasure.","At the doorway of the inner chamber hung a beaded curtain of colored glass, as resplendent as brocade embroidered with flowers.","These glazed glass pieces were a gift from the Second Madam on Cheng Zhao’s last birthday. Cheng Zhao had also added some diamonds, which had previously hung by the inner bedroom door of Nonghua Courtyard and have now been moved to Chengming Hall.","The morning sunlight streamed through the doorway, falling directly on the colored glass and refracting into a dazzling array of multicolored light that illuminated both the interior and exterior of the entrance.","\"How beautiful,\" Second Madam said.","\"Mother's gift is a fine one,\" Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","Second Madam finished her inspection, utterly delighted.","The stewards arrived one after another at the parlor of Chengming Hall to report their affairs, and Second Madam prepared to take her leave.","As she stepped out, Second Madam encountered two groups of stewards.","They each respectfully greeted her.","She also saw Huan Qingtang there."]},{"number":212,"title":"Chapter 212: Cheng Zhao Is Well-Informed","paragraphs":["Huan Qingtang paid her respects to Second Madam.","Second Madam nodded slightly and took a small oiled cart to Shou'an Court. Since she had come to Chengming Hall, she naturally had to make an appearance at Shou'an Court as well, lest the Dowager Madame find fault.","Huan Qingtang's maid could not help but say, \"Chengming Hall doesn't belong to the Second Branch, yet they all come running over.\"","Huan Qingtang said nothing, and stepped into Chengming Hall.","The five main rooms looked unchanged from the outside, but light spilled through the doorway, exceptionally lavish—the crystal beads at the entrance to the inner bedchamber were quite ostentatious.","Both cheap and conspicuous, like certain people.","Huan Qingtang looked away.","Cheng Zhao had also arrived early and was seated in the flower hall, flipping through the registry of names.","She had not managed affairs for over half a month, and her side had accumulated quite a lot of work. The stewards were all waiting for her decisions.","Even though matters were pressing, Cheng Zhao did not begin right away. She waited for Huan Qingtang to arrive.","The Dowager Madame had said that from now on, Cheng Zhao and Huan Qingtang would manage the household together—it was not Cheng Zhao's sole decision.","\"Since everyone is here, shall we begin?\" the chief steward asked the two young mistresses.","Cheng Zhao looked at Huan Qingtang: \"Sister-in-law?\"","Huan Qingtang nodded slightly and also picked up the registry.","The morning's business proceeded in the usual order, with each department reporting in turn.","Cheng Zhao handled matters with great efficiency.","Even though she had not attended to affairs for over half a month, she knew everything that happened in the household, down to the smallest detail.","For instance, regarding the invitations at the gate—which ones the Dowager Madame had already replied to, which required gifts and her decision—she knew them all by heart. The needlework department and the main kitchen's affairs, she managed with familiarity, without needing to ask for details.","Her manner intimidated the stewards. Huan Qingtang tried hard to contain herself, but could not help showing a trace of surprise.","When the morning ended, Cheng Zhao had her meal in Chengming Hall, unhurriedly.","As the others left Chengming Hall, they all discussed among themselves.","\"The Third Young Mistress has eyes and ears everywhere. How many people has she bought over?\"","\"Who among us is her spy or confidant, we don't know. Best be careful from now on.\"","\"She is the Duchess, and she has moved into Chengming Hall. This household is hers. The battle lines are clear. Anyone who still doesn't know where they stand is a fool.\"","In other words, Huan Qingtang's defeat was already certain.","The steward at the gate was not one of Cheng Zhao's people—he remained the Dowager Madame's trusted man.","But even during Cheng Zhao's absence from the residence, Cheng Zhao knew everything about the gate's affairs. The steward broke out in a cold sweat.","Who exactly was the spy beside him? If the Dowager Madame suspected him of betrayal, how would he defend himself?","\"Perhaps I should simply switch allegiance,\" he said to himself. \"The Dowager Madame is old. How much longer can she manage?\"","If he threw in his lot with Cheng Zhao, the benefits in the future might be considerable.","After all, Cheng Zhao had brought few retainers with her. She would inevitably rely on the old stewards.","The gate steward's mind raced in turmoil, and his resolve was already wavering.","Huan Qingtang returned to Cuiyun Court.","Cuiyun Court was very close to Chengming Hall. She walked back in a few steps and sat down in silence.","\"Eldest Young Mistress, have some tea to calm yourself,\" her trusted maid said, handing her a cup. \"Don't worry.\"","\"Cheng Zhao has quite the skill. That retreat of hers was a clever move. She leaves for half a month and comes back to win a stunning victory,\" Huan Qingtang said.","With three parts of effort, she gained a full ten parts of merit.","In less than two hours this morning, Cheng Zhao had secured the hearts of the stewards with her proficiency.","Even if they were not willing to be loyal to her, they would fear her.","Such skill, such worldliness, and such well-informed intelligence—how could any steward remain indifferent? Even Huan Qingtang herself had been deeply shaken.","\"Don't rush,\" her trusted maid said to Huan Qingtang. \"The Dowager Madame is more anxious than you. The one who doesn't want Cheng to manage the household is not you—it's the Dowager Madame.\"","What the Dowager Madame wanted was servants and stewards, not a mistress of the house.","What Cheng Zhao was encroaching upon was not Huan Qingtang's position, but the Dowager Madame's.","The Dowager Madame would be the first to find her intolerable.","\"She's showing off too much. The Dowager Madame will become wary,\" the maid said.","Huan Qingtang silently stirred the floating tea leaves with her cup. A thought lingered on her lips, but she did not voice it: if the Dowager Madame were truly so formidable, Cheng Zhao would never have moved into Chengming Hall.","Cheng Zhao moving in meant that the Dowager Madame had lost ground.","Huan Qingtang did not know how Cheng Zhao—or rather, Zhou Yuanshen—had pressured the Dowager Madame.","Not only had the Dowager Madame allowed Cheng Zhao to move into Chengming Hall, but she had also taken out silver to distribute to each branch—not a few hundred taels as a token, but fifty thousand taels a year.","To cut flesh and let blood like that showed how badly the Dowager Madame was losing.","Huan Qingtang's father had a reputation but held a modest official rank. Many matters he did not know either. Huan Qingtang felt that the struggle between the Dowager Madame and Zhou Yuanshen might be playing out at court or in the palace, but she could not get word of it.","If she had Cheng Zhao's connections, she would have done better than Cheng Zhao.","\"Grandmother is getting senile. At a time like this, she is still hiding things. If she doesn't want to keep losing, she should support me with everything she has,\" Huan Qingtang suddenly said.","Her trusted maid immediately replied, \"Will you go speak with her?\"","\"I cannot speak to her face to face,\" Huan Qingtang said.","If she had to, she could tell Nanny Sun, and Nanny Sun would relay it to the Dowager Madame.","But because of the Mid-Autumn Festival banquet incident, Huan Qingtang had offended Nanny Sun.","Now Nanny Sun guarded against Huan Qingtang as warily as she guarded against Cheng Zhao.","Over on Cheng Zhao's side, they were all of one mind—no one was dragging their feet. Everyone wished Cheng Zhao well and worked hard to support her. On Huan Qingtang's side, by contrast, everyone had their own schemes.","\"I must try again,\" Huan Qingtang said.","Inside Chengming Hall, Cheng Zhao had finished her midday meal when Zhou Yuanshen's page boy Nanfeng arrived.","\"...The garden's procurement has been switched to two new vendors,\" Nanfeng told Cheng Zhao.","During Cheng Zhao's absence, Nanfeng and Mingyu from the outer study had quietly gathered much information on her behalf.","The main kitchen staff had also contributed, passing on what they knew to Cheng Zhao's steward, Nanny Li.","Cheng Zhao listened quietly.","\"This afternoon, I'll deal with the garden matter,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"Once these affairs are straightened out, they probably won't dare stir up trouble deliberately anymore.\"","First intimidate the hearts of men. Once they dared not act recklessly, they would not be swayed into becoming others' tools.","Huan Qingtang excelled at driving others to make trouble while she stayed safely behind the scenes.","Cheng Zhao would first suppress the stewards and see what other tricks Huan Qingtang had when she no longer had people to move.","\"Qiubai, give some money to Nanfeng,\" Cheng Zhao instructed. \"Go buy yourself something good to eat. You did exceptionally well this time.\"","Nanfeng thanked her.","Then he added, \"Young Mistress, if you're satisfied with my service, please don't forget to mention it to Lord Duke.\"","Everyone laughed at this.","Cheng Zhao smiled as well: \"You're very clever, Nanfeng. Don't worry—men of real substance like you, Lord Duke will surely reward and promote.\"","That was the truth.","Given time, Nanfeng would surely become Zhou Yuanshen's right-hand man.","Young as he was, he was not just flexible in handling matters—he also thought long-term. That kind of foresight was nothing short of wise.","Cheng Zhao thought that, in the future, the chief steward of the ducal residence would be none other than Nanfeng.","Nanfeng was so delighted his eyes crinkled: \"Thank you, Young Mistress.\"","Zhou Yuanshen returned to the residence in the evening, when the stewards had all left.","Cheng Zhao was not in Chengming Hall either.","\"Young Mistress has gone to Jiangyun Court for the evening meal,\" Nanny Li told him.","Zhou Yuanshen headed to Jiangyun Court instead.","When he arrived, he happened to see his mother practicing with a spear, while Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanqi sat off to the side playing chess.","The Second Master had returned and, after changing his clothes, came out to wait for dinner.","The setting sun shone into the courtyard, bathing the little yard in a golden afterglow, cozy and lively.","“...Tonight we’re having sour radish duck soup,” Cheng Zhao told Zhou Yuanqi.","Zhou Yuanqi swallowed hard. “Fine, I’ll let you have two moves.”","Cheng Zhao: “Check!”","“I give you a courtesy, and you go for my throat?” Zhou Yuanqi’s little face scrunched up.","The Second Master came over to watch the game and couldn’t help but burst out laughing.","Zhou Yuanshen stepped into the courtyard."]},{"number":213,"title":"Chapter 213: Not Taking a Concubine","paragraphs":["After the evening meal, the family sat together at leisure.","Second Madam noticed that although they lived farther and farther apart from their son and daughter-in-law, their feelings for one another had actually grown closer.","\"...Two stewards in the rear garden have asked to retire and leave.\" Cheng Zhao brought up the afternoon's events.","\"They were being pushed out. They're people under Eldest Madam Song.\" Second Master said.","Cheng Zhao nodded: \"Yes.\"","\"Then let them go.\" Second Madam said.","Eldest Madam Song was beyond saving; her people couldn't be kept. Even if they were kept, they wouldn't be loyal to Cheng Zhao.","Stewards being released on account of old age was a common occurrence, not something Cheng Zhao could be faulted for.","\"Mother, it can't be handled so simply. We talked about 'the fox grieving for the hare' last time — the other stewards are watching. How the master treats those who came before is how they'll be treated in the future. If we do this, who would dare serve with total loyalty and give their all?\" Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam agreed deeply: \"That's true. So what did you do?\"","\"I had Nanfeng make inquiries in advance. One steward was given a retirement allowance plus an extra sum, because he was returning to his ancestral home; the other also received a retirement allowance but no bonus — instead, his second son was given a post in the rear garden.\" Cheng Zhao said.","Everyone looked at her.","Second Master laughed: \"I imagine both were satisfied?\"","\"Both stewards wept for joy. The other stewards praised me for handling it fairly.\" Cheng Zhao said.","Huan Qingtang's expression at the time hadn't been good.","She had probably assumed this was a trap for Cheng Zhao.","The Dowager Madame's people were squeezing out Eldest Madam Song's people, and Huan Qingtang had deliberately left this matter until Cheng Zhao returned, precisely to put Cheng Zhao in an impossible position.","Those two stewards who were leaving were full of resentment, because it wasn't what they wanted.","No matter what Cheng Zhao did, she would leave herself open to criticism.","But Cheng Zhao had covered every angle, soothing both men completely.","Seeing her handle things this way, what did the other stewards have to worry about? When they grew old in the future, Cheng Zhao wouldn't kick them aside after their use was spent.","Cheng Zhao only needed to look at Huan Qingtang's strained expression to know she had handled the matter very well.","\"Reading truly pays off. Young ladies from scholarly families are clever and sensible — their work truly leaves no cracks.\" Second Madam said with a smile.","Full of pride.","There was a time when she cursed scholarly families for being hypocritical — Second Master thought of this and glanced at her with a smile.","Second Madam knew what he was thinking. She shot him a look, stifling his words, forbidding him to speak. Second Master just smiled and indeed said nothing.","\"I used to mock others for putting on a show. But now I see — being able to put on a flawless show is a real skill.\" Second Madam added.","\"Mother, why don't you go apprentice under Third Sister-in-Law, learn her 'needlework,' and polish your own showmanship smooth as well.\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Second Madam: \"Are you asking for a beating?\"","Zhou Yuanqi: \"...\"","The room filled with laughter and cheerful talk.","Once the matter was settled, Cheng Zhao and the others rose to take their leave.","She and Zhou Yuanshen walked back together.","The weather was neither hot nor cold, perfect for a stroll to aid digestion after the meal.","\"First battle won — you should be quite pleased.\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao smiled: \"Nanfeng helped me a great deal. He's your manservant, so I suppose that means you helped me a great deal.\"","Zhou Yuanshen took her hand: \"And how will the Duchess thank me?\"","He called her \"Duchess\" several times.","The night breeze was cool but not biting, softly brushing past her temples, teasing loose strands of hair that tickled her skin.","Cheng Zhao laced her fingers with his, walking slowly: \"What thanks do you want?\"","\"How about we go out for a trip?\" he said.","Cheng Zhao laughed: \"Where?\"","\"To the salt fields at the North Sea, and while we're at it, commission a new statue of Guanyin.\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao was taken aback.","She had assumed \"going out\" meant wandering the streets of the capital, visiting shops for jewelry, or having a nice meal at a restaurant.","\"We just moved back — do we have to leave so soon?\" Cheng Zhao wasn't sure. \"Besides, the weather is getting colder by the day. It might snow any time, and travel would be inconvenient.\"","Zhou Yuanshen: \"You think of everything. We'll go in early spring then.\"","Then he added, \"Would you make me a pair of shoes?\"","That was simple.","Cheng Zhao agreed: \"I can finish in ten days. I'll make you a beautiful pair of double-rimmed shoes.\"","She couldn't help thinking that a husband's clothes and footwear, especially the undergarments, were usually made by his wife. If she was truly too busy, she would delegate to a personal maid or a concubine — though needlework done by servants was considered an intimate matter of the household.","Zhou Yuanshen didn't have such strict notions, and Cheng Zhao was too busy; neither of them had thought of it at first.","Mothers-in-law from well-established families would usually remind the couple.","Cheng Zhao's mother-in-law never meddled in her son and daughter-in-law's private affairs — she had never even asked.","The couple walked back to Chenming Hall under the moonlight.","Compared to the former Ronghua Court, Chenming Hall was far more spacious and imposing.","Cheng Zhao's six dowry maids all slept in the side chambers, along with Nanny Li; now two older matrons had also been added.","These two matrons were originally from Zhou Yuanshen's outer study. He had brought them over from the general's residence — they were extremely diligent and loyal.","\"...If you need more people, I can transfer two more from the outer study.\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao: \"No need. If I need more help, I'll bring in my own dowry retainers. I have that authority now.\"","The inner bedroom of Chenming Hall was twice as large as that of Ronghua Court, feeling all the more empty. To fill that emptiness, a warm alcove had been installed in the inner bedroom.","The alcove was like a small room, or a much larger bed — sleeping in it during winter was especially cozy and snug.","Everything else remained unchanged.","After washing up, Cheng Zhao let down her hair and was about to reach for her sewing basket when Zhou Yuanshen pulled her back.","The couple slipped past the screen and onto the bed, and he gripped her waist with both hands: \"Let's rest early. No rush on the shoes.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","Given how you look right now, tonight will hardly be early.","He kissed her cheeks tenderly, then gently nibbled her earlobe: \"Cheng Zhao, come sit in my arms.\"","The room was slightly cold, and Cheng Zhao shivered as her clothes fell away. Zhou Yuanshen's hands slowly traced over her skin.","His palms were scorching.","Soon, Cheng Zhao no longer felt the cold.","Her thick hair fell across her shoulders, and she felt stifled, as if about to sweat, so she swept her dark locks behind her.","The lamp by the bedside flickered and brightened. When she came to her senses, she found Zhou Yuanshen watching her, his gaze burning.","Instinctively she wanted to hide, and she tucked her hair back over her shoulder.","Like an ostrich burying its head — it concealed nothing at all.","The hands gripping her waist, hardened from holding a spear for so long, never slackened. She couldn't bear it anymore and collapsed against him.","\"Tired?\" he asked.","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","When the passion finally subsided, he carried her to bathe and dressed her again. The lingering heat in her body finally dispersed.","\"...Zhou Yuanshen, if you want to carry on like this again, you need to come home earlier.\" Cheng Zhao mumbled sleepily. \"Staying up so late — I won't be able to get up tomorrow.\"","\"If you can't get up, open the doors late. Chenming Hall is yours — you decide.\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Then he added, \"Cheng Zhao, should I clear out Chenhui Courtyard and make it a dedicated courtyard for meetings?\"","Cheng Zhao's drowsiness vanished completely: \"Then where would the inner study go?\"","\"I want to tear down Li Jing Court and Yu Jin Court entirely, and rebuild Chenhui Courtyard along with them. It can be done in three months.","The rear would serve as the private study and a small drill ground, while the front would be the meeting hall, connected by a side gate. Normally, the side gate could be locked, and opened when needed,\" he said.","This was the second time he had said this.","The Courtyard of Beauty and the Jade Brocade Courtyard were meant to house concubines.","Would any new concubine be placed in another courtyard, or would he promise not to take one at all?","No, he could not make such a promise.","Noble families had their own rules—namely, the head of the household would keep concubines. If the Zhou family were to stand apart, they might face gossip and exclusion.","Some things could be done, but not spoken of openly.","No one would hound you daily about how many concubines you kept, so long as you didn't loudly boast that the men of your household never took them.","Cheng Zhao's mind turned quickly, even in her state of utter exhaustion.","This concerned her future.","\"Grandmother won't agree,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"Concubine Mu and the Second Concubine are still here.\"","\"They can be moved elsewhere,\" Zhou Yuanshen said."]},{"number":214,"title":"Chapter 214: I Can Wait for You, Cheng Zhao","paragraphs":["Zhou Yuanshen brought the matter up with Cheng Zhao again.","Cheng Zhao knew there were many difficulties involved.","But Zhou Yuanshen was not a man who acted without a plan. Since he had mentioned it twice, he clearly already had one—and that plan had now taken another step forward.","Cheng Zhao rested against his chest. “What have you been doing lately? Aside from dealing with that new consort.”","“Consort Wu,” Zhou Yuanshen said. His hand gently stroked the dark hair cascading down her back. “Cheng Zhao, never overlook anyone. Even if that person is temporarily one of our chess pieces.”","Even an insignificant ant could brew a great disaster.","And a favored consort possessed tremendous power. She was certainly no mere ant.","“Tell me about her,” Cheng Zhao said. “The next time I enter the palace to pay my respects to the empress, I may run into her.”","Zhou Yuanshen nodded.","He began explaining slowly.","To gauge the emperor’s preferences, he had first needed to win over the eunuchs the emperor trusted most. They often understood the emperor better than the court officials did.","There was always a reason behind which consorts received the emperor’s favor. It showed what sort of women he preferred.","After finding three or five women of the same type, one could draw a conclusion. Their appearance, personality, and even family background could all be imitated.","Zhou Yuanshen had asked his maternal uncle, Fan Xiao, for help. After spending more than half a year, they had found a woman who fit the type.","“When did you start preparing?” Cheng Zhao asked in surprise.","“A few days before Grandmother forced me to take a concubine,” Zhou Yuanshen replied.","Cheng Zhao fell silent.","To accomplish great things, one had to endure and bide one’s time. A powerful family was like a miniature imperial court: it required a slow, steady simmer, not the gratification of settling every grievance at once.","Sometimes there was no clear verdict between victory and defeat, nor any definite boundary between them. Everything blended into gray. Even when one won, one might still be left feeling stifled and aggrieved.","Just like Zhou Yuanshen. Though he now possessed the ability to resist the matriarch and manipulate the emperor, he still could not erase the grievances he had suffered before.","The only option was to let go oneself.","“So you’re actually wary of Consort Wu as well,” Cheng Zhao said.","“From the moment she entered the palace, we could no longer treat her as a chess piece. At this stage, we’re merely using each other. We need to keep her under control, but we also have to offer her benefits,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","“You helped her win the emperor’s favor.”","“One of the emperor’s trusted confidants will speak on her behalf. That is the connection I gave her. I also gave her money. In the palace, the warmth and coldness of human relations are especially obvious. Without money or influence, no one can go far.”","He continued, “I also treated her with respect. I will never let anyone know about our relationship.”","“I understand. If I see her in the palace from now on, she’ll be the newly favored consort. I’ll treat her with the proper respect,” Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen kissed the center of her brow. “If you dislike it, you don’t have to enter the palace. Don’t force yourself to suffer.”","There were some burdens he could bear alone.","Cheng Zhao smiled. “It’s all right. I’ll have to learn eventually. I learn quickly.”","From Consort Wu, the couple’s conversation returned to the matter of the council chamber in Chengming Hall.","The council chamber had been placed in Chengming Hall. This had been the Zhou family’s practice for more than a decade, deliberately emphasizing Chengming Hall’s importance.","To gain something, one had to sacrifice something else. For example, having to report there every day meant Cheng Zhao had less freedom.","“Don’t rush. Take your time and find a way to renovate Chenhui Court. I’ll continue handling official matters here for another year or two. Once my authority is completely established, we can move the council chamber elsewhere,” Cheng Zhao said.","She needed time.","Every fruit needed time to ripen. There was no point in rushing it.","“All right. We’ll take it slowly,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","He pulled her closer. “Cheng Zhao, it’s rare to see someone so composed at your age.”","“I intend to become the matriarch of a noble household. I can’t afford to make a single mistake.”","One wrong step, and she would tumble downward.","Zhou Yuanshen kissed her. “The question I asked you last time—did you eventually ask your mother and eldest sister about it?”","Cheng Zhao hesitated for a moment before answering, “I told Eldest Sister. She told me to figure it out for myself.”","“What do you think?”","“I haven’t figured it out yet,” Cheng Zhao said.","She wanted to let things take their natural course.","There was no need to say it aloud.","The intimate bond between two people was like a rope. If the rope existed, it could naturally be seen. If it could not be seen, then it did not exist.","Cheng Zhao thought that once she and Zhou Yuanshen developed a deep bond, he would know. She would not need to ask him directly.","She had been trying her best, too.","He treated her well, and Cheng Zhao returned his kindness. Especially in the bedroom, she had become far less coy and reserved.","“I can wait,” Zhou Yuanshen said. “Cheng Zhao, I’m not lacking in patience.”","Cheng Zhao moved closer to him. Taking advantage of the opportunity, he tightened his arms around her and held her firmly against his chest.","The couple lay pressed closely together and gradually fell asleep.","The next morning, Zhou Yuanshen rose early to attend court. After he left, before the hour of the Rabbit had even arrived, Nanny Li came to wake Cheng Zhao.","Nanny Li was even more anxious than Cheng Zhao, afraid that she would oversleep and be seen by the household stewards.","Cheng Zhao woke up.","She practiced her swordplay, washed, ate breakfast, and practiced calligraphy for a while. Only then did the stewards begin arriving one after another.","Without the need to travel back and forth, she seemed to have gained much more time. Even a quarter of an hour could be spared for practicing calligraphy.","Cheng Zhao was very pleased.","Nothing of note happened that day.","In late September, Cheng Zhao heard that an illegally concealed iron mine in the western suburbs had been exposed, implicating a number of officials.","Several meritorious aristocratic families were involved as well.","Among them was the Marquis of Changling’s residence, the family of Madam Song, the eldest aunt’s maiden home.","Everyone in the Zhou household discussed the matter incessantly.","Cheng Zhao, Zhou Yuanshen, and Zhou Yuanqi had all gone to Jiangyun Court for dinner. The subject came up there.","“Has the Song family gone mad? They actually dared to tamper with government iron? That’s a crime punishable by the extermination of nine familial relations,” the second madam said.","“More than a dozen officials have been implicated,” the second master said.","“Could this bring trouble down on us?” the second madam asked.","“That’s unlikely. Eldest Sister-in-law has been married into the Zhou family for more than twenty years. As for her maternal family...”","“Could the censors take the opportunity to impeach us? After all, they’re her in-laws. Technically, that makes them part of the nine familial relations,” the second madam said.","The second master replied, “We’ll have to see how the situation develops.”","The matter quickly grew serious, and the authorities began arresting people.","Everyone cried out that they were innocent.","Among the relatives of the officials involved, those who could sever their ties with them hurried to do so.","The aristocratic families on good terms with the Zhou family also sent people to advise them to have Madam Song sever ties with the Marquis of Changling’s residence. They urged the Zhou family not to let themselves be dragged into the affair.","The old madam was heartbroken. “The Marquis of Changling’s residence was simply too foolish. They were driven to desperation by poverty. If they were short of money, they could have come to me. How could I have refused to help them? Instead, they had to do something like this.”","One of the visiting ladies said, “It’s too late for regrets now, Old Madam. You should have Eldest Madam sever ties with them at once.”","Tears welled in the old madam’s eyes. “How could I bear to do that?”","She was deeply torn.","Not only did her close friends from outside come to persuade her, but members of the Zhou clan did as well. Even the household stewards knelt before the old madam, begging her to save the lives of the entire Zhou clan and to steel her heart.","Huan Qingtang went to persuade her too.","Cheng Zhao and the second madam did not go.","The main reason was that the second madam refused.","“...I can’t say such hypocritical things. I’d end up rolling my eyes,” the second madam said. “Even putting on an act requires some restraint.”","She looked at Cheng Zhao again. “Should we go?”","“Mother, there are already plenty of people persuading her. We won’t be missed. If you can’t bring yourself to do it, then don’t,” Cheng Zhao said.","Cheng Zhao was strict with herself, but she never used that standard to force the people around her. She respected everyone.","Especially her mother-in-law.","With her daughter-in-law’s support, the second madam indeed did not go.","Cheng Zhao stayed away as well.","She even told the stewards, “I know Grandmother is in a difficult position. She’s the one suffering most right now. How could I make things worse for her?”","The old madam could not bring herself to make a decision.","Nanny Sun had no choice but to go in her place.","She went to Madam Song and told her to sever ties with her family.","Madam Song was fiercely resolute. She would rather die than submit, and that very night, she hanged herself.","They could not save her."]},{"number":215,"title":"Chapter 215: All Scores Settled","paragraphs":["Madam Song was dead.","Her remains were transported back to the Duke of Chen’s residence for the funeral.","There was much talk among the common people.","Every guest who came to pay their respects to the Zhou family wore an expression of grief. One and all kept their heads bowed, dejected and wary.","Of course, they were not mourning for the Zhou family or First Madam Song. They were worried about their own safety.","The recent forged-iron case had implicated more than a dozen families. The prominent clans of the capital were connected by marriage, their relationships tangled and intricate. No one dared claim that their own family could emerge from it completely unscathed.","The Zhou family had few members. First Madam Song had hanged herself, preserving her reputation. She had done right by both her maternal family and the Zhou family, and there were actually quite a few people who envied her.","Everyone praised her for her “loyalty.”","The one who felt angry was Second Madam.","Second Madam sat alone in Jiangyun Court, silent for a long time.","Cheng Zhao had to oversee the funeral arrangements.","A mourning shed had been erected outside the Duke of Chen’s residence, and the coffin rested in the outer courtyard. Zhou Yuanshen and Second Master were busy handling matters outside, while Zhou Yuanqi had to kneel in the mourning hall every day.","First Madam had lost both her husband and her son. The only person who could smash the funeral basin for her was her nephew. Huan Qingtang also had to observe heavy mourning.","Huan Qingtang wept as though her heart were being torn apart and was almost incapable of managing anything.","All the matters within the residence, as well as receiving the female guests, fell entirely upon Cheng Zhao.","She had to rise before dawn each day and remain busy until midafternoon, when she finally found time to visit Jiangyun Court.","She carried a small food box.","When Second Madam saw her, she came back to herself somewhat. Forcing herself to sit up, she said, “Should I go to Chengming Hall and help you?”","“There’s no need. Grandmother is also hiding in Shou’an Court, crying. It’s only natural for you to be heartbroken. I can manage,” Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam studied her and thought she looked haggard.","A funeral was a major affair, one that was difficult to encounter in a lifetime. A lady of the house was not considered truly capable until she had overseen a funeral.","This time, Huan Qingtang had to give the opportunity to Cheng Zhao. Otherwise, it would be considered unfilial of her toward First Madam.","And being branded unfilial would be even worse for her.","Cheng Zhao had been presented with a good opportunity, and Second Madam ought to have been happy for her.","Yet her spirits remained low.","“Mother, try some of this,” Cheng Zhao said, opening the food box she had brought.","Second Madam glanced inside.","It was a bowl of almond tea.","“...Winter hasn’t even arrived yet, and you’re already having almond tea?” Second Madam asked.","When the weather turned bitterly cold, almond tea became very popular in the capital. Fragrant, warm, and sweet, it made one’s entire body feel heated and comfortable after a single bowl.","It took considerable effort and ingredients to prepare, so eating it under ordinary circumstances was somewhat extravagant.","Everyone tacitly regarded it as a winter food. Making it casually at other times would invite people to call one greedy.","“I suddenly felt like having some,” Cheng Zhao said. “I was so tired by midafternoon that I couldn’t keep going without something nice to eat.”","She handed it to Second Madam.","Unlike the almond tea served piping hot in winter, this bowl had been allowed to cool to a lukewarm temperature.","Second Madam ate it with Cheng Zhao.","After taking a sip, she said, “It’s so sweet!”","Far too sweet.","“Perhaps you haven’t had anything sweet in a long time, so you’re not used to it. I think it’s fine,” Cheng Zhao said.","She coaxed Second Madam, and the mother- and daughter-in-law ate the bowl of almond tea together.","It was indeed sweet—Cheng Zhao had added two extra spoonfuls of sugar—but it was not cloying. The first sip was overwhelmingly sweet, but after a few more mouthfuls, it became quite pleasant.","After finishing the bowl, Second Madam unexpectedly felt much more at ease.","The tension in her face softened.","Whenever Cheng Zhao was unhappy, it was as though her own joy had frozen solid. Eating something sweet slowly brought it back to room temperature.","She used this method to comfort her mother-in-law.","She knew what was troubling Second Madam.","First Madam Song had certainly not taken her own life.","At a time like this, she had to die. The Zhou family had no place for her anymore. One could imagine how she had died and what torment she had endured before her death.","Second Madam had been her sister-in-law for twenty years. The two had never been close and Second Madam had suffered greatly at her hands. Thus, even shedding tears for her seemed meaningless.","And yet, on an emotional level, it was still painful.","Cheng Zhao understood that all too well.","“Mother, if you feel unwell, you can tell me,” Cheng Zhao said. “There was a filthy little dog by the roadside. It was terribly annoying, and it even chased me once, nearly biting me.","“But when it was run over by a carriage, lying there with its entrails torn open, I still felt sad.”","Disliking Madam Song and sympathizing with what had happened to her were two different emotions. Cheng Zhao did not think they conflicted.","Second Madam blinked.","She held back and held back, but in the end tears still welled in her eyes. “The Old Lady warned you in advance. It seems even the Marquis of Changling’s residence was caught in a scheme. If we refuse to obey in the future, we’ll meet the same fate.”","She continued, “We’re all outsiders, Zhaozhao.”","Cheng Zhao took her hand. “Mother, don’t be afraid. First Madam didn’t die because she was an outsider. She died because she failed.”","Second Madam’s eyes brimmed with tears as she looked at Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao assured her, “We won’t lose. As long as we don’t fail, we won’t die. Mother, believe in me—and believe in the Lord Duke!”","Tears slid down Second Madam’s cheeks. “I’m not only worried about you all. I also pity your First Madam.”","“I understand,” Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam cried for a while.","Then she talked with Cheng Zhao at length, voicing all her worries. Along with the sweet almond tea, it left her feeling much more relaxed.","Second Master and Zhou Yuanqi also returned to Jiangyun Court.","Second Madam had already washed her face.","Her eyes were still red, however, and the traces of crying were obvious.","“...Were things not busy outside?” she asked her husband and son.","Zhou Yuanqi answered, “Even if we’re busy, we still have to eat. Third Brother has someone bringing him food in the mourning hall, so he can manage. Who told him to be the Duke of Chen?”","Second Madam: “...”","“Mother, are you still upset? Have you forgotten how First Madam used to bully you?” Zhou Yuanqi asked.","Second Master lightly patted his son’s shoulder. “The dead deserve respect. You must not speak carelessly of your First Madam. It’s all over now.”","She was dead.","All past grievances had been wiped away.","“But my mother suffered so much because of her. She didn’t die at my mother’s hands, so why should everything end just because she’s dead?” Zhou Yuanqi said.","Second Madam said, “Enough. If your father says it’s over, then it’s over. You mustn’t speak carelessly of your parents either.”","Zhou Yuanqi: “...”","Seeing her younger brother-in-law caught in the middle and unable to please either side, Cheng Zhao could not help laughing.","Yet what truly eased Second Madam’s heart was Zhou Yuanqi’s words.","Her children understood her, and her husband favored her. That was enough for her to let go.","Whatever hatred or resentment she had felt was merely emotional grievance. Once someone understood her and someone cared for her, that grievance was like snow beneath the spring sun—it melted away in the light, leaving no trace behind.","Second Madam said to Cheng Zhao, “Go on and attend to your duties. Don’t worry about me.”","Then she added, “You’re so busy, yet you still take the time to look after me. I know how filial you are. Don’t worry—I’ll listen to everything you say. We absolutely will not lose.”","Cheng Zhao said, “Mother loves me best.”","Second Madam stroked her head and adjusted the white flower at her temple.","That evening, Zhou Yuanshen returned to Chengming Hall.","Cheng Zhao told him that Mother had recovered.","“...Mother is very softhearted. In truth, she was a little afraid. She was frightened,” Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen nodded. “She witnessed many things, especially the killings during the late years of the late emperor’s reign. She can’t bring herself to speak of them, but she knows.”","Because she knew, she was afraid.","Cheng Zhao and the others had not seen those things themselves, so their fear was limited. They were ignorant, and therefore fearless.","“I told her to believe in us,” Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen nodded."]},{"number":216,"title":"Chapter 216: “Praise Killing Cheng Zhao”","paragraphs":["In the inner room of Chengming Hall, neither Cheng Zhao nor Zhou Yuanshen had gone to sleep.","Zhou Yuanshen still had to go to the mourning hall later. For the next few days, he would have to keep vigil by the coffin.","“...Cheng Zhao, if I tell you not to be afraid, will you be afraid?” Zhou Yuanshen asked her.","“I’m not afraid,” Cheng Zhao replied.","“You’re an intelligent person. You understand what I mean.”","Cheng Zhao fell silent.","“My father once said that Aunt, my eldest uncle, and my second cousin all died under very suspicious circumstances,” Zhou Yuanshen continued.","Anyone who considered the cause of Eldest Madam Song’s death would understand exactly where the suspicion lay.","No one was allowed to stand in the way.","The Zhou family’s power and status were the path to the Grand Madam’s wealth and glory. There could not be a single obstacle on that road.","“There are still three brothers in our branch. That’s more than enough. Even if two more were to die, it wouldn’t matter,” Zhou Yuanshen added.","Cheng Zhao shivered.","Outside, the shadows of the trees swayed. Then, all at once, a gust of wind rose.","The wind grew stronger, rattling the windows. Startled by the sudden commotion, Cheng Zhao instinctively moved closer to Zhou Yuanshen.","He wrapped an arm around her.","She put her arms around his waist and simply nestled into his embrace.","After a while, the wind still had not stopped. In fact, it grew fiercer by the moment.","Nanny Li instructed the maids on night duty to secure the doors and windows once more.","Only then did Cheng Zhao say, “The weather is going to change these next few days. It was unnaturally hot during the day.”","“Yes.”","It was merely a coincidence that the wind had risen in the middle of the night.","A remarkably convenient coincidence, considering what they had been discussing.","Zhou Yuanshen said, “I’m not going to keep vigil tonight. I’ll stay with you. Let Father and Yuanqi go instead.”","“The sudden wind will make the mourning hall frightening enough. Don’t frighten Yuanqi as well,” Cheng Zhao said. “You should go. I’ll have Qiubai and Suyue come in and sleep with me.”","She glanced at the warm chamber and continued, “We’ll sleep in the warm chamber tonight. Close both doors of the room. Then there’ll be nothing to fear.”","“Are you really all right?” Zhou Yuanshen asked.","“It isn’t only family members who are keeping vigil. There are also members of the clan and the household stewards. We can’t give anyone an opportunity to find fault with us, especially at a time like this,” Cheng Zhao said.","If they made even one mistake, they would have less leverage when facing the Grand Madam in the future.","Zhou Yuanshen gently kissed her between the brows. “Make sure you keep the doors and windows shut.”","“All right,” Cheng Zhao replied.","She still saw him out.","In the middle of the night, the wind suddenly rose. It was fierce enough to make the treetops in the distance seem to wail, while Zhou Yuanshen’s mourning robes fluttered wildly.","Nanfeng was waiting at the gate, carrying a windproof lantern.","But the wind was too strong. Even the lantern was blown this way and that, its light flickering between brightness and darkness.","After Zhou Yuanshen left, Nanny Li ordered the courtyard gate to be shut.","Suyue and Qiubai stayed with Cheng Zhao in the warm chamber, while Nanny Li slept on the heated brick bed by the window.","The wind outside showed no sign of stopping. It carried a mournful edge, like the cries of ghosts.","Cheng Zhao could not sleep.","Qiubai and Suyue were awake as well. Whenever they heard her turn over, they asked whether she wanted some water. Nanny Li, on the other hand, had fallen sound asleep on the heated bed and was even snoring softly.","The sound was oddly comforting amid the noisy night.","Cheng Zhao felt thirsty.","Qiubai poured three cups of water and carried them into the warm chamber. The three women sat up to drink and chat.","“...Second Madam is truly softhearted,” Suyue said. “I certainly wouldn’t feel sorry for Eldest Madam. She tried to burn you to death last time.”","Cheng Zhao sipped her water slowly. Only after a moment did she say, “Mother-in-law has many virtues. People with obvious strengths often have equally obvious weaknesses. I don’t mind that she’s softhearted. She may be gentle, but she never holds us back.”","“That’s true,” Suyue said.","Qiubai added, “Compared with most women, Second Madam really is very good to our Young Madam.”","“If I had any other mother-in-law, my path would not have been so smooth,” Cheng Zhao said.","Qiubai and Suyue both nodded.","After finishing their cups of water, Suyue went out to put them away and covered the bright-angle lamp on the table.","The warm chamber sank into darkness.","Nanny Li slept deeply, her snores growing louder. In the chaotic night of wind and rain, the familiar sound was strangely reassuring.","“Do you think it will snow tonight?” Qiubai asked.","“It probably won’t,” Suyue replied. “The weather was so fine during the day. If it were going to snow, the sky would have to remain overcast for several days.”","“I think it will probably rain.”","Cheng Zhao thought so too.","Not long after they finished speaking, raindrops began to strike the roof and windowsills.","Mixed with the wind, the sound of rain finally lulled Cheng Zhao to sleep.","Nanny Li woke her at dawn the next morning.","It was still raining outside.","The wind had not stopped. The rain was not heavy, but it drifted everywhere in fine, dense sheets.","The temperature had dropped sharply. The previous morning, a single layer of clothing had been enough; today, she needed padded clothes, and could even wear a light winter coat.","“Do you think anyone will come to offer condolences today?” Suyue asked.","“In this cold, rainy weather, there probably won’t be many visitors,” Cheng Zhao replied.","Nanny Li brought out Cheng Zhao’s wind cloak and draped it over her shoulders. “Even if no one comes, we still have to be prepared.”","The bitter wind and rain did not stop until the following dawn, as though someone had been weeping over their sorrow and resentment.","After the rain, the sky remained overcast. Once the wind died down, guests offering condolences suddenly began arriving in large numbers. Everyone was afraid of encountering another bout of bad weather and being unable to make the journey in time.","Cheng Zhao was busy from morning until night.","Huan Qingtang fainted from grief three times in the mourning hall. Cheng Zhao sent her nourishing tonics and personally went to comfort her.","Many people witnessed it.","When the Zhou family’s funeral was over, Eldest Madam Song was buried in the Zhou family’s ancestral tombs, and her memorial tablet was placed in the ancestral shrine. The Marquis of Changling’s title was stripped from the estate; some were executed, while others were exiled. The entire household collapsed in an instant.","Quite a few families were implicated along with the Marquis of Changling’s residence.","Throughout the early winter in the capital, the great clans and noble families grew bleak and withdrawn. Banquets among the highborn became increasingly rare, and everyone shut themselves indoors to “avoid the cold.”","Someone began singing Cheng Zhao’s praises.","“She handled everything during the funeral with such care. No wonder she’s the legitimate daughter of the Cheng clan of Wu Commandery. She truly has grace and ability.”","At the same time, they disparaged Huan Qingtang.","“She does nothing but cry. When something happens, she has no idea what to do. You can’t rely on her.”","When Cheng Zhao’s mother heard about it, she sent a senior steward woman to deliver winter tonics and told Cheng Zhao what was being said.","“Why would anyone spread such rumors?” Cheng Zhao asked with a frown.","Belittling Huan Qingtang while excessively praising Cheng Zhao—what was the purpose? In such turbulent times, whoever was behind it was deliberately creating trouble for Cheng Zhao.","“I don’t know who started it. Madam said she would ask the Princess of Jingnan to help clarify matters on your behalf. Madam and the Princess of Jingnan both have considerable influence among the noblewomen,” the steward woman said.","“Please thank Mother for me,” Cheng Zhao replied.","And so Cheng Zhao’s mother and the Princess of Jingnan began saying that Cheng Zhao had been efficient because the Zhou household was well ordered, because the Grand Madam commanded great respect, and because everyone was willing to show Cheng Zhao deference. As for Huan Qingtang fainting several times from grief, it was simply because she was filial.","The label of “filial” suited her perfectly. No one could use it as an excuse to accuse Huan Qingtang of incompetence.","Little by little, the voices praising Cheng Zhao while belittling Huan Qingtang died down.","“Those people watching from the outside never fear making matters worse,” Suyue said. “They’re terrified you might suffer too little.”","Cheng Zhao replied, “Things have been too chaotic lately. It doesn’t matter. They can’t damage my foundations.”","“The Eldest Young Madam’s side still thinks you were the one who started those rumors,” Suyue said angrily. “I ran into the chief maid beside her this morning. She was practically sticking her nose in the air at me.”","Cheng Zhao told her not to get angry.","Then she said, “With Eldest Uncle’s wife gone, she’s the only person left in the eldest branch.”","“She has no children and no imperial title. To put it harshly, there’s practically no eldest branch left. She can’t hold it up on her own,” Suyue said.","A woman could not be considered an independent household unless the court had granted her the right to establish a separate female household. A widowed woman with an imperial title naturally still possessed some standing.","Huan Qingtang had none of that.","She might not have been pretending when she fainted from grief during her mother-in-law’s funeral.","Her circumstances had become exceedingly difficult.","“What I’m afraid of is that she’ll take desperate measures and become even more unhinged,” Nanny Li said. “It’s best not to provoke her.”","“Who has the time to provoke her? Our young madam is far too busy,” Suyue replied.","But would Huan Qingtang really behave herself if they left her alone?","A cornered dog would leap over the wall. Who knew what she might do in the future? The thought made Suyue glance at Cheng Zhao worriedly.","Cheng Zhao, however, remained perfectly calm.","“Life has to be lived one day at a time,” Cheng Zhao said.","Whether it was soldiers at the gate or floodwaters breaking through, she would deal with each problem as it came. The road ahead was never destined to be smooth, and Cheng Zhao had been prepared for that from the start."]},{"number":217,"title":"Chapter 217: Madame from the Sky","paragraphs":["After the funeral of Eldest Madam Song, the Duke of Chen’s residence had yet to return to normal when the Grand Dowager fell ill, and Huan Qingtang withdrew from everyone, refusing to see visitors. She had to observe the mourning period.","Cheng Zhao managed the household alone.","She left all the duties under Huan Qingtang’s supervision untouched, keeping everything as it had been.","“If anything unexpected happens, I’ll send someone to ask Eldest Sister-in-law at Cuilun Courtyard,” Cheng Zhao told the steward in charge of that side. “But it would be best not to disturb her. Eldest Sister-in-law hasn’t been feeling well these days.”","Everyone acknowledged her instructions.","As for the staff under Huan Qingtang, Cheng Zhao did nothing more than check the attendance register each day, making sure everyone was present and carrying out their duties.","Beyond that, she left them alone.","Once Cheng Zhao had finished handling the household affairs, she would send a small carriage to fetch her mother-in-law, and the two of them would go to Shou’an Courtyard to attend to the Grand Dowager.","They went almost every day.","The Grand Dowager grew annoyed and said to the two of them, “You’re both filial, and I understand that. There’s no need to tire yourselves out like this. The weather is growing colder by the day.”","Nanny Sun added from the side, “The Grand Dowager isn’t feeling well and can’t bear any disturbances. Eldest Young Madam wanted to come copy scriptures these past few days, but this old servant sent her back.”","In other words, the Grand Dowager would not even see Huan Qingtang, let alone Cheng Zhao and the Second Madam, whom she disliked.","Cheng Zhao had no intention of deliberately tormenting anyone.","She had come to the Duke of Chen’s residence to be the senior matriarch, not to make trouble for people.","Hearing the Grand Dowager and Nanny Sun, she apologized gently. “I was only concerned and lost my composure. I’ve disturbed Grandmother’s rest.”","Then she said, “From now on, we’ll come to pay our respects on the fifth and fifteenth of each month. If Grandmother wants anything to eat or needs anything else, Nanny Sun, please send someone to Chengming Hall and tell me.”","Nanny Sun acknowledged her.","Her manner was cold.","The Grand Dowager remained benevolent and praised Cheng Zhao for being thoughtful.","The Second Madam sat silently beside them.","After the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law left Shou’an Courtyard, the Second Madam said, “She doesn’t feel guilty in the slightest.”","Cheng Zhao slipped her arm through the Second Madam’s and said softly, “Mother, what others think is their concern. We won’t join them in their wrongdoing.”","The Second Madam let out a sigh. “Forget it. Since she doesn’t want me there, I can’t be bothered to go either.”","She returned to Jiangyun Courtyard.","That evening, when Zhou Yuanshen returned to the residence, he deliberately summoned Cheng Zhao, and the couple went to Shou’an Courtyard once more.","The Grand Dowager was slightly surprised.","“His Majesty has bestowed some tonics,” Zhou Yuanshen said. “He knows that Grandmother has been unwell lately and urged you to set aside your grief. He even wanted to come and see you personally, but I stopped him.","“An enormous case involving the state monopoly on iron has broken out, and His Majesty is exhausted. Even if I am his ‘son-in-law,’ there is still a distinction between sovereign and subject. I told him that I would fulfill my filial duty on his behalf and help him shoulder the burden of serving the state. Only then was His Majesty reassured.”","The Grand Dowager’s cheek twitched violently. For a moment, she failed to keep her expression under control.","Cheng Zhao sat beside them with her eyes lowered.","She did not look closely at the Grand Dowager, nor did she glance at Zhou Yuanshen.","But she understood what he meant.","Zhou Yuanshen had gained the emperor’s trust. Using that trust, he was slowly severing the “rope” that bound the Grand Dowager to the emperor.","The emperor had wanted to visit the Duke of Chen’s residence, but Zhou Yuanshen had stopped him. If the Grand Dowager went to the palace, Consort Wu would already be lying in wait beside the emperor, ensuring that the two of them could not speak privately.","Once too many people were mixed into a close relationship, the inability to meet would gradually cause that relationship to grow distant.","And once they grew distant, any attempt at sowing discord would give rise to misunderstandings.","Even the Grand Dowager could not guarantee that the emperor would always treat her with the affection due a birth mother. After all, they shared no blood.","Without making a fuss or acting rashly, Zhou Yuanshen had quietly driven a hard wedge between the emperor and the Grand Dowager.","That wedge was digging painfully into her.","“Grandmother, is there somewhere you’re uncomfortable?” Zhou Yuanshen asked. “His Majesty told me to report back to him. If you truly aren’t well, I can ask him to come visit you tomorrow.”","If he invited the emperor to visit her, the news would reach the censors, who would raise an uproar.","Whenever the emperor came to the Zhou residence, it was done “in private.” At the very least, they dared not invite him openly.","After the iron monopoly case, many people had died, and the Censorate was already holding back a great deal of anger. The emperor had used the incident to eliminate a group of disobedient officials and powerful clans he disliked. The court officials all understood this.","They had already begun to question the suspicious circumstances revealed by the case.","At such a time, the emperor did not dare provoke the Censorate.","The Grand Dowager knew this perfectly well. That was why she understood the source of Zhou Yuanshen’s threat.","She was so furious that she could not speak, yet she had no choice but to answer.","“I haven’t slept well these past two days. I’ve already asked an imperial physician to prescribe medicine,” the Grand Dowager said with a smile. “You shouldn’t have told His Majesty.”","Then she added, “With all the children and grandchildren in the family showing me such filial devotion, how could I possibly be dissatisfied? Especially with my grandson being so capable.”","She then asked Zhou Yuanshen, “When will you be going to the Capital Garrison?”","“Recently, there has been a great deal to deal with, and the Capital Garrison has remained peaceful, so His Majesty ordered me not to go for the next two months. It is an exception granted by imperial decree,” Zhou Yuanshen replied.","The Grand Dowager asked, “What are you busy with?”","“Teaching the Crown Prince to practice calligraphy. His writing isn’t very good, and His Majesty, the Empress, and Grand Preceptor Guo are all dissatisfied. The other tutors can’t get him to study properly, but he learns well when I teach him,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao continued to sit silently, utterly still.","From the corner of her eye, she saw the Grand Dowager’s lips move, as though she wanted to say something.","Zhou Yuanshen had not only won the emperor’s favor, but had also gained the Crown Prince’s protection.","His advantage had grown yet another layer stronger.","The Grand Dowager was probably furious enough to cough blood, but she did not let it show on her face.","Cheng Zhao thought to herself, If I were that old and had to swallow this many grievances, I’d rather throw caution to the wind and make a scene. Keeping it all bottled up is bound to make her ill.","But the Grand Dowager had worn her mask for too long. She no longer even dared to tear it off.","“You’re a military man. You can actually teach the Crown Prince calligraphy?” the Grand Dowager said.","Though her words sounded teasing, there was also a hint of disdain in them.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, “That is simply the bond between the Crown Prince and me.”","Grandmother and grandson exchanged a few more verbal thrusts.","Zhou Yuanshen then brought up the renovations to the inner study.","He wanted to connect Chenhui Courtyard, Lijing Courtyard, and Yujin Courtyard into one.","“...Where will the concubines live?” the Grand Dowager asked.","“Behind Nonghua Courtyard, there are several other courtyards,” Zhou Yuanshen replied.","“They’re all too far away and too dilapidated.”","“I used to live in Nonghua Courtyard, and I never thought it too far or too old. I am the Duke of Chen. If I can live there, why can’t the concubines?” Zhou Yuanshen said.","The Grand Dowager fell silent.","His words were practically an accusation that she had mistreated him and Cheng Zhao.","She had treated him as though he were a servant of the household, even while making him inherit the title of Duke of Chen. She had humiliated both him and his parents.","Now that he possessed power of his own, he was striking back at the Grand Dowager.","This was a contest of authority.","If the Grand Dowager agreed to renovate the inner study, she would lose all control over the Duke’s residence.","“The placement of the residences was calculated by an expert in geomancy. We cannot move things carelessly. The feng shui will suffer if we do,” the Grand Dowager said.","“We can invite another expert to inspect the layout and calculate it again,” Zhou Yuanshen replied.","“Don’t stir up such matters at a time like this. All right, it’s getting late. You should both go back.”","After saying this, the Grand Dowager’s expression grew increasingly ugly.","She would never agree.","Zhou Yuanshen rose with Cheng Zhao and took his leave.","Once they stepped out of Shou’an Courtyard, the cold wind hissed through their sleeves and seeped into their clothes. Cheng Zhao shivered.","Zhou Yuanshen took her hand.","His palm was dry and warm, and his hand was large enough to enfold hers completely.","“I told you Grandmother wouldn’t agree,” Cheng Zhao whispered.","She leaned close to speak to him, her voice lingering between them before scattering into the wind.","“She will agree,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Hearing the certainty in his voice, Cheng Zhao asked, “What plan have you come up with this time?”","“I’ll tell you when I get back. Whether it happens or not, we’ll see when the first snow falls this year,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Then he added, “Perhaps the year’s first snow will come in half a month.”"]},{"number":218,"title":"Chapter 218: He Really Likes Cheng Zhao","paragraphs":["With Zhou Yuanshen at home, Cheng Zhao felt very safe living in Chengming Hall.","Even when the wind rose at night, she was not afraid.","However, Chengming Hall was surrounded on both sides by Mu Jiang’s Lijing Court and Huan Qingtang’s Cuiyun Court, as though it had fallen into an encirclement.","Cheng Zhao was not busy today and had time to sit beneath the lamplight, embroidering the upper of a shoe.","Zhou Yuanshen sat beside her, reading a formation manual. He moved the lamp closer to Cheng Zhao and said, “Have the maids do the embroidery. You can make a few stitches to show your sincerity. I’ll appreciate the thought.”","Cheng Zhao said, “How can I be so perfunctory?”","She had always been thorough in everything she did. Once she agreed to something, she would carry it out properly and never cut corners.","“I’m afraid you’ll tire yourself.”","“I’m not tired.” Cheng Zhao raised her eyes and gave him a faint smile. “Don’t worry. I take good care of myself. If I become tired, I won’t force myself to keep going.”","Her smile was beautiful. Her teeth were white and even, and her dimples were more alluring than flowers.","Zhou Yuanshen’s heart stirred.","He came over, took the needle and thread from her hands, and gently drew her into his arms. “I don’t need to observe mourning for Eldest Aunt.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","He looked steadily at her. “Cheng Zhao, are you really not tired?”","Cheng Zhao lifted her face and lightly kissed his chin. Smiling, she said nothing, merely gazing at him with bright, shining eyes.","Zhou Yuanshen lowered his head and sealed her lips with his own.","Holding her, he carried her around the screen and laid her on the bed.","The curtains fell, and the inner bed curtain slipped from its golden hooks, blocking out the light. In the darkness, their breathing became clearer.","Cheng Zhao could feel the heat of his breath, while the fine sheen of sweat on her body brushed against his palm.","“Cheng Zhao,” he murmured.","Cheng Zhao answered him.","At that moment, she felt that her name sounded beautiful. Coming from his lips, it was especially moving, making her ears tingle and grow weak.","Amid the tenderness and passion, she suddenly understood.","So he really did love her.","What about her?","Did she have the same clinging affection for him in her heart?","For a moment, Cheng Zhao felt flustered. She wrapped her arms around him and held him tightly, their bodies pressed closely together.","Zhou Yuanshen smiled and tightened his embrace. The brocade quilt enveloped them in that small space, leaving only the two of them.","Cheng Zhao once again experienced an intense, exquisite pleasure.","On that chilly early-winter night.","After bathing, neither husband nor wife felt much like sleeping. Both were in an excellent mood.","A small palace lamp sat inside the bed curtains, mostly covered so that only a thin, dim glow remained. The soft yellow light made the space feel exceptionally warm.","Zhou Yuanshen held Cheng Zhao in his arms, while she rested against his chest.","“...Mu Jiang has been very quiet these past few days,” Cheng Zhao suddenly said.","The last time she had seen Mu Jiang was before the fire at Nonghua Court.","In that short span of time, Cheng Zhao had moved from Nonghua Court to Chengming Hall; Eldest Madam Song had been sent away for setting the fire, and then, after something happened to her maternal family, she had “hanged herself.”","Now Eldest Madam Song’s funeral was over.","So many things had happened, and everything had been so chaotic and busy that the Mid-Autumn Festival seemed to have taken place a very long time ago.","In truth, less than two months had passed.","During the Zhou family’s funeral, Mu Jiang could have taken the opportunity to cause trouble, but she had not.","More precisely, she had been unable to.","“Do I need to go see her?” Cheng Zhao asked, raising her eyes to Zhou Yuanshen.","“No need,” Zhou Yuanshen replied.","“You and her...”","The question seemed to have been in Cheng Zhao’s heart for a long time.","Although she had learned many secrets, she had never personally heard Zhou Yuanshen speak of his past with Mu Jiang.","After all, the two of them had grown up in the same household.","“We aren’t close,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","He seemed unwilling to elaborate, but he noticed Cheng Zhao’s hesitation and continued, “I was never favored by Grandmother. When we were living on the frontier, we stayed in separate courtyards.”","He had not lived with the Grand Duchess, the main branch, or the Emperor and Empress. He had lived with his parents in the residence of the Fan family.","“We had heard that an orphan girl had been taken in. Grandmother and the others returned to the capital first, while we did not come back until the second year after the Emperor ascended the throne.","“By then, the Zhou family had been granted a title and given a dukedom. The main branch guarded against us as though we were thieves, and Grandmother also disliked my frequent visits to Shou’an Court,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao said, “...That was her prejudice against you.”","“I didn’t spend many years at the clan academy either. Because they were so wary of me, Zhou Yuancheng picked fights with me every day. My mother suffered a great deal because of me, so I ran back to the frontier and stayed by my maternal grandfather’s side,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Thus, he and the orphan girl raised by the Grand Duchess could hardly be called childhood sweethearts.","They had barely seen each other a handful of times.","“I only returned to the capital after I was appointed General of the Pacifying West. Not long after I came back, I inherited the title and was granted a marriage,” he said.","It was all very simple.","His relationship with Mu Jiang was straightforward and unambiguous, without the slightest entanglement.","“...Taking her as a concubine was the Emperor’s hint and Grandmother’s wish,” Zhou Yuanshen continued. “I have never once stayed at Lijing Court.","“However, I agreed to let her put on a show of influence and helped her boast by sending her gifts. She also needed to give the others an explanation and was afraid of being mocked by the servants, so she was willing to cooperate with me.”","At this, Cheng Zhao remembered the time Qiubai had been poisoned by a snake and she had gone to Lijing Court to find him.","Mu Jiang had cursed her terribly then.","But Zhou Yuanshen had not come out of Lijing Court. He had arrived by the small path from Chenhui Court.","Nanfeng was very sharp. Cheng Zhao’s shouting at the entrance of Lijing Court might not have been heard inside Chenhui Court, but Nanfeng must have known about it.","He would have told Zhou Yuanshen, who had been resting in Chenhui Court.","Zhou Yuanshen finished speaking and gently lifted her chin. “Do you believe me?”","Cheng Zhao said, “I do.”","Why would he lie about something like this?","Zhou Yuanshen kissed her lips. “Cheng Zhao, you’re truly a straightforward person. You’re different from what I imagined.”","“You imagined me?”","“I thought you would be delicate and timid,” he said.","Cheng Zhao: “...”","He asked her again, “When you were given this marriage, were you afraid? Did you ever wonder what kind of person I was?”","“Why would I wonder? Once the marriage was arranged, my family thoroughly investigated you and the Duke of Chen’s family. My second brother even took me to a teahouse to watch you,” Cheng Zhao replied.","Know yourself and know your enemy, and you will never be defeated.","Wasn’t that a military strategy too?","He read military texts all day long. What exactly had he learned from them?","Zhou Yuanshen: “...”","He understood the disdain in Cheng Zhao’s eyes and kissed her firmly again.","When Cheng Zhao pushed him away and rolled into his arms, she said, “If you keep this up, I won’t talk to you anymore.”","He obediently lay still.","The couple had previously cleared up the misunderstanding involving Huan Qingtang. Now that they had also clarified the matter of Mu Jiang, Cheng Zhao felt that they had become one entity as husband and wife—the two closest people in the world.","“Don’t concern yourself with Mu Jiang. Grandmother will deal with her,” Zhou Yuanshen said. “This is a dispute between them. No matter what you and I do, we’ll end up blamed from both sides.”","Cheng Zhao understood.","“It’s just that you suggested rebuilding the inner study, and I’m afraid Grandmother will use Mu Jiang,” Cheng Zhao said.","“An old fox who has become desperate will be the one to fall into the trap,” Zhou Yuanshen replied.","Cheng Zhao nodded.","The couple talked for a long time.","The next day, news came that something had happened at Lijing Court.","Mu Jiang had been coughing for many days, and the previous night she had coughed up blood.","The physician said that the weather was growing colder by the day and was unsuitable for her recovery. She should be moved to the hot-spring estate, where the climate was warm and humid.","“Once the weather warms after spring arrives, she can be brought back,” the physician said.","The Grand Duchess immediately sent people to make the arrangements.","However, the Zhou family’s hot-spring estate was very close to the estate of Grand Princess Fukang, who also intended to escape the winter cold there.","“Having a patient living next door is most inauspicious, and she may disturb the princess. Why not move her to one of the estates in the south? She can recuperate there for a year or two,” Nanny Sun suggested.","The Grand Dowager Lady summoned Zhou Yuanshen and Cheng Zhao to discuss the matter.","Zhou Yuanshen said, “I will abide by Grandmother’s decision in all things.”","Cheng Zhao then said, “As for Madam Ru, naturally the decision rests with Grandmother and the Duke of State.”","She knew that once Mu Jiang left, she would probably never return.","The Grand Dowager Lady was not giving her up because she had found a better choice. It was because the burden had become too heavy, and she had to cast it off."]},{"number":219,"title":"Chapter 219: Nobody's Gossiping","paragraphs":["Mu Jiang was sent away.","When she left, she was so ill that she was barely conscious. Supported by maids and old matrons, she was dressed in heavy layers; because she could not be exposed to the wind, her head and face were wrapped up.","Even after she was helped into the carriage, her coughing could still be heard.","Her breath was weak, and even her coughs were faint, as though she might stop breathing at any moment.","Huan Qingtang had been hiding in her courtyard and refusing to go out these days. It was from the people around her that she heard about what had happened.","“What are the servants saying?” she asked, slowly stirring aside the floating tea leaves, her tone indifferent.","Her confidante replied, “Almost no one is talking about it.”","Huan Qingtang’s hand paused.","She slowly lifted her eyes. A glimmer of moisture seemed to gather in them. “No one is gossiping?”","Her confidante fell silent.","Mu Jiang had been Duke Chen’s concubine. Yet no one openly discussed her departure from the duke’s residence. This showed just how formidable Cheng Zhao’s authority had become.","The servants had all tacitly accepted that Mu Jiang would never return, while the Duke’s wife, Cheng Zhao, naturally possessed the rightful position. Speaking about the matter would only invite trouble.","Huan Qingtang lowered her head and took a sip of tea.","The tea was scalding hot, leaving the tip of her tongue numb. For a long while, she could taste nothing at all.","She ought to go out and resume handling affairs.","At Jingyun Court, Second Madam did ask Cheng Zhao about it.","“...It really was your grandmother’s idea?” Second Madam asked.","“Yes.”","“Shouldn’t your grandmother have kept her around so she could continue making trouble and causing you all difficulties?” Second Madam asked, puzzled.","“After she was beaten with the boards, she had no value left, Mother,” Cheng Zhao replied.","Second Madam sighed softly.","She said nothing more.","Mu Jiang left quietly, without causing a stir.","Xian Si, who lived in Yujin Court, had always been a quiet person. After Mu Jiang left, she became even more withdrawn.","The more dutifully she behaved, the more people watched her.","Everyone from Shou’an Court to Huan Qingtang, even the servants, seemed curious about how she would win the Duke’s favor.","Even the people around Cheng Zhao remained wary of her, keeping a close eye on her at all times.","“Young Madam, do you think she feels that her opportunity has arrived?” Suyue asked.","“From the few times I’ve interacted with her, she does seem dutiful,” Cheng Zhao said.","“Do you think she’s a good person?”","“Suyue, what does it mean to be a good person? In the eyes of the Dowager Madame, Mu Jiang, and the Huan family, I’m not a good person either,” Cheng Zhao replied.","Suyue fell silent.","“I once wanted to live in Chengming Hall. Now, I want to secure my place in Chengming Hall. Everything else is merely a trivial detail and isn’t worth too much of my attention,” Cheng Zhao said.","Nanny Li praised her from the side. “Young Madam truly thinks far ahead.”","The lady of the house, who managed the inner household, was busy every day. Keeping watch over the concubines would only distract her and waste her energy.","It truly was not worth it.","Many titled noblewomen only gradually came to understand this once they grew older. Yet Cheng Zhao was still young, and she and the Duke were currently as close as honey and oil. Even so, she could already see through these matters. She was remarkably wise.","“Bring out my sewing basket,” Cheng Zhao instructed. “When I have some free time, I’ll make the Duke a pair of shoes.”","Qiubai went to fetch it.","Cheng Zhao’s hands were quick and nimble. Before long, she had embroidered the uppers. The work was not exquisite, but it was quite presentable.","Two days later, the shoes were finished.","Zhou Yuanshen put them on, and his dark eyes brightened slightly. “They’re very comfortable.”","“If you like them, I’ll make you another pair next time,” Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","It had taken a great deal of time and left her neck and wrists aching, but when she saw the look on his face, she still could not help but be generous again.","“I’m worried you’ll tire yourself out,” he said. “One pair is more than enough.”","He wore the shoes when they went to Jingyun Court for dinner.","Second Madam noticed them at once. “What a finely made pair of double-soled shoes. Where did they come from?”","“Cheng Zhao made them,” Zhou Yuanshen replied.","“Zhaozhao can do this as well?” Second Madam asked, pleasantly surprised.","Beside them, Zhou Yuanqi said, “Why won’t you make me a pair?”","“Wait for your wife to make them for you,” Cheng Zhao replied.","Second Madam added, “Your sister-in-law is very busy. How could she have time to make shoes?”","Zhou Yuanqi curled his lips. “That brute is rough and careless. He’ll wear through a pair in just a few days. Giving them to him would be a waste.”","—You might as well give them to me.","“No need to trouble yourself,” Zhou Yuanshen said blandly.","He very casually stretched his foot a little farther out.","Zhou Yuanqi spotted it immediately and cursed him inwardly for showing off.","They finished dinner amid lively banter.","Second Madam did not bring up a single troubling matter—not Song-shi’s death, Huan Qingtang’s low profile, or Mu Jiang’s departure.","She merely said to Cheng Zhao, “The weather is growing colder by the day. You live so far away now, so you needn’t come here every day.”","“Mother, we have the small carriage. Its walls are made thicker for winter, and there’s a brazier inside. We won’t be cold,” Cheng Zhao said. Then she added, “Are you tired of having us around?”","“What a childish thing to say,” Second Madam replied, pretending to scold her.","“Coming over every day, even if it’s only to sit for a while and exchange a few words, is how we remain close as a family,” Cheng Zhao said. “A good blade may be precious and sharp, but if it’s left unused for too long, it will rust.”","She used an analogy Second Madam could understand.","Zhou Yuanqi said from the side, “Mother, it’s a long way for me to come from the outer residence too. I’m still a child. Why don’t you feel sorry for me?”","“What are you, a child, afraid of?” Second Madam replied.","“I’m going to tell Grandmother that you’re being far too biased now. You don’t love me,” Zhou Yuanqi threatened.","“The fact that I haven’t beaten you is already proof that I love you. And you still dare to complain?” Second Madam said.","Zhou Yuanqi was rendered speechless.","After this exchange of teasing and banter, Second Madam no longer refused to let her son and daughter-in-law come for dinner every day.","A brief meeting allowed them to keep track of one another’s circumstances and prevented malicious people from driving a wedge between them and creating discord within the family.","The fact that Cheng Zhao continued dining at Jingyun Court also spread throughout the Duke’s residence.","The servants all praised Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen for their filial devotion.","The Dowager Madame was convinced that Cheng Zhao was flaunting herself. “She makes a spectacle of even the smallest matter. She’s become far too pleased with herself lately.”","Nanny Sun still suggested giving Cheng Zhao a little warning, so she would understand her place and stop displaying herself so openly.","The Dowager Madame shook her head. “There are more important matters at hand. Let her be as arrogant as she likes.”","Huan Qingtang heard about it as well.","“I’m going to Shou’an Court,” she told her confidante.","The following morning, Huan Qingtang rose early and went to Shou’an Court to pay her respects.","This time, the Dowager Madame received her.","Huan Qingtang’s eyes were slightly swollen, as though she had been crying for a long time—or perhaps had slept poorly.","“...Although I’m in mourning, I shouldn’t let it interfere with managing the household affairs. Leaving everything to my younger sister-in-law is truly too much of a burden for her,” Huan Qingtang said. “She already has so much responsibility on her shoulders and needs to take care of her health.”","One of Cheng Zhao’s burdens was providing the Zhou family with an heir.","With Mu Jiang gone and Xian Si unable to win the Duke’s favor, the continuation of the Zhou family bloodline rested entirely on her.","Huan Qingtang was hinting to the Dowager Madame that this matter could be used to pressure Cheng Zhao.","They could even threaten her: if she remained childless, the Zhou family would divorce her.","The Dowager Madame smiled. “You’re concerned only for your younger sister-in-law. That shows your kindness. But you must also take care of yourself. You have responsibilities on your shoulders as well.”","Tears glimmered in Huan Qingtang’s eyes.","“I will never disappoint Grandmother’s expectations,” Huan Qingtang said.","The Dowager Madame patted her hand and praised her for being obedient and filial.","In early October, Huan Qingtang appeared in the meeting hall of Chengming Hall.","The flower hall fell silent.","The various stewards looked from Huan Qingtang to Cheng Zhao. No one dared speak rashly, afraid of offending either side.","Cheng Zhao stood and asked with concern, “Elder Sister-in-law, are you feeling better?”","“I’m much better now.”","Huan Qingtang was dressed in mourning clothes, with a white flower still pinned at her temple. The plain white garments lent her a graceful, delicate air, making her look even more beautiful and aloof.","“Elder Sister-in-law, please sit. I haven’t called the roll yet,” Cheng Zhao said."]},{"number":220,"title":"Chapter 220: The Worst Strategy","paragraphs":["The Chen Duke’s residence was like a pond: the slightest breeze was enough to stir up waves.","After the First Madam’s death, Huan Qingtang came to Chengming Hall to take charge of affairs and accomplished several things in a row, all with the Grand Madam’s support behind the scenes.","“Even if the Third Young Madam has moved into Chengming Hall, the situation is still unclear. The Grand Madam is still alive.”","Cheng Zhao might not necessarily become the future mistress of the Duke’s residence.","The servants were all like rootless duckweed, drifting wherever the current took them. One moment the wind blew this way, and the next it blew that way.","Suyue had a fiery and impatient temperament. “What a bunch of fence-sitters!”","Qiubai comforted her, and Nanny Li also told her not to worry.","Cheng Zhao remained composed.","She neither grew proud nor impatient, and simply took care of the matters at hand.","“Things went smoothly before. Did you think victory was already ours?” Cheng Zhao teased Suyue with a smile.","Suyue let out an exasperated cry, her brows drawing together. “And you can still joke at a time like this?”","Cheng Zhao smiled. “First Sister-in-law hasn’t won, and we haven’t lost either. What are you fretting about?”","Suyue: “...”","The situation was better than Cheng Zhao had expected, and she was quite satisfied.","Her composure encouraged her trusted aides. Suyue gradually stopped panicking and settled down. Chengming Hall remained impregnable, both inside and out.","Just then, another complication arose.","The invitations arriving at the gatehouse no longer passed through Cheng Zhao’s hands. The stewards delivered every one of them to the Hall of Longevity instead.","After the Iron Case had come to an end, the capital had fallen quiet for a time. Now it was lively again, with far more banquets and weddings than usual.","The Grand Madam handed all the invitations to Huan Qingtang.","Once, twice—the stewards began to feel uneasy.","This time, even Nanny Li, who served at Cheng Zhao’s side, grew anxious.","“The Grand Madam’s move is truly ruthless. First Young Madam is still in mourning, yet she’s sending her out to attend banquets while keeping you confined at home. She’s trying to suppress you!” Nanny Li said.","One person was being raised up while another was being pushed down, and all the attention was turning toward Huan Qingtang.","“She has no sense of propriety. Isn’t she afraid people will laugh at us? It makes it seem as though there’s no one else in the Duke’s residence,” Suyue said anxiously once more.","Nanny Li said, “That’s precisely the point. Apart from First Young Madam, there’s no one else.”","Suyue’s expression changed drastically. “The Grand Madam has truly lost her mind!”","Qiubai also looked toward Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao remained impassive.","“...Young Madam knows what she’s doing.” Qiubai was comforting the others—and herself. “You don’t care about it at all, do you, Young Madam?”","Cheng Zhao said, “I do care.”","Qiubai: “...”","After Cheng Zhao said this, she saw her trusted aides looking as though they had been struck by lightning and could not help laughing.","“I’ll think of a solution,” Cheng Zhao said with a smile. “The sky hasn’t fallen yet. It’s still too early to talk about who has won or lost.”","That evening, when Zhou Yuanshen returned, he saw that everyone in Chengming Hall was dispirited, while Cheng Zhao’s expression remained unchanged. He gave her a puzzled look.","After they went to Jiangyun Courtyard for dinner, the couple returned, washed up, and lay down. Only then did he ask, “What happened here? Is it about the gatehouse?”","Cheng Zhao said, “Nothing escapes your notice.”","“There isn’t much happening in the household,” he replied.","Not just in the household—even the entire imperial court revolved around little more than these same matters.","“Nanny Li and the others are worried about me,” Cheng Zhao said.","“...Are you worried?” Zhou Yuanshen asked.","Cheng Zhao replied, “No. First Young Madam is still in mourning. If she keeps going out to attend banquets and socialize, she’ll give people countless things to talk about in the future.”","Zhou Yuanshen nodded slightly. “I also think this is the worst possible strategy. Her frequent outings will only bring trouble upon herself. That’s why I didn’t intervene on your behalf.”","He added, “It’s good that you understand everything.”","Cheng Zhao said, “Mother hasn’t heard about it yet. Once she does, she’ll be worried.”","“I’ll speak with her tomorrow after dinner,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","The couple chatted softly as they settled down. Then he pulled Cheng Zhao into his arms once more.","The night stretched on.","Meanwhile, in Jiangyun Courtyard, the Second Madam had caught wind of something and was instructing Nanny Fan to investigate it the next day.","The Second Master said, “There’s no need to investigate. I happen to know something about it.”","He told the Second Madam about the Grand Madam taking control of the gatehouse, giving all the invitations to Huan Qingtang, and restricting Cheng Zhao from going out.","The more the Second Madam heard, the angrier she became.","“...Zhaozhao hasn’t said anything,” she forced herself to calm down and said.","The Second Master replied, “She and Yuanshen haven’t fallen behind. The fact that neither of them is doing anything means they’re waiting to see what happens next.”","“We don’t need to worry?”","“No.” The Second Master smiled. “Lady Huan is still in deep mourning.”","“That old woman has lost her senses too. She’s acting out of desperation,” the Second Madam said coldly.","The Second Master replied, “The desperate one is Lady Huan. Mother still has cards in her hand, and she’s waiting to use them to control Lady Huan.”","The Second Madam said, “...The Grand Madam trusts no one. She has never regarded her daughters-in-law or granddaughters-in-law as members of the family.”","The Second Master fell silent.","It was only now that the Second Madam understood this truth.","And who, exactly, besides daughters-in-law and granddaughters-in-law, was not considered family?","That night, the Second Madam slept poorly.","Their circumstances were clearly improving—so why did she feel her heart growing colder?","In the past, she had suffered under the Grand Madam and Madam Song. Yet in her heart, the Zhou family of the Chen Duke’s residence had still been a family.","Its relationships might have been battered and broken, but it had been a family all the same.","Now, looking at it again, it seemed she had been the only one who thought so.","The Chen Duke’s residence, its wounds laid bare, was not a family at all. It was a stage. Everyone had to perform a scene to amuse the Grand Madam.","If they performed poorly, someone else would be brought in to take their place.","And the only person seated in the audience was the Grand Madam.","At the thought, the Second Madam shuddered.","The Second Master took her hand and said softly, “Go to sleep. Don’t dwell on it.”","The next day, Cheng Zhao continued managing affairs. Some of the stewards in Chengming Hall were restless, but every one of Cheng Zhao’s own people remained calm and orderly.","Zhou Yuanshen went to court.","He had not originally intended to interfere, but when he saw how worried the servants in Chengming Hall were, he decided to lend a hand.","He made a trip to the Du residence and sought out Cheng Zhao’s eldest sister, asking her to do him a favor.","Several days later, the sky turned overcast.","Judging by the weather, it seemed that the first snow of the year was about to fall.","Nanny Li remarked, “This year’s first snow is rather late. It’s already the tenth month.”","“This year has been warm,” Cheng Zhao said.","Since snow was expected, Cheng Zhao reminded Huan Qingtang, who was in charge of the storerooms, “First Sister-in-law, the winter supplies for the various quarters should be distributed.”","Huan Qingtang smiled. “I was just preparing to do that. I’ve instructed the stewards to draw up a list and send it to each quarter. Tomorrow, I’ll have the stewardesses from each quarter collect the supplies according to the list.”","“That would be excellent,” Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","Huan Qingtang said, “It’s already the tenth month. Even if the sky weren’t overcast, the winter supplies should have been distributed by now.”","Cheng Zhao chatted with her for a while.","Neither of them mentioned the matter of going out to attend banquets.","The skies remained overcast for several days. The north wind howled, and sure enough, tiny pellets of snow began to fall at dusk. Gradually, they turned into snowflakes, drifting lightly onto the roofs and treetops.","When they opened their eyes the next morning, bright daylight filled the windows, and the courtyard was covered in snow an inch deep.","“What a heavy snowfall.” Cheng Zhao was delighted.","The first snow of every year was always enough to bring joy.","Zhou Yuanshen had risen early to attend court, and Nanny Li had instructed the rough servants to clear the snow from the pathways.","But the snow was still falling. In no time, another layer of white had settled over the flagstones.","“Tomorrow, I can invite my sister and sisters-in-law over to warm themselves by the brazier and brew tea,” Cheng Zhao said.","Nanny Li smiled. “I’m afraid Second Young Madam will invite you first.”","“Second Sister-in-law does love hosting guests when the first snow falls,” Cheng Zhao said.","The snow stopped in the middle of the morning.","It had been neither too heavy nor too light—not enough to cause a disaster, but more than sufficient for brewing tea, admiring the snow, and holding a festive gathering.","In the middle of the afternoon, the gatehouse delivered an invitation to Cheng Zhao.","Nanny Li’s face lit up with delight.","On closer inspection, her delight faded.","“Young Madam, it really is an invitation from the Cheng family,” Nanny Li said.","She had thought the Grand Dowager Lady would pass along invitations from other households to Cheng Zhao as well. As it turned out, only invitations from the Cheng family—and those specifically addressed to Cheng Zhao—had been sent over."]},{"number":221,"title":"Chapter 221: Who Is the Hostess","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao received an invitation from her second sister-in-law in her maiden family, inviting her to return home to admire the snow.","She wrote a reply and had Nanny Li personally deliver it to her sister-in-law.","When Nanny Li returned, she said to Cheng Zhao, “This old servant told the Second Young Madam about what has been happening here.”","She glanced at Cheng Zhao timidly, as though regretting her actions. “I couldn’t hold my tongue for a moment.”","Cheng Zhao smiled. “I never go out to attend social gatherings. Sooner or later, my family was bound to find out. It’s good that you told Second Sister-in-law. Otherwise, everyone at home might start guessing and end up worrying about me. You haven’t caused me any trouble.”","Nanny Li secretly let out a sigh of relief.","That evening, after the passion between them had subsided beneath the bed curtains, Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen changed clothes and lay down, chatting idly for a while.","Cheng Zhao kept her voice low, not wanting those on night duty to hear. “I don’t mind being forbidden from attending the banquet. I deliberately did nothing, too, so that the people around me would rein in their arrogance.”","After moving to Chengming Hall, Cheng Zhao knew very well that she was still a long way from the destination she desired. Yet the people around her were delighted.","Pride could easily lead to carelessness.","Cheng Zhao wanted them to calm down.","But no matter how many words she spoke, nothing worked as well as a single lesson.","“Nanny Li and Suyue are actually quite good.” Cheng Zhao was afraid Zhou Yuanshen would look down on her trusted aides, so she defended them. “They’re very loyal. They’re simply happy for me. A little pride is only human nature.”","Zhou Yuanshen turned his face slightly toward her. “Cheng Zhao, you take every step very steadily.”","“There are times when I act rashly, too,” Cheng Zhao replied.","Setting fire to the small Buddhist shrine in Nonghua Court had certainly been a risky move.","Of course, even if she had not set the fire, the Buddhist scriptures Eldest Madam Song had sent would have caught fire sooner or later. If she had simply waited, the damage might have been considerable—or someone might even have died.","“Boldness backed by certainty can’t be called rashness,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao smiled.","She rolled into his arms. His clothes had been warmed by his body heat and felt comfortably cozy.","Zhou Yuanshen wrapped his arms around her and gently kissed her brow. “Cheng Zhao...”","“No!” Cheng Zhao refused.","If they went at it twice in one night, she might as well forget about sleeping.","Zhou Yuanshen kissed her lips, his breath mingling with hers. “What if I’m quick?”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","Cheng Zhao, who did not fall asleep until midnight, decided that she would never be softhearted toward him again. Indulging him only left her short on sleep.","The next morning, when they rose, Zhou Yuanshen said to Cheng Zhao, “You’ll receive good news soon. Your sisters will all help.”","Cheng Zhao had not slept enough and was still half-asleep. She heard only the word “sisters.”","By the time she was fully awake, it was already late. She hurriedly changed and washed, completely forgetting the few words she had heard that morning.","While handling household affairs, Cheng Zhao asked about the supplies needed for winter: coal, padded clothing for the servants, the organization of the storerooms, and the heated greenhouses in the rear garden.","Huan Qingtang smiled. “You’ve already asked about this twice, Sister-in-law. There’s no need to be so anxious. I’ve taken care of everything that falls under my responsibilities.”","The reception hall suddenly fell silent.","Huan Qingtang was accusing Cheng Zhao of acting as though she were the principal mistress of the household.","Although Cheng Zhao had moved into Chengming Hall, she was not the woman in charge of the household accounts and domestic management.","The Dowager Madame was still alive. Moreover, the Dowager Madame had explicitly stated that household affairs were to be entrusted to Cheng Zhao and Huan Qingtang.","Cheng Zhao oversaw the main kitchen, the gatehouse, the carriage and horse room, and the sewing room.","The main kitchen was important, and it had already become Cheng Zhao’s stronghold. The gatehouse was equally important, but Cheng Zhao had been unable to get a hand in there. The Dowager Madame had no intention of giving it to her.","The remaining areas were managed by Huan Qingtang.","If there were any objections, the matter could be brought before the Dowager Madame, just as it had been before.","Yet Cheng Zhao had repeatedly overstepped her boundaries.","She had even tried to interfere in Huan Qingtang’s “assigned duties.”","“Sister-in-law, the Duke’s Estate is one household. The duties in your hands are also household affairs. Now that we’re managing things together, if anything goes wrong, people won’t curse the person in charge—they’ll curse me, the Duke’s wife.","“After several years, ten years, or even a hundred years, the one they’ll ridicule will still be me, the Duke’s wife.”","Cheng Zhao’s expression did not change. She merely smiled faintly as she spoke.","The household stewards were once again shocked.","The Duke’s wife had a sharp tongue. Every word struck home, leaving no room for mercy.","They had thought the Eldest Young Madam had backed her into a corner, but they had never expected Cheng Zhao to turn around and slap her with an even harder blow.","The stewards who had wavered slightly and waited to see Cheng Zhao make a fool of herself now felt as if they had each been slapped. Their cheeks burned, and they lowered their eyes, not daring to make a sound.","Huan Qingtang’s calm eyes trembled faintly.","A surge of anger rose within her, but she quickly suppressed it.","She, too, felt as if she had been slapped across the face.","It was true that Cheng Zhao was constrained by the Dowager Madame. But Cheng Zhao held the rank and prestige of a titled lady as the Duke’s wife, and she had moved into Chengming Hall. Sooner or later, this household would belong to her.","The Dowager Madame was advanced in years and would have to relinquish control eventually.","Even if Cheng Zhao was overstepping at present, what could anyone do about it? If the Duke’s Estate were compared to the imperial court, Cheng Zhao was the “heir apparent.”","The only person who could question her and accuse her of interfering too much was the Dowager Madame—not Huan Qingtang.","In truth, it was Huan Qingtang who had overstepped.","The reception hall was utterly silent.","“...Since the winter supplies have already been put away, I trust Sister-in-law’s ability to handle matters, so I won’t ask any further questions. Let’s take tomorrow off,” Cheng Zhao said.","Her words broke the silence in the reception hall.","Nanny Qian, who managed the main kitchen and was one of Cheng Zhao’s trusted aides, asked with a smile, “Tomorrow isn’t the fifth or fifteenth of the month, Third Young Madam. Why are we taking the day off?”","“My sister-in-law from my maiden family invited me home to admire the snow,” Cheng Zhao replied.","Then she added, “Sister-in-law may continue handling matters as usual.”","Huan Qingtang, who had been standing nearby, had already recovered herself.","Her expression was gentle and dignified, as though she felt no embarrassment at all. She joined in, saying, “I’ll be taking the day off as well.”","“Is Eldest Young Madam attending a banquet too?”","“The Princess Consort Jingnan is holding a snow-viewing banquet. I’m going in Grandmother’s place,” Huan Qingtang said.","Nanny Qian glanced at Cheng Zhao again.","The Prince of Jingnan’s residence was related by marriage to the Cheng family—it was the family of Cheng Zhao’s third elder sister’s husband. Yet although the Princess Consort had invited them, the Dowager Madame had not called for Cheng Zhao. Instead, she had chosen Huan Qingtang.","It was a slap in Cheng Zhao’s face.","The New Year was approaching. If the Dowager Madame also refused to let Cheng Zhao attend the spring banquet during the first month of the following year, Cheng Zhao would lose all face.","The prestige she had accumulated as the Duke’s wife would vanish. The title “Duke’s wife” would become worthless.","The Dowager Madame’s move was ruthless.","The authority of the household head had Cheng Zhao completely constrained. If Cheng Zhao truly resisted, the virtue of filial obedience would be used to force her to kneel all the same.","In her struggle against the Dowager Madame, Cheng Zhao was still too inexperienced.","“Then that’s perfect. We’ll all take tomorrow off. If there’s anything to handle, we’ll do it the day after,” Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","Everyone dispersed.","Cheng Zhao rose and returned to the inner room.","Ever since Cheng Zhao had moved into Chengming Hall, Suyue and Nanny Li had stood outside the curtains of the reception hall to attend her whenever she handled household affairs.","They knew everything that had happened in the hall just now.","Both of them held their breath and remained silent.","Nanny Li brought in a cup of tea. Seeing Cheng Zhao lost in thought, she gently urged her, “Young Madam, take your time. Don’t keep everything bottled up inside. It will only harm you.”","Cheng Zhao came back to herself and smiled. “I’m not angry. I was just thinking.”","Then she continued, “The Princess Consort Jingnan has never liked drawing attention, and she has never been close to the Zhou family. With the official iron case causing such a stir recently, given her temperament, she absolutely would not host a snow-viewing banquet—much less invite the Zhou family.”","Cheng Zhao understood the personalities of the principal ladies of her family’s relations by marriage as well as she understood her own.","Even after Cheng Zhao married into the Zhou family, the Prince of Jingnan’s residence had not increased its contact with the Zhou family.","The Prince of Jingnan still enjoyed the emperor’s favor. The princely residence kept itself apart, unwilling to become embroiled in a situation as dangerous as a fire beneath a blazing pot.","If the Princess Consort had truly changed her ways and wanted to join in the festivities, she would have invited only a few close relatives. Why invite the Chen Duke’s household as well?","“Do you find it suspicious?” her maid, Qiubai, asked.","Cheng Zhao gave a slight nod.","Then she remembered something. “The Duke called me ‘Elder Sister’ this morning. Could it be related to this? I’ll ask him when he returns.”"]},{"number":222,"title":"Chapter 222: Childhood Fun","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao waited for Zhou Yuanshen to return.","Zhou Yuanshen came back rather early that day.","Seeing that the stewards had already dispersed from the reception hall, he asked, “Are today’s affairs over so quickly?”","“They quarreled a little. Since tomorrow’s matters have to be put off again, they simply postponed the afternoon’s work as well,” Cheng Zhao replied.","The household affairs of the Duke of Chen’s residence were orderly and well managed. Even if no one attended to them for half a month, nothing would go wrong. Of course, if the head of the household was incompetent and weak, it could just as easily result in wicked servants bullying their master.","The Dowager Madame was indeed highly capable. Although she had not managed affairs for many years, her authority was deeply rooted in everyone’s hearts.","Cheng Zhao’s feelings toward the Dowager Madame were exceedingly complicated. She admired her, detested her, and felt that she resembled her greatly—yet she was determined not to become like her...","“Who was quarreling with whom?” Zhou Yuanshen asked.","His question brought Cheng Zhao back to herself.","Cheng Zhao told him about the disagreement between herself and Huan Qingtang.","Zhou Yuanshen praised her. “That was a fine retort. Cheng Zhao, there’s nothing you can’t answer and no situation you can’t handle.”","Cheng Zhao broke into a nervous sweat. “What scheme are you plotting now?”","The previous night, he had praised her a little too much. Overcome with emotion, Cheng Zhao had climbed into his arms, costing herself more than an hour of sleep.","There was no smile on Zhou Yuanshen’s face, but his eyes were unnaturally bright. He reached out and stroked her head.","Cheng Zhao: “...”","Perhaps his palm was simply too warm. A wave of heat rose to her cheeks, and the tips of her ears began to burn.","“Talk about serious matters!” she said, shifting to the side.","She mentioned the snow-viewing banquet at the Prince of Jingnan’s residence and then asked Zhou Yuanshen about what he had said that morning.","Knowing that she had not heard him clearly earlier, Zhou Yuanshen repeated himself.","Cheng Zhao was astonished after hearing him out. “For such a minor matter, you dragged my eldest and third sisters into it?”","“No matter how capable a general is, without thousands of troops under his command, it is difficult to win every battle. We have never fought alone.","“As long as we remain undefeated, if your eldest or third sister ever encounters difficulties, I will do my best to help them. I can repay that favor.","“And as for matters within the inner household, it would be inappropriate for me to interfere on your behalf. Was I supposed to stand by and watch you fall behind? I had no choice but to ask them for help,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao stared at him blankly, unable to speak for a moment.","Only after the warmth in her heart had gradually subsided was she able to reply calmly, “They’re all trivial matters.”","“I only helped with a small thing,” he said.","Cheng Zhao reached out and took his hand.","Zhou Yuanshen clasped hers in return and pulled her over. Cheng Zhao ended up sitting in his lap.","He kissed her gently.","The husband and wife leaned against each other, neither saying another word. The room was heated by an underfloor warming system, and as the warm air drifted around them, Cheng Zhao felt both her face and her heart slowly beginning to burn.","It was still a long while before nightfall...","She stood up. “There’s still snow in the courtyard. Let’s build a snowman.”","Then, after thinking it over, she changed her mind. “Let’s go build one in Jiangyun Court and show it off to Fifth Younger Brother.”","Whenever she got something good, she wanted to show it off to Zhou Yuanqi.","Showing it to other people would be frivolous bragging. Showing it to Zhou Yuanqi was simply a way to annoy him.","Zhou Yuanshen agreed without hesitation. “All right.”","He did not mock Cheng Zhao for being childish.","The couple took a small carriage to Jiangyun Court.","The underfloor heating had also been lit in Jiangyun Court. The large heated brick bed beside the eastern side room’s window was warm as well. The Second Madam ordered the maids to serve hot tea and asked the couple, “Why have you come so early today?”","Cheng Zhao replied, “We wanted to build a snowman.”","The Second Madam’s eyes lit up. “That sounds fun.”","She never spoiled anyone’s mood and was an excellent mother-in-law.","With Zhou Yuanshen doing most of the work, while the Second Madam and two sturdy older maids assisted him, they soon built an angler in the courtyard.","The Second Madam then called for a maid. “Go find a straw rain cape and bamboo hat.”","The maid acknowledged the order.","When Zhou Yuanqi entered, it was dusk, and the light was gradually fading. Seeing someone sitting in the courtyard, he jumped in surprise.","“Who is that?”","Cheng Zhao and the Second Madam were each holding a hand warmer beneath the eaves, chatting idly. Zhou Yuanshen stood with his hands behind his back, occasionally adding a comment.","Hearing Zhou Yuanqi’s voice, Cheng Zhao laughed. “What do you think of this?”","Zhou Yuanqi had thought it was his father sitting in the courtyard. As it happened, his father came out after changing clothes, wearing a cloak with a fur collar.","“Who could be so bored as to make such a useless thing?” Zhou Yuanqi glanced at his elder brother.","“I built it,” Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi looked the snowman up and down for a long while before sneering. “You packed it so tightly. Where would you have gotten the strength?”","It must have been made by a brute.","“You have a sharp eye. Lord Duke did indeed make it,” Cheng Zhao said. “Isn’t it lifelike?”","Zhou Yuanqi: “...”","No one had praised him. Why were you acting as though you had something to be proud of?","Building an angler in the courtyard was vulgar and uninteresting.","He would not look at it again. Otherwise, he might become vulgar as well.","That was what Zhou Yuanqi told himself, yet he still circled the snowman twice.","The Second Madam suppressed a laugh. “Yuanqi, if you truly like it so much, ask your Third Brother to build one in your courtyard too.”","“Such a little trinket of clever workmanship is nothing I need. There are bamboo plants in my courtyard. They are refined enough,” Zhou Yuanqi replied.","“A bamboo grove beneath the snow, with an angler among it—that sounds even more poetic,” the Second Madam said.","Zhou Yuanqi: “...”","After dinner, Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen took the small carriage back home.","The Second Madam instructed the older maids to arrange another small carriage for Zhou Yuanqi as well.","Zhou Yuanqi dawdled and refused to leave.","“What is it?” the Second Master asked him. “Did you leave something behind?”","“Father, move that angler to my courtyard. Be careful when you carry it, or it might fall apart,” Zhou Yuanqi said.","The Second Madam asked, “Weren’t you just calling it vulgar?”","“A scholar isn’t afraid of vulgar objects. I can keep them under control,” Zhou Yuanqi said.","The Second Madam replied, “If you like it, just say so. There’s nothing embarrassing about that.”","Zhou Yuanqi: “...”","The Second Master doted on his child. Sure enough, he found a handcart and helped Zhou Yuanqi move the snowman to his courtyard.","Fortunately, Zhou Yuanshen was strong, and the snow had indeed been packed very firmly. Even after being carried and shifted around like that, the snowman did not come loose in the slightest.","“Next time you take a fancy to something, ask your Third Brother to make it for you,” the Second Master said. “Who told him to be your elder brother?”","Zhou Yuanqi raised his chin proudly. “If his work is worthy of my attention, he ought to feel honored.”","The Second Master said, “After the New Year, you won’t be allowed to talk like that anymore.”","“Why not?”","“You’re getting older by the day. You’re no longer a little child. If you keep speaking this way, your Third Brother will hit you,” the Second Master said with a laugh.","Zhou Yuanqi: “...”","Having obtained the snowman, Zhou Yuanqi was delighted, though he still put on an air of indifference. He amused the Second Master immensely.","He really was still a child.","Zhaozhao could be like a child sometimes too. Her proud manner was exactly like Zhou Yuanqi’s.","The next day, Cheng Zhao returned to her parents’ home.","As expected, her second sister-in-law had invited quite a few people to view the snow. They were all young married ladies of her acquaintance, along with relatives and friends she got along well with.","“...I also invited Eldest Sister and A-Ying, but neither of them is coming. A-Ying’s family is hosting a banquet, while Eldest Sister accepted an invitation from the Princess Consort Jingnan and went to the Zhang residence,” the second sister-in-law said.","Cheng Zhao did not mention the plans they had made for that day. She merely said, “We see each other every day anyway. Missing one occasion won’t hurt. Another day, we can invite them to view the plum blossoms.”","She smoothly changed the subject.","When they went to change clothes midway through the gathering, the sisters-in-law spoke privately. The second sister-in-law even asked Cheng Zhao, “Have you been bullied? Mammy Li said the Dowager Madame was restricting your outings.”","Cheng Zhao explained the matter to her.","The Dowager Madame had not forbidden her from going out; it was simply that invitations no longer passed through her hands.","The second sister-in-law studied her expression. “You don’t seem discouraged at all.”","“Just a small matter.”","“That’s exactly how it should be,” her second sister-in-law said with a smile.","Cheng Zhao had a very pleasant day at her family home.","When she returned to the Duke of Chen’s residence, she first went to pay her respects to the Dowager Madame, then headed to Jiangyun Courtyard.","By the time she arrived, Zhou Yuanqi was there as well, carrying a generous selection of pastries.","“They were given to me by Grandmother. They’re delicious, so I brought them for you and Third Brother. That way, you won’t accuse me of keeping all the good things for myself,” Zhou Yuanqi said.","Cheng Zhao couldn’t help laughing at his teasing.","Huan Qingtang returned rather early that day.","The rumors about her did not reach the Second Madam’s ears until the following day. The Second Madam then told Cheng Zhao about them."]},{"number":223,"title":"Chapter 223: The Past Exposed","paragraphs":["Before lunch, Second Madam made a special trip to Chengming Hall.","Cheng Zhao had just finished handling her affairs and was preparing to eat. When she saw Second Madam, she rose to greet her. “Mother?”","Second Madam looked as though she wanted to say something but could not bring herself to speak.","Cheng Zhao instructed Nanny Li, “Have the main kitchen send the meal over.”","Then she asked Second Madam, “Mother, have you eaten?”","“Not yet.”","“Then eat here with me,” Cheng Zhao said. Turning to Nanny Li, she added, “Bring my mother’s meal over as well.”","Nanny Li acknowledged the order and left.","After Suyue served the tea, she led all the attendants away. Only the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law remained in the side room. Lowering her voice, Second Madam said, “Madam Sheng came by earlier and mentioned something that happened yesterday.”","Madam Sheng, the wife of General Sheng, was her mother-in-law’s close friend from girlhood. She often came to visit, and Cheng Zhao knew this.","The only matter connected to the Zhou family that could have happened yesterday was the snow-viewing banquet at Prince Jingnan’s residence.","“Was it about Eldest Sister-in-law?” Cheng Zhao asked.","Second Madam said, “As expected of you, Zhaozhao. You’re so clever.”","Cheng Zhao smiled. “What happened?”","“Lady Huan pushed County Princess Xizhen into the pond. Princess Qing’an wanted to have her arrested and handed over to the authorities, but Princess Consort Jingnan persuaded her to let the matter go,” Second Madam said.","Cheng Zhao was speechless.","County Princess Xizhen was Princess Qing’an’s daughter. Because she had been overly particular about choosing a husband, she had reached the age of twenty without becoming betrothed, making her a constant topic of conversation in the capital.","The entanglement between her, Huan Qingtang, and the Duke of Chen’s household went back to the time when Huan Qingtang had used Zhou Yuanshen and Princess Qing’an as stepping stones to marry into the Duke of Chen’s residence.","“Many titled ladies were present,” Second Madam continued. “Princess Qing’an said that Lady Huan had schemed against her back then and used Ah Shen as a stepping stone to marry into the Duke of Chen’s household. Madam Sheng said everyone was stunned. None of them had known about this hidden history.”","As she spoke, Second Madam looked both irritated and delighted.","She hated verbal sparring. It would be better to fight openly and have done with it. Whenever she heard other people arguing, she wished she could hand each of them a spear and let them settle it properly.","Yet Zhou Yuanshen’s grievances had finally come to light.","And it was Princess Qing’an herself—the woman who had set the scheme in motion—who had exposed them.","Huan Qingtang and Princess Qing’an had never regarded Zhou Yuanshen as a person. They had trampled all over him simply to secure a marriage with the Duke of Chen’s household. What they had really been scheming for was Zhou Yuancheng.","Who could have known that Zhou Yuanshen would ultimately inherit the title?","The two women had turned on each other. Princess Qing’an would rather injure herself than let Huan Qingtang escape unscathed, and so she had exposed the past before everyone present.","From then on, everyone would know that Zhou Yuanshen had never had an improper relationship with his widowed sister-in-law. He had merely been the victim.","Now that he had become the Duke of Chen, both Huan Qingtang and Princess Qing’an had clearly misjudged him.","Such gossip was bound to be popular. It was more exciting than a stage performance and more deeply satisfying—who did not enjoy this kind of drama?","At the thought, Second Madam felt thoroughly vindicated.","Cheng Zhao’s heart stirred slightly.","“No wonder Eldest Sister-in-law didn’t come to Chengming Hall this morning to handle affairs. Her maid said she had caught a slight chill,” Cheng Zhao remarked.","Second Madam sneered. “How could she still have the face to show herself?”","Nanny Li returned with two rough-serving women carrying a food chest. Suyue and Qiubai set the table.","After Cheng Zhao and Second Madam finished lunch, Cheng Zhao sent Second Madam home in a small covered carriage.","She handled affairs as usual in the afternoon, finishing in less than half an hour.","Then Cheng Zhao went to visit her eldest sister.","Her eldest sister was teaching her daughter to practice calligraphy by tracing red characters.","Cheng Zhao had brought a delicate little toy for her niece, Heng’er. Heng’er was delighted and kept praising her, saying that Fifth Aunt was the best and that she liked Fifth Aunt the most.","The wet nurse took the child outside, and Cheng Zhao immediately asked, “What happened yesterday?”","Her eldest sister could not help laughing. “You couldn’t even wait one night? You came rushing over in the middle of the afternoon.”","“It really was unexpected.”","“It was nothing more than sowing discord. Princess Qing’an’s household has repeatedly meddled in court affairs and has even grown quite close to the Fourth Prince. Princess Consort Jingnan has taken issue with that.","“Prince Jingnan is loyal to the Crown Prince. What he fears most are ambitious members of the imperial clan. Princess Consort Jingnan wanted to reduce her dealings with Princess Qing’an but had no excuse to do so.","“I mentioned the Duke of Chen to Ah Ying, and the princess consort said, ‘Why not force the princess to say something reckless and make a scene? Then I’ll have an excuse to distance myself from her.’","“Princess Consort Jingnan knows Princess Qing’an very well. With Ah Ying and me egging things on from the side—and with your sister-in-law from your husband’s family so eager to show herself—that scene came about.”","At the banquet, Huan Qingtang and Princess Qing’an’s daughter, County Princess Xizhen, had not gotten along.","It was Cheng Zhao’s eldest sister, Cheng Han, who had deliberately brought up County Princess Xizhen’s marriage, using deliberately inappropriate words to provoke Huan Qingtang.","County Princess Xizhen had still not married, all because of what Huan Qingtang had done in the past, and she was full of resentment. Huan Qingtang, meanwhile, felt guilty and was desperately trying to make amends while also attempting to appear gracious and composed.","Princess Consort Jingnan’s snow-viewing banquet was not a family gathering of the Zhou clan. No one was there to flatter Huan Qingtang, and no one was willing to act as her henchman and help her out. As a result, she struggled to cope.","She was already making mistakes in her fluster. Then County Princess Xizhen deliberately picked a fight, and the two of them made an utter spectacle of themselves. The hostess, Princess Consort Jingnan, not only failed to mediate but fanned the flames, causing County Princess Xizhen’s mother, Princess Qing’an, to become furious as well.","“Still, County Princess Xizhen is spoiled,” her eldest sister added. “She was the one who tried to shove your sister-in-law. She simply wasn’t as strong, so she ended up falling into the water herself.”","Cheng Zhao said, “That was quite a show. Fortunately, I didn’t go. Otherwise, I would have been dragged into that mess too.”","“Exactly. Since this involved the Duke of Chen, your sister-in-law might have used you if you had been there,” her eldest sister said.","Cheng Zhao took her eldest sister’s hand. “I know you dislike getting involved in such schemes. You did this for me.”","“Yesterday’s performance could never have taken place if any one of your sister-in-law, Princess Qing’an, or County Princess Xizhen had been innocent.","“They brought this on themselves. It was simply the retribution for all the wicked things they had done. I have no qualms about involving myself in a matter that will not touch me,” her eldest sister said with a smile.","Then she added, “Your brother-in-law’s appointment was secured through Yuanshen’s efforts. He asked me to help him, so how could I refuse to repay the favor?”","“He also said that he ‘owed his eldest and third sisters-in-law a favor.’ If you need anything in the future, just go to him,” Cheng Zhao said.","Her eldest sister laughed. “Then I won’t stand on ceremony.”","The sisters were chatting and laughing when a maid from the front gate announced, “A nanny from the Cheng family has arrived.”","Both of them hurriedly stood up.","Her eldest sister said, “Invite her in at once.”","It was the senior woman in charge of their mother’s attendants.","After offering her greetings, the woman asked with a smile, “The Fifth Lady is here too?”","“Yes.”","“Madam only wishes to know what happened at the prince’s residence yesterday. The whole city is in an uproar today. Even the kitchen’s purchasing servants have heard about it and repeated it to Madam.","“Madam was very worried, so she sent for Eldest Lady to come home and ask about it. She has also sent people to summon Third Lady and Fifth Lady.”","Cheng Zhao was speechless.","Bad news truly traveled a thousand li.","Princess Qing’an and the Duke of Chen’s household were both prominent families. Their scandals were bound to become the subject of endless gossip. If they had been an insignificant household, far fewer people would have cared about their romantic entanglements.","And now there was the added titbit of two women—a widowed sister-in-law and a county princess—fighting over a marriage into the Duke of Chen’s household while trampling Zhou Yuanshen in the process. It made the story all the more sensational.","If the Duke of Chen had been Zhou Yuancheng, the matter would not have spread so quickly. But Zhou Yuanshen had unexpectedly inherited the title.","The despised Third Young Master of the Zhou family had now risen to immense power. Back then, those women had trampled all over him simply because they believed he had no future.","That kind of reversal was immensely entertaining, like oil poured onto a blazing fire. In less than a day, the story had already spread throughout the capital’s prestigious military and meritorious families.","It would likely travel much farther still.","Perhaps before long, the teahouses in the market districts would even be making up stories about the whole affair.","Cheng Zhao wasn’t worried. In this matter, Zhou Yuanshen wasn’t the fool made to look ridiculous.","He might even win some sympathy."]},{"number":224,"title":"Chapter 224: Cheng Zhao's Arrogance Grows Even More Unbridled","paragraphs":["It was already getting late, and Cheng Zhao could no longer make it back to her family home.","She did not want to give the Grand Lady any excuse to find fault with her.","The Grand Lady was probably furious by now.","After such an ugly commotion, she would certainly assume that Cheng Zhao’s sisters had sabotaged things and destroyed the pawn in her hands.","“...I’ll go back tomorrow. Tomorrow is a day of rest, after all,” Cheng Zhao said.","The older woman acknowledged her.","The eldest sister said, “Then I’ll go tomorrow as well. Linlang said she invited us to play cards.”","Linlang was Cheng Zhao’s second sister-in-law. Her maiden name was Yin Linlang.","The older woman returned to report what had happened.","Cheng Zhao also rose and returned to the Duke Chen’s residence.","Zhou Yuanshen had already arrived home. He was in the adjoining room, looking over some documents and dealing with miscellaneous matters. The page Nanfeng and the maid Mingyu stood nearby, reporting to him.","When they saw Cheng Zhao return, Nanfeng and Mingyu bowed. Each then went off to attend to their assigned duties.","Cheng Zhao sat down opposite Zhou Yuanshen. “Have you heard?”","“Mingyu just told me,” Zhou Yuanshen replied. “The matter at Prince Jingnan’s residence is quite interesting.”","“The Princess Consort wants to distance herself from the princess. The princess and her consort have ambitions of their own and want to win over Prince Jingnan, while the Princess Consort and the prince have long been on their guard against them,” Cheng Zhao said.","This time, what appeared to be a quarrel among women in the inner residence was actually an extension of the struggle at court.","If Princess Qing’an had merely been an ordinary member of the nobility, the Princess Consort would never have allowed Cheng Zhao’s sisters to cause such a scene at her snow-viewing banquet.","Without the hostess’s tacit approval, the tiny spark between County Princess Xizhen and Huan Qingtang would have been snuffed out the moment it appeared.","Who would have dared to add fuel to the fire and push matters to this point?","“...We’ve been very fortunate,” Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","With all sorts of circumstances coming together, Huan Qingtang had been forced to answer for her past, her reputation had been utterly ruined, and she no longer had the standing to suppress Cheng Zhao.","Zhou Yuanshen, meanwhile, had gained an excellent reputation.","It seemed that without any one of these pieces, they could never have achieved such a result.","Cheng Zhao understood the will of Heaven all too well.","For instance, the Grand Lady and Huan Qingtang had planned to use the banquet to elevate Huan Qingtang before the public. Even if she encountered a little suspicion, it would not have mattered.","The Grand Lady’s power as the Empress Dowager’s equal would have gilded Huan Qingtang with a layer of gold.","In this world, the voice of power rang the loudest.","They had planned everything so perfectly, even going so far as to trample Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen beneath their feet, yet in the end their scheme had fallen apart. That was “Heaven’s will denying them.”","Cheng Zhao’s counterattack, on the other hand, had effortlessly produced an even better result than she had anticipated. That was “Heaven’s will aiding her.”","“I have indeed been fortunate these past few years,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","A casual marriage decree from the Empress had given him a duchess who was as beautiful as a fairy and as intelligent as she was perceptive. His good fortune had begun at that very moment.","Once he had seized the right opportunity, he had set foot on a broad official road.","From then on, his path had been smooth.","Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen talked for quite some time.","She said, “I’m going back to my family home tomorrow. Would you like to come with me?”","Zhou Yuanshen replied, “The first snow of the year fell the day before yesterday.”","“Hm?”","Her question and his answer had nothing to do with each other.","“I’m making preparations for something, and I’ll probably be rather busy these next few days,” Zhou Yuanshen said. “If you need me to accompany you, I can—”","“No need. Your important business comes first,” Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen rose and walked over to her side. He slipped an arm gently around her and whispered against her ear, “Cheng Zhao, I’ll take Xian Si out tomorrow.”","Cheng Zhao froze.","He leaned closer and explained the matter to her in a voice so low that only she could hear.","When she had finished listening, Cheng Zhao was somewhat surprised. “Will it work? This is too...”","Too crude, too commonplace.","She was afraid it might have no effect.","“It’s worth a try,” he said. “If it succeeds, Lady Huan will be completely discarded. With Xian Si’s identity, she’ll have no choice but to work for you and me rather than Grandmother.”","Cheng Zhao moved closer to him.","She looked into his eyes.","His dark eyes were quiet and deep, filled with certainty—but also with the desperate determination of someone staking everything on a single throw. If he did not succeed, he would perish trying.","Cheng Zhao liked that ruthlessness.","To climb out of a desperate situation, one had to take risks.","She nodded lightly. “There’s nothing I can do to help. I’ll pray for your success.”","Zhou Yuanshen tightened his arms around her.","Held against him, Cheng Zhao found it a little difficult to breathe. Only after a while did he loosen his embrace somewhat.","She hesitated before asking, “Should I be advising you to be more cautious?”","As his wife, was she supposed to counsel him when he was about to take such a dangerous gamble?","It seemed that she should.","Zhou Yuanshen smiled.","He bent down and lightly kissed Cheng Zhao. “Do you want to advise me?”","“...Not particularly.”","The husband and wife exchanged a smile.","The next day, Zhou Yuanshen left very early.","The sky had not cleared after the snowfall. It was overcast, and the snow piled up in the courtyard had not yet melted.","It was not especially cold, either.","Cheng Zhao took her time eating breakfast, then did her hair and makeup as she prepared to visit her family home.","Qiubai had already gone to the outer courtyard to order a carriage for her, while Nanny Li went to prepare gifts.","Suyue stayed at Cheng Zhao’s side and told her about Huan Qingtang.","Even the servants in the main kitchen had heard.","By now, the whole household probably knew.","“...The Grand Lady is furious,” Suyue said in a low voice. “I heard Nanny Sun lashed out at the senior maidservant. That was the Grand Lady’s order.","“The Grand Lady has always treated the servants kindly, and a senior maidservant is practically a second-rank mistress in the household. If she hadn’t been enraged, she wouldn’t have humiliated her like that.”","Cheng Zhao selected a box of rouge and dabbed some onto her lips with her fingertip.","She pressed her lips together to blend it in, so her words came out muffled, almost hidden in her mouth. “Be careful these next few days. Don’t let yourself fall into the Grand Lady’s hands.”","Suyue said, “You can rest assured. Our people know their limits. If anything really does happen, they’ll kneel, weep, and beg forgiveness. The Grand Lady won’t truly make things difficult for the servants.”","The Grand Lady’s benevolent expression was not one she would readily cast aside.","Cheng Zhao was about to say something else when a maid outside announced, “Third Young Madam, the Eldest Young Madame is here.”","Suyue looked faintly surprised.","Cheng Zhao gave her a meaningful glance. Suyue understood at once and hurried out from the inner room.","Through the thin curtain of glazed beads, Cheng Zhao heard Suyue say, “Eldest Young Madame, our mistress is doing her makeup. You’ve come rather early. Is there some urgent matter?”","“Ask her to come out. I have something to say to her. Otherwise, I’ll go in myself!” Huan Qingtang said.","Her words were sharp and her tone severe.","Cheng Zhao had been her sister-in-law for more than a year, and this was the first time she had ever heard Huan Qingtang raise her voice like that.","Huan Qingtang had also modeled herself after the Grand Lady, cultivating a gentle and gracious image in ordinary times. Other people handled all the dirty work for her, while she enjoyed every benefit.","To barge into Cheng Zhao’s residence, Chengming Hall, with such an aggressive attitude was highly unusual.","Had she gone mad with rage?","Cheng Zhao motioned for the maid doing her hair to secure the last hairpin. She put on her earrings herself, then lifted the beaded curtain and walked out.","There was no sunlight. Even the glazed beads gave off no radiance in the dimness, their dazzling colors withdrawn.","“Eldest Sister-in-law...”","“Cheng Zhao, what exactly are you trying to do?” Huan Qingtang took two steps forward, her face stiff and stern as she stared intently at Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao met her gaze. “What am I trying to do?”","“You set a trap to harm me. Do you think it’s only me you’ve ruined? You’ve damaged the reputation of the Duke’s residence, Grandmother’s life’s work, and the dignity of our entire clan!” Huan Qingtang’s voice was loud.","It was anger.","It was accusation.","More than that, it was an attempt to pin all the blame on her.","Several household managers stood at the entrance, having come with her. They seemed more like people who had followed her to persuade her to calm down, and none of them dared approach.","Cheng Zhao stepped forward. “How did I set a trap to harm you? Explain it clearly. Don’t leave out a single word.”","Her voice was just as loud.","Huan Qingtang refused to yield. “You had your sisters—”","“Did I ask you to attend the banquet at Prince Jingnan’s residence?” Cheng Zhao cut in, overpowering her voice.","Cheng Zhao practiced swordsmanship every morning, and her abundant vitality gave her a much stronger voice than Huan Qingtang’s.","“Grandmother was the one who summoned you. How could she possibly be trying to harm you?”","“And you actually dare slander Grandmother...”","“Was I the one who told you to use Princess Qing’an? Was I the one who instructed someone else to push the County Princess into the pond?” Cheng Zhao pressed.","Her confidence grew.","Her arrogance became even more brazen.","Huan Qingtang was nearly unable to withstand her onslaught."]},{"number":225,"title":"Chapter 225: Push One's Advantage","paragraphs":["This was the first time Cheng Zhao and Huan Qingtang had ever quarreled.","Both of them came from illustrious families. From childhood, they had known what face to present to the world to preserve their dignity, and how to conduct themselves to their own advantage.","Given the similar upbringing they had received, Second Madam might have been utterly baffled by Huan Qingtang’s decision to start a quarrel today and tear away her gentle façade without a care. But Cheng Zhao understood perfectly.","Her reputation outside the household was already beyond saving, so she had come to reclaim some dignity within it.","Huan Qingtang had deliberately acted out of character, creating the impression that she was the victim of a conspiracy and shifting all the blame onto Cheng Zhao.","She had chosen to come and argue instead of crying to the Dowager Madame because she wanted to catch Cheng Zhao off guard.","She was taking a gamble.","She was betting that, for the sake of her position as Duchess, Cheng Zhao would not dare fight back while she was making a scene.","She had not even intended to say much.","She only wanted to make a commotion, let the words spread, restore some of her reputation, and then retreat at once.","But she had underestimated Cheng Zhao.","Of the three Cheng sisters, Cheng Zhao was the most mischievous and ambitious. She had also spent her entire childhood arguing with her fourth elder brother, Cheng Chao, so she was highly experienced at dealing with provocations.","Cheng Zhao alone could hold her own against both Cheng Chao and Helian Xuan, and had never once lost.","In an instant, she could see through her opponent’s intentions and methods, then respond with perfect clarity.","Cheng Zhao scarcely gave Huan Qingtang a chance to speak. The moment she caught the end of one of Huan Qingtang’s sentences, she shoved every accusation Huan Qingtang had intended to pin on her right back at her.","“Is your sister-in-law’s anger because Grandmother made you attend social functions during your mourning period, or because Princess Qing’an exposed what happened back then?” Cheng Zhao asked again.","Huan Qingtang’s expression shifted several times.","Perhaps she was used to sailing across a calm little lake. She could deal with the occasional ripple—for instance, County Princess Xizhen had already suffered another loss at her hands.","But Cheng Zhao had seen the towering waves of the open sea.","After being struck by several questions hurled at her in rapid succession, Huan Qingtang was stunned by the “waves” Cheng Zhao had unleashed. Her face turned pale, then green.","“You needn’t drag innocent people into this. Your two sisters poured filth all over me...” Huan Qingtang said through clenched teeth.","“What filth? Which part was filth? If anyone poured mud on you, it was the conflict between you and Princess Qing’an. You were the one who dragged my sisters into it—that is slander!” Cheng Zhao said.","She continued, “As sisters-in-law, even if we are not on good terms, have I ever involved your family? Yet you dragged my family into this. Since you have made such vicious accusations, let us go and ask Grandmother to judge between us!”","As she spoke, she reached out and tugged at Huan Qingtang’s sleeve.","Huan Qingtang tried to shake her off.","Cheng Zhao appeared to lose her balance.","Suyue hurriedly supported her, then shouted toward the steward and several maids standing by the courtyard gate, “What are you waiting for? Come help! The First Young Madam is attacking our Duchess!”","She glared resentfully at Huan Qingtang. “First Young Madam, how could you be so outrageous? You actually came to make a scene in Chengming Hall!”","Huan Qingtang’s face grew even paler. “When did I push her?”","Cheng Zhao only managed to steady herself with Suyue’s support.","In the midst of the chaos, Nanny Sun from Shou’an Residence arrived with several maids.","She surveyed the scene and said to Cheng Zhao and Huan Qingtang, “The two of you are making such a racket. Do you still have any regard for the Dowager Madame?”","Tears sprang into Cheng Zhao’s eyes. “Nanny Sun, I am in my own courtyard, and I was not the one who started this. I have suffered an enormous injustice, yet the moment you arrive, you treat us both as equally at fault.","“I am going to ask the Empress to judge this matter. This marriage of mine was bestowed by the Empress. If she will not protect me and allows you to trample on and humiliate me, I will throw myself against the walls of Kunning Palace and die.”","With that, she turned and walked out.","Nanny Sun: “...”","The message she had received was that Huan Qingtang had come to Chengming Hall to cause trouble, only to be scolded into silence by Cheng Zhao.","And now, looking at Huan Qingtang—who appeared thoroughly enraged—it was obvious that Cheng Zhao had not suffered the slightest loss.","Yet Cheng Zhao was still putting on this pitiful display.","She was far too difficult to deal with!","Nanny Sun had crossed paths with Cheng Zhao several times and knew all too well how painful Cheng Zhao’s soft knives could be.","She could not allow Cheng Zhao to go make a complaint.","Huan Qingtang’s reputation had already been ruined. If the Empress reprimanded her as well, she would have no face left to live.","Nor could the Zhou family afford another spectacle like this.","Nanny Sun had no choice but to go after Cheng Zhao and grab her. “Duchess!”","She did not call her Young Madam, but Duchess.","“The Dowager Madame is unwell. Are you trying to drive her to her death by making such a disturbance? If anything happens to her, the charge of ‘filial impiety’ will not be borne by you alone,” Nanny Sun said.","If Cheng Zhao were deemed unfilial, her maternal family would lose face as well.","Though the words were stern, Nanny Sun’s tone was gentle, half coaxing and half persuading.","Cheng Zhao carelessly wiped away her tears. “How could I bear to trouble Grandmother? Once one becomes another family’s granddaughter-in-law, one inevitably has to endure some grievances.”","Nanny Sun: “...”","The steward and the servants of Chengming Hall had all heard those words.","Huan Qingtang had come to make trouble, but instead of gaining the upper hand over Cheng Zhao, she had merely covered herself in mud.","Nanny Sun glanced at Huan Qingtang. She had now seen clearly that within this household, Huan Qingtang was no match for Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao had not even used all her strength, yet she had already turned defeat into victory.","Nanny Sun ordered both of them to go to Shou’an Residence.","The Dowager Madame did not see them. She merely called out loudly from the inner room, “Have them copy Buddhist scriptures for four hours and calm themselves down. Quarreling at home is utterly unbecoming!”","Then she added, “If they refuse to copy, have their families come and take them away.”","Cheng Zhao silently went to do as she was told.","Huan Qingtang followed as well.","The small Buddhist chapel had no underfloor heating, and after the snow, the sky was overcast and the air bitterly cold.","By the time the four hours were over, the light outside the window had faded, and night was drawing near.","Cheng Zhao was both exhausted and hungry.","She handed the copied scriptures to Nanny Sun.","Her handwriting was neat and orderly. Even on the final pages, there was not the slightest trace of carelessness.","Huan Qingtang’s handwriting was also excellent, without a single messy stroke. She had simply copied nearly half a section fewer than Cheng Zhao. Her stamina was inferior to Cheng Zhao’s, and her pace had slowed considerably toward the end.","The Dowager Madame had only ordered them to copy for four hours; she had never said how many pages they had to complete.","When Cheng Zhao stepped out of the small Buddhist chapel, she saw Zhou Yuanshen.","He stood upright beneath the eaves.","His gaze did not linger on anyone else. It settled only on Cheng Zhao’s face. “Finished copying?”","“Yes.”","“Nanny Sun, if Grandmother is well, we will return and have our meal,” Zhou Yuanshen said, turning to Nanny Sun.","“She is fine now. The Duchess may return,” Nanny Sun replied.","Zhou Yuanshen then left with Cheng Zhao without going to see the Dowager Madame.","Nanny Sun, meanwhile, summoned Huan Qingtang into the Dowager Madame’s inner room.","The Dowager Madame said to her, “You keep making one foolish move after another. You have disappointed me greatly.”","Huan Qingtang was exhausted and hungry, with barely enough strength left to speak.","She sat there in a daze, like a block of wood. The composure and quick-wittedness she had shown before were nowhere to be seen.","The Dowager Madame recalled why she had chosen her in the first place. She had valued Huan Qingtang’s father for his potential to become a teacher renowned throughout the realm. She had also valued Huan Qingtang’s scholarly family background, her refinement and learning, and the fact that she seemed easy to control.","And what had come of it?","Her father was a hopeless case, making no progress whatsoever in officialdom. Instead, because of his high-minded and eccentric nature, he had become estranged from his colleagues.","As for Huan Qingtang, when circumstances favored her, she could put on a convincing show. But whenever anything happened, her shortcomings immediately became apparent.","Of course, the Dowager Madame did not blame herself for having chosen Huan Qingtang in the first place.","She blamed Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao had not been her choice.","As an outsider who had invaded the family, Cheng Zhao had disrupted the Zhou family’s plans. And Cheng Zhao was simply too difficult to handle—she was nothing like the daughters of respectable scholarly families, but was bold, fierce, and unruly.","Yet in ordinary times, she could also be gentle and composed, never harming her reputation in the slightest. Whenever trouble arose, however, she pounced like a vicious wolf and tore into her opponent without mercy.","Even the Dowager Madame felt somewhat intimidated by her.","“Grandmother, is there still a way out for me?” After a long silence, Huan Qingtang lifted her eyes and asked the Dowager Madame softly.","The Dowager Madame had been waiting for her to say those words.","“How can you already be at the end of the road?” the Dowager Madame said. “You’re still young, and you have a long road ahead of you—as long as you’re willing to walk it.”","“I am, Grandmother. Please, show me a way out,” Huan Qingtang said."]},{"number":226,"title":"Chapter 226: A Substantial Harvest","paragraphs":["A small covered carriage waited outside Shou’an Hall.","Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen had gone to Jiangyun Court for dinner.","Second Madam had already learned everything that had happened that day, including the fact that Cheng Zhao had spent four hours copying Buddhist scriptures in Shou’an Hall.","Her heart ached for her and she had a rough-serving matron massage Cheng Zhao, loosening her muscles and bones so they would not stiffen and ache.","Cheng Zhao did not refuse.","“...Lady Huan is hateful, and the Old Lady is hateful too!” Second Madam cursed. “Why don’t we take this matter to the Empress and see what they can do!”","They always picked on the weakest target, bullying such a lovely young girl, fair as frost and snow.","How could they be so vicious and heartless?","They might as well torment her instead. She could endure it. But how could Zhao Zhao possibly stand it?","Second Madam was both furious and heartbroken, wishing she could storm over to Shou’an Hall and demand an explanation. Nanny Fan persuaded her not to; when Second Master returned, he held her back as well.","Cheng Zhao smiled. “Mother, making a scene would only hurt me. At a time like this, if I resist Grandmother and earn a reputation for being unfilial, wouldn’t I just be helping Eldest Sister-in-law? I would rather copy Buddhist scriptures.”","When she needed to be forceful, Cheng Zhao gave up not an inch. When she needed to show weakness, she could lower her head as well.","“That’s true. Everyone outside is talking about her. If the subject turns to you, she’ll be delighted,” Second Madam said.","Second Master nodded from the side. “Zhao Zhao knows exactly where to draw the line. No one can find fault with anything she does.”","The Cheng family had deep roots and placed great importance on proper upbringing. That was how they had raised such an exceptional daughter.","Whoever’s household Cheng Zhao became mistress of would be blessed by her.","Second Master felt that he and his wife could now enjoy their later years in peace. Cheng Zhao was capable of managing everything, and they would no longer need to worry on her behalf.","She truly had that ability.","Even when facing the Dowager Madame, Second Master would feel intimidated. Cheng Zhao, however, could employ both firmness and softness, never allowing herself to fall into a disadvantageous position.","“Does your hand still hurt?” Zhou Yuanqi asked as well.","“A little,” Cheng Zhao replied.","“Copying for four hours straight—you really are something,” Zhou Yuanqi said. “If I held a brush for four hours, my wrist would swell.”","Second Madam said, “That’s because you’re useless. I told you to practice with your spear.”","Then she added, “Your third brother has been practicing spear work since he began his lessons. His wrist has never swelled.”","Zhou Yuanqi was deeply displeased. “Mother!”","He had been showing concern for his sister-in-law. How had his mother suddenly turned around and started criticizing him?","His mother came back to herself when he called out, and ordered the chief maid, “Bring in a handkerchief soaked in hot water and have the Young Madam use it as a compress.”","The chief maid went to do so.","Once the massage was over, Cheng Zhao obediently draped the hot handkerchief over her right wrist.","It was time to eat, and Second Madam once again ordered the chief maid to feed Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao hurriedly said she did not need help.","After dinner, they returned.","Second Madam spent the entire evening sighing over Cheng Zhao’s suffering, while Second Master said that the Dowager Madame was already a spent force.","“...I only hope the children understand what must never be done,” Second Master said suddenly.","Second Madam did not understand. “What must never be done?”","Second Master remained silent for a long while.","He was very afraid that the Dowager Madame would die at the hands of Zhou Yuanshen and Cheng Zhao.","That could not happen. It would leave them with a disgraceful reputation that would be condemned for generations.","He only hoped the children understood the seriousness of the matter. Even if they were driven to the brink, they must not commit an irreversible mistake.","Cheng Zhao returned to Chengming Hall, where Nanny Li and the others immediately came out to welcome her.","“This old servant went back to the Cheng residence and informed Madam and the others about what happened to you,” Nanny Li said. “I’ll go again tomorrow to let them know you’re safe.”","Cheng Zhao had said she would return home, only to end up not going. Naturally, the Cheng family had been anxious as well.","“I’ll go back tomorrow,” Cheng Zhao said.","Nanny Li nodded, then looked her over. “Did you suffer much? I heard you were punished by being made to copy Buddhist scriptures.”","Unless someone deliberately concealed what had happened in Shou’an Hall, the entire household would soon know.","Cheng Zhao said, “This little bit of hardship is nothing. When I was young, my mother often punished me by making me copy scriptures too, to teach me and my fourth brother a lesson.”","She added, “Whenever I was punished as a child, it was always together with my fourth brother.”","Nanny Li thought Cheng Zhao was about to sigh over the deep bond between herself and Cheng Chao, siblings who had grown up inseparable. Instead, she heard her say, “That scoundrel Cheng Chao was always dragging me into trouble.”","Nanny Li: “...”","To be fair, it was not entirely Fourth Young Master’s fault every time they were punished together...","But that could not be said aloud. The moment it was mentioned, Cheng Zhao would lose her temper.","That night, beneath the bed curtains, Zhou Yuanshen also massaged her wrist.","His hands were strong, and before long the skin around Cheng Zhao’s wrist felt warm.","She wanted to talk about something, but she was too tired. The moment she closed her eyes, she sank into dreams and slept utterly unaware of the world.","When she awoke the next morning, daylight had already filled the room. To her surprise, Zhou Yuanshen was still there.","“...I don’t have to attend court today. I’ll accompany you to your parents’ home,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao agreed.","Perhaps her grandfather and father wanted to speak with him as well. After all, he was also involved in the rumors surrounding the Jingnan Prince’s residence.","The gifts prepared the day before were still there. Qiubai arranged for them to be carried to the carriage, and the young couple set out.","When Cheng Zhao arrived at the Cheng residence, she found Eldest Sister, Third Sister, and her second sister-in-law all in her mother’s courtyard.","Her two sisters had stayed at their parents’ home after Cheng Zhao failed to arrive the previous day.","Zhou Yuanshen exchanged greetings with everyone before being led by a servant to the outer study to meet Cheng Zhao’s grandfather.","“How is it?” Eldest Sister took her hand and examined her repeatedly. “Is your hand swollen?”","“My mother-in-law had someone massage it for me and then applied a hot compress. It’s perfectly fine this morning,” Cheng Zhao said.","She moved her wrist around.","She used this hand for calligraphy, sword practice, and needlework on a daily basis. How could it be so easily injured? She was not made of clay.","“Did Lady Huan deliberately provoke you?” her mother asked.","Cheng Zhao nodded.","She then told her mother and sisters how Huan Qingtang had behaved at the time.","“Lady Huan does seem rather calculating,” her second sister-in-law said.","“She has all the cunning, but none of the strategy. If she wanted to attack, she should at least have known herself and her enemy. She charged in without even knowing how much food or how many soldiers the other side had,” Third Sister, Cheng Ying, said.","Huan Qingtang had not understood Cheng Zhao’s temperament in the slightest.","They had been sisters-in-law for so long. Cheng Zhao had been steadily chipping away at Huan Qingtang’s position, yet Huan Qingtang still looked down on her so thoroughly. Cheng Ying found the woman baffling.","Perhaps she did understand Cheng Zhao, but had overestimated herself, believing she could win an argument with her.","In any case, every one of Huan Qingtang’s defeats began with her making the first move. She had brought it upon herself; no one else could be blamed.","“Zhao Zhao handled it perfectly,” her mother said with great satisfaction. “She did not yield an inch to Lady Huan, yet she did not put on airs before the Dowager Madame.”","Being able to swallow one’s anger for the moment was a quality possessed by extraordinary people.","“Grandmother was waiting for me to offend her. Then she would have dragged my grandfather into it and accused the Cheng family of being ‘unfilial,’” Cheng Zhao said.","The others burst out laughing.","At midday, Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen ate separately. She had lunch with her mother, while Zhou Yuanshen ate with Cheng Zhao’s grandfather in the outer study.","In the middle of the afternoon, Cheng Zhao’s father returned home. Zhou Yuanshen spoke with him for quite some time, and Cheng Zhao’s two elder brothers also went to the outer study to meet him.","As a result, the young couple did not leave the Cheng residence until dusk, when darkness was already approaching.","“What did they say to you?” Cheng Zhao asked.","“Congratulations,” Zhou Yuanshen replied.","Cheng Zhao did not understand. “Congratulations on what?”","As for taking on dual marital obligations and taking concubines, Zhou Yuanshen had already dealt with everything. What else was there to congratulate him on?","“Last year, I carried out the Emperor’s orders to confiscate the estates of several high-ranking noble families, which earned me quite a bit of abuse among the common people. Although my maternal uncle arranged for people to defend my reputation, some unpleasant rumors remained after all.","“But now that this has happened, the rumor that County Princess Xizhen and my cousin’s wife once ganged up on me has become firmly entrenched in everyone’s minds. Risqué gossip carries more weight and is easier to remember.","Grandfather congratulated me, saying that this would erase—or at least downplay—the disgraceful reputation of ‘harming a court official,’” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao had actually forgotten about that.","There had indeed been several incidents last year, and Zhou Yuanqi had even feared being implicated by his elder brother.","For an official, harming a fellow courtier was a stain on his reputation. That stain could become a major problem or a minor one in the future—even if the emperor himself had ordered him to do it. But scandalous romantic rumors were merely entertaining gossip; they did not strike at his foundations.","By replacing the former with the latter, Zhou Yuanshen had made a profit without taking any losses.","Cheng Zhao had not expected such an unexpected benefit.","“I really ought to kowtow to Sister-in-Law,” Cheng Zhao said. “I completely forgot about this. If I’d remembered, I would have let her scold me a few times yesterday and considered it repayment for her kindness.”","Zhou Yuanshen: “......”"]},{"number":227,"title":"Chapter 227: Happy Event","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen returned to the Duke of Chen’s residence quite late.","“Did anything happen today?” Cheng Zhao asked Nanny Li.","Nanny Li replied, “The steward from the gatehouse came by. But since you weren’t handling affairs and the Eldest Young Madame didn’t come either, I told him to return tomorrow and report then. Other than that, nothing happened.”","Cheng Zhao nodded slightly.","The young couple went to bed early.","As usual, they chatted for quite a while before falling asleep.","“I’ll have to go to the Metropolitan Garrison again in a few days,” he said.","“You don’t need to worry about me,” Cheng Zhao replied.","“I’ll delay it as long as I can,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Then he added, “I have some good news to tell you.”","“Good news?”","“Young Uncle is getting married.”","Cheng Zhao was a little surprised. “Which family’s daughter?”","She hadn’t heard anything about it.","Second Madam probably didn’t know either. Given her mother-in-law’s personality, the moment she found out, she would tell Cheng Zhao at once rather than keep it until the next day.","“The daughter of Vice Minister Song. She put off marriage to observe mourning for her mother. Later, because of the severe drought in the two lake regions and the disaster that struck her hometown, she was stranded there for several years. She and Young Uncle are the same age,” Zhou Yuanshen explained.","“How old is Young Uncle this year?”","“Twenty-eight.”","Cheng Zhao said, “A young woman who has remained unmarried until twenty-eight must have some reason behind it, surely. Is she very ugly?”","“...Cheng Zhao, how are you so sharp? The young lady isn’t ugly. There is a reason.”","It was a long story.","Zhou Yuanshen told Cheng Zhao that Vice Minister Song was a member of the Ministry of Rites, and the girl was his third daughter. Of course, he had no connection whatsoever with the Eldest Aunt’s maternal family, the Marquis of Changling’s household.","The reason Third Miss Song had waited until she was twenty-eight to discuss marriage—and was now marrying a widower—was that the Duke of Pi had taken a fancy to her when she was young.","Neither Vice Minister Song nor Third Miss Song was the type to covet wealth or status.","The Duke of Pi had been remarrying as well; this would be his third wife. Furthermore, he was more than twenty years older than Third Miss Song, so the Song family was unwilling to agree to the match.","But they did not dare offend the Duke of Pi.","Vice Minister Song used an excuse to send his daughter back to their ancestral home. Two years later, the girl’s mother fell ill and died, and she observed mourning for a year. Since her hometown truly had been struck by disaster, she entered a Buddhist convent as a laywoman to pray for the villagers, voluntarily abstaining from meat and reciting Buddhist scriptures for five years.","The story became a celebrated one in the region, and even the prefect submitted a memorial praising her.","In the second year after Third Miss Song left the capital, the Duke of Pi married another young and beautiful woman as his third wife.","He declared that he would destroy the Song family and that Third Miss Song could marry no one but him. If she did not want to become his principal wife, then she could become his concubine.","Fortunately, Vice Minister Song had fellow disciples and was not without support. He stood his ground. However, he made no progress in his official career for many years, and his future was more difficult than that of others.","The Duke of Pi wielded considerable influence.","His nephew was the Fifth Prince, and his daughter was Consort Dou. It was not until last year, when the Fifth Prince died in the Dowager Madame’s formation, that the Duke of Pi’s household lost its imperial prince and its greatest source of support. Only then did it gradually fall into decline.","A close friend of Vice Minister Song’s had also been promoted to Chief Justice. With his friend’s support, Vice Minister Song finally dared bring his daughter back.","The match had been arranged by his superior, Chief Justice Fan Xiao.","“...From the sound of it, the Song family has good character. The young lady is strong-willed and decisive, and Vice Minister Song truly cares about his daughter,” Cheng Zhao said.","He had not sold his daughter for the sake of wealth and glory.","“Come to think of it, Third Miss Song does have some connection with our family. Not only was the Duke of Pi’s household weakened by the Fifth Prince’s death, which was related to Grandmother, but back when she was being forced into marriage, your grandfather submitted a memorial accusing the Duke of Pi.","“The Duke of Pi was confined and had his salary docked, giving the Song family a chance to catch their breath. That was how Vice Minister Song managed to send his daughter away. Otherwise, how could she ever have escaped the capital?” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao remembered the matter.","The reason Consort Dou had treated Cheng Zhao with such hostility when they first met was precisely because of this old grudge between the Cheng family and her maternal family, the Duke of Pi’s household.","“What a tangled web of fate,” Cheng Zhao said with a smile. “The two people who are meant to become husband and wife must have some connection destined by heaven.”","Zhou Yuanshen thought so too.","After inheriting the title, he had never considered marriage. Then the Empress suddenly bestowed a marriage upon him.","As for Cheng Zhao, among the young ladies of the capital, she was not particularly well known and rarely socialized. If the Zhou family had taken the initiative to seek a marriage alliance for Zhou Yuanshen, they would never have considered Cheng Zhao.","They did not even know she existed.","And yet, through a twist of fate, Cheng Zhao had become his wife. What an extraordinary bond that was!","At the thought, Zhou Yuanshen tightened his arms around her.","Cheng Zhao gently pushed him away. “I’m going to sleep!”","Zhou Yuanshen merely held her and did nothing else. “Go to sleep.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","He truly did not do anything. Cheng Zhao was genuinely tired as well, and she gradually fell into a deep sleep.","When she awoke, Zhou Yuanshen had already gone to court. Cheng Zhao washed, changed, and ate breakfast before sitting down to handle household affairs.","The stewards arrived one after another.","Huan Qingtang did not come.","Many of the stewards had previously thought that if the Dowager Madame sent Huan Qingtang out to attend social events, she would suppress Cheng Zhao.","Unexpectedly, the situation had turned around. Huan Qingtang had instead become the target of ridicule.","Cheng Zhao’s position as Duchess had become even more secure.","Seven-tenths of the stewards, whether they had originally belonged to the Dowager Madame’s faction or the Eldest Madam’s, had come to acknowledge Cheng Zhao in their hearts and wanted to place themselves under her protection.","The gatehouse steward in particular had such thoughts.","“I may not have many people under my command, but even if I submit to her, I can’t let her control me entirely. I need to show her a little authority first, so she’ll respect me from the bottom of her heart,” he had said to his wife.","Thus, during this period, he had deliberately delivered invitations from the gatehouse to the Dowager Madame, encouraging her to place Cheng Zhao under “confinement.”","His original plan had been quite perfect. Once the time was right, he would offer the Duchess a little “sweetness.” Perhaps Cheng Zhao would come to rely on him in every matter from then on.","Maybe she would even promote him to chief steward in the future.","Unexpectedly, Huan Qingtang had fallen first.","The stewards could not imagine how she might recover from this.","Perhaps Huan Qingtang would be better off moving to Qingfeng Court and living out her days in the idle peace of a widow. For the sake of her own dignity, the Duchess would surely treat her well and care for her until the end of her life.","“...If there’s nothing else, everyone may leave,” Cheng Zhao said.","There was not the slightest trace of smugness on her face. Her unfathomable composure was frightening.","Many young masters and madames of eminent families possessed less dignity than old stewards, especially when the Dowager Madame was still alive.","Yet Cheng Zhao had established her authority in a very short time.","“Young Madam, will the Eldest Young Madame continue managing affairs in the future?” one of the stewards asked Cheng Zhao.","“That is not something you should ask me about. If you’re curious, you may ask the Dowager Madame.”","She glanced over them.","“Of course, someone who takes such an interest in other people’s business may well displease the Dowager Madame.”","The steward lowered his head.","After everyone had left, Nanny Li said with a smile, “There weren’t any troublemakers today.”","“Let’s wait and see,” Cheng Zhao replied.","Then she added, “They’re waiting for me to make a mistake. The moment I do something inappropriate, they’ll find an excuse not to work, and I won’t be able to do much about it.”","“They all think you have no one to use,” Nanny Li said.","When Cheng Zhao had married into the family, her mother had told her to keep her household retainers stationed outside. The purpose was to protect them from being pushed aside by the old stewards.","Once her own people lost confidence and authority under that pressure, it would be difficult for them to become a source of support for her in the future.","“My mother really did see far ahead,” Cheng Zhao said.","The matter was set aside for the time being.","Two days later, Nanny Qian from the main kitchen quietly came to Chengming Hall and said to Cheng Zhao, “The meals for Jade Brocade Court haven’t been collected for several days. Is the Second Concubine ill? I had the servants keep it quiet and wanted to inform you first.”","Cheng Zhao smiled faintly. “I already know. Just continue doing your work as usual. There’s no need to hide anything.”","Nanny Qian was completely bewildered, but she did not ask any further questions and respectfully replied, “Yes.”"]},{"number":228,"title":"Chapter 228: Beautiful as an Immortal","paragraphs":["Several days after the snowfall, the skies finally cleared.","The weather had grown a little warmer, and the sunshine was bright and splendid.","Zhou Yuanshen did not go to the Capital Garrison. He was still in the Eastern Palace, teaching the Crown Prince calligraphy. Cheng Zhao handled the household affairs as usual. In the evenings, she chatted with her mother-in-law about amusing bits of gossip and traded barbs with Zhou Yuanqi.","Huan Qingtang did not appear before anyone.","She seemed to have been thoroughly beaten down.","Her “fight” with County Princess Xizhen, fueled by certain people’s deliberate spreading of the tale, had indeed become known throughout the capital.","Not only had every noble household heard of it; it had even become a favorite topic in teahouses and among commoners.","“Will County Princess Xizhen never be able to marry?” Second Madam asked Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao replied, “Marrying upward will be difficult for her. Marrying beneath her station, her parents will not be willing. You are right—her marriage prospects are rather troublesome.”","Second Madam shook her head.","Then she asked about Huan Qingtang. “Has she stopped stirring up trouble these days?”","“She has been fairly quiet,” Cheng Zhao said. “She claims to be ill and has shut herself away in her courtyard.”","“Zhaozhao, if she truly claims illness and ceases managing affairs, then after a year or two asks to move into a more secluded courtyard, she would be a clever woman.","“She is the eldest sister-in-law. Even fifty years from now, you would still have to show her some measure of respect. For the sake of your and Ashen’s reputations, you would have to provide for her properly,” Second Madam said.","Nanny Fan, who was attending nearby, could not help laughing.","Second Madam asked, “Did I say something wrong?”","“No,” Nanny Fan replied. “This servant merely thinks that Madam has become very thoughtful in her considerations. If Eldest Young Madame is truly clever, keeping quiet would benefit her more.","“If she truly hates Lord Duke and Third Young Madam, she ought to act discreetly. Her very existence is an eyesore; for the rest of her life, she could make things unpleasant for our Third Young Madam.”","Second Madam nodded.","They thought so, and others thought the same.","“Mother, it is easy to say, but difficult to do. She harbors resentment and bitterness. If she wishes to use silence and the passing years to make my life difficult, the first question is whether she can truly settle her heart and remain still,” Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","“I certainly could not do it,” Second Madam said.","“Neither could this servant,” Nanny Fan added.","“Eldest Sister-in-law is even more restless by nature. Though she does not show it, she wants far too much, and none of it is within her reach.","“If she truly settles down, there is indeed nothing I could do about it. She could vex me for decades. But I do not think she has the patience to remain quiet,” Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam sighed again after hearing this.","Leaning against her bolster, she was silent for a long while, seemingly at a loss for words.","Seeing how dispirited she looked, Cheng Zhao feared that she would grow depressed. She deliberately changed the subject to cheer her up. “Mother, have you heard that my maternal uncle is discussing marriage?”","The moment those words were spoken, both Second Madam and Nanny Fan were startled.","“Where did you hear that?” Second Madam hurriedly asked.","She sat up straight, her eyes brightening considerably, filled with astonishment and curiosity.","Cheng Zhao smiled. “Lord Duke told me.”","“No one told me!” Second Madam said, hastily sitting upright. “When is he getting married? Whose daughter is it? Who is arranging the match?”","Before Cheng Zhao could answer, she stood. “You cannot possibly know all the details. I am going to the Grand General’s residence.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","Second Madam acted with tremendous haste, and Nanny Fan was just as efficient. Though it was already late afternoon, mistress and servant set off at once.","They ran into Zhou Yuanqi as he was entering.","“Mother, what has happened?” Zhou Yuanqi asked.","“Your maternal uncle is about to take a wife.”","“A second wife.”","“Do not quibble over the wording,” Second Madam said. “I have not heard anything about it, so I am going to ask.”","“I have not heard either. I am coming too.”","He followed them out.","Cheng Zhao was left standing in the doorway. “...”","That day, Cheng Zhao did not have dinner at Cloud-Red Courtyard. Instead, she returned to Chengming Hall.","When Zhou Yuanshen came back, Cheng Zhao told him what had happened.","“Let my mother go,” Zhou Yuanshen said. “Neither the Fan family nor the Song family intends to make the matter public. My mother ought to know in advance.”","A marriage to take a second wife could be conducted with varying degrees of ceremony. It could be kept very simple, and no one would criticize the families for keeping it low-key.","The Duke of Pi was still alive, and the Dou family had not completely fallen from power. Vice Minister Song did not dare make much of a show of marrying off his daughter. The Fan family, meanwhile, did not wish to involve itself too deeply in political affairs.","Thus, it was only after the marriage negotiations were nearly completed and the auspicious wedding date of the seventeenth day of the eleventh lunar month had been set that Zhou Yuanshen dared reveal the news.","Had Zhou Yuanshen not mentioned it, Second Madam likely would not have learned of it until her younger brother’s wedding day.","She would have been furious.","“Not only will Mother be angry; Fifth Brother will be angry as well. He loves organizing things, and he is Grandmother’s favorite, yet he was not told,” Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","Zhou Yuanshen thought she, too, was enjoying the excitement.","Perhaps happy occasions naturally brought people joy and made them inclined to join in the fun.","Recently, they truly needed a little good news.","“Go ask tomorrow and see what they have found out,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao nodded.","The next day, as soon as she had finished handling her affairs, Cheng Zhao went straight to Cloud-Red Courtyard.","Second Madam dearly wished to gossip with her, but she was afraid of disturbing her and did not feel it appropriate to go to Chengming Hall.","The moment Cheng Zhao arrived, Second Madam began talking without pause.","She introduced Third Miss Song to Cheng Zhao all over again.","“The wedding date has been set?” Cheng Zhao deliberately asked.","“The seventeenth day of the eleventh lunar month,” Second Madam said. “There is no time for me to prepare any substantial wedding gift. I discussed it with your father-in-law; when the time comes, we can only give money.”","“Money is practical,” Cheng Zhao said. “My maternal uncle can buy whatever he needs himself. The expensive gifts sent by relatives may not be useful and will simply sit in the storeroom. Left there too long, they may be looked down upon when they are later given away as gifts to others.”","It was like Cheng Zhao’s first birthday after entering the Zhou family, when the eldest madam and Huan Qingtang had selected presents for her from the storeroom. She had known at a glance that they had been sitting there for a very long time.","“You are right,” Second Madam said with a smile.","She was in high spirits.","Second Madam also said, “The family has seen Third Miss Song. She is very beautiful. Her looks are comparable to yours.”","Then, afraid Cheng Zhao might be displeased, she added, “Of course, that is only praise for the new bride. I have never seen anyone more beautiful than you.”","Cheng Zhao lowered her voice. “The Duke of Pi is extravagant and licentious. Any girl who catches his eye must surely be a peerless beauty.”","Second Madam heartily agreed.","She was entirely delighted, without the slightest fear of the Dou family’s influence at the Duke of Pi’s residence.","Vice Minister Song had found himself a powerful and formidable in-law.","Second Madam even suggested to Cheng Zhao, “Should we sneak over and take a look?”","“Mother, do not make a mess of things,” Cheng Zhao said. “If you are truly curious, ask Madam Sheng to inquire for you.”","“But I have not seen her with my own eyes.”","Cheng Zhao laughed.","Second Madam’s heart was so full of joy over her younger brother’s wedding that she failed to notice the rumors spreading through the residence: Second Concubine Xian Si might have gone missing.","Xian Si had been taken away by Zhou Yuanshen. On the eighth day, when Zhou Yuanshen returned in the middle of the afternoon, Xian Si followed behind him.","The two entered the Duke’s residence one after the other.","The news spread immediately.","There were all sorts of rumors.","Some even claimed that the Duchess was jealous, and that Lord Duke did not dare favor Second Concubine in the residence, so he had no choice but to take her elsewhere.","Second Concubine had not returned for several days, yet Lord Duke had come home every day.","Second Madam finally heard the rumors.","In an instant, her joyful mood sank to the bottom.","“Where is Ashen?” she asked Nanny Fan. “Go wait in the outer court. When he returns, bring him here at once!”","He had only just settled down for a few days. Why was he causing trouble again?","Zhou Yuanshen had not returned, but Fan Xiao came instead."]},{"number":229,"title":"Chapter 229: Zhou Yuanshen's Plan Takes Effect","paragraphs":["Fan Xiao entered and, seeing the Second Madam’s dark expression, asked with a smile, “What happened? Who upset you?”","“Your nephew!”","“Yuan Qi was being naughty again?” Fan Xiao asked.","“The other one.”","“Yuanshen? Then it must be a misunderstanding.”","“Are you trying to make me angry too?” the Second Madam snapped. Then she took out her frustration on him as well. “Why have you come? Don’t tell me you’re here to plead for him?”","Fan Xiao had no idea what had happened.","The Second Madam poured out the whole story in one breath.","Fan Xiao smiled. “Sister, if you ask Yuanshen about this, he may not be willing to tell you. Ask anyone else, and they won’t know the details. But I know everything.”","The Second Madam’s anger subsided somewhat.","She looked at Fan Xiao doubtfully. “You know?”","“I was there.”","The Second Madam fell silent.","Fan Xiao then told her what had happened.","“Every year when the first snow falls, His Majesty disguises himself and goes to the hot-spring estate at Mount Jing. Mount Jing is normally guarded with extreme strictness—you know that, don’t you?” Fan Xiao asked.","The Second Madam said, “I’ve long heard there’s an imperial residence on Mount Jing. But they borrowed someone else’s name for it, I suppose, to prevent the censors from making a fuss and accusing His Majesty of extravagance.”","“There’s no ‘imperial residence,’ exactly, but there is a hot-spring estate and a hunting ground. They were originally registered under Prince An’s name, and are now registered under Helian Xuan, Prince of Andong. He and his father manage Mount Jing for His Majesty,” Fan Xiao explained.","The Second Madam fell silent.","No wonder the Prince of Andong was so favored.","It was not merely because he was a close blood relative. He had also done a great deal for the emperor.","Zhou Yuanshen had likewise earned the emperor’s trust by carrying out killings on his behalf.","An emperor like this could never raise scholars of integrity or worthy ministers. Of course, saying that would also mean insulting her own son and younger brother.","The Second Madam let the words circle once around the tip of her tongue, then swallowed them.","“This year, when the first snow fell, His Majesty selected several people to accompany him, and Yuanshen invited me as well,” Fan Xiao continued.","The emperor was rather fond of Fan Xiao too.","Compared with Zhou Yuanshen, Fan Xiao was witty and eloquent, and could always amuse His Majesty.","“He had a young servant with him. I could tell at a glance that something was off—the boy was far too slight. But we were accompanying His Majesty, and no one had the time to concern themselves with it.","“Mount Jing stands high, so it receives much more snow than the capital. The whole mountain was blanketed in white, a magnificent sight. While the skies over the city remained cloudy, by midafternoon the sun had appeared over Mount Jing.","“Toward evening, the attendants and the rest of us accompanied His Majesty along the mountain path to admire the snow. That was when we saw someone dancing beneath a tree. The dance was so beautiful, set against the evening glow and the white snow, that I was completely transfixed.”","The Second Madam glared fiercely at him.","Fan Xiao was simply being honest. “That scene had been carefully arranged by Yuanshen. Black hair, a red dress, an alluring dance—and the heavens themselves had provided the perfect backdrop. It drew everyone’s eyes more than any scenery could have, including Helian Xuan’s.","“Yuanshen reached out and knocked the dancer’s veil from her face. She was Xian Si, the concubine His Majesty had bestowed upon him. Yuanshen apologized and claimed that Xian Si had disguised herself as a servant and followed him out without his knowledge. He said that he had been too busy to spend nights at the Jade Brocade Residence and therefore did not know her very well.”","The Second Madam stared at him. “And the emperor believed such nonsense? How could a servant accompanying him be replaced without him noticing?”","A personal servant was his master’s right hand. How could he not know if his own hand had been switched out?","Fan Xiao said, “Sister, people only hear what they want to hear. You heard only the word ‘disguised.’","“But at that moment, His Majesty was captivated and confused by desire. All he heard was Yuanshen saying that he had never touched Xian Si. And Xian Si was originally a dancer from the imperial estate at the hunting ground. She was His Majesty’s servant.”","The Second Madam fell silent again.","So the emperor’s desire for this woman was perfectly reasonable.","At the hunting ground, the emperor had chosen two dancers—one to give to Zhou Yuanshen and one to give to Helian Xuan. It was a warning to both of them.","When he had selected Xian Si, His Majesty had clearly been captivated by her seductive beauty. Fan Xiao even suspected that the emperor’s original intention might not have been to give her away at all.","But once matters had developed to that point, the emperor had no shortage of women and simply used the two of them as tools. When striking someone, one used whatever happened to be at hand.","Thus, Xian Si had been bestowed upon Zhou Yuanshen.","Zhou Yuanshen had returned her untouched, sending her back exactly as she had come. It had become a celebrated story—so long as an explanation could make sense, the emperor was willing to accept it.","“We descended the mountain that very night. His Majesty didn’t come down until the following day,” Fan Xiao said. “As for Xian Si, she has been in the palace these past few days.”","The Second Madam said nothing.","“Sister, you’ll never guess how she ended up in the palace,” Fan Xiao added.","“How difficult can it be to guess?”","“His Majesty dressed her as a palace maid and secretly brought her back. These past few days, he had her settled in Consort Wu’s palace,” Fan Xiao said.","The Second Madam frowned. “Then why send her back?”","“The Zhou family needs someone like her,” Fan Xiao replied. “Have you forgotten about the pregnant Mu Jiang?”","The Second Madam sat stunned for a long while.","Then she shuddered violently, nearly retching.","“That’s disgusting!” she cried, furious and horrified. “Ah Shen has to suffer that humiliation all over again? Why should he? He’s a subject, and an exceptionally capable one at that. He isn’t the emperor’s slave!”","Fan Xiao also felt sorry for his nephew.","However, this entire matter had been planned by Zhou Yuanshen.","Even his staying the night at Consort Wu’s palace had been arranged after Zhou Yuanshen subtly prompted Consort Wu to persuade him.","Zhou Yuanshen seemed to want things this way.","“Go ask Yuanshen yourself. Perhaps he simply couldn’t be bothered to explain it to you,” Fan Xiao said.","The Second Madam fell silent and sat there for a long time.","Zhou Yuanshen had not yet returned when Cheng Zhao arrived.","Seeing Fan Xiao, Cheng Zhao stepped forward and paid her respects. “Little Uncle.”","Then she offered him her congratulations. “Congratulations, Little Uncle.”","Fan Xiao accepted her felicitations.","“I know you’re very curious about Third Miss Song. I’ve already sent someone to make arrangements with the Song family. In a few days, they’ll be going to Jin’an Temple to offer incense. You can arrange to encounter them there and meet the Song family,” Fan Xiao said.","The Second Madam was no longer in the mood.","She reproached Fan Xiao. “How could you be so thoughtless? What if the Song family misunderstands?”","“They won’t. The Song family is quite understanding. If such a small matter creates a rift between us, then the two families simply aren’t meant to be connected,” Fan Xiao said with a smile. “Sister, don’t worry. Just go with the Duchess.”","He turned to praise Cheng Zhao as well. “With the Duchess there, you’re sure to have an enjoyable outing.”","The Second Madam was speechless.","Cheng Zhao picked up the conversation. “We’ll go. Which day has been arranged?”","“The twenty-fifth,” Fan Xiao replied.","Cheng Zhao said, “That works perfectly. We’re free that day.”","It was getting late. Second Master returned, and Yuan Qi also came over for dinner.","Only Zhou Yuanshen arrived very late.","The Second Madam looked at her son and nearly burst into tears from heartache.","The moment Zhou Yuanshen appeared, Zhou Yuan Qi immediately shouted, “Did you bully my sister-in-law?”","The Second Madam shot him a look. “Shut up!”","Since Fan Xiao had come, Cheng Zhao instructed the servants to go to the main kitchen and have two additional dishes prepared for him. Dinner was fairly simple.","However, Fan Xiao had not come merely for the meal.","He repeated to everyone what he had just told the Second Madam.","He described everything with vivid flair.","In particular, when he recounted Xian Si dancing against the evening glow and snow-covered landscape, everyone listening felt as though they were witnessing the scene themselves.","That included Cheng Zhao.","She had seen Xian Si before and knew how alluring she was.","With a little imagination, Cheng Zhao could easily picture how enchanting she must have been that day. The emperor had been drawn to her from the beginning; otherwise, she could never have been chosen from among so many dancers.","It was an obvious beauty trap.","Cheng Zhao glanced at Zhou Yuanshen.","It was a common and unremarkable strategy—yet its effect had been extraordinarily good."]},{"number":230,"title":"Chapter 230: Harmony","paragraphs":["There were many things in the Zhou family that Second Madam did not know.","Whether it was Zhou Yuanshen, Cheng Zhao, or Second Master, none of them could bring themselves to explain the matter to her plainly, piece by piece.","Some things were simply too difficult to say aloud.","But if they did not speak directly, Second Madam could not understand.","She asked Zhou Yuanshen, “Why bring Xian Si back? She has already been favored by His Majesty. Can’t the inner palace find a place for her?”","Then she turned to Cheng Zhao. “Perhaps the two of us should go to the palace and see the Empress, and ask her to decide this matter.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","Zhou Yuanshen said, “Mother, there’s nothing wrong with bringing her back.”","Second Madam stared at him in disbelief. “Have you lost your mind too?”","If Xian Si returned, it would mean humiliating Zhou Yuanshen.","Many people knew that the emperor had favored the concubine Zhou Yuanshen had sent him, just as he had with Mu Jiang in the past. Mu Jiang had also been forced upon Zhou Yuanshen by the emperor and the Dowager Madame.","And then there was the Dowager Madame...","Second Madam vaguely sensed that she understood something, but when she tried to think more deeply, she could not make sense of it.","“Send her away!” Second Madam declared. “What if she becomes pregnant too? Then Zhaozhao will be the one who suffers. The household stewards are all fair-weather friends, fawning on those with power and trampling those who have fallen. Zhaozhao has only just begun to recover.”","Zhou Yuanshen fell silent.","For a moment, Second Master did not know what to say. He cast his wife a warning glance.","She ignored him.","Fan Xiao was a guest, and there were certain things he could not say either, even though he knew every secret of the Duke of Chen’s residence.","Cheng Zhao was even less able to broach the subject.","Though she was quick-witted and sharp-tongued, she was still a young woman. Certain words were nauseating no matter who spoke them.","Zhou Yuanqi looked from one person to another and finally spoke. “That is precisely why she must become pregnant. The Zhou family must produce a prince. It is what Grandmother and His Majesty both want.”","Second Madam stared at her younger son in shock.","She was not a foolish woman. It was merely that a thin veil had clouded her understanding.","Once she connected this with what had happened to Mu Jiang, she understood.","She understood it—and yet she could not bring herself to believe it. She chose to regard it as nothing more than a child’s innocent idea.","Otherwise, it would be far too disgusting.","She looked at Zhou Yuanshen, then at Second Master and Cheng Zhao.","None of them contradicted Zhou Yuanqi. Cheng Zhao, meanwhile, lowered her head somewhat awkwardly, avoiding Second Madam’s gaze.","“This isn’t a family,” Second Madam said, her voice slightly choked. “What kind of family treats Ah Shen this way?”","“He is the Duke of Chen. Only he can take the blame. His title wasn’t given to him for nothing,” Zhou Yuanqi said.","He was still young.","With so many matters, it was as though he were watching a fire from across the river. He understood them, but he had not experienced them. Thus, they were like the evening clouds—things that fell into his eyes but not into his heart.","He could say them without the slightest burden, his tone light and devoid of heaviness.","Only after he had weathered the blows of time would he come to understand the pain and bitterness hidden behind every one of those matters.","Of course, Cheng Zhao hoped he would never understand. She wished for him to remain a younger brother sheltered by his elder brother and sister-in-law, content to study the teachings of the sages and live an easy, carefree life.","“Mother, I am the Duke of Chen.” Zhou Yuanshen also spoke, taking up his younger brother’s words. “I have no regrets about becoming the Duke of Chen.”","He glanced at Cheng Zhao.","It was precisely because he was the Duke of Chen that he had been able to make Cheng Zhao his wife.","Heaven had given him many humiliations, but it had also gifted him a priceless pearl.","“Sis, fortune and misfortune are intertwined, and prosperity and decline each have their measure,” Fan Xiao said. “Otherwise, given Yuanshen’s status and position, he would have had to wait at least fifty years to obtain a title like this.”","Was it worth it?","That was the question Second Madam asked herself—and Zhou Yuanshen as well.","And the children had given her their answer.","They all believed it was worth it.","After dinner, Fan Xiao returned home. Zhou Yuanshen and Cheng Zhao saw him to the main gate.","The couple walked back slowly.","Cheng Zhao asked him, “Does Grandmother know yet?”","“Not yet,” Zhou Yuanshen replied.","Xian Si had entered the palace and was staying in Consort Wu’s residence, where the Dowager Madame had no informants. As for what had happened at the hot-spring estate on Mount Jingshan, Fan Xiao knew it all clearly, but most people remained unaware.","The Dowager Madame had been feeling unwell these past few days, and she had not yet received word.","“But she will find out soon,” Zhou Yuanshen said. “With so many things happening lately, she will certainly have to find a way to respond.”","The Dowager Madame had sent Mu Jiang away to rid herself of that useless burden and to lay the groundwork for her next plan.","She had repeatedly sent Huan Qingtang out to attend banquets. Perhaps her objective had already been achieved. This method was different from what she had originally expected, but it was even better.","In the Dowager Madame’s eyes, perhaps the plan Zhou Yuanshen and Cheng Zhao had devised had conveniently done her a great favor.","“Cheng Zhao, about Xian Si...”","“It won’t affect anything fundamental,” Cheng Zhao said. “No matter how favored Second Concubine is, can she really become the lady of the house? The stewards are all shrewd. They won’t change their allegiance over something so minor.”","She added, “I’ll show her concern as well. I’ll let the servants see that I’m a generous and magnanimous wife.”","Zhou Yuanshen: “...”","He took Cheng Zhao’s hand.","If he could, he wished Cheng Zhao would not have to become entangled in such a difficult dilemma.","Unfortunately, circumstances left him no choice.","He was still too young, and his birth and position were already set. In many matters, he had no choice but to select the most acceptable option from among the worst.","He had failed Cheng Zhao.","He had not given her the best.","Cheng Zhao, however, remained optimistic. As soon as they returned to Chengming Hall, she ordered the maids to open the storerooms so that she could select some precious tonics and rare fabrics as gifts for Xian Si.","The next afternoon, after finishing the household affairs, Cheng Zhao specifically sent someone to summon Xian Si to Chengming Hall.","Xian Si was still wearing her silver ornaments. She looked delicate and pitiful, yet exceptionally beautiful. There was not the slightest trace of smugness on her face. As before, she respectfully knelt and kowtowed to Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao said, “Rise quickly. There’s no need for such a grand ceremony between the wives and concubines of our household.”","“Madam, the Duke and you have given this servant a new lease on life. I have every right to kowtow to you. It is my good fortune,” Xian Si replied.","Cheng Zhao understood what she meant.","Xian Si was grateful to Zhou Yuanshen for giving her a path forward. At the same time, she was declaring her loyalty to Cheng Zhao and making it clear that she knew how to appreciate kindness.","She would continue to rely on the Duke and Duchess of Chen in the days ahead.","Being an imperial consort was not easy.","She was a dancer with no maternal family to support her. Even if she gave birth to a prince and truly received a title, so what? Anyone in the inner palace could step on her.","Besides, she had received nothing at all.","The emperor had not even rewarded her with any money.","Xian Si was neither anxious nor pleased with herself. She was merely doing what she ought to do.","Just as Cheng Zhao had thought when they first met, Xian Si was very well-behaved.","Xian Si was cautious.","Caution was a good thing. It benefited both her and those who assisted her.","Cheng Zhao stepped forward and helped her up. “Second Concubine, like you, I have a master above me. I am not the head of this household, and I cannot claim to have given you a new lease on life.","“However, I can provide enough food, drink, and necessities for you here. If you lack anything, just come and tell me. In our household, it remains to be seen which of us will prove more capable.”","She deliberately glanced at Xian Si’s belly.","On the surface, it sounded as though she were talking about which of them would be the first to bear the Duke’s eldest son.","Tears quickly gathered in Xian Si’s eyes. “This servant will never betray Madam’s trust. I am a useless person. I only hope I can do my part for the Duke and Madam.”","A maid brought her a brocade stool. After offering another formal salute, Xian Si sat down.","Inside Chengming Hall, the Duke of Chen’s wife and concubine appeared to be perfectly harmonious.","Meanwhile, the Dowager Madame was trying to find a way to meet the emperor.","She knew nothing about what Zhou Yuanshen had done."]},{"number":231,"title":"Chapter 231: The Emperor Refused","paragraphs":["The Dowager Madame had gone to the palace.","She met with the Emperor in the Imperial Study.","There was an unfamiliar Chief Brush Eunuch in the room.","The Dowager Madame smiled and asked, “Is this Eunuch Sheng? Where is Eunuch Feng?”","“Dowager Madame, my master sprained his foot. His Majesty has graciously permitted him to leave the palace and recuperate. I am taking his place on duty. You have an excellent memory, Dowager Madame. I’m deeply honored that you still remember me.” Eunuch Sheng was profoundly grateful.","He appeared genuinely frightened and respectful.","His attitude was exactly the same as that of Consort Wu, who had recently gained the Emperor’s favor.","The Emperor liked the people around him to act this way toward the Dowager Madame.","It proved that he was doing a good job as her “son.”","He needed that sense of accomplishment.","Of course, the Emperor would not punish anyone for failing to abase themselves before her. He simply would not spare them a second glance.","The Dowager Madame’s heart turned cold.","She immediately understood that Eunuch Feng’s injury and departure from the palace were probably Zhou Yuanshen’s doing. And this Eunuch Sheng, like Consort Wu, was one of Zhou Yuanshen’s spies.","After winning the Emperor’s favor, Zhou Yuanshen had quietly planted quite a few people around him.","The Dowager Madame had to be even more careful with her words.","“Winter is so cold. His Majesty used to love date-paste pastries. If we brew tea beside the brazier and serve it with a plate of date-paste pastries made from the fine dates of the northwest, it should be a delightful treat,” the Dowager Madame said with a smile.","The Emperor replied, “Mother-in-law, if I have the time, I’ll visit the Duke’s residence and sit with you for a while.”","Then he added, “It is time I paid a visit there.”","Mentioning the date-paste pastries suddenly reminded the Emperor of jade dumpling cakes.","He said, “Mother-in-law, it has been many years since I last had jade dumpling cakes.”","The Dowager Madame’s heart gave a sudden jolt.","“I haven’t had them in many years either,” she said with a smile. “We can make some.”","She did not mention the jade dumpling cakes Cheng Zhao had presented to her when she had first entered the household.","The Emperor glanced at her.","There were some things he wanted to say, but could not be bothered to.","The Dowager Madame merely smiled.","There was another matter she needed to discuss with the Emperor. She wanted him to visit the Chen Duke’s residence, even if doing so went against propriety.","The Emperor agreed. “There is indeed something I wish to discuss with you.”","The Dowager Madame looked at him in puzzlement. “Your Majesty may speak frankly.”","The Emperor smiled. “We’ll discuss it when we go to the Duke’s residence.”","He gave her no further hint, merely setting a date for their visit to the Chen Duke’s residence.","When the Dowager Madame returned to the Shou’an Court, the tightness in her chest finally eased somewhat.","Although matters had turned out worse than she had imagined, everything was still within her control. Zhou Yuanshen had gained some ground for the moment, but that did not matter. She would slowly teach him the consequences of crossing her.","“You sent for Lady Huan,” the Dowager Madame instructed Nanny Sun.","Nanny Sun acknowledged the order.","Huan Qingtang arrived soon after.","“...We already have some leads. You only need to put your mind at ease,” the Dowager Madame told her kindly.","Huan Qingtang had been slightly puffy these past few days, perhaps because she had been resting in her courtyard and lying down all day.","Even so, her appearance remained striking.","At her age, she was like a fruit just beginning to ripen on a branch—fragrant and enticing, with several years yet before it would reach full maturity and begin to decay.","She could withstand any upheaval and endure wind and rain.","“Grandmother, I certainly won’t disappoint you,” Huan Qingtang said.","As she spoke, her cheeks flushed slightly, but her eyes were resolute.","She was shy, yet filled with yearning.","Her attitude was entirely different from that of the foolish Mu Jiang.","The Dowager Madame was greatly pleased.","“In the future, don’t say that this Duke’s residence belongs to you. Perhaps the entire realm will belong to you as well,” the Dowager Madame said.","Huan Qingtang’s eyes flickered. “I wouldn’t dare harbor such ambitions. I only ask that Grandmother look after me, so that I may have a small place to call my own. Besides, Cheng Shi is trying to drive me to my death.”","She lifted her eyes and looked deeply at the Dowager Madame.","She hoped the Dowager Madame would give her a promise: if they succeeded, Cheng Zhao must not be spared.","It was Cheng Zhao who had ruined her.","“Good and evil will always receive their due. Heaven will not forgive her,” the Dowager Madame said calmly.","Her tone was very light.","It was as though speaking any more forcefully would cause the hatred she felt for Cheng Zhao to spill out.","Given the Dowager Madame’s status, wealth, and age, why would she hate a junior like Cheng Zhao? To do so would be to elevate Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao was not worthy of that.","And yet, Cheng Zhao had somehow made the Dowager Madame regard her with more importance than she should have.","The Dowager Madame hated her bitterly as well.","Was it Huan Qingtang’s resentment toward Cheng Zhao that had infected the Dowager Madame?","The Dowager Madame smiled at Huan Qingtang. “Our grandmother and granddaughter will have good days ahead. Women in this world do not have to depend on men to survive. Without a husband, there are sons; without sons, there are grandsons. In the end, they will all be useful to us.”","Huan Qingtang took the lesson to heart. “I’ll remember that.”","Then she left.","Two days later, in the middle of the afternoon, the Emperor once again left the palace in disguise. He wandered through the bustling streets before arriving at the Chen Duke’s residence.","It was dusk.","The weather was cold, yet the evening clouds glowed brilliantly. They reminded the Emperor of Xian Si.","His heart stirred for no discernible reason.","The Duke’s residence was on full alert. Starting from the main gate, the gatekeepers were no longer members of the Zhou family. The Shou’an Court was also under strict guard. Unrelated people were kept away to prevent any rumors from spreading.","Nanny Sun and Huan Qingtang stood nearby to attend to them.","Huan Qingtang had changed into plain white clothing.","It resembled mourning attire.","Against the white, her face appeared as pale as snow, while her lips looked especially fresh and vivid. She seemed fragile and pitiful, and was exceptionally captivating.","The Emperor was distracted and barely spared her a glance.","The Dowager Madame brought out the jade dumpling cakes made in the household.","The Emperor took one bite, then did not eat any more. He still remembered the jade dumpling cakes of those years ago. He also remembered his paternal aunt—and the proud cousin in her household who had never once looked him in the eye.","What was her name again?","He remembered only her title: Zhaoyang.","The daughter of a Grand Princess was not ordinarily entitled to be named a commandery princess. She could only be made a county princess, unless the Emperor issued a special decree granting her the higher title.","Commandery Princess Zhaoyang had been deeply favored by the Emperor, and the late Emperor had doted on her especially.","The Emperor looked toward the Dowager Madame. “Mother-in-law, I still want a Crown Prince born of the Chen Duke’s residence.”","Huan Qingtang, standing to one side, felt her heart leap.","Even though the Dowager Madame had already told her, even though she had been mentally prepared, hearing the words still left her deeply shocked.","How could anyone harbor such an unfathomable notion?","What was the source of his obsession?","“It is Ah Jiang who has failed to deliver,” the Dowager Madame sighed.","Then she glanced at Huan Qingtang. “However...”","The Emperor also looked at Huan Qingtang.","His brows drew together slightly.","The Dowager Madame noticed his expression, and her heart sank.","“Mother-in-law, Xian Si is still living in the Yujin Court? From now on, have the Duchess treat her well. Yuanshen knows my intentions,” the Emperor said.","The Dowager Madame stared at him in astonishment.","Huan Qingtang abruptly raised her head, forgetting all about propriety as she looked at the Emperor.","Then she looked toward the Dowager Madame.","She was unwilling to accept this.","Why had an opportunity that was right before her eyes been allowed to slip away?","The Dowager Madame gave the slightest shake of her head.","Huan Qingtang recalled what the Dowager Madame had told her about the reason Mu Jiang had been beaten with the rod. She desperately wanted to do something, yet feared that acting rashly would only make matters worse.","Her face went deathly pale.","The Emperor noticed and spoke displeasedly. “You may withdraw. Nanny Sun’s presence is sufficient.”","He added, “You’re so clumsy. If you were in the palace, a servant like you would be beaten to death.”","Huan Qingtang hurriedly acknowledged his command and withdrew in disarray.","The Dowager Madame’s heart sank into an abyss.","Xian Si—the dancer?","The Emperor had not spoken this way before. He had wanted the Dowager Madame to raise and educate the Crown Prince for him. But what about now?","Did he think that notion was completely groundless? Had he been unable to break his word, and therefore decided that someone from Zhou Yuanshen’s side would do instead?","The Emperor remained seated only a short while before leaving.","Peace and quiet returned to the Duke’s residence.","That night, a knock sounded at the door of Cheng Zhao’s inner chamber. Zhou Yuanshen sat up abruptly, startling Cheng Zhao awake as well."]},{"number":232,"title":"Chapter 232: Blood Vomiting","paragraphs":["A nanny on duty at the second gate quietly made her way to Chengming Hall.","Qiubai was on duty that night.","When Qiubai received the news, she knocked on the inner chamber door despite the late hour.","“...The Dowager Madame vomited blood and fainted. Nanny Sun has sent someone to fetch the imperial physician, but he hasn’t arrived yet,” Qiubai reported.","Zhou Yuanshen swiftly changed clothes.","After a quick wash, Cheng Zhao combed his hair. He was just about to leave when he took Cheng Zhao’s hand.","“You should rest. I’ll go take a look.”","“I’m coming too!”","Zhou Yuanshen tightened his grip slightly. “Wait here for now. If someone happens to be there, you may become the target of their anger.”","Cheng Zhao understood that he was referring to the Emperor.","He was afraid the Emperor might come.","Cheng Zhao clasped his hand in return, squeezing hard. “Yuanshen, be careful!”","Zhou Yuanshen froze for a moment.","Then, instead, he smiled with relief.","It was a rare smile, and it was remarkably charming. He nodded. “Don’t worry.”","He turned and left.","How could Cheng Zhao sleep now? She changed clothes and sat on the heated brick platform by the window.","The few trusted servants who had woken up gathered around her and spoke in low voices.","“How could the Dowager Madame have vomited blood out of nowhere?” Suyue asked. “Could she have fallen ill?”","Though the Dowager Madame had seemed low in spirits lately, there had been no word that she was seriously ill.","Cheng Zhao believed she had been angered into it.","It had to be because of Xian Si. The Dowager Madame must have learned what had happened.","The Dowager Madame had probably intended to offer Huan Qingtang to the Emperor. But the plan had evidently failed, with no possibility of salvaging it.","Her schemes had come to nothing. In a fit of rage, the Dowager Madame had suffered an attack of anger, vomited blood, and fainted.","“Young Madam, shall I go to Shou’an Courtyard and take a look?” Qiubai asked. “I can hide in a tree nearby without anyone noticing.”","“No!” Cheng Zhao said sharply.","Qiubai was highly skilled and could easily gather information.","But Cheng Zhao was afraid the Emperor might come.","If he did, the highly trained imperial guards accompanying him would mistake Qiubai for an assassin. They would kill her on the spot, and no one would be able to protect her.","In a hushed voice, Cheng Zhao told her trusted servants what she believed had happened.","Qiubai broke out in a cold sweat. “This servant would never act rashly. Please rest assured.”","Cheng Zhao could only wait.","She waited until dawn, when Zhou Yuanshen finally returned.","Cheng Zhao had fallen asleep, slumped against the heated brick platform by the window.","Nanny Li hurriedly instructed a maid to brew some strong tea and brought it over. She asked solicitously, “Lord Duke, are you hungry?”","“Has Young Madam had breakfast?” he asked.","“Not yet,” Nanny Li replied. “She only just fell asleep. She was awake the entire night.”","“Don’t disturb her,” Zhou Yuanshen said. “Bring out my court robes. I’m leaving. Tell Young Madam not to go to Shou’an Courtyard and not to ask too many questions.”","Nanny Li acknowledged the order.","Zhou Yuanshen drained the strong tea in one gulp, changed clothes, and left.","Cheng Zhao dozed for a while. When she woke, she learned that Zhou Yuanshen had returned and already gone out again.","She was annoyed with herself. “You should have woken me.”","She wanted to know how the Dowager Madame was doing.","“Lord Duke looked perfectly well and not tired at all,” Nanny Li said. “I assume everything is ‘calm and peaceful.’”","Cheng Zhao cleared her head. “You’re right.”","She pulled herself together and went about her usual household duties.","None of the stewards mentioned the Dowager Madame vomiting blood or the physician being summoned the night before. The news must have been sealed off. Even the gatekeeper, the only steward who knew what had happened, did not let a single word slip.","Zhou Yuanshen returned around noon.","“...The imperial physician said it was nothing serious, merely coughing up blood due to an adverse flow of qi. She needs to rest quietly,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","“Does the Emperor know?”","“He didn’t come again last night. However, I went to the Imperial Study to report to him. I told him that Grandmother probably did not wish to see him for the time being,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao was horrified. “What if he finds out?”","“I said it was only my speculation. If Your Majesty didn’t believe me, he could come to the Duke’s residence again,” Zhou Yuanshen replied. “The Emperor knew the reason. He thought Grandmother was angry with him.","“He was somewhat displeased as well. He said that he had always shown the Dowager Madame the utmost respect and had never forgotten their former affection. If the Dowager Madame couldn’t even make allowances for him in such a small matter, then, in the end, who was the sovereign and who was the subject?”","Cheng Zhao’s eyes widened slightly.","In such a short time, two people who had been “as close as mother and son” had developed a distinction between “sovereign and subject.”","Indeed, people could not allow too many others—or too many interests—to come between them. Once each person took a different position, it became difficult to return to the way things had been.","This also reminded Cheng Zhao that if she wanted a loving relationship with her husband, no third person could be allowed to act as a messenger between them.","Everything had to be explained face-to-face.","She also needed to determine whether someone else’s words carried more weight in their lives than her own.","The Emperor had acted this way because of Consort Wu.","Consort Wu had won the Emperor’s heart. She had not replaced the Empress or any of his other favored consorts; she had replaced the Dowager Madame instead.","Zhou Yuanshen had actually managed to accomplish this. He had found the key to the Dowager Madame’s close relationship with the Emperor and deliberately disrupted it, inserting Consort Wu into the gap.","No one was irreplaceable.","“...What did Grandmother say? Do we need to go attend to her?” Cheng Zhao asked.","“Grandmother doesn’t want anyone else to know that she’s ill,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","When she had been pretending to be sick, she had made sure the entire household knew. Now that she was truly ill, she wanted to keep it secret, afraid that someone might take advantage of her weakness to cause trouble.","Cheng Zhao said no more.","Before long, it was the twenty-fifth day of the tenth month. The clouds were somewhat heavy early that morning, and the sky was gloomy, but the sun emerged before midmorning.","Jin’an Temple was crowded with worshippers.","In a meditation room in the rear courtyard, Cheng Zhao and Second Madam encountered Mrs. Song and her daughters.","Miss Song was tall and beautiful, with a pair of unusually composed eyes. Yet whenever she looked at someone, her gaze was exceptionally gentle.","She was like a celestial maiden who had descended into the mortal world and gathered dust all over herself as she tumbled down—yet, because of it, she had acquired a touch of human warmth and compassion.","Only...","“She looks very kind,” Second Madam remarked on the way back.","Cheng Zhao agreed with her mother-in-law. “Yes.”","“Your maternal uncle has certainly had good luck,” Second Madam said with a smile.","“Vice Minister Song has as well,” Cheng Zhao replied.","Praising someone else while complimenting her own family too—Second Madam smiled knowingly.","Cheng Zhao’s smile faded slightly. She had caught sight of Miss Song’s hand earlier, and it had reminded her of someone she knew.","Perhaps she was simply overthinking it.","When they were descending the mountain, Fan Xiao unexpectedly arrived. After exchanging a few words with them, he went to see the Song women.","To avoid impropriety, Third Miss Song boarded the carriage first while Fan Xiao chatted with Mrs. Song.","Afterward, he came over to speak with Cheng Zhao and Second Madam.","“Has Yuanshen been very busy lately?” Fan Xiao even asked Cheng Zhao.","“Many matters have arisen at court. He has always been busy,” Cheng Zhao replied.","He held several official posts.","“...It’s nothing urgent. I’ll look for him to share a drink another day,” Fan Xiao said with a smile.","“When would he have time to drink with you?” Second Madam said. “And you—your wedding is just around the corner, yet you still have time to go drinking?”","Fan Xiao was speechless.","On the way home, Cheng Zhao kept thinking about Fan Xiao’s expression just then.","He seemed to have something to say, yet also seemed unsure how to begin.","That evening, when she saw Zhou Yuanshen, Cheng Zhao told him everything that had happened, including Fan Xiao’s behavior.","Zhou Yuanshen pondered briefly. “I’ll pay a visit to the Pillar-State Grand General’s residence. You don’t need to wait for me. I’ll sleep in the outer study.”","Guessing that Cheng Zhao was curious, he added, “I’ll come in early tomorrow and tell you what he said.”","Cheng Zhao was speechless.","It wasn’t as though she was that curious.","Zhou Yuanshen left.","At that very moment, Fan Xiao had already been talking with his mother for nearly an hour."]},{"number":233,"title":"Chapter 233: Brother and Sister","paragraphs":["Old Madam Fan had witnessed two dynasties and was extremely well - informed.","Fan Xiao's restaurant was a place where news spread quickly, and he had many friends from all walks of life.","The news that the Prince of Andong had secretly allied with the Huan family and met with Huan Qingtang, who had returned to her natal family, reached Fan Xiao's ears.","This matter was carried out extremely secretly.","“... Shopkeeper Wu is very grateful to me for saving his daughter from the brothel back then, and he told me about this. Master Qingshan only lets Shopkeeper Wu help sell his pills.","Just after my attendant found out that the Prince of Andong had secretly gone to the Huan family, Shopkeeper Wu contacted me. He said that someone had bought one of Master Qingshan's pills, which was eventually delivered to the trusted aide of the Prince of Andong.” Fan Xiao said.","Old Madam Fan asked, “What kind of pill is it?”","Old Madam Fan was aware of all of Fan Xiao's friends.","Shopkeeper Wu ran a pharmacy. His real surname was “Wu”. As for how he got such a nickname, it was related to his heavy drinking in his early years.","He had reformed and was now taking care of the pharmacy for the divine physician, Master Qingshan.","Master Qingshan didn't like to deal with worldly affairs. If someone wanted him to save a life, they had to go through Shopkeeper Wu. A few years ago, Shopkeeper Wu's daughter had gone missing during the Lantern Festival. It was done by one of Fan Xiao's old enemies from his days in the martial arts world.","Fan Xiao happened to have some connections and managed to rescue the girl. Shopkeeper Wu was very grateful to him.","If Master Qingshan's pills were sold one by one, they were almost sky - high in price, no less than a hundred taels of gold.","The information about the sellers was kept strictly confidential by Shopkeeper Wu and Master Qingshan. Shopkeeper Wu was willing to break the rule and tell Fan Xiao only to repay the favor of saving his daughter, fearing that Fan Xiao might make more excessive demands in the future.","“What kind of pill is this?” Old Madam Fan asked again.","“The 'Resurrection Pill',” Fan Xiao replied.","“Explain,” Old Madam Fan said.","“After taking it, the person will fall into a deep sleep, appearing to be alive. In fact, they are already dead. After a month, there will be corpse spots, and only then will people notice,” Fan Xiao explained.","“Do you suspect that he wants to target someone in the Zhou family? The Dowager Madame?” Old Madam Fan asked.","Fan Xiao nodded.","This kind of poison was hard to detect at first, and people would just think the old lady was in a coma.","It was quite normal for elderly people to be sleepy. If it was delayed for ten days or half a month, it would be too late by the time something was noticed.","After some more time, the person would be completely dead.","In the eyes of the court officials, Zhou Yuanshen was in the emperor's good graces largely because of the Dowager Madame.","The emperor's rewards to the Duke of Chen's mansion always went to the Dowager Madame first.","Without the Dowager Madame, the relationship between Zhou Yuanshen and the emperor would not be as close. The Prince of Andong wanted to be the top among the officials, so he must push Zhou Yuanshen aside.","“As long as Ah Shen falls out of the emperor's favor, after the emperor's death, the Prince of Andong will be the next Prince An, and the young emperor will be his puppet,” Fan Xiao said.","“Ah Shen's being in the emperor's favor has little to do with the Dowager Madame,” Old Madam Fan said.","“We know this, but outsiders may not,” Fan Xiao replied.","Fan Xiao had inferred all this from the slightest clues.","“If something happens to the Dowager Madame... for Ah Shen, it would mean getting rid of a constraint,” Old Madam Fan mused for a while and then said.","“I didn't tell Ah Shen because of this concern. Only our close relatives know how much suffering Ah Shen has endured at the hands of the Dowager Madame.","The Dowager Madame is in her sixties and could live another twenty years. The emperor will also live for a long time. Ah Shen is having a hard time,” Fan Xiao said.","If they told Zhou Yuanshen about the Prince of Andong's sinister plot, would Zhou Yuanshen try to stop it or not?","After all, the Dowager Madame was his grandmother.","Old Madam Fan pondered for a long time.","The room became extremely quiet, with only the whistling of the night wind outside the window.","Fan Xiao looked at his mother, seeking a bit of support.","\"Let you be the bad guy. You're his uncle, so bear the responsibility for this matter. If Ah Shen blames you in the future, just take it,\" Old Madam Fan said after a long while.","Fan Xiao's hesitant look in his eyes gradually turned into determination. \"Then I won't tell Ah Shen. I'll just say that the Prince of Andong is in contact with the Huan family and won't mention the matter about the medicine.\"","Old Madam Fan nodded.","Just as they finished speaking, a maid standing in the courtyard announced loudly, \"The Duke of Chen has arrived.\"","Fan Xiao stood up.","Sure enough, he told Zhou Yuanshen what he had learned about the Prince of Andong's contact with the Huan family and Huan Qingtang's meeting with him during her visit back to her natal family.","Zhou Yuanshen frowned tightly upon hearing this.","\"Is there anything else you want to tell me?\" he asked.","Fan Xiao replied, \"What do you want to hear?\"","\"About the Prince of Andong.\"","\"He's making good progress in bribing officials in thirty prefectures of seven northern regions. The regions in the north are far away and the officials there are not very wealthy. Money is quite persuasive,\" Fan Xiao said.","Zhou Yuanshen frowned even more deeply.","\"Don't be angry. It's not any better in the capital either. With an often - crazy emperor on the throne, it's no wonder the official governance is in a mess,\" Fan Xiao added.","Zhou Yuanshen didn't say anything more.","\"Time is getting late. I'll go back first,\" he said. \"Keep an eye on the Prince of Andong's contact with the Huan family.\"","\"Sure, you can rest assured and leave it to me,\" Fan Xiao said with a smile.","Then he added, \"Your duchess is very perceptive. She even knew I had something to say.\"","The frown on Zhou Yuanshen's forehead eased a bit. \"She's always like this. She has great natural talent.\"","Fan Xiao: \"...\"","Zhou Yuanshen had planned to have a in - depth chat with Fan Xiao, but unexpectedly, Fan Xiao wrapped up the conversation in just a few words. It was still early when he got back. Instead of staying in the outer study, he went straight back to the Chengming Hall.","He told Cheng Zhao about this matter.","Cheng Zhao was puzzled. \"Why did Uncle Fan seem to hold back? If it was just about the Prince of Andong's contact with Sister - in - law, he could have just told me directly and asked me to remind you.\"","As if thinking of something, her expression changed slightly. \"Is my fourth brother involved? He's always so thoughtless.\"","Zhou Yuanshen replied, \"Uncle Fan didn't mention it. He indeed had something unsaid. He must have his reasons.\"","\"You're right. Your uncle won't do you any harm,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"I need to go back to my natal family and ask Cheng Chao. If that guy has caused trouble for me, I'll tear him apart. He's always been unable to tell right from wrong and insists on being friends with Helian Xuan!\"","She continued, \"When we were kids, he always brought Helian Xuan to provoke me. I really should have given them a good thrashing back then.\"","Zhou Yuanshen couldn't help but smile.","He put his arms around Cheng Zhao. \"You're so funny.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","They were having a serious conversation, and suddenly he hugged her and gave such an off - the - mark compliment. What was wrong with him?","Could it be that just because Cheng Chao was mentioned, that kind of foolishness had passed on to Zhou Yuanshen through the conversation?","She glared at him unhappily.","This glare had no deterrent effect at all, but her fluttering eyes were really charming. With great self - restraint, Zhou Yuanshen gently kissed her lips.","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","What strange men!","From Cheng Chao to Zhou Yuanshen, Cheng Zhao simply couldn't understand what they were thinking at certain moments. On the contrary, Zhou Yuanqi was better. His thoughts were as transparent as day, and Cheng Zhao liked to play with him.","The Dowager Madame fell ill. The Shou'an Courtyard started to keep the news under wraps. Except for Huan Qingtang who was allowed to attend to her, no one else knew about the Dowager Madame's condition.","Cheng Zhao went back to the Cheng family.","She asked Cheng Chao what he and Helian Xuan had been up to recently.","\"I haven't seen him for quite some time,\" Cheng Chao said. \"It's been at least two or three months.\"","He added, \"His ambition is growing bigger and bigger. If I'm not careful, he might drag me and the Cheng family into trouble. It's really dangerous. So I've deliberately kept my distance from him. The court situation has been extremely unstable recently, and he's gone crazy.\"","Cheng Zhao almost started chanting Buddhist scriptures and sighed with emotion, \"You've finally shown a bit of sense.\"","\"You should also use your head. Do you have a brain as small as an almond? How could you suspect that I'd make a mistake? Even a pig wouldn't be that stupid,\" Cheng Chao said disdainfully.","Cheng Zhao almost got into a fight with him.","It was the senior maid beside their mother who came over and called the siblings to have a meal, so they temporarily made peace and stopped arguing."]},{"number":234,"title":"Chapter 234: Huan Qingtang Must Seize the Opportunity","paragraphs":["Father was at home.","When he saw Cheng Zhao, Father gave a slight nod. “Have you come home for something?”","Cheng Zhao answered in a stiff, proper manner, “I wanted to speak with Fourth Brother.”","Father turned his gaze to Cheng Chao.","Cheng Chao was usually cheeky in front of Cheng Zhao, but the moment he saw Father, he became tense. His features settled into a dignified, refined expression, and even his speech grew gentle and unhurried.","“Zhaozhao was asking about Helian Xuan.”","“...The Prince of Andong has been highly favored of late. His influence is at its height,” Father said.","Cheng Chao replied, “I’m not coveting his overwhelming power and influence. As long as his reputation remains untarnished, the Cheng clan of Wu Commandery will remain invincible. That isn’t something money or power alone can accomplish.”","Father looked pleased, and his expression relaxed somewhat. “Very good. You’ve remembered your grandfather’s teachings.”","Cheng Chao secretly breathed a sigh of relief. His back was no longer quite so rigid.","Cheng Zhao inwardly cursed him for being so spineless. He was a grown man who dared to act recklessly behind Father’s back, yet in Father’s presence, even his calves cramped with fear.","Just as she was thinking this, Father turned his gaze toward her, and her own back instantly stiffened.","“I certainly won’t associate with Helian Xuan either. He’s bullied me since we were children, and I haven’t gotten my revenge yet. He’s meddling in the affairs of the Chen State Duke’s household and secretly dealing with the Huan family, so I came to warn Fourth Brother,” Cheng Zhao said.","Father’s brows drew together slightly.","“Fourth Brother has his own judgment. A few words from him actually put my mind at ease, so I’ve let go of my needless worries,” Cheng Zhao added.","Father’s brows relaxed somewhat. “Siblings must not harbor suspicions of one another. If there’s something to say, make it clear.”","Cheng Zhao and Cheng Chao both agreed.","After dinner, Cheng Zhao returned to the Chen State Duke’s residence, with Cheng Chao seeing her off.","The siblings mocked each other, calling one another cowards.","“What are you afraid of? You’re already married. Can he still punish you?”","“You’re the one who’ll take my punishment for me. I’m helping you avoid disaster, and you still don’t appreciate it?” Cheng Zhao said.","Cheng Chao was speechless.","He should never have shown her any kindness. Without even seeing Cheng Zhao to her carriage, Cheng Chao flung his sleeve and turned back inside.","By the time Cheng Zhao returned to the Chen State Duke’s residence, the first watch had already begun.","Two large lanterns hung at the entrance, bathing the vermilion steps in a wash of red light. Cheng Zhao had just stepped down from her carriage when another carriage stopped behind her.","She turned around and saw Huan Qingtang.","“Elder Sister-in-law,” Cheng Zhao called out first, leaving Huan Qingtang no opportunity to find fault with her.","Even if the two of them came to blows, as long as Huan Qingtang remained a member of the Zhou family for even one day, Cheng Zhao would still address her as sister-in-law.","Huan Qingtang’s complexion was not very good.","She seemed to want to smile, but failed. She merely inclined her head slightly. “Younger sister-in-law.”","“Elder Sister-in-law, why have you returned so late? Where have you been?” Cheng Zhao asked.","Huan Qingtang replied, “Grandmother has been unwell, so I went to Jin’an Temple to pray for her. The talisman for Grandmother had to be blessed with sutra recitations, which is why I was delayed.”","Cheng Zhao was puzzled. “At this hour? The city gates have been closed for ages.”","Huan Qingtang panicked for a moment.","It was not especially obvious, but she tried desperately to suppress it. “I returned while it was still early. I saw some shops while passing through the streets and bought some pastries, which is why I was late.”","Cheng Zhao glanced at the coachman.","He seemed to be one of Huan Qingtang’s personal servants, not a member of the Zhou family.","Huan Qingtang’s senior maid was with her as well. That maid was usually sharp-tongued and eloquent, but at this moment she said nothing, standing quietly to the side with her eyes lowered.","Cheng Zhao did not say anything more.","The two sisters-in-law returned to their respective courtyards.","After sitting down, Huan Qingtang fell silent, staring blankly into space.","“Miss.” Her senior maid no longer called her Young Madam. In private, she had reverted to addressing her as Miss.","Huan Qingtang drew a deep breath.","“Have you still not made up your mind?” the maid asked. “The medicine the Prince of Andong gave you can make the Grand Dowager Lady sleep for half a month. Once she wakes, all four of her limbs will be immobile.”","Huan Qingtang said nothing.","The maid asked, “What are you worried about?”","If the Grand Dowager Lady were rendered unconscious and then left paralyzed in bed, like a stroke victim who could barely speak and could not move, would she not have to rely on Huan Qingtang for everything?","Then Huan Qingtang’s good days would truly begin.","She would have the Grand Dowager Lady in her grasp.","Huan Qingtang had made all her preparations, but the Emperor had refused her. Not only had the Grand Dowager Lady suffered a tremendous blow, so had Huan Qingtang.","The Grand Dowager Lady had been struck even harder. She knew perfectly well that Zhou Yuanshen had succeeded, and that her own power had become extremely weak.","“If Grandmother really becomes paralyzed, unable to move or speak even after regaining consciousness, that would naturally benefit me greatly,” Huan Qingtang said.","The maid replied, “When will you give it to her, then? During this trip to pray, the abbot gave you talisman paper. You can mix the medicine into the talisman water and feed it to the Grand Dowager Lady. She believes in blessed water.”","“No. I just...” Huan Qingtang fell silent for a long while before looking up at her trusted confidante. “I just feel that the Prince of Andong cannot be trusted.”","He had appeared out of nowhere.","Previously, he had barely had any dealings with the Huan family.","Her father had been won over by him and placed all his trust in him, even hoping to use him to rise to great heights in the future.","Huan Qingtang wondered why Helian Xuan wanted to help her. Was it merely because of her father?","Her father did not possess that kind of ability.","If Helian Xuan was not helping her, but instead trying to suppress Zhou Yuanshen, did he want the Grand Dowager Lady dead—or merely paralyzed and unable to move?","Huan Qingtang believed it was the former.","The former would resolve everything once and for all.","Using Huan Qingtang’s hand to kill the Grand Dowager Lady would sever Zhou Yuanshen’s old relationship with the Emperor and drive Zhou Yuanshen out of the picture.","That was Huan Qingtang’s own speculation.","“...Of course, paralyzing the Grand Dowager Lady would also benefit Helian Xuan. They say that there are no truly filial sons once a parent has been bedridden for a long time. When the Emperor thinks of the Grand Dowager Lady in that state, yet finds himself powerless to help, he might even vent his anger on Zhou Yuanshen,” Huan Qingtang added.","Her senior maid listened as she repeatedly analyzed the matter, growing increasingly anxious. “Miss, you must seize this opportunity.","“You said it yourself—the Prince of Andong has no deep ties with the Huan family. He won’t help you again and again. Have you forgotten how Cheng Zhao obtained her title as an Imperial Mandate Lady?”","The moment she saw even the slightest sign of an opportunity, Cheng Zhao had seized it at once.","She had never wavered or agonized over gains and losses when faced with an opportunity.","Those words struck Huan Qingtang, and all the calm and reason in her mind vanished.","If the Grand Dowager Lady died, Huan Qingtang would indeed be completely finished. But if Helian Xuan was telling the truth and the Grand Dowager Lady would only be paralyzed, then Huan Qingtang would possess a guarantee of survival from that point onward.","Had she not endured so many grievances for the sake of this very moment?","“I’ll give the medicine to the Grand Dowager Lady tomorrow morning. You’ll distract Nanny Sun when the time comes,” Huan Qingtang said.","The two of them discussed the matter at length: how to lure Nanny Sun away, and how to give the medicine to the Grand Dowager Lady without arousing suspicion.","They talked for quite some time.","Cheng Zhao returned to Chengming Hall, while Zhou Yuanshen went to the Jiangyun Court.","She took a small covered cart over there as well.","Zhou Yuanqi was there too. The family of four was chatting together.","“...My Fourth Brother said he would be careful,” Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, “Your Fourth Brother isn’t a foolish man. You can rest easy.”","The Second Madam asked what had happened.","Cheng Zhao told her everything.","She also mentioned encountering Huan Qingtang at the entrance.","“...Since she’s been associating with Helian Xuan, could she be plotting against our family?” Cheng Zhao asked. “Or perhaps against Grandmother?”","“Has she gone mad? If anything happened to your grandmother, she’d become a helpless duckweed, with nothing left to her. She would never dare harm your grandmother,” the Second Madam said.","The Second Master added, “She probably wouldn’t go that far. If it became known that Helian Xuan had been dealing with her in secret, he wouldn’t be able to escape responsibility either.”","Zhou Yuanqi said, “But she might still take the risk out of desperation. We should send more people to guard Grandmother.”","Zhou Yuanshen said, “We can’t interfere in Shou’an Court. If anything goes wrong, we won’t be able to answer to His Majesty. By then, we could be accused of ‘stealing under our watch,’ and they might say we were the ones who harmed Grandmother. We’d never be able to explain ourselves.”","“Then what do we do?”","“I can think of only one way,” Zhou Yuanshen said."]},{"number":235,"title":"Chapter 235: The Bride's Flaw","paragraphs":["“What way?”","Zhou Yuanqi was extremely curious and immediately asked his older brother.","“If you want to know, figure it out yourself,” Zhou Yuanshen said. “A learned scholar like you ought to be clever enough to guess.”","Zhou Yuanqi: “...”","He turned to Cheng Zhao. “You don’t want to know?”","“Lord Duke will tell me,” Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","He’s only keeping it from you.","Zhou Yuanqi’s cheeks puffed up in anger, and Cheng Zhao could not help laughing.","Second Madam laughed along with them. It was rare for her to be in such a relaxed mood.","Yet she could also sense that a storm was brewing in the household, much like the days before the fire at Nonghua Court.","After living in one place for a long time, even the courtyards seemed to acquire souls of their own. Whenever trouble was about to break out, they gave off an uneasy warning.","In the past, Second Madam had deliberately ignored such feelings, attributing them to bad weather or shortness of breath.","They chatted a little longer, with Zhou Yuanshen and Cheng Zhao teasing Zhou Yuanqi. It was getting late, so the young couple returned to Chengming Hall.","“Your Young Uncle is hiding something from you,” Cheng Zhao said again.","She could not help feeling somewhat worried. “Why won’t he simply tell us? If he did, we could think of a solution together.”","“Once it’s spoken aloud, the matter will become even more troublesome,” Zhou Yuanshen said. “I’m also keeping something from him.”","“What is it?”","Zhou Yuanshen gently stroked her hair. “It has nothing to do with the Chen State Duke’s residence.”","After a long silence, he said, “It’s an old matter concerning the Fan family. It was also something that weighed on Grandfather’s mind until the moment he died.”","“If he couldn’t let it go even on his deathbed, then it must be serious,” Cheng Zhao said. “You’re hiding something this important from him? And you haven’t told the Fan family?”","“Mm.”","That was why Zhou Yuanshen could understand Fan Xiao’s difficulties.","Cheng Zhao sighed.","She was not the sort of person who liked to force others, so she said, “You arrogant men always think you’re acting for the sake of your loved ones, so you shoulder everything yourselves. May you all have good fortune, and may everything remain within your control.”","Zhou Yuanshen pulled her into his arms. “With you by my side, I’m sure to have my wish.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","When had she acquired such miraculous powers?","Her life continued as usual, moving steadily forward.","Winter in Shengjing was clear and bright. The brighter the sky, however, the more bitter the cold. The wind cut like knives.","The Dowager Madame’s Shou’an Court was very quiet.","Nanny Sun personally oversaw every medical consultation and every dose of medicine, taking care over everything.","At the beginning of the eleventh month, a heavy snow fell.","This snowfall was much heavier than the first.","The gatehouse steward was a man named Sun Cheng’an. He was the son of one of the Dowager Madame’s personal attendants and enjoyed her deep trust. Anyone who could work at the gatehouse was a trusted confidant.","Cheng Zhao was extremely wary of him. On the surface, however, she deliberately tried to win him over and treated him with great courtesy.","“...Nanny Sun sent someone to invite Master Qingshan, and she also sent for Master Zhao, the retired former chief physician of the Imperial Medical Academy,” Sun Cheng’an reported.","“Master Qingshan? He rarely comes out to see patients. And didn’t Master Zhao return to his native town? He retired several years ago,” Cheng Zhao said.","“Yes. Both of them are difficult to summon. Most likely, they won’t come unless Lord Duke goes personally. Nanny Sun is even planning to enter the palace and ask for an audience with His Majesty,” Manager Sun said.","Cheng Zhao appeared astonished. “Is Grandmother seriously ill?”","“This servant doesn’t know. Nanny Sun hasn’t told anyone anything about Shou’an Court. Aside from her, probably only the chief steward knows,” Manager Sun replied.","Cheng Zhao rose to her feet, looking worried and somewhat helpless. “What are we to do? I’ll send someone to find Lord Duke.”","“Madam, Nanny Sun forbade me from telling you or Lord Duke. If you fail to keep this secret, Nanny Sun will never forgive me,” Sun Cheng’an said.","Cheng Zhao forced herself to calm down, though she still looked rather flustered. “Then I won’t say anything. Grandmother has a noble destiny. Nothing will happen to her.”","And indeed, she did nothing.","Zhou Yuanshen returned rather late that day.","He said to Cheng Zhao, “Nanny Sun went to the palace gates and tried to request an audience with the Emperor. The guards at the entrance ignored her. I heard it from some of the guards on duty.”","He had bought off quite a few informants within the inner court.","The government was in complete disarray, and the inner court was equally corrupt and rotten.","With a murderous, deranged emperor on the throne, the entire imperial court was constantly on the verge of collapse.","Nanny Sun was merely a servant. She had no right to request an audience with the Emperor.","Having served the Dowager Madame for so many years, her ambitions had apparently grown to such a degree that she thought she could meet the Emperor simply by presenting herself.","In the end, she could not even get through the palace gates.","“Something serious must have happened to Grandmother,” Cheng Zhao said.","She looked at Zhou Yuanshen, her voice very soft. “Should we just force our way into Shou’an Court? Even if the Emperor asks about it, we can say we were acting out of filial devotion.”","Zhou Yuanshen fell silent for a moment. “That would be inappropriate.”","“Are we simply going to wait?”","“We can afford to wait. Others cannot. Marquis Qingyuan will be coming soon,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Marquis Qingyuan was the Dowager Madame’s nephew, a member of her maternal family.","If Nanny Sun failed to summon a divine physician and could not see the Emperor, she would certainly seek out Marquis Qingyuan and ask him to support the Dowager Madame.","Only after the loyal servant and the maternal relatives had each performed their part would it be time for the children and grandchildren to speak. In the Dowager Madame’s heart, the Sun family mattered far more than the Zhou family.","“Yuanshen, if...”","Zhou Yuanshen clasped her hand tightly. “Don’t be afraid.”","“All right.” A flicker passed through Cheng Zhao’s eyes, her emotions rising before she forced them back down.","The husband and wife sat in silence. Neither spoke again. Countless thoughts raced through their minds, yet not a single one could be voiced.","“We won’t go to Jiangyun Court tonight. Suyue, go tell Mother,” Cheng Zhao said.","Suyue acknowledged the order.","The couple had dinner in Chengming Hall.","Zhou Yuanshen still had some business to attend to, so he went to the outer study for a while. Cheng Zhao sat beneath the lamplight and tried to look through the account books. Unable to settle her mind, she picked up her needlework instead.","Snow had piled up along the corners of the courtyard walls. Only the paths had been cleared for walking. The reflected snowlight shone against the windows, making it seem as though there were still daylight outside.","It was colder now.","The floor heating kept the room warm, so Cheng Zhao wore only a light padded jacket.","She embroidered a sachet while waiting for Zhou Yuanshen to return.","He came back after being gone for more than half an hour.","The inner chamber of Chengming Hall was too large, and even the floor heating was not enough to keep it warm at night. The couple had already moved their bed into the heated alcove.","With the folding doors shut, the alcove was as warm as spring, almost like a larger bed.","Neither Cheng Zhao nor Zhou Yuanshen could sleep. They exchanged a few idle remarks. The things they truly wanted to say were difficult to voice directly, so their conversation wandered from one unrelated topic to another.","A few days later, the snow began to melt, and the cold grew even harsher. It was cold enough to split the skin, and in the mornings and evenings people could barely stretch out their hands when going outside.","Marquis Qingyuan did indeed visit the Chen State Duke’s residence.","The gatehouse steward told Cheng Zhao that Nanny Sun had failed to summon Master Qingshan, but had managed to invite Master Zhao, the retired former chief physician of the Imperial Medical Academy.","As for Master Zhao’s diagnosis, no outsider knew anything about it.","Cheng Zhao included.","Cheng Zhao went to Jiangyun Court to have dinner with Second Madam, but did not mention Shou’an Court in the slightest.","Even though the situation there had already been abnormal for several days.","“Mother, when Nanny Li was sorting through the trunks, I found quite a lot of furs.” Cheng Zhao pointed at the chests being carried in by the maids. “I’ll have two thick fur-lined garments made for you and Yuanqi.”","Second Madam smiled. “I don’t need any. Have more made for Yuanqi. It’s cold at the academy.”","She did not think to ask about the Dowager Madame or Huan Qingtang at all. Instead, she cheerfully began discussing her younger brother’s wedding date.","The day of Fan Xiao’s wedding was fast approaching.","Cheng Zhao thought of Third Miss Song, and her heart tightened slightly.","There was no other reason. Third Miss Song was highly skilled with the sword, and her hands were exactly like those of Master Dai, who served beside Cheng Zhao’s third elder sister.","Master Dai’s daughter was also highly skilled with the sword, and her hands looked the same.","Cheng Zhao still remembered how Master Dai had specifically pointed out that the hands of someone who had practiced swordsmanship since childhood were different from those of ordinary people.","Vice Minister Song was a scholar, and the Song family was renowned for its scholarly tradition.","No one had ever mentioned that Third Miss Song was particularly skilled with a sword.","When Third Miss Song met Cheng Zhao and Second Madam, she caught sight of Fan Xiao and avoided him...","Which was only reasonable. An unmarried couple had to keep their distance.","The betrothal was a matter for the elders of both families. The two might not even see each other again until their wedding night; communication between the Fan and Song families was handled by the matchmaker.","Among the women of the Fan family, it seemed that only Second Aunt had seen Third Miss Song once—and even then, she had merely glimpsed her from afar. As her future mother-in-law, the Dowager Madame probably had not met her yet."]},{"number":236,"title":"Chapter 236: The Passing of My Grandmother","paragraphs":["On the surface, the Chen State Duke’s residence had been peaceful these past few days.","Everyone went about their lives as usual.","The Shou’an Court was under lockdown, and most of the servants had no idea what had happened. Huan Qingtang remained behind closed doors, occasionally visiting the Shou’an Court to attend to the sick.","One evening at dinner, Zhou Yuanqi said, “This afternoon, I saw a carriage from Marquis Qingyuan’s residence at the gate.","“The Sun family has sent someone again. I saw them here last time, too. They’ve been coming so frequently. Has something happened to the Sun family, or is there some problem with Grandmother?”","He looked at Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao shook her head. “Although the gatehouse is technically under my authority, Grandmother is the one who actually makes the decisions. I don’t know why Marquis Qingyuan has come, and Grandmother hasn’t ordered the main kitchen to prepare any extra dishes.”","“When something unusual happens, there’s bound to be something sinister behind it,” Zhou Yuanqi said. “I’ll go find out.”","Cheng Zhao asked, “How will you find out?”","“Ask Nanfeng.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","The Second Madam was amused. “You might as well ask your sister-in-law directly.”","Cheng Zhao waved her hand. “This time, I truly don’t know.”","The Second Madam could not be bothered with it. “That old lady is formidable. She can conjure a thousand hands and a thousand eyes all by herself. You’re all still too inexperienced. How could it possibly be your turn to worry about her?”","She then had a maid bring out a newly made garment for Zhou Yuanqi. “This crane-patterned cloak is excellent. The fur lining inside was given by your sister-in-law. Wear it when your maternal uncle gets married.”","She added, “In another five days, it will be a joyous occasion.”","The days passed quickly.","Cheng Zhao calculated that it had already been more than half a month since the Dowager Madame had vomited blood and fallen ill. It had also been more than ten days since Cheng Zhao had last seen Huan Qingtang.","What exactly was Huan Qingtang plotting with Helian Xuan?","They had been preparing for more than ten days. Surely there would be some movement soon?","While Cheng Zhao’s thoughts ran wild, Zhou Yuanshen went to the Imperial Study.","He asked the Emperor to visit the Chen State Duke’s residence.","“...Grandmother is furious and has refused to see me to this day. Nanny Sun has been rushing in and out, and Marquis Qingyuan has come several times. I’m terribly afraid that something might happen to Grandmother.","“When I went to the entrance of the Shou’an Court, Nanny Sun stopped me and refused to let me in. Your Majesty, Grandmother is already so old. Even if she were angry, she could scold or beat me as she pleased, but she cannot keep it all bottled up inside.","“I would like to ask Your Majesty to make a visit and help resolve the misunderstanding between Grandmother and me. Even if I am punished, I will accept it willingly,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","He had run out of options.","The Emperor frowned.","He felt that the Dowager Madame was not merely quarreling with Zhou Yuanshen. She was angry with him.","The Emperor respected and loved the Dowager Madame and had never forgotten what had happened in the past.","But too much time had passed. The past was like a magnificent brocade robe. The years had worn it down, and it could no longer withstand close inspection or being pulled apart.","When left untouched, it still looked as it had from afar. But once examined closely, its colors were no longer bright.","Now, because of Xian Si, the Dowager Madame was “scolding the mulberry while pointing at the locust tree.” She appeared to be losing her temper with Zhou Yuanshen, but in truth, she was angry with the Emperor.","The Emperor felt somewhat displeased.","His mother-in-law should not treat him this way.","She had always favored him, understood him, cared for him, and trusted him.","Why was she no longer willing to indulge him? Just because he had refused her once, she had thrown such a terrible fit. Had she changed?","“It would not be appropriate for Me to go again. There are no walls without cracks. As an imperial censor, you know that better than anyone. The censors merely turn a blind eye and pretend not to see.","“If I go there twice in such a short time, won’t the censors seize the opportunity to denounce us? Go and take a look. Come back and report to Me,” the Emperor said irritably.","Zhou Yuanshen said, “But Grandmother won’t let me in. What should I do?”","“Me will give you an oral decree. You will enter under imperial authority to inquire after her health,” the Emperor said.","Zhou Yuanshen acknowledged the order.","After leaving the palace, Zhou Yuanshen returned home.","The sun was bright that day. The snow from the last snowfall had melted away, and there was an unusual touch of warmth in the air.","Huan Qingtang paced back and forth inside the Cuiyun Court, deeply unsettled. Her chief maid, He’er, had disappeared.","Two days earlier, Huan Qingtang had sent He’er out to return to the Huan family home and meet with the Prince of Andong.","The medicine the Prince of Andong had given her was supposed to make the Dowager Madame unconscious for ten days to half a month. Afterward, she would awaken with all four limbs paralyzed, barely able to say a few words.","But something was wrong with the Dowager Madame.","Not only had she shown no sign of waking, but her breathing had grown weaker over the past few days. Her complexion had become increasingly gray and pale, and there was even a strong stench of decay.","Nanny Sun was in a panic.","Huan Qingtang was panicking as well.","She had wondered whether the Prince of Andong might have intended to kill the Dowager Madame. But her chief maid had repeatedly urged her to make a decision quickly, even bringing up Cheng Zhao’s past as an example.","Whenever Cheng Zhao was mentioned, Huan Qingtang’s mind boiled over, making it impossible for her to remain calm.","Before Cheng Zhao entered the household, Huan Qingtang’s life had been smooth, and her future had seemed bright. All she had to do was follow the path laid out before her. Chengming Hall would belong to her, and so would the Duke’s residence.","Cheng Zhao had changed everything.","She could not afford to lose again.","This was the one time she had acted impulsively and taken a risk, struggling forward just as Cheng Zhao had.","But now, things had gone wrong.","Huan Qingtang had sent her chief maid back to her mother’s family to find a way to contact the Prince of Andong again. Yet the maid had vanished without a trace.","Huan Qingtang had barely slept the previous night.","“Could she have been bought off by the Prince of Andong and become his spy, deliberately misleading me?” Huan Qingtang wondered.","That did not seem likely.","Her chief maid had served at her side since childhood, always accompanying her and never leaving her line of sight. The Prince of Andong could not possibly have reached so far or bought her maid off.","Then had something happened to her?","Huan Qingtang desperately wanted to return to the Huan family home herself, but she could not find a suitable excuse. She was even more afraid that going back at this time would expose her and make her suspicions impossible to dispel.","All she could do was wait.","When she could bear it no longer, she went to the Shou’an Court again. There, she happened to encounter Zhou Yuanshen at the entrance.","Huan Qingtang wore a cloak trimmed with white fox fur. The cold wind had brought a faint flush to her pale face.","“Duke, Grandmother should have retired for the night,” Huan Qingtang said.","Zhou Yuanshen was not alone at the entrance of the Shou’an Court. Two coarse-serving matrons had stopped him and refused to let him enter.","Nanny Sun was just coming out from the inner room.","These past few days, Nanny Sun had visibly withered. Most of her hair had turned white overnight, leaving her looking terribly old.","“Duke, the Dowager Madame does not wish to see you. Please go back,” she said firmly.","Zhou Yuanshen looked at her quietly. “I bear an oral decree from the Emperor. I have come under imperial orders to inquire after her health. If you refuse to let me enter, you will be executed without exception.”","His voice was not loud, and his speech was unhurried.","Those words fell upon Nanny Sun’s ears like a thunderclap.","Her haggard face took on an even more venomous expression. “How dare you fabricate an imperial decree?”","“I would not dare. I will not risk my life and the entire Zhou family’s for an argument with Grandmother,” Zhou Yuanshen said. “If you refuse to let me in, then so be it. Once Grandmother wakes, she may explain matters to the Emperor herself.”","Nanny Sun said, “Since it is an imperial decree, Duke, please enter.”","“Has Grandmother truly fallen unconscious?” Zhou Yuanshen asked.","Nanny Sun: “...”","He entered, and Huan Qingtang followed him inside.","But when they reached the entrance to the main hall, Huan Qingtang stopped. She did not want to go any farther.","She was afraid for no reason she could explain.","The fear had come without warning, halting her in her tracks.","Zhou Yuanshen entered the inner room and saw the Dowager Madame.","Nanny Sun stood beside the bed, exhausted and worried.","Zhou Yuanshen bent down and reached out to check whether the Dowager Madame was breathing. Nanny Sun immediately shouted, “Duke, what are you doing?”","Zhou Yuanshen ignored her.","He checked the Dowager Madame’s breath, then felt for the pulse in her neck.","After a long silence, he straightened.","“Grandmother has passed away.”","Nanny Sun was enraged. “You’re talking nonsense!”","“Someone come!” Zhou Yuanshen suddenly shouted.","His voice rang throughout the Shou’an Court, inside and out.","A group of deputy generals clad in armor and wielding blades stormed into Shou’an Court. There were dozens of them—she had never seen any of them before.","“Someone murdered the Dowager Madame. Surround Shou’an Court. Every person here is to be interrogated,” Zhou Yuanshen ordered. “I’m going to the palace.”","He turned and left.","Huan Qingtang was stunned.","It was only after Zhou Yuanshen had walked out that she thought to grab him, but by then, she could no longer catch up."]},{"number":237,"title":"Chapter 237: The Useless Son-in-Law Must Go","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao was at Jiangyun Court.","She, her mother-in-law, and Zhou Yuanqi were mildly startled when they heard voices speaking outside the gate.","“This is Jiangyun Court. The Duchess of Chen and the Duchess of Chen’s mother-in-law are both here. On what grounds do you need to stand guard?” a matron demanded.","The Second Madam frowned and glanced at Nanny Fan.","Nanny Fan immediately walked beneath the eaves and called out loudly, “Who is making all that noise?”","The Second Madam and the others also came out of the side room.","It was midafternoon, but the sunlight was wan and pale. It offered no warmth at all, while the bitter wind howled through the courtyard.","The matron opened the gate, revealing two soldiers standing outside, each holding a weapon.","The Second Madam’s brows drew together.","Zhou Yuanqi was even more annoyed. “Whose men are being so insolent?”","“Those at the gate, come in and speak!” the Second Madam called out as well.","The two soldiers exchanged a glance. One stepped over the threshold and bowed to the Second Madam.","“Madam, this humble one is from the residence of the General of the Pacified West.”","The Second Madam breathed a sigh of relief.","Zhou Yuanqi grew even angrier. “Since you are from the general’s residence, what are you doing causing trouble at Jiangyun Court? You are outrageously bold.”","Cheng Zhao’s heart began to pound. She clenched her hands, forcing down the sudden surge of unease.","“Lord Duke ordered us to stand guard,” the soldier explained. “Every courtyard in the Duke’s residence is to be watched. Not even a fly is to be allowed to wander about.”","The Second Madam’s brows furrowed. “What happened?”","“Dowager Madame has been attacked.”","The Second Madam’s body swayed.","Cheng Zhao reacted quickly and caught her. “Mother...”","Nanny Fan was startled as well. Once she recovered, she hurried over to support the Second Madam’s other arm.","The Second Madam steadied herself, her face turning deathly pale. Only after a long while did some color slowly return to it. She glanced at Cheng Zhao, then at Zhou Yuanqi.","She did not know what to say.","Zhou Yuanqi was equally shocked.","He asked the soldier, “What do you mean by ‘attacked’? Was she gravely injured, or did she die suddenly?”","“...She has passed away.”","Jiangyun Court was home not only to the masters but also to more than a dozen maids and working matrons. They had been occupied with their various tasks, but every word of the exchange had reached their ears. Now they all stopped what they were doing and stood frozen in place.","“I—I need to go to Shou’an Court!” the Second Madam said.","Cheng Zhao and Nanny Fan each seized one of her arms.","“Mother, you cannot go,” Zhou Yuanqi said. “Didn’t you hear? No one is allowed to move about freely.”","“But...”","“This is Third Brother’s way of protecting us,” Zhou Yuanqi continued. “Everything must be in chaos right now. If we all go there, who knows what might happen to us—or what blame we might end up shouldering?”","The Second Madam looked at Cheng Zhao, her eyes carrying a plea for help.","Cheng Zhao nodded. “Mother, Fifth Brother is right. We should follow Lord Duke’s arrangements.”","Then she added, “Let’s go inside. The wind at the gate is freezing. My face has gone numb.”","Only then did the Second Madam realize how cold she was.","Her entire body felt as though it had frozen stiff.","The Second Madam went into the eastern side room. Cheng Zhao asked Zhou Yuanqi to sit with her, then instructed a maid to bring in another hand warmer and told Nanny Fan to brew some hot tea.","The maids remained outside the curtain. Only Nanny Fan stayed inside with the three members of the family, and Cheng Zhao also urged her to drink some tea.","The heated brick platform by the window was warm, and with the hand warmer as well, the Second Madam gradually thawed. She was no longer as tense as before.","“Where is your father-in-law?” the Second Madam asked Cheng Zhao.","“Lord Duke must have sent someone to look for him,” Cheng Zhao replied. “He is probably at Shou’an Court as well.”","“Are we really not going there?”","“If the Emperor happens to be there, he could start killing people indiscriminately. It would not be easy for Lord Duke and Father-in-law to protect all three of us.","“Lord Duke has confined us here while openly searching for the murderer precisely to keep us safe. Mother, we are in our own courtyard. We will not be in danger.”","Zhou Yuanqi nodded.","His expression had changed as well.","The Second Madam rubbed her hands forcefully over the hand warmer, as though it still was not warm enough.","“How could Grandmother... how could she have died?” she murmured. “I thought she would at least live to be eighty.”","Wasn’t there a saying that calamities befell wicked people for a thousand years?","Dowager Madame spent every day plotting against others, yet she was fiercely protective of her own life. The whole family, young and old, had to prolong it for her. When Zhou Yuanqi had been burning with fever, she had possessed the life-saving Ziyang Pill but refused to take it out. She cared only about herself.","Selfish people were usually very good at taking care of themselves. How could she have died?","And they said she had been attacked...","“Who killed her?” the Second Madam asked Cheng Zhao again, sounding frustrated and vexed. “We know nothing at all.”","“Perhaps it was Lady Huan,” Cheng Zhao said.","She no longer referred to Huan Qingtang as her elder sister-in-law.","“She did it? Would she have the courage?”","Cheng Zhao told the Second Madam about the secret that Fan Xiao had previously revealed to Zhou Yuanshen.","“Prince of Andong has been in close contact with the Huan family.”","The Second Madam’s heart jolted.","Once a household matter was investigated deeply enough, it became a political struggle.","“Using Lady Huan’s hand to kill Dowager Madame and completely bring down the Duke of Chen’s residence?” the Second Madam said. “That is truly a ruthless move.”","Even the Second Madam, as a member of the Zhou family, believed that all of the Duke of Chen’s family’s favor with the Emperor came from Dowager Madame alone.","The Emperor had repeatedly visited the Zhou residence, and the rumors had long since spread far and wide. The censors simply had not openly submitted memorials to stop it.","When censors submitted memorials, some did so for the sake of good governance, while others sought to make a name for themselves. The Emperor visited the Zhou family because his first wife, the woman he had married before ascending the throne, was the Zhou family’s daughter.","He was visiting Dowager Madame.","The matter would not amount to “neglecting state affairs for a beauty,” nor would it interfere with governing. It could even be described as filial piety. Any censor who condemned him might instead find himself accused of being unfilial.","After weighing all these considerations, everyone understood the truth while pretending to be blind.","Even though Zhou Yuanshen had killed people on the Emperor’s behalf, to this day the court officials and common people still believed that he owed his current position to his grandmother.","The Second Madam knew that Dowager Madame disliked Zhou Yuanshen and had suppressed him at every turn. Yet she also believed that once Dowager Madame died, the bond between the Emperor and the Zhou family would be severed.","Thus, Helian Xuan’s use of Huan Qingtang to poison Dowager Madame had been a brilliant move.","Cheng Zhao, who truly understood the whole story, quietly sat beside the Second Madam and comforted her in a gentle voice. “Mother, don’t worry. You must trust Lord Duke.”","“Third Brother can beat Helian Xuan,” Zhou Yuanqi said.","Then, unable to contain his annoyance, he added, “Why is that man so detestable? I even thought before that it would be wonderful if he could marry into Third Sister-in-law’s family.”","The Second Madam and Cheng Zhao both looked at him.","Cheng Zhao asked first, “Marry into my family? How exactly?”","Zhou Yuanqi fell silent.","The Second Madam said, “What kind of nonsense is in your head? Where did that idea come from? Explain yourself, or I’ll break your legs.","“Since we can’t leave this place, you’ll be trapped in this courtyard. Let’s see where you can run—or what reinforcements you can bring in!”","Zhou Yuanqi fell silent again.","He stammered and eventually explained his idea to the Second Madam and Cheng Zhao.","“...If Third Brother were adopted into the main branch and married the widow there, what would happen to Third Sister-in-law? He would have to find someone else,” Zhou Yuanqi said.","A child’s ideas could be utterly fantastical.","Cheng Zhao and the Second Madam both laughed. They were exasperated and amused, yet also somewhat touched.","“I haven’t told this to anyone,” Zhou Yuanqi said. “Now that Third Brother doesn’t have to go to the main branch and is still here in our branch, of course I hope he and my sister-in-law can stay together. If he doesn’t betray my sister-in-law, I won’t insist on him leaving.”","Cheng Zhao could not help smiling. “Thank you, Yuanqi.”","The Second Madam said, “And you indulge him?”","“Mother, if Third Brother really goes to the main branch, you’ll lose both your son and your daughter-in-law. I’m leaving you one child, at least. Shouldn’t you be grateful?” Zhou Yuanqi asked her.","Second Madam was momentarily speechless.","Cheng Zhao answered for her. “Yes. Thank you, Yuanqi.”","Zhou Yuanqi seemed ready to puff up with pride again.","Second Madam suddenly remembered her mother’s words: Zhou Yuanqi had been born lucky. He was destined to have money to spend and people to dote on him.","His maternal grandmother cherished him, his parents adored him, and even his sister-in-law indulged him.","Forget it. She would let him off for today and give him a proper beating another time.","After all the joking and banter, Second Madam temporarily forgot the news of Dowager Madame’s death, and her spirits lifted somewhat."]},{"number":238,"title":"Chapter 238: The Grand Lady Has Done Every Manner of Evil","paragraphs":["There was no dinner, so Nanny Fan and the senior maids rummaged up a few pastries and brought them out for Second Madam and the others to fill their stomachs.","Second Madam had no appetite.","Cheng Zhao asked Nanny Fan, “Are there any pastries left? Give a few to everyone in the courtyard. Don’t save them—we’ll surely be able to leave tomorrow.”","Nanny Fan assented.","There weren’t many pastries prepared for Jiangyun Courtyard, so each maid and old servant received only two.","Cheng Zhao urged Second Madam to eat as well. “If they summon us in the middle of the night, Mother won’t have the strength to deal with it on an empty stomach.”","Second Madam nodded and forced down two pastries with some tea.","Zhou Yuanqi also ate his pastries quietly.","Without him joking around, Second Madam’s thoughts returned to the Grand Dowager Lady, and her spirits grew heavy.","“I spent my whole life suffering under her. I was always thinking about how free I’d be once she was gone. I never imagined she would be murdered,” Second Madam said.","She sighed deeply.","The last time Eldest Madam Song had died, Second Madam had cried.","This time, she could not.","She had no tears left to shed. Her low spirits came partly from surprise, but mostly from fear.","The Grand Dowager Lady had been the Zhou family’s “main pillar.” Second Madam had endured all her torment without leaving because of the prestige attached to the Duke of Chen’s residence.","Now, among her children, only Zhou Yuanshen was married and had established himself. Two others remained without prospects, and Second Madam had no idea what the future held.","Her heart was in turmoil.","When people had lived in a familiar environment for too long, they grew accustomed to it. A sudden change could leave them at a loss—even if that change might ultimately be for the better.","Second Madam now felt as though she were suspended in midair, unable to reach either above or below.","Fortunately, Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanqi were beside her, giving her some sense of reality.","“...It must be retribution. Eldest Uncle’s wife was murdered too. Father even said Aunt Zhou died the same way,” Zhou Yuanqi suddenly said.","Second Madam stared at him in surprise. “Your aunt? She died of an illness.”","“Father didn’t say that.”","Second Madam was even more astonished. “When did your father say that? He never told me.”","“He said it to Third Brother years ago. I was sitting beside them practicing calligraphy,” Zhou Yuanqi said.","“Years ago? How long?”","“Three or four years ago.”","Second Madam said, “You were only four or five then. You actually understood what you heard and remembered it?”","“Mother, when I was four, I could already recite the passages my tutor read. You were so pleased. Why, then, do you assume I can’t understand or remember family gossip?”","Second Madam fell silent.","After a moment, she asked, “What did your father say about your aunt’s death?”","“Father said Aunt Zhou and the Tenth Prince were both young. As husband and wife, they often had disagreements and occasionally exchanged angry words. Every time, Grandmother would berate Aunt Zhou.","“Later, the Tenth Prince took a fancy to one of Aunt Zhou’s maids. Aunt Zhou refused, but Grandmother took charge and gave the maid to the Tenth Prince.","“Aunt Zhou quarreled with Grandmother over that for quite some time. Then the maid took her own life, but Grandmother claimed that Aunt Zhou had killed her. The Tenth Prince took the opportunity to blame Aunt Zhou as well.","“Aunt Zhou was always ill. Before the Tenth Prince returned to the capital, he had even worried that she would have difficulty bearing children. He had already begun to look down on her. After he returned to the capital and ascended the throne, Aunt Zhou fell ill and died soon afterward. She didn’t burden the Tenth Prince in the slightest,” Zhou Yuanqi said.","Second Madam said, “Are you saying...”","“Those were Father’s words.”","Second Madam suddenly remembered something. “We only returned after the emperor ascended the throne. I remember that when your grandmother and the others were returning to the capital, your father tried to persuade your aunt to wait two years and return with us.","“But your aunt refused and even quarreled with your father. I was angry at the time, so I went out and argued with her too. She didn’t look well then. She wept bitterly while cursing me, almost as if she were out of her mind.”","Cheng Zhao sat beside them, piecing together what had happened from Zhou Yuanqi and Second Madam’s conversation.","The Grand Dowager Lady had set her heart on using the Tenth Prince to rise to power.","She had not been certain that he would ascend the throne; she had merely preserved that possibility.","And she had pursued that hope by trampling her own daughter.","The Zhou family’s married daughter had been the first stepping stone.","By suppressing and humiliating her own daughter, the Grand Dowager Lady had won the Tenth Prince’s heartfelt gratitude and trust. Under her constant manipulation, he had come to feel nothing but disdain and loathing for his first wife.","Once he knew that all his elder brothers had died in the struggle for power, he would ascend the throne. He had been deeply unwilling to share his glory with the wife he hated.","Perhaps the Zhou family’s married daughter had been unable to swallow that injustice and had insisted on making them suffer too.","Cheng Zhao thought that, by then, her only thought had probably been to make them miserable. She had not considered her own life or future at all.","The Grand Dowager Lady and the Tenth Prince had kept pressuring and humiliating her.","When she followed them back to the capital, Second Master Zhou had sensed that something was wrong and tried to persuade her to stay.","The Zhou family’s married daughter had not wanted any more people dragged into that whirlpool. She had cursed the elder brother and sister-in-law who wanted to save her, unable to bear the thought of them falling into the same pit of fire.","She must have been in unbearable pain. That was why she had cursed them while weeping.","Cheng Zhao further guessed that Second Master Zhou had not truly understood Aunt Zhou’s condition. Second Madam and Zhou Yuanshen had both told Cheng Zhao that they had not lived with the Grand Dowager Lady and the others at the time.","They had lived separately. Second Master Zhou might have known what was happening on the Grand Dowager Lady’s side only through observation or scattered bits of information.","Once the Zhou family’s married daughter was dead, the Tenth Prince was free of his burden.","At that point, he would have felt even more grateful to the Grand Dowager Lady. The dead still left behind a lingering attachment. They had been only fifteen or sixteen when they married; perhaps they had once shared happy days.","In any case, through the blood of the Zhou family’s married daughter, the Grand Dowager Lady had completely secured the emperor’s loyalty.","Only after the Zhou family’s married daughter died did Second Master Zhou realize what had happened.","“...If that’s true, then the old woman deserved her retribution!” Second Madam said furiously.","Then she added, “It was far too easy for her. She died so quickly, without suffering for even a day. Why should she have been so lucky?”","Zhou Yuanqi asked, “Do you feel a little better now?”","Second Madam fell silent.","Seeing that she was still in a panic, Cheng Zhao leaned forward and hugged her tightly, pressing her cheek against Second Madam’s.","Second Madam was taken aback, but she allowed Cheng Zhao to hold her. The two remained pressed together.","In the latter half of the night, Zhou Yuanqi could no longer keep his eyes open and fell asleep first.","Cheng Zhao and Second Madam had no sleepiness at all.","Second Madam worried about her husband and son, afraid they were even now being tortured by that mad emperor. More than that, she feared the emperor might take his anger over the Grand Dowager Lady’s death out on Zhou Yuanshen.","Cheng Zhao could not sleep either.","She was thinking not only about the upheaval within the Zhou family, but about the entire imperial court.","Helian Xuan’s treacherous ambitions certainly did not end with inciting Lady Huan to kill the Grand Dowager Lady. If he intended to provoke the garrison forces and the princes into rebellion, then this realm was about to be torn apart by war.","Only in complete chaos would he have a chance...","Would he really do it?","It was easy to ignite the flames of war, but extinguishing them was far more difficult. In the best-case scenario, peace might return in three to five years. In the worst, decades of warfare could leave the realm fragmented and its people scattered.","Cheng Zhao even felt that Helian Xuan would do it.","There seemed to be a streak of madness in the Helian family. Two emperors had been like that; Helian Xuan might be the same.","In wartime, no one could remain untouched.","Cheng Zhao felt a tightening in her chest again and again, unable to fall asleep.","“Damn Helian Xuan!”","Neither Second Madam nor Cheng Zhao spoke to the other. It was nearly dawn before they managed to doze off for a while.","“Madam, Young Madam, the Duke has returned!”","Nanny Fan’s voice seemed to come from within a dream, yet also from right beside her ear. Cheng Zhao jolted awake."]},{"number":239,"title":"Chapter 239: Sons Can Be Just as Considerate","paragraphs":["Zhou Yuanshen came in.","Cheng Zhao was the first to wake. She immediately slipped on her shoes and stepped out from the eastern side room, coming face-to-face with Zhou Yuanshen, who was covered in frost and dust from his journey.","They had been apart for less than a day, yet she felt as though they had not seen each other in years.","Ignoring the fact that Nanny Fan and the others were present, Cheng Zhao threw herself into Zhou Yuanshen’s arms.","He caught her and held her tightly, murmuring softly, “Don’t be afraid. Cheng Zhao, don’t be afraid.”","Cheng Zhao pressed herself against him.","Nanny Fan immediately sent the senior maids away and withdrew outside herself.","Rubbing his sleepy eyes, Zhou Yuanqi also came out of the eastern side room. “Third Brother.”","Cheng Zhao released her hold, and Zhou Yuanshen relaxed his arms and let her go as well.","“Where’s Father?” Zhou Yuanqi asked.","“Father went outside to prepare the mourning shed,” Zhou Yuanshen replied.","“Is Grandmother going to be buried?” Zhou Yuanqi asked again, now fully awake.","“Yes.”","“Then we’re all safe now,” Zhou Yuanqi said.","The emperor was willing to let the Dowager Madame be buried, which meant he had uncovered the truth and would not implicate the other members of the Zhou family. They no longer had to remain confined.","As long as their branch of the family was safe, Zhou Yuanqi did not care about anyone else.","“Was it Eldest Sister-in-law who killed Grandmother?” he asked again.","“It was her. She conspired with Helian Xuan to poison the Dowager Madame,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Second Madam had also awakened.","The light of dawn gradually filtered in through the doorway and windows, while the candlelight and oil lamps slowly dimmed.","As Second Madam instructed the maids to prepare hot water for her and Cheng Zhao to wash up, she also ordered them to make hot tea.","After a simple wash, Zhou Yuanshen used the water Cheng Zhao had washed her face with to wipe down his own face. Only then did he sit down in the eastern side room to drink tea.","Everyone was exhausted and hungry.","However, the main kitchen would not be lit at this hour, so they probably would not have a proper meal until late morning.","Just then, the young servant Nanfeng entered.","“Duke, these are pastries, fried flatbreads, and meat buns bought outside.” He carried in two large food boxes and set them on the table. “I’ve already delivered some to Second Master’s residence.”","Second Madam: “...”","Zhou Yuanshen said, “Mother, none of you had time to eat last night, did you? Have something first. You’ll all have to kneel before the spirit tablet this morning.”","Second Madam had only managed a short nap and had woken up ravenous.","Everyone ate considerably more than usual at breakfast. There was still quite a lot left over, so Second Madam had Nanny Fan distribute it among the maids.","Once they were full, they sat down to talk, and Second Madam asked the same questions again.","Was the Dowager Madame really dead?","Who had killed her?","“...I had already thought that as long as we caught Lady Huan’s personal maid and obtained some evidence, then with her testimony, we could implicate Lady Huan. The evidence didn’t need to be particularly conclusive. We only needed the emperor to believe us. This went more smoothly than I expected. The emperor believed it very quickly,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","The Dowager Madame had wanted to offer Huan Qingtang to the emperor, hoping she would take Mu Jiang’s former position, but the emperor had refused.","Thus, the emperor assumed that Huan Qingtang had harbored a grudge and wanted to kill the Dowager Madame—in truth, she had intended to assassinate him.","“How was she dealt with?” Second Madam asked, her voice somewhat tense.","Poisoning the Dowager Madame was a capital offense, and even her entire clan could have been implicated.","How foolish she had been!","And how utterly innocent her clan and relatives were!","People like Lady Huan, who deserved death, never spared a thought for anyone else. They took pleasure in harming others.","But Zhou Yuanshen said, “His Majesty killed her with his own sword.”","Second Madam: “!”","Why had he done that again...?","The emperor had personally killed quite a number of people. As the emperor, did he really need to do such things himself? Centuries later, the histories would not have a single good word to say about him.","His reputation after death would be utterly disgraceful.","What exactly did he want by insisting on killing people himself?","“Since she’s dead, will the case still be made public? Will her clan escape disaster?” Second Madam asked.","“It won’t be tried. Officially, we’ll say that the Dowager Madame was elderly and gravely ill, and died peacefully in bed. Lady Huan was heartbroken and followed her in death, her filial devotion shining as brightly as the moon.”","This was to preserve the dignity of the Duke of Chen’s Estate.","If the case were truly investigated, the estate’s reputation would be ruined.","From this, it was clear that even without the Dowager Madame, the emperor would still take the Zhou family’s reputation into consideration. Was this because he valued Zhou Yuanshen?","Thinking of this, Second Madam glanced at her son. “Since it won’t be made public, then Helian Xuan...”","“The emperor doesn’t believe that he was the one stirring things up. Lady Huan and a maid cannot bring him down. Even if Lady Huan’s father came forward, I’m afraid it still wouldn’t be enough,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao’s heart sank.","The emperor favored Zhou Yuanshen, and he would favor Helian Xuan as well. Zhou Yuanshen had planted spies, and so had Helian Xuan. Neither of them was easy to deal with.","That man had no sense of right or wrong, no distinction between good and evil. He had only his lust for power.","Second Madam sighed deeply. After a while, she said, “I hope peace will come to the realm soon, so that we can live properly.”","Zhou Yuanshen said nothing.","“Is the Duke of Chen’s Estate holding two funerals at once? Lady Huan murdered the old madam—will she still be buried in the Zhou family’s ancestral grave?” Second Madam asked again.","“Since the truth won’t be made public, naturally the two funerals will be held together. Bury her in the ancestral grave. Once she’s underground, she can continue fighting with Grandmother.”","Second Madam: “...”","She could already imagine how the entire capital would laugh at the Zhou family.","At that moment, Second Madam had completely forgotten that her younger brother was about to be married.","Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen went out first.","Since they were holding a funeral, there was a mountain of work waiting for Cheng Zhao.","The Dowager Madame was dead, and Lady Huan was dead as well. From now on, the entire Duke’s Estate would belong to Cheng Zhao. If everything went smoothly, she would become the senior lady of the household. Her goal was about to be achieved.","Why, then, did she feel not the slightest bit of joy?","Was it because she had anticipated the turmoil to come?","Cheng Zhao could not explain it.","At Jiangyun Courtyard, Zhou Yuanqi had not yet left. He and Second Madam continued waiting for news. Once the body had been prepared for burial, they would go kneel before the spirit tablet.","“I truly never imagined that the old madam would meet such an end,” Second Madam said.","It was completely unexpected.","It was like a beautiful garment whose final sleeve had been sewn on in tatters, clashing utterly with the rest.","Or like a carefully composed essay, its opening written in neat, elegant characters, only for the final lines to be filled with crooked, disorderly ink—nothing like the meticulous planning that had come before.","Zhou Yuanqi said, “The histories record many people who enjoyed glory and success in their youth, only to meet an exceedingly shabby end in their final years.”","He gave Second Madam several examples.","A brave and battle-hardened general, renowned throughout the realm for both his person and his blade, with countless victories to his name, died at forty-one from a bout of diarrhea.","A poet of dazzling talent, who had left behind countless beloved verses, encountered war and upheaval in his later years. Unable to pay a toll for passage, he was beheaded by a low-ranking soldier. At the time, several rulers were still trying to recruit him and lamenting the loss of such talent.","There was also a strategist who could sway the world with his eloquence, a single tongue worth a thousand troops. During the Lantern Festival, he drank wine and listened to music aboard a pleasure boat, only to fall into the water and drown.","“...Life is accidental, and so is death. No one decreed that Grandmother had to die in any particular way,” Zhou Yuanqi said.","Second Madam looked at him. “You’ve read a great many books.”","“That’s why I don’t get caught up in pointless worries. Mother, you should read more too. Then you won’t panic whenever something happens,” Zhou Yuanqi said.","For once, Second Madam took his advice and nodded. “Just look at you, and then look at your sister-in-law. Reading really is useful. Once this turmoil has passed, I’ll read a little myself.”","After hearing a few words from Zhou Yuanqi, Second Madam felt somewhat relieved. Her son really was considerate.","Zhou Yuanqi, meanwhile, was secretly astonished.","His mother had looked down on scholars her entire life, always saying that scholarly families were hypocritical. Yet now she had actually relented and planned to start studying herself.","—Fate was truly wondrous.","The funeral at the Duke of Chen’s Estate once again sent shock waves throughout the entire capital.","The Dowager Madame was dead, and Lady Huan was dead.","Neither the Qingyuan Marquis’s household—the Dowager Madame’s natal family—nor Lady Huan’s family made any attempt to cause a commotion. They simply accepted what had happened.","The Qingyuan Marquis had come several times while the Dowager Madame was unconscious, terrified that the emperor might take his anger out on them. The Huan family was even more frightened out of their wits."]},{"number":240,"title":"Chapter 240: Having Someone in My Heart","paragraphs":["The Duke of Chen’s residence held a funeral.","“The celestial omens are inauspicious. There have been rather too many funerals lately.”","“After the Iron Tribunal case, so many people died that everyone was living in fear. It took the first snow to ease the tension a little, and only then did people begin holding banquets again. Now someone else has died.”","“The Eldest Madam of the Zhou family just passed away, and now the Eldest Young Madame and the Dowager Madame are dead too. It’s truly eerie. Could they have been murdered?”","“The Dowager Madame had even more influence than the empress dowager. What benefit would killing her bring the Duke of Chen? If she was murdered, it must have been by an enemy. The Zhou family is finished.”","Rumors spread more thickly and chaotically than the snowflakes filling the sky.","The mourning shed had been erected, and by mid-afternoon, snow began to fall.","The snow drifted down in soft, swirling flakes, trampled into the mud. Everywhere was a mire. The mourning robes of the Zhou men were all stained with mud up to the knees, leaving them looking thoroughly disheveled.","Fan Xiao also came to offer his condolences.","The Second Master said, “Your wedding is tomorrow, so we won’t be able to attend the wedding feast. Is there anything you need help with?”","“Everything has been properly arranged. Brother-in-law, you needn’t worry,” Fan Xiao replied.","He exchanged a few private words with Zhou Yuanshen.","He told Zhou Yuanshen what he had said to his mother.","“...I didn’t tell you beforehand. The Dowager Madame would rather perish together with you than let you go. She was bound to make a move against you. Yet, because of filial duty, you could only defend yourself and not retaliate. My grandmother and I were both afraid you would come to harm,” Fan Xiao said.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, “I could guess as much.”","He had to do something, but he could not go too far.","His solution had been to seize the chief maidservant serving Huan Qingtang. Once the truth came to light, the maidservant’s testimony could clear him of suspicion.","He simply had not expected the Emperor to kill Huan Qingtang outright.","There was no longer any need for the maidservant’s testimony. The Emperor did not need evidence. He believed Huan Qingtang was the culprit, so he punished her.","Perhaps the Emperor had merely lost his temper and gone mad with rage. Perhaps he wanted to conceal the truth behind the Dowager Madame’s death. He might even have wanted to remove Helian Xuan from suspicion.","The Emperor believed Helian Xuan had been wronged.","Huan Qingtang had insisted again and again that the medicine Helian Xuan gave her was only meant to control the Dowager Madame.","The Emperor reasoned that perhaps that was indeed the case. Helian Xuan had only wanted to win over the Huan family; he had not intended to harm the Dowager Madame.","The one who deserved to die was Huan Qingtang.","That woman had led Helian Xuan astray.","With her dead, the Dowager Madame’s death had been avenged. Helian Xuan had merely made a mistake, and a minor punishment would serve as a warning. His reckoning could wait.","“Yuanshen, now that the Dowager Madame is dead, your next opponent is Helian Xuan,” Fan Xiao said.","Zhou Yuanshen’s expression remained indifferent. After a long pause, he said, “It isn’t him.”","Fan Xiao’s heart jolted.","He knew whom Zhou Yuanshen meant.","The Emperor, of course.","It was the Emperor who had forced him to inherit the title. It was the Emperor who had foisted Mu Jiang upon him and made him endure humiliation. It was also the Emperor who had colluded with the Dowager Madame and backed her.","It was this Emperor who had made Zhou Yuanshen suffer one grievance after another.","Fan Xiao was anxious. “Yuanshen, you must think of the reputation you’ll leave behind. Some stains can never be washed away. The historians’ pens are as sharp as knives.”","Zhou Yuanshen said, “I won’t do that. Rest easy, Little Uncle.”","Fan Xiao was still somewhat worried. “I know you’ve planted quite a few people around the Emperor...”","“Helian Xuan used the Huan family to kill my grandmother. Why can’t I use his hand to kill my enemy?” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Fan Xiao fell silent.","“Little Uncle, you spared me from a dilemma. My feelings for you remain unchanged,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Fan Xiao was getting married the next day, and with the Dowager Madame’s death weighing on him, he failed to notice the deeper meaning in Zhou Yuanshen’s words. He gave a bitter smile. “Do we really need to be so formal with each other, uncle and nephew?”","Zhou Yuanshen inclined his head slightly.","“I’m getting married tomorrow,” Fan Xiao suddenly said. “Lord Pei has repeatedly tried to play matchmaker for me. This marriage is a good one.”","The matchmaker was his superior, Pei Yanhe.","Even when Pei Yanhe had still been the Vice Minister of the Court of Judicial Review, he had constantly supported and promoted Fan Xiao. Later, when Pei Yanhe was promoted, Fan Xiao succeeded him as Vice Minister of the Court of Judicial Review.","Thanks to Pei Yanhe’s constant care, Fan Xiao’s career in the capital had proceeded with remarkable smoothness.","Otherwise, given his origins in the Duke Protector-General’s residence, he would have faced the scholars’ exclusion and suspicion.","Pei Yanhe had arranged the match and told him about Third Miss Song’s past. Fan Xiao had been deeply moved.","Vice Minister Song was upright and unafraid of power. Fan Xiao needed a family like that behind him.","Third Miss Song also needed a marriage. She deserved one.","It would be good for them both.","Yet, for some reason, the closer the wedding day came, the more stifled Fan Xiao felt.","It was not because he was thinking of his late wife. His late wife had always despised him, and they had barely spoken. There had never been any real affection between them.","Nor was he afraid of the hardships of marriage. Whether the relationship was good or bad, life was lived all the same.","He simply felt stifled.","If a person never knew what he liked, a marriage arranged by the family would not cause him pain. But, unfortunately, he did know.","“Lord Pei has indeed looked after you very well,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Marriage was not merely about acquiring in-laws. It also meant gaining a superior’s support.","The intricate web of connections in officialdom made every link important.","“Yes.” Fan Xiao’s voice was distant and indistinct. “I will treat her well.”","Then he added, “If two people can become relatives, it means they are fated to meet. She and I will probably live well together.”","He sounded as though he were comforting himself, and perhaps also saying it for Zhou Yuanshen’s benefit.","Zhou Yuanshen glanced at him.","“You’re still busy here, so I’ll head back first,” Fan Xiao said. “We’ll each attend to our own affairs and meet again when we have time.”","Zhou Yuanshen saw him out.","The snow outside had grown heavier, swirling and billowing like torn cotton. It quickly covered the ground in a layer of white, making the roads even harder to travel.","“I’m afraid this snow won’t stop tomorrow,” Fan Xiao said.","The road to his wedding would be just as muddy and difficult to traverse.","He drew a deep breath.","Zhou Yuanshen watched him ride away. He remained outside for a long while before returning, and soon a layer of snow had gathered over his brows. He reached up and brushed it away, then turned and entered the mourning shed.","Inside Chengming Hall, Cheng Zhao was assigning the various funeral arrangements.","The funeral was chaotic. Fortunately, she had handled the funeral of Eldest Madam Song before and knew where problems were likely to arise. She managed to put everything in order.","“The Eldest Young Madame’s coffin will first be placed in the small courtyard behind the rear garden. Assign people to guard it. The Dowager Madame’s body will remain here until her burial. Only after her funeral is completed will we hold the Eldest Young Madame’s,” Cheng Zhao instructed the household managers.","The managers had still been wondering how to arrange two funerals at once and what to do.","Now they understood that the ceremonies would be held separately.","That was indeed the proper arrangement.","The two women had different statuses and ranks. Their funerals could not possibly be conducted on the same scale.","The Dowager Madame had been the wife of the Duke of Chen; Lady Huan did not even hold an imperial title.","After assigning all the tasks, Cheng Zhao remained busy until mid-afternoon before finally having lunch.","Second Madam came over.","“Your Little Uncle is getting married tomorrow. I’ve sent Nanny Fan back with a wedding gift. I’m going to kneel and keep vigil for the Old Lady,” Second Madam said.","Cheng Zhao replied, “Mother, I’ve had the eastern upper rooms prepared for you. You can rest there when you’re keeping vigil instead of traveling back and forth. The snow is so heavy, and it’s terribly cold.”","Second Madam did not stand on ceremony with her.","The Dowager Madame and Huan Qingtang were both dead. The Duke of Chen’s residence now belonged to Zhou Yuanshen. Wherever Second Madam chose to rest, it would not be inappropriate.","She ought to have been happy.","Yet she could not feel happy at all.","Perhaps the overcast, damp, and bitterly cold weather had affected her spirits.","Even the thought of Fan Xiao’s wedding could not bring her much comfort.","“I hope the Emperor doesn’t come,” Second Madam thought.","She was truly afraid of him now.","All she wanted was peace. She was terrified that something else might happen to the family.","Snow fell without pause throughout the Dowager Madame’s funeral, just as rain had fallen during Eldest Madam Song’s funeral. The heavens seemed determined to make things difficult.","Perhaps it was because neither of them had died a natural death."]},{"number":241,"title":"Chapter 241: Epilogue (1)","paragraphs":["On the seventeenth day of the eleventh month, snow was still falling over Shengjing.","Compared with yesterday, today’s snowfall was lighter, like willow catkins drifting in early spring.","The snow on the streets had been trampled into slush, blending with the mud until everywhere was a mire. Both people and horses were liable to slip.","The Duke of Chen’s residence was holding a funeral, while the residence of the Pillar of State General was holding a wedding.","Late in the morning, Cheng Zhao’s family came to offer their condolences.","Her brothers and sisters had arranged to come together to the Duke of Chen’s residence. Cheng Zhao left the various funeral arrangements to her mother-in-law and led her family to Morning Radiance Court beside Chengming Hall, where they could speak in private.","“...We were all shocked when we heard the news. Grandfather immediately sent people out to make inquiries, to see whether there were any rumors detrimental to your husband,” said Cheng Zhao’s second brother, Cheng Yan.","“Thank you, Second Brother,” Cheng Zhao said. “Dowager Madame simply passed away from illness. Yuanshen and I have been filial. Not a single person from her maternal family has said anything against us.”","Her second brother gave a slight nod. “I sent people to ask around, and everyone was indeed surprised. There were no unpleasant rumors. Grandfather and Father and Mother were able to set their minds at ease.”","Zhou Yuanshen had not left behind the slightest suspicion that anyone could seize upon and use for gossip.","When Dowager Madame had vomited blood, Nanny Sun had concealed it from Zhou Yuanshen and summoned an imperial physician. That could be verified.","For an elderly person, there could be nearly half a month between vomiting blood and death. It made perfect sense. The vomiting might simply have been a sign that her illness had reached its final stage.","Afterward, Nanny Sun had summoned Master Qingshan, then Master Zhao, and finally a nephew from Dowager Madame’s maternal family to come and visit her.","Everything suggested that Dowager Madame had been on the verge of death, and that her loyal servant had merely been making a frantic, futile attempt to keep her alive.","They had concealed it from Zhou Yuanshen.","Zhou Yuanshen had had to seek the emperor’s permission in the Imperial Study before he could go and visit Dowager Madame. This, too, had reached the ears of the court officials.","Every detail indicated that Dowager Madame’s death had not been unexpected.","The suspicious one was Huan Qingtang’s death.","But who cared?","She had been a widow from an insignificant family. She had no parents-in-law or husband, no children, and no rank or title bestowed upon her. People were not particularly interested in discussing her.","The only thing they could talk about was probably the disgrace she had suffered at Prince Jingnan’s residence.","“I heard that your elder sister-in-law’s reputation has been ruined,” said Cheng Zhao’s second sister-in-law, Yin Linglang. “She used the Duke to marry into the Zhou family and has already earned everyone’s contempt. Everyone knows it.","“Now that Dowager Madame is dead, she may fall into your hands and your husband’s. She must have feared that you would take revenge, and that her own family might be implicated.","“So she followed Dowager Madame in death. Perhaps the emperor, moved by her filial devotion and loyalty, will promote her father. At the very least, she has won her family a good reputation.”","“The Duke had people spread that explanation,” Cheng Zhao said.","“It makes perfect sense,” her third sister said. “Whatever old grievances there may have been, we need to make the story coherent and stop it from casting further suspicion on you and your husband.”","Cheng Zhao nodded.","Her family cared about her. They had all come to support her, and she felt her strength returning.","No matter how busy or exhausted she was, she no longer felt worn down.","Her grandfather, her parents, her brothers, her sisters-in-law, and her sisters would always stand behind her.","Cheng Zhao had been blessed with so much.","Her eldest sister even said, “Should I stay and help you manage things? Right now, you have only yourself and a single pair of hands.”","Her eldest brother-in-law added, “I can send the children to the Cheng family residence, where Mother-in-law can help look after them. Let your eldest sister stay here with you.”","Cheng Zhao’s heart grew warm.","Even with the ground frozen and the weather bitterly cold outside, she felt surrounded by warmth.","She shook her head. “I plan to take this opportunity to bring all my household stewards and attendants into the estate. Once the funeral is over, I’ll spend a large sum of money. Any managers who are willing to retire can take the money and leave.","“I expect at least half of them will be willing to go. If they stay, their monthly wages, together with the retirement stipends they’ll receive later, won’t amount to much.","“The remaining managers will be fewer in number and weaker in influence, so they won’t dare make too much trouble. This way, my own people won’t dare become too arrogant, but they also won’t be so constrained that they can’t act.”","Cheng Zhao intended to make use of them, but she would not rely solely on them.","With the two sides evenly matched, both would have to curry favor with her and strive to become her trusted aides. As a result, both sides would work hard to prove themselves.","Her second sister-in-law could not help laughing. “What a clever plan! I always said our little sister was the smartest. Mother really never needed to worry about you.”","Her eldest sister also breathed a sigh of relief. “Then I don’t need to worry about you working yourself to exhaustion.”","She urged Cheng Zhao repeatedly, “Get plenty of rest. You don’t need to do everything perfectly. As long as things are passable, that’s enough. From now on, you’re the lady of the house.”","Cheng Zhao nodded.","The Cheng siblings chatted for quite some time, surrounding Cheng Zhao the entire while.","Qiubai entered and said to her, “Young Madam, Prince of Andong has come to offer his condolences. The Duke is receiving him outside.”","Cheng Zhao’s expression changed. “He actually dares come here!”","Her third sister placed a hand on her arm. “Don’t get angry. Don’t let him provoke you so easily.”","She continued, “He came to offer his condolences—that is only proper etiquette. Once he has paid his respects, he’ll leave.”","“He murdered Dowager Madame!” Cheng Zhao said.","Cheng Zhao’s eldest brother-in-law remained silent for a long while.","When her second brother saw that he was not speaking, he asked, “Eldest Brother-in-law, is something wrong?”","“What does Prince of Andong hope to gain by arranging all of this?” Du Anli said. “He should understand better than anyone that His Majesty trusts your husband not because of Dowager Madame.”","“I also don’t believe he did all this merely to sever the Zhou family’s close relationship with the emperor,” her third sister said. “That man is deeply sinister.”","Several people turned to Cheng Chao.","Cheng Chao was in an awkward position. “I truly have no idea what Prince An and his son were doing in Qinzhou. Helian Xuan never revealed any secrets to me.","“Back then, he only associated with me because he was infatuated with our little sister and hoped to befriend her. Who could have known that she would want nothing to do with him, and that one of her attendants would die afterward?”","Cheng Zhao abruptly turned to him. “Don’t disgust me!”","Cheng Chao fell silent.","Her third sister then said, “It’s true, Zhaozhao. Back then, Dowager Consort An was afraid that Helian Xuan would ask to marry you, so she requested that Empress Guo arrange a marriage for you. She wanted to marry you off to just anyone.”","Cheng Zhao was somewhat surprised.","So that had been the truth.","The scheme was hardly impressive—not painful or damaging in the slightest. Instead, it had given Cheng Zhao such an excellent marriage.","“I married the Duke of Chen. Was Dowager Consort An out of her mind? How was that supposed to harm me?” Cheng Zhao said.","The youngest duke in the dynasty—how could he possibly be inferior to a prince?","Besides, Zhou Yuanshen was far more handsome than Helian Xuan, and much more imposing. He might not be especially obedient, but his parents-in-law were easy to get along with, and his younger brother was adorable. Apart from being quiet, Zhou Yuanshen was efficient and considerate in everything he did.","Cheng Zhao had been extremely fortunate in her marriage.","She really ought to thank Dowager Consort An.","“Dowager Consort An simply didn’t want you to marry Prince of Andong; she wasn’t trying to ruin your life. Our family isn’t one that Dowager Consort An and Empress Guo could manipulate at will.","“If the marriage had been too humiliating, Dowager Consort An’s scheme would never have succeeded. And Empress Guo must have had her own reasons for cooperating with her,” her third sister said.","Everyone came from powerful, distinguished families. Whenever they acted, who did not weigh the benefits and consequences?","Could Empress Guo really have been moved solely by an old friendship, rushing to resolve Dowager Consort An’s problem and avenge her without a second thought?","“I should thank Dowager Consort An,” Cheng Zhao said.","Then she added, “I never felt that Helian Xuan was in love with me.”","A young man’s infatuation was a blazing, passionate thing. How could anyone fail to sense it?","Cheng Zhao hardly ever thought about love, yet even she could tell how much Zhou Yuanshen cared for her.","If she had felt nothing, then there had been nothing to feel. Helian Xuan had not loved Cheng Zhao as much as he claimed.","Or perhaps it would be more accurate to say that his pride mattered more to him than his feelings for Cheng Zhao.","He wanted Cheng Zhao to submit to him.","As if she would ever agree!","Just then, the maid Suyue came in and said, “Young Madam, the women from the Prince of Andong’s residence have also come to offer their condolences. They would like to see you and offer you a few words of comfort on behalf of the prince.”","Cheng Zhao asked, “Is Dowager Consort An here?”","“No. It’s one of the prince’s secondary consorts,” Suyue replied.","Cheng Zhao frowned."]},{"number":242,"title":"Chapter 242: Epilogue (2)","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao had never heard that the Prince of Andong had a secondary consort.","Not only had she never heard of it, neither had her second sister-in-law or her sisters.","Her second sister-in-law asked Cheng Chao, “He has a secondary consort? When did that happen?”","Cheng Chao was equally bewildered. “I’ve been avoiding him lately and haven’t had any dealings with him for quite some time. I haven’t seen him in at least three months. Even when we met before, we never had the chance to talk at length.”","Then he added, “Could it be that dancer? The one the emperor bestowed upon him?”","“That dancer is called Xian Xiang. We ran into her at Jin’an Temple last time, and she was with Dowager Consort An,” Cheng Zhao said.","At the time, Xian Xiang had said that Xian Si was her younger sister and that she wanted to visit her at the Chen family residence. Cheng Zhao had refused.","Xian Si, however, had never mentioned her, nor had she ever said she wanted to leave the residence to visit her.","“It shouldn’t be her, should it? If a dancer became a secondary consort and still went out to attend social functions, wouldn’t the commandery prince and the dowager consort lose all face?” her eldest sister said.","“Enough guessing. Let’s go see for ourselves.” Third Sister stood up. “I’ll go with you.”","Cheng Chao also rose. “I’m coming too.”","The reception hall of Chengming Hall usually served as a meeting room. During the funeral, it was being used to entertain female mourners. At present, there was only one guest. She sat on one side with Cheng Zhao’s mother-in-law on the other, drinking tea and making polite conversation.","Cheng Zhao frowned slightly—not because the guest’s clothes were luxurious, brightly colored, and ostentatious, hardly appropriate for someone paying respects to the dead, but because six maids followed behind her.","Even Cheng Zhao, a duchess of the highest rank, brought at most two personal maids when visiting someone else’s home. Most of the time, she brought only one.","Such a grand retinue was rather strange.","Everything about this was strange.","Just as Cheng Zhao was about to enter, Cheng Chao suddenly strode forward. With practiced ease and excessive warmth, he said, “You must be the commandery prince’s secondary consort? I can’t believe we’ve never met.”","Then he added, “I’m Cheng Chao. The commandery prince and I have been friends since childhood. He got married without even inviting me to drink with him. He’s become rather distant from his friends. What could I possibly have done to offend him?”","At his display, Cheng Zhao and Cheng Ying exchanged glances, surprise in their eyes. The Second Madam was startled as well.","In her eyes, every one of the Cheng children had been raised with impeccable manners. Cheng Chao’s attitude was simply too ingratiating, and thoroughly improper.","She did not interrupt, merely turning to look at Cheng Zhao.","The commandery prince’s secondary consort rose and smiled. “Young Master Cheng, I’ve heard the commandery prince mention you many times. Meeting you is even better than hearing about you. You truly possess an extraordinary bearing, worthy of being Chancellor Cheng’s eldest grandson.”","She then looked toward Cheng Zhao and Cheng Ying.","Cheng Zhao was dressed in mourning clothes, with a white flower in her hair. It was immediately obvious that she was the Duchess of Chen.","“Duchess of Chen, I have accompanied the commandery prince here to pay our respects. Please accept my condolences,” she said.","With that, she stepped forward and reached for Cheng Zhao’s hand.","At that moment, Cheng Chao suddenly struck.","The short dagger in his hand dropped downward, its sheath flying free as a flash of cold steel shot toward the secondary consort. Because he had been standing close while speaking and moved with such speed, blood was drawn in an instant.","His blade slashed across the secondary consort’s face.","The commandery prince’s secondary consort stumbled back several paces, both enraged and shocked, and immediately struck back.","Cheng Zhao was stunned for a moment. Her mother-in-law, meanwhile, snatched up the decorative spear resting nearby and joined Cheng Chao.","A soft sword was concealed in Third Sister Cheng Ying’s sash.","Its blade was so flexible that it could not be used to block, but when swung, it was sharp enough to cut.","Suyue and Qiubai stood behind Cheng Zhao.","Suyue immediately shielded her. “Young Madam, be careful.”","Qiubai also had a dagger on her and rushed into the fight.","Without any apparent planning, the four of them quickly surrounded the commandery prince’s secondary consort. The six maids behind her froze for an instant before charging forward.","Each of them had concealed a weapon, though the weapons varied.","Cheng Zhao immediately withdrew from the reception hall.","“Prepare the small crossbows!” she ordered Suyue. “Quickly!”","Her maids knew how to use the small crossbows. Even if they merely struck threatening poses, the sight alone would be enough to intimidate people.","Suyue hurried off.","Fortunately, all of Cheng Zhao’s people were in Chengming Hall. Suyue opened the chests, and several maids grabbed the small crossbows without a word and rushed into the reception hall.","The fighting inside was fierce.","The seven women from Helian Xuan’s residence each had weapons hidden on them. Cheng Chao wielded a short dagger, which had limited power, while the Second Madam’s spear was merely a decorative piece.","Cheng Zhao turned around to look for proper weapons.","Zhou Yuanshen’s residence had several weapons suitable for combat. Cheng Zhao took a long spear and a long sword, then threw them to her mother-in-law and Cheng Chao.","“Catch!”","Qiubai and Cheng Ying moved in to take their places, while Cheng Chao first withdrew from the fight to catch the sword.","Meanwhile, Cheng Zhao’s maids had already formed a line behind her, crossbows raised protectively.","Suyue fired an arrow, striking one of the commandery prince’s maids in the shoulder. The woman’s weapon fell from her hand.","The secondary consort tried to charge toward Cheng Zhao, but stopped when she saw the maids holding crossbows. She had no idea how skilled they were, and Suyue’s arrow had been frighteningly accurate.","In truth, only Suyue and Qiubai knew how to use the weapons. The others did not, but their imposing presence was enough to make a convincing show. They were all remarkably good at bluffing.","When Cheng Zhao had first married into the family, even the Second Madam had been intimidated by that very display.","“Withdraw!” the secondary consort ordered under her breath.","They turned and tried to flee.","The Second Madam shouted sternly, “Don’t let them get away! Zhao Zhao, go call for reinforcements! Keep them here!”","She and Cheng Chao continued grappling with the secondary consort.","When the secondary consort found an opening and tried to escape, Cheng Ying ignored the maid fighting her and broke away to block the woman’s path. Her arm was slashed, but her soft sword struck the secondary consort.","The secondary consort staggered as the blade sank into her, blood gushing from the wound. Her strength gave out at once, and she collapsed.","The Second Madam’s spear pinned her down, and she planted one foot firmly on the woman.","The other women from the commandery prince’s residence immediately fell into disarray. They were clearly still capable of fighting, yet one by one, they panicked.","Suyue seized the opportunity to fire another arrow, while Qiubai followed up by stabbing one of them.","Only two maids remained. One had already fled to the rear window. Apparently uncertain that she could jump out safely—and afraid of being shot in the back—she threw down her weapon.","The other surrendered as well.","Cheng Zhao soon brought several sturdy servant women and male attendants to the hall.","Everyone pinned down the women from the commandery prince’s residence and bound them tightly.","Only then did the Second Madam speak. “What exactly are we doing?”","Blood from Cheng Ying’s right arm had run down to the back of her hand, but she seemed not to notice. She calmly wiped her soft sword clean.","“I don’t know,” she said.","The Second Madam: “...”","If you didn’t know, why had you fought as though your lives depended on it?","After calling for help, Cheng Zhao returned to the reception hall. She supported Cheng Ying. “Third Sister, is your injury serious?”","“Just a superficial wound. It isn’t deep.” Cheng Ying glanced at it.","Then she looked toward Cheng Chao. “What happened?”","Cheng Chao pointed at the woman who had been bound from head to toe, a deep bloody slash marring her cheek. “She’s one of Helian Xuan’s covert guards. I’ve seen her before.”","The secondary consort’s eyes flickered.","The Second Madam and Cheng Zhao both turned to look at her.","No wonder she had dressed so flamboyantly, drawing everyone’s attention to her clothes and distracting them from everything else. And because she seemed frivolous and extravagant, no one had thought it strange that she brought six maids with her.","They had come to cause trouble.","“What were they planning to do? Assassinate the Duchess of Chen?” the Second Madam asked.","“What were you planning to do?” Cheng Chao demanded directly of the covert guard.","The woman tried to bite through her tongue and kill herself, but Cheng Chao moved swiftly and seized her jaw, dislocating it.","“Lock them up. They won’t talk unless we use harsher methods,” Cheng Chao said. “These maids have some skill, but they aren’t death soldiers.”","Only then, amid the drifting snow and the biting winter wind, did Cheng Zhao belatedly realize that her clothes were soaked through with sweat."]},{"number":243,"title":"Chapter 243: Epilogue (3)","paragraphs":["Helian Xuan was in the outer courtyard of the Duke of Chen’s residence.","Apart from him, several other guests who had come to pay their respects were making small talk with Zhou Yuanshen and the Second Master—offering words of comfort to the family and discussing a few inconsequential matters.","Helian Xuan remained calm and composed throughout, without the slightest sign of unease.","That was until the young servant Nanfeng entered and whispered a few words to Zhou Yuanshen.","Zhou Yuanshen looked at Helian Xuan. “Your Highness, why have the women from your household entered the inner residence and attempted to murder the Duchess?”","There was a prince consort present, along with two heads of prominent families and their neighbor, Prince Rong.","Everyone froze.","Helian Xuan himself appeared somewhat stunned. It was only after a long moment that he said, “Duke of Chen, isn’t that a little too serious? The women from the Prince’s residence merely came to offer their condolences.”","“They used weapons. After your secondary consort failed, she even attempted to take her own life, but was stopped. They have all been bound,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","His expression was impassive, and his voice was not loud.","He was not merely speaking for Helian Xuan’s benefit, but for the ears of every guest present.","Prince Rong was astonished. He glanced at the others but did not rashly intervene. He was Helian Xuan’s uncle. If he did not speak, the others had even less standing to do so.","The Second Master remained silent as well.","For a moment, no one said anything.","The atmosphere was strange and unnaturally quiet, save for the weeping from the mourning shed outside.","“...This truly comes as a shock to me. I have no idea how such a thing happened,” Helian Xuan said.","“Then send them to the Court of Judicial Review,” Zhou Yuanshen replied. “That will give the Duchess justice, and it will also clear Your Highness’s name.”","Prince Rong spoke up at this point. “Sending them to the Court of Judicial Review would indeed be best and most impartial. I refuse to believe Xuan could commit such a foolish act as attempting murder in the Duke of Chen’s residence.","“If he were to bear such a reputation, not only would it tarnish the posthumous honor of Prince An, but Xuan himself would suffer—and His Majesty would be angered as well. Xuan is His Majesty’s nephew and enjoys His Majesty’s favor.”","Those words praised Helian Xuan highly, leaving him no room to refuse being sent to the authorities. At the same time, Prince Rong was reminding Zhou Yuanshen to be wary of the emperor covering for Helian Xuan.","In Prince Rong’s eyes, the Dowager Madame had already passed away, and the Zhou family’s imperial favor would gradually fade. Zhou Yuanshen might not be able to contend with Helian Xuan.","While warning Zhou Yuanshen to be careful, he was also hinting that Zhou Yuanshen should think twice about whether it was worth opposing Helian Xuan.","The reason Prince Rong was willing to take a side was that he intended to form a marriage alliance with the Cheng family by marrying his youngest daughter to Cheng Chao.","Marriage ties were deeply intertwined. The Prince Rong’s residence and the Duke of Chen’s residence were neighbors, and from now on, they would be “family” who stood together.","“Yuanshen, perhaps you should ask a few more questions?” the Second Master said.","He had no idea what had happened in the inner residence, but he had understood every implication in Prince Rong’s words.","The prince was warning Zhou Yuanshen.","“Father, someone entering the inner residence to murder another person is utterly deranged! Without justice, everyone in the capital will live in fear,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","The Second Master replied, “Then send them to the Court of Judicial Review.”","He turned to Helian Xuan. “Your Highness, do you have some other opinion?”","Helian Xuan still looked somewhat dazed.","He seemed to have completely lost his footing, as though he had no idea what had happened. In confusion, he nodded. “Send them to the Court of Judicial Review. I would also like to know who was so vicious as to frame me with such a scheme.”","“I’ll make the arrangements myself,” Zhou Yuanshen said. “Father, I’ll leave things here to you. Prince Rong, and gentlemen, forgive my lack of hospitality.”","He turned and left.","Prince Rong looked at Helian Xuan again.","Helian Xuan appeared both innocent and uneasy. “Uncle Prince Rong, what should I do now?”","“You might want to visit the Court of Judicial Review and smooth things over, lest there be something being kept from you. It’s best to make preparations early,” Prince Rong said.","The words sounded as though he were showing great concern for Helian Xuan, but in truth, they were useless platitudes.","Who did not know that one ought to pull strings with the authorities?","What he was really telling Helian Xuan was that he could find an excuse to leave.","Whatever had happened in the Zhou family’s inner residence, there was no point in Helian Xuan staying there. Whether he was truly innocent or merely pretending, he could withdraw for now.","Helian Xuan rose to his feet.","Once he left the Duke of Chen’s residence, his expression darkened.","He asked his attendant, “What happened to Jin Shu?”","Jin Shu was his secret guard, the woman disguised as his secondary consort.","His trusted attendant replied, “Whether she succeeded or failed, she was supposed to send a signal. But no signal ever came.”","“She was discovered?” Helian Xuan asked, his expression turning sinister.","“She is cautious and has received training since childhood. She has considerable experience. She should not have been discovered so easily. This subordinate does not know what went wrong.”","Helian Xuan clenched his teeth and forced down his anger.","After a while, he asked, “What about the Fan family? Has anyone come to report?”","Seeing his master’s grim expression, the attendant hesitated. “Master...”","“Speak plainly!”","“The Fan family used the excuse that it was merely a remarriage and arranged all the banquet guests in the reception hall in the rear gardens, isolating them there.","“When the bridal sedan entered the residence, a large group of armed soldiers from the Prince of Pingxi’s estate rushed into the Fan family residence. They had just been about to act when they were subdued.”","Helian Xuan abruptly turned his head, his expression vicious. “They failed?”","After years of planning, it had actually failed so easily?","“...Yes,” the attendant said.","“Why didn’t you tell me sooner?”","“This subordinate was about to enter and report it, but Your Highness had already come out. I had only just received the news as well,” the attendant explained.","Helian Xuan leaned against the carriage wall. His chest heaved, and he could not suppress his emotions for a long while. His breathing grew rapid, and both hands clenched into fists, the veins standing out on the backs of them.","The attendant remained silent.","Only after a long time did Helian Xuan say, “What are you waiting for? Return to the residence.”","He needed to prepare himself to persuade the emperor and make His Majesty continue to trust him.","Lately, Zhou Yuanshen had done far better than Helian Xuan when it came to earning trust.","There were palace consorts who belonged to Helian Xuan’s faction, but their favor was limited.","By contrast, Consort Wu, whom Zhou Yuanshen had placed in the palace, did not appear to possess any especially remarkable beauty. She was certainly beautiful, but which palace consort was not?","The emperor’s temperament and habits were familiar to Helian Xuan as well. The beauties he had sent into the palace had likewise studied the emperor’s preferences, yet none of them had done so nearly as well as Consort Wu.","Why was Zhou Yuanshen so fortunate?","But this was not the time to dwell on that. Helian Xuan had to find a way to clear his name.","At the Duke of Chen’s residence, guests continued to arrive in an endless stream to offer their condolences.","Even though snow was still falling outside.","As a result, everyone saw the seven women being escorted away by constables from the Court of Judicial Review. Each of them was shackled.","“Who are they?”","“Why has this alarmed the Court of Judicial Review?”","The news that the women of the Prince of Andong’s residence had “killed someone” inside the Duke of Chen’s residence spread like wildfire, even faster than news of the Duke of Chen’s funeral.","It was simply too absurd.","Everyone who heard it instinctively asked, “What happened?”","They were all eager to learn the truth and uncover the details. The news spread at astonishing speed, reaching every prominent family in the capital within half a day.","“The Zhou family is finished. There have been far too many rumors about them lately.”","In the eyes of the capital’s noble and meritorious families, the foundation of a clan’s enduring wealth and influence was its good reputation.","The Cheng family was a perfect example.","The Wu Commandery Cheng clan had never been associated with any scandalous rumors, much less news that shook the entire realm. When a particular noble house was constantly linked to words such as “assassination,” “a widowed sister-in-law plotting against her cousin,” and “an old matriarch dying a tragic death,” that family lost the halo of respect surrounding a distinguished lineage.","Building that halo was extraordinarily difficult. Destroying it, however, took only an instant.","The Zhou family’s Dowager Madame had spent her entire life pursuing the words “a pure and honorable household.” She had never attained them—not even by the time she died.","Families with discerning eyes judged the Duke of Chen’s residence by these events and reached their own conclusions about its future.","When it came to reputation, the Zhou family had suffered a complete defeat."]},{"number":244,"title":"Chapter 244: Epilogue (4)","paragraphs":["After the bailiffs from the Dali Temple left, the stone steps outside the Duke of Chen’s residence were even muddier.","They were covered in a mixture of snowmelt and mud.","But no one cared.","The members of the Cheng family were preparing to take their leave as well.","“Fourth Brother, thank you!” Zhou Yuanshen cupped his hands toward Cheng Chao, then said to Cheng Ying, “I’m sorry to have gotten Third Sister injured.”","Cheng Ying smiled faintly. “It’s only a minor injury. Nothing to worry about.”","Cheng Chao also told him not to stand on ceremony.","“Thank you for today, Fourth Brother.” Cheng Zhao rarely showed Cheng Chao such respect. “You noticed that something was wrong, and with one strike, you slashed that assassin’s face. You forced her to reveal her true identity. That was both brave and clever!”","Whether man or woman, anyone whose cheek was slashed would instinctively become completely guarded and fight back.","It had nothing to do with vanity. It was an intense sense of danger.","The head was vital yet fragile, and the face was particularly vulnerable to injury. The moment it was wounded, a person would feel as if they were facing a formidable enemy. Before reason had time to intervene, the brain would already compel them to strike back.","Cheng Chao had identified this weakness precisely.","He had easily broken through the assassin’s most vulnerable defense.","“It’s rare to hear you say something nice about me,” Cheng Chao remarked with a sigh.","The people present could not help laughing.","Zhou Yuanshen continued, “I have another favor to ask.”","Everyone put away their smiles.","Cheng Zhao glanced at him as well.","“The Duke Protector General’s residence will probably need some matters settled afterward. I can’t leave now, and I don’t dare depart rashly. I’d like to ask all of you to go to the Fan residence and take a look at the situation. If it’s convenient, send someone back to report to me. You’re different from ordinary attendants—you’re able to see through certain problems.”","Cheng Chao asked, “What happened at the Fan residence? Wasn’t a wedding being held there today?”","“Many years ago, two generals served under my maternal grandfather. They were bitter rivals. General Wei was exceptionally talented at strategy, but narrow-minded. General Xu was brave and skilled in battle, but hot-tempered. The two of them were at odds for seven or eight years. After General Wei’s younger son died, their conflict escalated to the point where one of them had to die.","“General Wei falsely accused General Xu of treason and had all the evidence prepared. My maternal grandfather believed him at the time and ordered men to arrest General Xu.","“General Xu had an impulsive nature. He resisted and fled. My maternal grandfather ordered his men to pursue him, so General Xu killed himself to prove his innocence. His wife and children fled. Later, it was proven that he truly had been innocent.","“This caused my maternal grandfather years of regret. Even on his deathbed, he could not let it go. He ordered us to continue searching for the Xu family’s surviving relatives, and he wanted to clear General Xu’s name.”","Zhou Yuanshen spoke very slowly.","The story was not complicated and was easy enough to understand.","Political persecution did not occur only at court; it happened in frontier armies as well.","Both men were great generals with the potential to become marshals one day. They had been at odds for years, and their minor conflicts had gradually accumulated into a major feud. Once a death was involved, their hostility became irreconcilable.","However, Cheng Zhao and the others did not understand why he had suddenly brought up this old affair.","“...Vice Minister Song’s ancestral home is in Songyang Prefecture. When I heard that name, I became wary, because I discovered that the last place where General Xu’s wife and children disappeared was near Songyang Prefecture.","“Bandits have run rampant there in recent years. Their tactics are refined and their knowledge of military strategy is impressive. They don’t seem like ordinary bandits. General Xu’s two sons also grew up with the border troops, just as I did.","“I sent people to investigate in secret. Vice Minister Song himself has no apparent problems, but his daughter is highly suspicious. The temple where she has been cultivating in seclusion has been attacked by bandits several times, yet she has always remained unharmed.","“She was probably being controlled, or perhaps she was bribed and willingly worked for them. There are also signs that Prince of Andong had bribed officials in Songyang Prefecture.","“The marriage was arranged so hastily, with the excuse that they feared Duke of Pi. I suspect someone is manipulating things behind the scenes. If I told my maternal uncle and grandmother, they might soften and let the matter go.","“The massacre that year was the result of the conflict between the Xu and Wei families. At most, my maternal grandfather had been negligent. If my maternal uncle and grandmother took pity on the survivors and spared them, those people would not be grateful. They would simply wait for another opportunity to rise again.","“Besides, they had become bandits over the years, plundering and robbing countless people and committing grave crimes. I kept this from my maternal uncle and did not tell him beforehand. Instead, I dispatched fifty of my personal guards from the general’s residence. Only after my maternal uncle had gone to escort the bride did I send someone to inform my grandmother.","“The matter over there should be over by now, and the losses ought to be minor. I’d like to ask you to go and see what happened.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","Her eldest sister asked, “This wasn’t a wedding at all, but a planned massacre meant to wipe out the entire Fan clan?”","“Yes.”","“Such a serious matter, and you waited until the bridal sedan was almost at the gate before telling us?” her eldest sister asked again.","“Yes.”","Her eldest sister: “...”","Cheng Zhao found it both infuriating and absurd. She could not help laughing.","Third Sister said, “Let’s go take a look. Though the plan was risky, it was like catching turtles in a jar, and the odds of victory were extremely high. Yuanshen truly deserves his reputation as a battle-seasoned general.”","Cheng Zhao found those words pleasing to hear.","Perhaps a trace of a smile had appeared on her face, because Third Sister glanced at her with a smile. Cheng Zhao immediately schooled her expression.","The Cheng family left, while Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen returned to Chengming Hall.","The Second Madam had already departed.","The maid said, “Madam said she was too tired. She went back to change and rest, and will return in an hour.”","Cheng Zhao could understand.","The Second Madam must have been terrified just now. There had been a fight, too.","The entire reception hall was in disarray, with bloodstains and broken porcelain scattered across the floor.","Cheng Zhao’s clothes were soaked through with sweat, and she now felt cold. She sneezed. Zhou Yuanshen’s shoes, socks, and trouser legs were all drenched with snowmelt, and he had lost all feeling in them from the cold.","“Bring in a bucket of hot water,” Cheng Zhao ordered.","The maid acknowledged the command.","Cheng Zhao divided half the water between them, quickly wiped herself down, and changed into clean underclothes. Zhou Yuanshen also tidied himself up without delay.","The couple sat facing the window on the heated brick bed, each holding a cup of hot tea, yet they still felt cold.","The chill had penetrated deep into their lungs, and it would take a while to warm up.","“Surely there were no casualties at the Fan residence?” Cheng Zhao asked.","“Mingyu returned to report that two deputy commanders suffered minor injuries, but everyone else is fine. The wedding escort consisted of more than thirty people, and they were all captured—including the bride,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao asked, “Who was the bride? One of General Xu’s subordinates, or his daughter?”","“His daughter. She had disguised herself and taken Miss Song’s place. Miss Song had been away from home for nearly nine years. Her parents and relatives only thought she had changed somewhat, so they didn’t look too closely into the reason.”","Cheng Zhao sighed.","“Mother doesn’t know yet. She’s bound to be disappointed. She’s been constantly concerned about my maternal uncle’s marriage.”","When the Second Madam had heard that Fan Xiao was going to marry, she had been overjoyed, as though a heavy burden had finally been lifted from her shoulders.","As the eldest sister, she regarded her younger brother as practically half a son. He was nearly thirty and still all alone. How could she not worry about him?","“His match simply hasn’t arrived yet,” Zhou Yuanshen said. “My maternal uncle already has someone in his heart.”","“Who?” Cheng Zhao momentarily forgot the cold and leaned a little closer.","Zhou Yuanshen said, “I probably don’t know her. He didn’t say. But he must have someone he loves but cannot have. Whenever he mentioned getting married, every sentence sounded like he was trying to comfort himself by saying, ‘I’ll just accept my fate.’”","Cheng Zhao said, “Go find out.”","Zhou Yuanshen glanced at her.","For the first time, Cheng Zhao saw an expression of difficulty on his face.","He had always been clear about right and wrong. If something could be done, he said so; if it could not, he said that too.","“All right, all right. You don’t have to ask around. I’ll have Mother and Zhou Yuanqi investigate next time,” Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi would certainly be willing to handle this sort of matter.","“...I’ll look into it for you. There’s no need to involve Yuanqi.” Zhou Yuanshen seemed to steel himself, gritting his teeth as he agreed.","Cheng Zhao hadn’t meant to provoke him, yet it seemed he had achieved precisely that: Zhou Yuanshen was unwilling to lose to his younger brother...","How had he become so childish too? Why was he competing with a child like Yuanqi?","Cheng Zhao slowly finished his cup of tea.","The warmth eased him, and his mood lightened somewhat.","“Yuanshen, was Helian Xuan the one manipulating today’s chain of schemes from behind the scenes?” Cheng Zhao asked him."]},{"number":245,"title":"Chapter 245: Epilogue (5)","paragraphs":["After Cheng Zhao finished her tea, Zhou Yuanshen poured her another cup.","He set down the teapot and said in an even tone, “It was him.”","Cheng Zhao asked, “The Fan family’s marriage proposal, Grandmother’s death, and arranging for people to enter the inner residence today—what does he want?”","Zhou Yuanshen raised his eyes.","Cheng Zhao looked incredulous. “To kidnap me?”","“Yes.”","“...Has everything gone too smoothly for him all these years, making him this arrogant?”","Did Helian Xuan look down on everyone, believing that the Cheng, Fan, and Zhou families were all fools? Or did he think the entire world was under his control?","“He wants to cast a great net over the Zhou and Fan families, then fish in the troubled waters,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","He had been buying off corrupt officials everywhere and making them work for him.","He had also allied himself with the bandits of Songyang Prefecture—the Xu clan members who had escaped.","He sold them information about wealthy merchants, allowing them to rob those merchants blind, and provided them with the protection of corrupt local officials.","The Xu children had grown powerful in Songyang Prefecture in a very short time, becoming a band of ruthless bandits that even the imperial court found troublesome. They had money and weapons.","And they wanted revenge.","General Wei and his family were still stationed at the border. He had received no promotions over the years, and the Xu children could not reach him. The Fan family was in the capital. They resented the Wei family, and they likewise hated Old General Fan, who had once commanded the army.","Without Helian Xuan arranging the connection, it would have been difficult for them to infiltrate the capital.","First, he would have the marriage settled. Then he would arrange for Lady Huan to poison the Dowager Madame.","If everything went smoothly, the Fan family’s wedding and the Zhou family’s funeral would take place around the same time. Even if there were some discrepancy, they would be no more than a few days apart.","The bride’s first task would be to assassinate the Fan family’s Old Dowager, followed by Fan Xiao.","Once the two of them were dead, someone from the Fan family would immediately come to the Zhou residence to deliver the news. Zhou Yuanshen and his parents would certainly rush to the Fan residence at once.","And with the Zhou family still holding a funeral, someone would have to remain behind to oversee everything.","That person would be Cheng Zhao, left alone.","As it happened, Prince of Andong would come to offer condolences.","His female relatives would enter the inner residence to pay their respects. Even if Cheng Zhao disliked the consort’s extravagance and ostentation, she would not be overly wary of her.","With several highly skilled maids accompanying the hidden guards, capturing Cheng Zhao would be effortless. Taking her away would be as easy as reaching into a bag.","By then, Helian Xuan would sever all ties with the hidden guards and refuse to acknowledge that the women belonged to him, shifting all the blame onto the Xu bandits, who had supposedly murdered the Fan family.","In the midst of such chaos, who would be able to find Cheng Zhao?","As for what happened afterward, that was not something he needed to consider yet.","“What a vicious man, and what a wicked scheme!” Cheng Zhao said. “Every step of his plan is well thought out. He simply underestimated other people’s alertness and connections.”","Zhou Yuanshen had known for some time that Helian Xuan was stirring up trouble in Songyang Prefecture and bribing officials. He had even followed the trail leading to Helian Xuan and found the Xu children.","Through the channels of the underworld, Fan Xiao had learned that Helian Xuan was buying medicine and meeting with Lady Huan.","Helian Xuan thought he had concealed everything perfectly.","But he was not the only man in the world with the means to uncover the truth.","He had come personally to the Zhou residence today, waiting for news from the Fan family so that he could accomplish his goal. He had never expected every step of his plan to fail.","“Yuanshen, we have to find a way to eliminate him,” Cheng Zhao said. “This man’s ambitions are too great. I’m afraid...”","“Are you afraid that he’ll use his hunger for power to plunge the realm into civil war?” Zhou Yuanshen asked.","Cheng Zhao nodded firmly.","He understood her after all.","“Over the years, several rebellions have been suppressed, but the state of the court is such that the people have long been discontented. The slightest spark could become a blaze that engulfs the heavens,” Cheng Zhao said.","The administration of every province and prefecture was corrupt. Capable ministers at court had withdrawn from public life. The princes and the generals stationed throughout the realm were all waiting for an excuse—one with a justifiable cause.","It was like a river swollen with water. Its force could already be seen, and the embankments were on the verge of collapse.","Helian Xuan needed only to create an excuse to breach the embankments. In an instant, a devastating flood would sweep across the entire realm.","Helian Xuan would not need to clean up the aftermath. He needed only chaos.","“Cheng Zhao, you’re frightened, aren’t you?” Zhou Yuanshen asked as he rose and came over to embrace her.","Cheng Zhao nodded again.","Of course she was afraid.","No one could escape unscathed from a war. Everyone would be swept up in its violence.","She wanted to live through peaceful times and become a venerable old lady, enjoying a life of wealth and tranquility with a future she could see clearly.","She liked taking paths whose destination was certain.","“I’ll do everything I can to stop him,” Zhou Yuanshen said quietly. “But the outlook isn’t good. He has been laying his plans for many years. Perhaps he and his father began preparing to seize the realm long ago.”","For no apparent reason, Cheng Zhao shivered.","She leaned against Zhou Yuanshen’s embrace, drawing a little warmth from him.","By the time the Cheng siblings arrived at the Grand General Protector’s residence, the snow had stopped.","As soon as they stepped down from the carriage, they ran into Fan Xiao, who was about to leave.","Fan Xiao froze.","“Senior Brother Du?” He noticed Du Anli first.","“How is everything at home?” Du Anli asked.","The others climbed down from the carriages one after another.","Fan Xiao saw Cheng Ying among them. Her face was somewhat pale, and one sleeve was in disarray, wrapped in a handkerchief. Blood had seeped through it, spreading like a flower in bloom.","He did not answer Du Anli. Instead, he asked, “Where have you all come from?”","“The Duke of Chen’s residence.”","“Has something happened to Yuanshen?” Fan Xiao asked anxiously.","“It’s been dealt with,” Du Anli replied. “My brother-in-law asked us to come and check on things here.”","“Only two people suffered minor injuries. We caught the bandits and sent them all to the authorities. I was about to go to the yamen.”","He paused, then added, “It can wait until tomorrow. Please, come in.”","He ushered them into the Grand General Protector’s residence.","The residence had been preparing to host a wedding banquet that morning. Red lanterns hung by the entrance, while wedding couplets and the character for “double happiness” adorned the doors.","Cheng Ying fell a few steps behind. Just as she crossed the Grand General Protector’s residence’s high threshold, Fan Xiao happened to step inside as well.","He turned to glance at her.","She looked straight ahead, her expression calm and indifferent, as though the vulgarities of the mortal world were separated from her by a thin veil.","She seemed detached from all worldly things.","Fan Xiao quickly withdrew his gaze. Something in his chest felt as though it had been pierced sharply.","The Cheng family went to see the Old Dowager.","Cheng Han, the eldest daughter of the Cheng family, reassured her repeatedly. “There were no casualties, and the vicious bandits were caught and removed from the people’s midst. This is good fortune. Master Fan’s destined marriage simply hasn’t arrived yet.”","The Old Dowager was calmer than Zhou Yuanshen had imagined.","With a composed expression, she nodded. “Indeed, it is fortunate. Ah Xiao’s marriage has, in a way, spared the people of Songyang Prefecture from disaster.”","“I’m glad you can see it that way. Don’t let worry harm your health. Yuanshen and his wife will be anxious,” Cheng Han said with a smile.","She offered a few more words of comfort.","When the Old Dowager noticed Cheng Ying, she asked, “Is the injury serious?”","“Only a flesh wound.”","“I would never have guessed that you practiced swordsmanship,” the Old Dowager remarked.","Cheng Ying replied, “A distant relative came to seek refuge with our family. She was proud and strong-willed. My mother worried that she would not want to stay with us for long, and that she would have no way to make a living if she left, so she asked the woman to teach my sisters and me how to use the sword. Her swordsmanship is exceptional.”","“You’ve followed her in practice for many years? That must not have been easy. Swordsmanship is tedious and exhausting,” the Old Dowager said.","Cheng Ying answered, “I’m used to it.”","The Old Dowager found her aura unusually refined. The slight injury only made her appear more aloof, as though she did not belong to the mortal world. She had not expected Cheng Ying to practice the sword, and found it rather surprising.","After some idle conversation and confirming that everything was stable and properly handled at the Fan residence, the Cheng family finally relaxed.","Cheng Han’s husband, Du Anli, went with Fan Xiao to the Duke of Chen’s residence, while the others returned home.","After resting, Zhou Yuanshen returned to the mourning tent, where he spoke at length with Du Anli and Fan Xiao.","“You really should have told me beforehand,” Fan Xiao said.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, “I was afraid you wouldn’t be able to keep it to yourself. We might have alerted them and lost the chance to wipe them all out.”","True enough.","Fan Xiao let out another sigh.","They had won, but it was a miserable victory—nothing to be happy about. Like the winter sun, no matter how bright it shone, it could not dispel the bitter cold that blanketed the world."]},{"number":246,"title":"Chapter 246: Epilogue (6)","paragraphs":["Old Madam Zhou lay in state for twenty-one days before being buried in the Zhou family ancestral graveyard.","During that time, when Vice Minister Song came to the Zhou residence to offer condolences, he spoke with Zhou Yuanshen and the Second Master about his daughter.","“...Brother Pei helped me. The bandits of Songyang Prefecture ‘admitted’ that they had killed my daughter and replaced her with someone else,” Vice Minister Song said.","His expression was dim, and he sighed after finishing.","Brother Pei was Pei Yanhe, the Minister of the Dali Temple and his close friend and former classmate. The two had always shared a deep personal friendship. Even after rising in rank, Pei Yanhe had never forgotten to support him.","Not only had Pei Yanhe helped smooth his way through official circles, he had also arranged a marriage for his daughter, hoping to put a complete end to the matter involving Duke Pi.","Although the Fan family came from a military background, their integrity was unexpectedly unyielding. Vice Minister Song found this most gratifying.","His daughter was nearly thirty, yet she had somehow been blessed with such a stroke of good fortune. A great weight had finally lifted from Vice Minister Song’s heart.","Who could have imagined that his daughter would become entangled with a female bandit?","She and Miss Xu had become close friends simply because Miss Xu had once saved her life. And his daughter had even privately pledged herself to the son of a local gentry family.","“...Her parents raised her and made every possible arrangement for her. They were even willing to risk their family’s fortune and their lives to protect her. When they offended Duke Pi for her sake, they were also offending Consort Dou and the Fifth Prince. The lives of the entire Song clan were hanging by a thread.","“She has forgotten all the kindness of those who gave her life and raised her. Yet because someone else saved her once, she was willing to take such a risk for that person, even if it meant placing the entire Song clan in danger once again.”","The more Vice Minister Song spoke, the quieter his voice became.","He was deeply disappointed.","And utterly bewildered.","He prided himself on clearly distinguishing right from wrong and understanding the greater principles. How could his daughter have become so foolish?","If he and his wife had mistreated her in any way, Vice Minister Song could have understood why she had aided evil.","But unfortunately...","“She has been away from home for nine years. A person can become very lonely. Someone took advantage of that loneliness and gained her trust. She may have been wrong, but how could she withstand another person’s deliberate scheming?” the Second Master said from the side.","He continued, “Anyone who means to manipulate you will target your weakest point. Don’t blame the child, and don’t let your heart grow cold toward her.”","Vice Minister Song sighed softly.","The Second Master added, “Taking advantage of the chaos to make it seem as though she was killed by ‘bandits’ and then erasing her existence may not be a bad thing. She can live a more peaceful life from now on.”","“The bandits are all admitting to it now. They only want to stay alive. Before this, they had still hoped to bring her back, which was why they hadn’t said she was ‘dead.’ But now, they have no choice except to let her ‘die,’” Vice Minister Song replied.","Zhou Yuanshen said, “As a father, you have done everything you could, both out of kindness and affection.”","Vice Minister Song’s eyes filled with tears.","He was furious with his daughter, yet he could not stop himself from feeling heartbroken.","“I’ve been unable to get away all these years. The government office keeps me busy from dawn to dusk, and I never once went to see her. If only I had gone even once, perhaps I would have recognized at first glance that the woman who returned to the capital was an impostor. Then none of this would have happened,” Vice Minister Song said.","If he had exposed the impostor, he could have brought his daughter home. Perhaps she really could have married Fan Xiao.","The Fan family was an excellent choice, and a marriage alliance with them would have given the Song family a powerful connection. Even if his daughter was angry and refused to speak to him, knowing that she was living well would have allowed Vice Minister Song to rest easy for the remainder of his life.","But it was too late.","For the rest of his life, whenever he thought of this youngest daughter, there would be a thorn in his heart. It would prick him whenever he was happy, or in the stillness of the night when he was alone with his thoughts.","Zhou Yuanshen, however, said, “It’s fortunate that you didn’t recognize her. The moment you exposed her, they would have wiped out your entire family. They came with a purpose—how could they have spared the lives of your family members? Vice Minister Song, you have saved your entire family once again.”","Vice Minister Song’s expression changed.","He had never considered that possibility. A sudden chill ran through him, and he broke out in a cold sweat.","“They didn’t kill your daughter only because she was foolish and believed she had no value to them. They thought it made no difference whether she lived or died.","“Look at it this way: you blame her for being foolish, but perhaps it was precisely because of that foolishness that she survived. When someone with a plan schemes against someone who is unprepared, there is no way to guard against everything.”","Vice Minister Song suddenly saw the truth of the matter.","Only at that moment did he truly understand what had happened.","His anger, resentment, unwillingness, and regret all turned into relief.","After he left, the Second Master let out a quiet sigh.","“We finally managed to calm him down. ‘Long-held guilt turns into hatred.’ We can’t allow him to keep feeling that he owes your maternal uncle,” the Second Master said.","Guilt was a dangerous emotion. Like a great favor, it was extremely delicate and could not be allowed to remain in a person’s heart for too long.","That was why the ancients said that excessive guilt could lead a person to seek death.","Vice Minister Song had come to speak of these matters today because he felt unbearably ashamed. His guilt had become overwhelming. The Second Master and Zhou Yuanshen were both shrewd men, and they had quickly noticed his state of mind.","They had comforted him and told him not to dwell on the matter.","He and his daughter were both victims of this affair—survivors. He did not need to feel indebted to anyone.","Zhou Yuanshen gave a slight nod.","The funeral for Old Madam Zhou came to an end. The weather was fine on the day she was buried. It had been clear for several days, neither damp nor windy, and there was even a hint of warmth in the air.","After the burial, the members of the clan and the servants all departed. Only several members of the Second Branch remained standing before the grave.","“Your Fourth Brother didn’t return to attend the funeral. Will people use that against him in the future?” the Second Madam asked.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, “Loyalty to the country takes precedence over filial piety. He is guarding the border and cannot leave without an imperial edict. No one will be able to attack him over this.”","The Second Madam’s worry was put to rest.","The soil of the new grave was still damp. The outermost layer soon froze into a thin sheet of frost, like the hair of someone who had aged overnight.","Only after Old Madam Zhou was buried did it come time for Huan Qingtang’s funeral.","Huan Qingtang was young and had neither a husband nor a son, so her funeral was extremely simple. Few people came to pay their respects.","Only three relatives from her mother’s family attended.","Among her closest relations—her maternal uncle, aunts, and others—not a single one had even sent a representative.","Her body lay in state for seven days before she was buried. Her new grave was positioned below Old Madam Zhou’s, on lower ground.","After the two funerals were finally concluded, it was the fifteenth day of the twelfth lunar month, with the New Year approaching.","“How shall we spend the New Year this year?” the Second Madam asked Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao replied, “Quietly. We are all in mourning, so we’ll stay behind closed doors and live our own lives. We won’t host any banquets or attend anyone else’s.”","“That sounds good. Perhaps it will be a peaceful, tranquil New Year,” the Second Madam said.","She then added, “If only Yuanjin could return. He’s still accompanying his maternal uncle, and we don’t know when he’ll be able to come back to the capital.”","“Perhaps he’ll return next year,” Cheng Zhao said.","The Second Madam held on to the same hope.","That New Year, the Duke’s residence enjoyed an unusually quiet celebration.","On New Year’s Eve, Cheng Zhao sent someone to summon Xian Si to Chengming Hall.","She said to Xian Si, “Old Madam Zhou has passed away. The Emperor may not continue to keep you in the Duke’s residence. You now have two possible paths ahead of you.”","Either she would enter the palace, or she would be sentenced to death.","Xian Si lowered her head.","“Will you make your decision soon, or will you wait?” Cheng Zhao asked her.","The couple had promised Xian Si that they would help her, and Xian Si had seized the opportunity firmly. She would not abandon everything halfway merely because Old Madam Zhou had died.","If Xian Si wished to fake her death and escape, Zhou Yuanshen could find a way to send her away. If the Emperor grew angry, he would bear the consequences himself.","“Second Concubine, you don’t need to answer me right away. You can wait until after the fifteenth day of the first lunar month,” Cheng Zhao said.","Xian Si slowly lifted her eyes.","She was far too soft. Her waist, honed by years of dancing, was supple and seemingly boneless, and there was the same softness in her gaze.","Yet this was the first time Cheng Zhao had seen determination in her eyes.","“Madam, I am willing to wait,” Xian Si said.","She did not want to leave again.","She was simply too beautiful. Without powerful protection, her beauty would invite covetous eyes wherever she went. To travel far from home with such a face was like a child walking through a marketplace while carrying a piece of gold. She would never come to a good end.","Entering the palace was the best path available to her. If that proved impossible, she was willing to grow old and die within the inner residence of the Duke’s household. Even if she had to remain behind closed doors and never venture out, she would still have enough to eat and wear.","She did not want to be seized and sold.","If the Duchess was worried about her, afraid that she might try to seduce the Duke, she could deliberately eat until she was plump over the course of three months.","Xian Si did not say any of this. She merely gazed steadily at Cheng Zhao.","“In that case, wait,” Cheng Zhao said.","Xian Si went back.","She did not have to wait long.","The Emperor soon remembered her. On New Year’s Eve, dancers had performed for the court, but no one could dance as well as Xian Si. At the New Year’s Day court assembly, the Emperor specifically kept Zhou Yuanshen behind and asked about Xian Si.","Zhou Yuanshen said, “...Just say she is a palace maid from Consort Wu’s quarters who has earned His Majesty’s favor. She can be made a Beauty.”","The Emperor considered it. “Make her a Jieyu as well. Promote Consort Wu to Zhaoyi.”","That evening, Xian Si entered the palace.","“I have fulfilled what I promised her. From now on, her fortunes and misfortunes are hers to bear,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao could not put her feelings into words.","This was the path Xian Si had chosen, and she was willing to walk it. In a life where she had never been given a choice, she had managed to choose a road for herself. Cheng Zhao thought she was remarkable."]},{"number":247,"title":"Chapter 247: Epilogue (7)","paragraphs":["The Zhou family had a quiet New Year.","No one went out to have fun. Cheng Zhao and the Second Madam did not return to their parents’ homes either. Every day was spent eating and drinking, playing cuju, practicing with spears, playing chess, and bickering.","“...Zhaozhao, when are you going to dismiss the household servants?” the Second Madam asked.","After the two funerals, Cheng Zhao had used the excuse that she needed more help and transferred all the servants who had come with her into the residence.","It was perfectly reasonable.","During those turbulent times, they had come into contact with the stewards and servants of the Duke of Chen’s residence, and the two groups had gotten to know one another.","During the New Year, the stewards took turns taking leave, while the servants also had time to spare.","Cheng Zhao said that she wanted to dismiss half the household’s stewards and servants. She would give each of them a generous sum of money and return their contracts of servitude to them.","The Second Madam asked when she intended to do this.","“I plan to wait until after the fifteenth day of the first lunar month,” Cheng Zhao said. “The government offices won’t reopen until then either.”","Then she asked, “Mother, do you want to recruit more people or dismiss them?”","“...This concerns Longevity Peace Court,” the Second Madam said. “Everyone there is the Dowager Madame’s trusted confidant. What do you plan to do?”","She continued, “Never mind the others. Nanny Sun is still there, and the Head Steward and his wife are also loyal to the Dowager Madame.”","“For those who are advanced in years, I’ll give them a generous retirement payment. They can return to their hometowns, build houses, buy a few acres of land, and enjoy their later years,” Cheng Zhao said.","“Are you dismissing Nanny Sun and the Head Steward and his wife as well?”","“If they don’t want to leave, I’ll arrange for them to serve at Clear Breeze Court and have them look after the residence,” Cheng Zhao said.","The Second Madam said, “But you absolutely cannot keep them here! Especially Nanny Sun. She’s sinister, like a poisonous snake. If she stays in the household, she’ll cause trouble for you.”","Cheng Zhao nodded. “I’ll be careful. I’ll discuss it with the Head Steward and his wife first and ask them to persuade Nanny Sun as well.”","She added, “I intend to give the Head Steward and Nanny Sun three thousand taels each as retirement pay.”","“That isn’t all that much. Their annual wages are more than two hundred taels. If the Dowager Madame hadn’t died, they would have had to work for at least another twenty years before retiring. Three thousand taels sounds like a lot, but they may feel that they’re losing out,” the Second Madam said.","She continued, “Still, with the Dowager Madame gone, they’ll have to leave sooner or later. If they leave this year, they’ll get three thousand taels. If they wait a few more years, they may get nothing at all. They’ll have to decide for themselves.”","Cheng Zhao nodded.","“Take care of it soon,” the Second Madam said.","Cheng Zhao knew that the Second Madam could never keep anything to herself for long. Smiling, she said, “All right. I’ll tell the Head Steward later. I’ll give them some time to consider it. This is a major matter.”","The Second Madam nodded.","On the fifth day of the first lunar month, Cheng Zhao summoned the Head Steward to Hall of Lasting Brightness.","The Head Steward happened to be on duty that day. He had taken six days off around the New Year.","Cheng Zhao explained her plan to him.","The Head Steward visibly relaxed.","Three thousand taels in retirement pay had probably exceeded his expectations, and he was very satisfied.","In the capital, three thousand taels was enough to buy a decent two-courtyard residence, leaving him with a home of his own. Or he could return to his hometown, buy some land, and build a house. Either way, he would be able to live quite comfortably.","Besides, he must have accumulated some savings over the years.","With an excellent way out available to him, most of the unease in his heart disappeared.","“The Duchess is kind-hearted and pities this old and feeble man. I’m willing to leave the residence of my own accord,” the Head Steward said.","He did not say that he would consider it. Instead, he agreed readily.","Cheng Zhao secretly breathed a sigh of relief as well.","“Nanny Sun has served the Dowager Madame, and her usual monthly wages are even higher than yours. Since she is leaving, I can only give her the same retirement payment as you. I can’t give her more than you receive.","“Please go and ask whether she is willing to leave. The Dowager Madame has passed away, and Nanny Sun is heartbroken. I’m afraid she may be upset and misunderstand my intentions. If I speak to her myself, she may think I’m discarding her after she has served her purpose, which would only make things more difficult,” Cheng Zhao said.","The Head Steward quickly agreed. “I’ll go speak with her.”","Nanny Sun was still at Longevity Peace Court.","She was deeply devoted to her mourning duties and knelt in the mourning hall every day to keep vigil for the Dowager Madame.","The atmosphere inside Longevity Peace Court was gloomy and eerie.","The maids and senior servants all cowered in their rooms like quails, trembling.","The underfloor heating was no longer lit. It was bitterly cold both inside and out. Perhaps because of the cold, everyone’s face had taken on a bluish cast, making them look as though they were possessed.","The Head Steward was startled.","He immediately regretted coming alone. He should have brought several strong young servants to give him courage.","He steeled himself and walked inside.","Nanny Sun was kneeling before the Buddha. Her appearance was even more haggard and disheveled than before.","The Head Steward stood beside her, but she did not get up. She continued chanting prayers.","“...The Duchess sent me to ask you about this. If there’s anything you disagree with, just tell me, and I’ll report it back to Her Grace,” the Head Steward said.","Nanny Sun did not answer.","The Head Steward thought she might not speak at all. Just as he was wondering what to do, she finally said, “Tell the Duchess to come and speak to me herself.”","The Head Steward was speechless.","Who did she think she was?","Even he, who now managed everyone in the residence, had to personally go to Hall of Lasting Brightness to receive the Duchess’s instructions.","She was a noblewoman of the highest rank, while Nanny Sun was merely a servant. Never mind that she had served the Dowager Madame—even if she had served the Empress Dowager, she still had no right to put on such airs.","The Head Steward fell silent, unsure how to respond.","As if she had seen through his thoughts, Nanny Sun said coolly, “Go tell her. Whether she comes or not is her affair, and has nothing to do with you.”","“Nanny Sun...”","“If you have nothing else to ask, then leave. This is the Dowager Madame’s residence. Be careful, or you may suffer retribution,” Nanny Sun said.","The Head Steward left the residence.","His good days were almost within reach, and he had no desire to get entangled in this matter.","In any case, he was not the one who had incited Nanny Sun. If he simply reported her words, the Duchess should be able to understand.","He repeated Nanny Sun’s exact words to Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao was not surprised in the slightest.","“The Dowager Madame’s people deserve to be treated with dignity. I’ll go see her,” she said.","Taking Nanny Li, Suyue, and Qiubai with her, Cheng Zhao went to Longevity Peace Court.","Nanny Li was highly wary. “Perhaps we should call a few more people.”","“Mother, if she wants to harm me, she’ll attack my mind, not my body,” Cheng Zhao said. “I’ll hear what she has to say.”","Then she flashed a sly smile. “I think she wants to talk about jade-skin pastries. Shall we make a wager?”","Nanny Li was speechless. “...And you can still joke at a time like this? You’re far too calm!”","Cheng Zhao stepped into the residence.","Unlike the Head Steward, she was not afraid of ghosts. Nor was she surprised by the current state of Longevity Peace Court.","She went to the small Buddhist hall.","Nanny Sun was still kneeling.","Before her stood a divine statue, solemn and magnificent, radiating majesty.","Cheng Zhao knelt on the prayer mat beside her and bowed three times to the statue.","“...Nanny Sun, the Head Steward said you wanted to see me?” Cheng Zhao spoke first.","If she did not speak, Nanny Sun would remain silent as well.","“Cheng Shi, you’re the one asking me for something now, not the other way around. If I were to die here in the Duke of Chen’s residence...”","“I would simply say that you had been praying at Clear Breeze Court. You are a bondservant whose contract is in my possession. Even if I beat you to death, do you really think the government offices would arrest me?” Cheng Zhao said coolly.","Nanny Sun’s haggard cheek twitched violently.","“I’m willing to treat you well only to set an example for the other servants, so they won’t feel abandoned when their old master is gone. If you make trouble, I’ll be delighted.","“From then on, no matter how I treat you, the stewards and servants will all say you deserved it, while I, the new mistress, did everything I could for you. I’m only afraid you won’t make trouble,” Cheng Zhao continued.","Nanny Sun’s lips began to tremble as well.","“If you make a scene, I’ll save the three thousand taels in support money. Let me make this clear: since you don’t want it, I’ll distribute it among the others. From now on, no one will speak a word on your behalf,” Cheng Zhao added.","Nanny Sun was furious to the point of trembling all over. She lay prostrate on the prayer mat."]},{"number":248,"title":"Chapter 248: Epilogue (8)","paragraphs":["Mother Sun was furious.","Suyue was terrified that her mistress might actually anger Nanny Sun to death.","After a long while, Nanny Sun finally steadied herself. Slowly straightening, she looked at Cheng Zhao. “I kept a trump card. The moment I die, someone will inform the Emperor that you are the orphaned daughter of Prince Jin and Commandery Princess Zhaoyang.”","“I know. Back then, of the late Emperor’s five legitimate sons, three died in the struggle for the throne. Only Prince Jin and the Tenth Prince, who had not yet been granted a princely title, remained. The latter is His Majesty.","“When the Northern Di surrendered, the late Emperor sent Prince Jin to the northwest to handle affairs, giving him the chance to win the army’s loyalty. Once he returned to the capital, he was to be made Crown Prince.","“Prince Jin’s betrothed—the Commandery Princess Zhaoyang—was very fond of fun and followed him to the frontier. Prince Jin had intended to consolidate his influence over the army, but the Zhou family unexpectedly discovered evidence that he had been secretly colluding with the Northern Di.","“To destroy the evidence, Prince Jin even caused the death of the Zhou family’s eldest master. The late Emperor felt guilty toward the Zhou family and was grateful that they had protected his only surviving legitimate son. That was why he granted Old General Zhou the title of ‘Duke of Chen.’” Cheng Zhao spoke calmly.","Nanny Sun abruptly turned to look at her.","Cheng Zhao continued, “Back then, Grand Madam sent the Commandery Princess Zhaoyang away on the pretext of inviting her to eat jade dumpling cakes. Afterward, the Commandery Princess escaped because the Tenth Prince could not bear to kill her.","“Grand Madam exhausted every means to find her, yet suddenly discovered a horribly disfigured corpse supposedly belonging to her. Grand Madam believed it was a substitute.","“So when I presented the jade dumpling cakes, you suspected that I was the daughter of the Commandery Princess Zhaoyang? Since you suspected it, why didn’t you tell the Emperor and have him kill me?","“Could it be that the Commandery Princess was actually captured by you, and that the Emperor did something to her? Is that why you absolutely dare not tell him that she might have had a child?”","Cold sweat poured down Nanny Sun’s face.","“How about I go tell the Emperor?” Cheng Zhao asked. “Perhaps I really am his daughter. What would he do then? Show gratitude to the Zhou family for killing people and paving the way for him time and again—or dig up Grand Madam’s grave?”","Nanny Sun collapsed onto the floor, unable even to sit steadily. “You—you really are...”","Cheng Zhao gazed at her quietly. “What do you think?”","Nanny Sun seemed unable to bear it any longer and let out a strange, shrill cry.","Cheng Zhao and the others left the small Buddhist shrine.","When they returned to Chengming Hall, Nanny Li, Suyue, and Qiubai all watched Cheng Zhao’s expression nervously, cautiously testing the waters.","“Fifth Miss... are you really the daughter of the Commandery Princess Zhaoyang? Is that what Madam told you?” Suyue asked.","She had started calling her “Fifth Miss” again.","Suyue and Qiubai were both stunned, for they had known nothing of this past history.","When Cheng Zhao had made the jade dumpling cakes upon entering the household, she had not explained anything to the people around her. She had always been headstrong from childhood, and even Nanny Li had never dared make decisions for her, only carrying out her orders.","After that, one difficulty after another had arisen in their dealings with the Zhou family. They had struggled forward through every obstacle, and gradually forgotten the small matter of the jade dumpling cakes.","“What, have you gone stupid too? The three of us sisters look alike. We were born to the same parents,” Cheng Zhao said.","“Actually, you don’t look that much alike. You’re all beauties, so I suppose there’s some resemblance. But you and Fourth Young Master look more alike...” Suyue muttered.","At that point, Suyue’s eyes widened slightly.","Cheng Zhao gave her a deep look, and Suyue immediately lowered her head.","Nanny Li and Qiubai remained silent.","“Bury this in your stomachs. Don’t go spreading these words,” Cheng Zhao said.","The three of them assented.","Cheng Zhao and Cheng Chao somewhat resembled their grandmother. Their grandmother, in turn, had been maternal cousins with Grand Princess Jianning, the birth mother of the Commandery Princess Zhaoyang.","Relations within an aristocratic family were always intricate. Many marital connections were never examined in detail; outsiders might not understand them, and even members of the family themselves might not have a complete grasp of them.","That evening, Zhou Yuanshen returned and asked about the day’s events.","Cheng Zhao told him about her visit to Nanny Sun, but she did not mention the Commandery Princess Zhaoyang.","Most likely, no one was willing to bring up that past.","In Cheng Zhao’s heart, she was unquestionably the daughter of the Cheng family.","“Back then, when my father went to Qinzhou, my mother set aside all the household affairs and took Fourth Brother and me with her. We were still quite young at the time,” Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","“Why did you suddenly bring that up?”","“It just came to mind. Prince An happened to be in Qinzhou as well. Our two households were neighbors, and quite a few things happened between us.","“It was also during those years in Qinzhou that Cheng Chao and I stayed by our parents’ side. My father was extremely strict. He wished he could shape the two of us into pillars of the nation, only to discover that neither of us was particularly promising.","“We were masters at slacking off and being slippery. The two of us came up with every possible trick to get out of our lessons. Even I thought I was incredibly clever for coming up with so many ways to fool him.","“Once, my father became especially angry and punished us rather severely, making us kneel beneath the blazing sun. Even now, Cheng Chao and I are both a little afraid of him. It left us with lasting shadows,” Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","“Your father-in-law only wanted the best for you.”","“Of course he did. What a pity we were destined to be two rather useless children. Cheng Chao is as stupid as a blockhead,” Cheng Zhao said.","Then she added, “I only have a little cleverness myself. When it comes to true intelligence, my eldest sister, second brother, and third sister are the ones with genuine talent.”","She continued, “But Cheng Chao and I were closer to our mother because of those years in Qinzhou. During that time, there were only the four of us. Aside from the hardship of studying, they were happy days.”","Zhou Yuanshen listened quietly.","Then he asked, “Do you feel there was something strange about it?”","The legitimate eldest son of an aristocratic family volunteering to gain experience in the provinces, his eldest daughter-in-law setting aside all household affairs, and a prince spending time with them...","“There was nothing strange about it. Many things are simply coincidences. If you insist on examining every detail, anything can seem suspicious,” Cheng Zhao said. “I was only sighing over how lucky I was to be born into the right family. My parents are the only truly good people in this world.”","Zhou Yuanshen pulled her into his arms.","Cheng Zhao murmured against his chest, “I want children too.”","She and Zhou Yuanshen would make wonderful parents as well.","Their child might be quick-witted and mischievous like her. Or perhaps cautious and reserved like Zhou Yuanshen. Even if they were unlucky enough to take after her uncle Cheng Chao and turn out a little foolish, it would not be a bad thing. Fools often had the best luck.","“When the weather warms up, shall we go pray to the Goddess of Fertility?” Zhou Yuanshen asked.","“Good!” Cheng Zhao agreed.","Before long, the fifteenth day of the first lunar month had passed, and Cheng Zhao carried out a thorough purge of every steward and servant in the household.","Those who ought to be released were released; those who ought to stay were retained.","Many servants had signed life contracts, yet Cheng Zhao still gave them money and returned their deeds of sale.","As a result, those who left were all deeply grateful.","The chief steward and Nanny Sun left as well.","Nanny Sun was in poor spirits, and her nephew took her away. Some said he brought her back to their ancestral home; others said she could not endure the journey and died halfway there.","Cheng Zhao did not concern herself with it any further.","She was not afraid that Nanny Sun might reveal anything. Compared with Cheng Zhao, Nanny Sun would never dare expose the Zhou family’s secrets. If she kept silent, she might survive. If she spoke, she would certainly die.","Grand Madam had committed too many sins.","Once the government offices reopened after the New Year, Zhou Yuanshen and the Second Master separately went to inquire about the women of Prince Andong’s household and the bandits from the Xu family. They were all still in prison.","However, the case had not yet been judged, and it would probably drag on for a long time.","Prince Andong had explained the situation to the Emperor. The Emperor trusted him and did not intend to investigate too deeply. Still, since knives had been drawn within the inner household, the Dali Temple would not release the women easily.","So the matter dragged on.","In the second month, Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen made a trip to the saltworks by the Eastern Sea and, while they were there, went to pray to the Goddess of Fertility.","In the third month, Cheng Zhao heard that the Seventh Miss of Prince Rong’s Mansion had become betrothed. The groom was the paternal cousin of Cheng Zhao’s second sister-in-law, Yin Linlang.","The Yin family was likewise a prominent clan of Wu Commandery, and Yin Linlang’s grandmother had been a princess of the imperial family.","Second Madam was surprised when she heard the news. “Wasn’t she supposed to be betrothed to your Fourth Brother?”","“She’s much younger than my Fourth Brother. She’s about the same age as my Second Sister-in-law’s cousin, so they’re a better match,” Cheng Zhao said. “Either way, it would still be a marriage between connected families.”","Then she lowered her voice and added, “My Fourth Brother is enamored of Guo Hanzhang, but he doesn’t dare say so. The family probably wouldn’t agree either.”","“That girl is quite formidable!” Second Madam said.","She still remembered how Guo Hanzhang had ridiculed so many noble ladies. And as the niece of Empress Guo, any family that married her would have a difficult time with her.","“It’s not that we’re afraid Guo Hanzhang would be difficult to handle. It’s just that the situation is unpredictable, and my maternal family doesn’t want to get involved too deeply,” Cheng Zhao said."]},{"number":249,"title":"Chapter 249: Epilogue (9)","paragraphs":["The affairs of state, when there was no war, did not affect ordinary people’s food and drink.","From the third month to the fourth, Zhou Yuanshen was stationed at the capital’s outskirts.","The young servant Nanfeng secretly told Cheng Zhao, “There’s been a rebellion in one of the prefectures in the northwest. Lord Duke went to deal with it on His Majesty’s behalf.”","“It wasn’t reported to the court?” Cheng Zhao asked.","Nanfeng said, “I don’t know the details. We should ask Sister Mingyu.”","Cheng Zhao sent someone to summon Mingyu.","Mingyu knew everything. She was responsible for passing messages between the Chen Duke’s residence and the residence of the General of Pacifying the West.","“The memorial reporting the matter to the court was withheld by the emperor and never circulated. He still sent Lord Duke there, just like last time. Officially, he’s an imperial commissioner; in truth, he’s been sent to kill people,” Mingyu said.","Cheng Zhao’s heart gave a hard jolt.","“This isn’t the first time he’s done this for the emperor. The rebels will be on guard against him,” Cheng Zhao said.","“Lord Duke told us not to tell you, because he was afraid you’d worry. But if he didn’t go, no one knows how much worse the situation might become.”","Cheng Zhao said nothing.","She sat alone, her heart heavy and troubled.","She could not help thinking of Zhou Yuanshen.","He hated the emperor deeply, but he did not want to see the world descend into chaos, either. He wanted peace. And so, with the realm as his first priority, he swallowed every grievance.","He continued to serve as that blade.","If he could intimidate the rebels and nip the beginnings of a bloody conflict in the bud, then it was worth it.","Cheng Zhao felt unbearably stifled.","Perhaps she had simply eaten too much at noon. The discomfort became more and more intolerable, and she began dry-heaving.","Nanny Li and the maids hurried over to surround her.","One brought a spittoon, another poured water for her to rinse her mouth, while someone else prepared a handkerchief to wipe her face.","Cheng Zhao brought up nothing. She only dry-heaved several times, coughing up tears and mucus and looking thoroughly disheveled.","Once she had been cleaned up, she said, “I couldn’t possibly be pregnant, could I?”","The moment the words left her mouth, she herself froze.","Nanny Li said, “Shall we send for a physician now, or wait a little? The last time you had your period was before you went to the saltworks.”","“It’s been two months since I returned from the saltworks.”","Then, afraid that her hopes might come to nothing, Cheng Zhao added, “I only made a few bows and didn’t even bring home an image of Guanyin. Could it really have worked that quickly?”","Nanny Li immediately told her not to tempt fate and advised her not to say any more for the time being.","Cheng Zhao did indeed send for a physician.","A doctor skilled in women’s ailments came, examined her pulse, and asked her a few questions. He said that her pulse was indeed slippery and showed signs of pregnancy. If she was still uncertain, she could invite several more physicians to examine her.","Cheng Zhao rewarded him generously.","She immediately sent someone to inform Second Madam. She also had Nanny Li return to the Cheng household and ask her mother to send a trusted physician to examine her.","That afternoon, her mother came to the Chen Duke’s residence with a physician in tow.","“It is a happy pulse. Congratulations, Madam.”","Her mother-in-law, who had been sitting beside her in obvious anxiety, was overjoyed at the news. Cheng Zhao’s mother was delighted as well.","“You must take good care of yourself and get plenty of rest. For now, only the family should know. Don’t tell anyone else,” her mother said.","“Yes.”","“Whatever you feel like eating, just send someone to tell me,” her mother added.","Cheng Zhao smiled. “What did you like to eat when you were pregnant with me?”","“There were far too many things to count. You weren’t a quiet one even when you were still in my belly.” Her mother laughed.","“Then send me some of them too. I’d like to try them,” Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","Second Madam laughed along with them.","The household servants still knew nothing of the matter. Second Madam came to Cheng Zhao’s Chengming Hall every day to see her, beaming with joy, while the Cheng family sent delicacies over every few days.","The fourth time Cheng Zhao’s mother came to the Chen Duke’s residence with fresh delicacies, she happened to run into Cheng Chao.","He said, “You’ve sent things over several times already. Don’t tell me she’s pregnant?”","His mother shot him a look. “You certainly notice everything.”","“She really is?” Cheng Chao was astonished. “She used to torment all of you every day. From now on, she’ll have a little one to torment her. What goes around comes around.”","His mother fell silent.","Cheng Chao was about to leave when his mother stopped him again.","“Don’t go telling people,” she said. “The first three months are not a time to make an announcement, and don’t tell your grandfather either. Once her pregnancy is stable, her family will send gifts, and we can mention it then.”","“Understood,” Cheng Chao said. “It hasn’t been easy for her. She’s been married nearly two years.”","“Yes. At last, there’s some good news.” His mother sounded relieved.","The worry that had been hanging over her heart finally eased.","Cheng Chao said, “The Chen Duke’s residence is a den of vipers. Not a day goes by without trouble. It would be strange if she could get pregnant there. When the weather is too cold or too hot, even hens stop laying eggs, let alone people.","“Now that everyone who needed to die is dead, Zhaozhao knows she’s safe, and she and her husband are living in harmony. Of course she’s pregnant now. It would have been strange if she’d conceived earlier.”","His mother stared at him. “That mouth of yours needs to quiet down too! Of my five children, only you and your sister spend all day bickering.”","“We came from the same womb.”","“Did the others spring from rocks?” His mother rolled her eyes. “Go tend to your own affairs. Don’t stay here and irritate me.”","Cheng Chao was just about to leave when his mother called him back once more.","She asked, “Have you made up your mind about what I asked you last time? Once you have, tell your father and grandfather.”","Cheng Chao refused. “I’m not telling them.”","His mother glared at him. “How long are you planning to drag this out?”","“I don’t want to marry Guo Hanzhang. It took us long enough to marry Zhaozhao off, so she wouldn’t have to serve that old lady anymore. Why would we invite another one into the family?” he said.","“You were born to serve difficult women!” his mother said. “I’ll ask you one more time. If you refuse, I’ll arrange another marriage for you myself. And don’t cause trouble like you did with the Prince Rong’s household and nearly offend them.”","Her tone grew sterner.","“If your sister-in-law hadn’t smoothed things over and the Yin family hadn’t helped, the matter with Prince Rong’s household would have turned into a feud.”","Cheng Chao fell silent.","His mother continued, “You’re not young anymore. Stop being so stubborn. How many more disasters are you going to cause me?”","After a long silence, Cheng Chao finally raised his eyes. “Isn’t this a very difficult situation? Grand Preceptor Guo is no kind man. I don’t want to put Grandfather in a difficult position.”","“A married daughter belongs to her husband’s family. If the Guo family truly commits some monstrous crime in the future, she can sever ties with them,” his mother said. “Our Cheng family can bear that.”","“Father and Mother have gone to such lengths to plan for us.”","“What parents don’t exhaust themselves for their children?” His mother smiled. “It’s rare to hear you say something so affectionate.”","Cheng Chao said, “I’ll find an opportunity to speak with Grandfather.”","Then he called out, “Mother.”","His mother looked at him in confusion. “What else do you want?”","“Nothing. I just wanted to call you.” Cheng Chao smiled. “Mother.”","Then he turned and walked away.","His mother stood where she was, her eyes slowly growing moist.","After the Dragon Boat Festival, Cheng Zhao finally came out of the early stages of pregnancy. She could eat and sleep normally again and continued to manage affairs as usual. Every day, she matched wits with the household managers—winning over those who needed winning over, suppressing those who needed suppressing, sometimes establishing her authority and sometimes demonstrating her mercy.","Her belly hardly showed, and she did not even feel pregnant herself.","Nanny Li was constantly on edge. She kept urging Cheng Zhao to rest more and take better care of herself.","“Using your mind tires you out too. You mustn’t exhaust yourself.”","When she failed to persuade her, she even asked Second Madam to help.","Second Madam said, “When I was pregnant with Ah Shen, I rode a horse for two whole days without the slightest problem. I still practiced with my spear as usual. Zhaozhao isn’t delicate. Just let her be.”","Nanny Li was speechless.","Second Madam was no help at all.","With no other choice, Nanny Li could only continue wearing away at Cheng Zhao, nagging in her ear and telling her to rest more.","Cheng Zhao was very easygoing. As long as no one overstepped their bounds and made decisions without her permission, she was tolerant of everything else. For instance, even when Nanny Li’s constant reminders made her ears ache, she merely let the words go in one ear and out the other without arguing."]},{"number":250,"title":"Chapter 250: Epilogue (10)","paragraphs":["Zhou Yuanshen was far away in the northwest.","He would receive a message from Mingyu every half a month.","In the early stage of pregnancy, it had to be kept secret, so Zhou Yuanshen didn't learn that his wife was pregnant until early May.","\"Act tonight. Under the guise of a surprise attack, I'll go for the assassination,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","The people around him were quite surprised.","Why was he suddenly being so reckless?","The rebellion in the northwest couldn't be concealed because the emperor was very angry and made it public, vowing to take the head of the rebellious general.","This also enraged many generals and princes.","There had been no further news of the rebellion for the time being. Maybe they were still preparing or just waiting and seeing.","Zhou Yuanshen had planned to proceed steadily, arranging the suppression on one hand and assassinating the rebellious generals on the other. But he suddenly wanted to end it quickly.","In the middle of the night, a team of less than two hundred people set off. They climbed over a mountain and reached the rebel camp directly.","At dawn, Zhou Yuanshen was covered in blood, carrying the head of the rebel general in his hand.","\"Send the good news to boost the morale,\" he said. \"Prepare the prisoners of war. I'll set off for the capital tomorrow.\"","The deputy general: \"...\"","The good news reached the capital before Zhou Yuanshen, and the emperor was overjoyed.","After this rebellion was quelled, those who had been eager to take action all stopped.","When Zhou Yuanshen returned to the capital, it was the hottest time of the year, and it was also approaching Cheng Zhao's birthday.","He rushed back to the capital on horseback, only bringing fifty prisoners of war.","He presented the prisoners at the Meridian Gate, and the capital was extremely lively for a moment.","Cheng Zhao was sitting in the east side room of Jiangyun Courtyard, eating cherries and waiting for Zhou Yuanshen to come back. Zhou Yuanqi and the Second Master had gone out to wait. The Second Lady kept looking towards the door from time to time.","\"He's only been away for three months. He quelled a rebellion in such a short time. The court officials must praise him!\" the Second Lady said.","\"The emperor must praise him too,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"He's really made a great contribution this time.\"","Mentioning the emperor, the Second Lady's mood dropped sharply.","She snorted: \"Who knows? He...\"","Looking at Cheng Zhao, she didn't say the rest. Some words were just for venting, meaningless and might cause trouble for the children.","Cheng Zhao smiled and said, \"No matter what the emperor does, Lord Duke will gain prestige in the court.\"","The Second Lady became happy again.","In the late afternoon of that day, Zhou Yuanqi came back first, braving the scorching sun.","\"Third brother has entered the mansion,\" he said loudly to Cheng Zhao and the Second Lady. His head and face were full of sweat, and the front of his linen robe was soaked.","Cheng Zhao quickly said, \"Come in quickly and cool off!\"","The Second Lady also scolded him: \"You're getting older year by year, but still running around wildly in the hot sun. You'll get a heat illness.\"","Then she ordered the maids, \"Quickly bring some cold tea.\"","Zhou Yuanqi: \"I was in a hurry to come back and tell you as soon as third brother entered the mansion.\"","\"Where is he?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","\"He's in Chenhui Courtyard, having a few words with father. He stank all over. He went to present the prisoners and meet the emperor like that. I can't stand the smell. I told him to take a bath before coming, so as not to stink you up. You're pregnant now,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Cheng Zhao couldn't help laughing.","The Second Lady: \"Rarely do you show such consideration.\"","\"Third sister - in - law couldn't even stand the smell of flowers some time ago,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Cheng Zhao: \"Yes, I really couldn't. Thank you, fifth brother, for thinking so carefully.\"","She was much better now and wasn't afraid of strange smells anymore, but she accepted Zhou Yuanqi's kindness.","After waiting for about half an hour, the Second Master and Zhou Yuanshen came to Jiangyun Courtyard together.","Cheng Zhao looked at him carefully.","He had taken a bath before coming and changed into clean clothes.","He had become much darker, and his cheeks were thinner, making him look even more rugged. He was wearing a light blue linen robe, and his hair was still wet, casually tied with a cap.","He also looked back at Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao's eyes were a bit moist, and she felt inexplicably wronged in her heart - maybe it wasn't really wronged. There was just a sudden urge to cry.","Anyway, it wasn't sadness or gratitude, just an inexplicable urge to shed tears.","She wasn't such a clingy person.","Zhou Yuanshen looked at her quietly, and there were surging emotions in his eyes: \"You look a bit thinner.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","\"No, she hasn't vomited once. She eats less, but she eats every day,\" the Second Lady said with a smile beside them.","Cheng Zhao had only retched for half a month and hadn't really vomited anything. She didn't like to eat before. Some days ago, when cherries were on the market, the Second Lady specially asked someone to find some for her.","Maybe Cheng Zhao got used to the taste and had an appetite, or maybe the early stage of pregnancy had passed. Since then, her diet had returned to normal, and she could feel hungry.","\"Mother took good care of her,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","The Second Lady just smiled.","She asked Zhou Yuanshen to sit down and let his hair dry before tying it up again, so as not to be stuffy with the damp heat and get a headache later.","She asked a lot of questions.","\"Is the emperor happy?\" the Second Lady asked again.","\"The budding rebellion has been nipped in the bud. He's very happy and rewarded me with a hundred taels of gold,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","The Second Lady: \"That's quite generous.\"","Although they didn't really need it.","After Dowager Madame passed away, Cheng Zhao took over all the fief - related properties of the Chenguo Duke's Mansion.","She told the Second Lady that the Zhou family had countless sacrificial fields, and the annual income from the fief - related properties was as high as 450,000 taels, definitely ranking first among the high - ranking noble families.","The Second Lady could also understand why Dowager Madame was so reluctant to let go.","Sometimes, power and wealth were like a curse. Once you got them, you were afraid of losing them and wouldn't let go until death. And it wasn't easy for the Zhou family to get these.","The Second Lady forced the Second Master to tell her, and only then did she know that many people in the family had died abnormally.","If the Second Master hadn't seemed \"incompetent\" in Dowager Madame's eyes and couldn't bring back much, he might have died too.","As for Huan Qingtang, she had helped Dowager Madame manage the rent for a while before. She might have known about 60 - 70% of the situation.","She was also blinded by wealth and just couldn't \"give it away\" voluntarily.","Both she and Dowager Madame died because of their greed. They thought they could control the gains and losses and fight against fate.","The Second Lady didn't need these silver coins. She just knew there was a lot. And for the emperor to reward a hundred taels of gold, the Second Lady didn't think it meant much.","After dinner, it was still very hot outside. The heatwaves were trapped between the courtyards and kept hitting people.","Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen took a small oil - powered cart back to Chengming Hall.","When they returned to the inner bedroom, she hugged him.","Zhou Yuanshen hugged her back, and the tears that Cheng Zhao had held back all night rolled down.","\"Why are you crying?\" He held her face in his hands. \"Are you not feeling well?\"","Cheng Zhao choked with sobs and couldn't speak clearly: \"No...\"","Maybe it was because of excessive longing.","She seemed to have never waited for anyone like this, and she would never have such emotional ups and downs because of someone's return.","- Of course, it might just be because she was pregnant and more vulnerable and thoughtful.","Cheng Zhao couldn't explain it clearly.","Zhou Yuanshen wiped the tears from her eyes and gently kissed her eyes: \"Don't cry.\"","Cheng Zhao couldn't hold back anymore and cried loudly.","In the second half of the night, the inner bedroom with ice finally cooled down. Zhou Yuanshen hugged Cheng Zhao in his arms.","Cheng Zhao still felt a bit hot, but she didn't push him away.","\"Was it very dangerous this time?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","Zhou Yuanshen: \"It was okay.\"","He told Cheng Zhao all about the situation at that time, including his surprise attack and assassination.","\"Was it also you who went for the assassination when there was a rebellion before and it was quickly quelled?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","Zhou Yuanshen admitted: \"Yes.\"","\"You've done a lot for the emperor,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen kissed her.","He asked about Cheng Zhao's pregnancy symptoms.","How she knew she was pregnant, how she felt, and how she was feeling now, etc. Cheng Zhao told him all about it one by one.","\"...Cheng Zhao, there's something I want to discuss with you. We need to handle it as soon as possible. The earlier, the better,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","\"What's the matter?\""]},{"number":251,"title":"Chapter 251: The Grand Finale (Part 1)","paragraphs":["Zhou Yuanshen wanted to deal with the Zhou family’s title estates.","“According to the standards of an ordinary duke’s residence, we’ll keep a portion of the farmland and vacate half of the estate as well,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao listened attentively.","“I agree,” she said. “‘Ill-gotten wealth’ will bring trouble sooner or later.”","Then she asked, “You’ve already seen the signs, haven’t you?”","“Prince of Andong is very likely the mastermind behind Grandmother’s murder. His hidden guards and maidservant are still in prison. When I mentioned this after receiving my meritorious promotion, the emperor even said that he would ‘be fair.’","“What could have been unfair enough for the emperor to feel that he had mistreated Helian Xuan? Nothing except the fact that the Zhou family possesses too many title estates, and that the Duke’s Residence is far too vast and extravagant.”","Cheng Zhao said, “There really are too many title estates.”","So many that they were beyond her expectations.","Even Cheng Zhao, who had seen plenty in her life, had been shaken by the sight.","Once this matter was exposed, the censors would curse the Zhou family to death. The family would have to bear the emperor’s accusations of “extravagance and debauchery,” and they would lose the people’s goodwill.","The people’s goodwill was their reputation.","“The deaths of Dowager Madame, Lady Huan, and our eldest aunt, Madam Song, have already brought the Zhou family more than enough gossip and slander. It will be difficult to recover. But falling all the way to the bottom would be easy,” Cheng Zhao said. “This was a farsighted move.”","“I’ll tell my mother in person.”","“Mother will understand. She can tell right from wrong, good from evil,” Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen gave a slight nod and pulled her more tightly into his arms.","The weather was hot, but he was even hotter.","He kissed her, and the kiss grew deeper and deeper...","By the middle of June, the Zhou family had made new arrangements. A tall wall was built to the east of Shou’an Court.","Including Shou’an Court, at least half of the Duke’s Residence was partitioned off and returned to the Ministry of Revenue.","Zhou Yuanshen also submitted a memorial, relinquishing most of the title estates.","“His Majesty is a filial son. These estates were originally bestowed for Grandmother’s sake. Now that Grandmother has passed away, her descendants dare not continue accepting such tremendous favor,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","He had only just distinguished himself by suppressing the rebellion, and the court officials already regarded him with great favor. Now that he had returned most of the title estates and part of the residence, he was praised even more.","The emperor nodded repeatedly.","He also commended Zhou Yuanshen several times.","That very night, Helian Xuan said to his advisers, “Jinshu and the others won’t be saved.”","His hidden guards and the maidservant had originally still had a chance of being rescued. There had also been some hope of muddling through the charge that they had entered the Duke’s Residence to “assassinate” a woman of the highest rank.","But Zhou Yuanshen’s move would force the emperor to make the charge stick.","Helian Xuan would not be able to escape.","Was Zhou Yuanshen afraid that prosperity would invite disaster, or was he simply venting Cheng Zhao’s anger for her?","“He’s redirecting the trouble elsewhere, leaving His Majesty no time to deal with these minor matters,” one adviser said.","“How will he redirect it?” Helian Xuan asked.","“Besides serving in the Metropolitan Camp, Zhou Yuanshen is also Grand Tutor Zhou. If something were to happen to the Eastern Palace...”","“The weather is terribly hot, and malaria has been spreading lately.”","Malaria was a virulent disease. From the onset of symptoms to death could take only a few days, and it was highly contagious.","Most people drank water from the rivers, while also washing clothes and rinsing chamber pots in them. Malaria could cause diarrhea and spread through feces.","When one adviser proposed this plan, several others objected.","“Malaria strikes too quickly, while medicinal decoctions take time to work. Once it spreads, we may not escape unscathed either.”","Helian Xuan spoke quietly. “Don’t drink raw water these days, and don’t bathe in it. Other than that, there’s no need to worry.”","Everyone shuddered.","After the Zhou family returned its title estates, the emperor suddenly “remembered” Prince of Andong’s hidden guards and the assassination attempt that had taken place in the Duke’s Residence.","Just as he was about to deal with the case, a messenger arrived from the Eastern Palace: the Crown Prince had diarrhea and a high fever.","“What about the imperial physicians?” the emperor asked coldly.","He had never been particularly fond of the Crown Prince.","At the time, it had been Grand Preceptor Guo who, together with the court officials, had pressured him into establishing the Crown Prince.","The Crown Prince displeased him in every way.","If he absolutely had to choose someone, he would rather choose Zhou Yuanshen.","If only Dowager Madame were still alive. She could have trained a suitable heir for him.","At that thought, the emperor was suddenly overcome with sorrow. After Dowager Madame’s death, he had grieved for many days, but he had eventually been able to accept it. She had, after all, been advanced in years.","Then the rebellion had stirred up his mind, and other matters had occupied him. He had come to feel that Dowager Madame had not meant all that much to him.","Until this moment.","An indescribable longing and reluctance surged through his heart.","“Your Majesty, you cannot go to the Eastern Palace. If this is malaria, you may become infected,” one imperial physician said.","The emperor flew into a rage. “Seal off the Eastern Palace at once and cut off its water supply. Where did the Crown Prince contract it?”","“His Highness has not left the palace recently. He merely indulged in the coolness and ate too much fruit.”","“Malaria can spread through feces. Perhaps the fruit was fertilized with manure and the peels were not washed properly.”","The emperor was speechless for a moment. “...He truly is useless!”","He was cursing the Crown Prince.","The empress went to the Eastern Palace every day.","The Crown Prince did indeed have malaria. He suffered from a high fever and diarrhea, and on the fifth day, he died. He had always been weak and frail.","The empress wept until she fainted.","The emperor still had two sons alive, though he had lost his legitimate heir. He was not as grief-stricken as the empress.","He ordered a thorough investigation of the Eastern Palace.","All the officials of the Eastern Palace were to be implicated, including Zhou Yuanshen.","“It was Prince of Andong who murdered His Highness the Crown Prince,” one official submitted in a memorial, accusing Helian Xuan.","When the news reached Helian Xuan, he realized that there was a spy among his people. It could not have been one of the emperor’s men. It was probably someone planted by Zhou Yuanshen.","Before the accusation could be confirmed, Helian Xuan fled.","He went to Qinzhou.","The military commanders of the seven prefectures and thirty provinces in the south pledged allegiance to him. With an army of five hundred thousand men, Helian Xuan rebelled.","Once he raised his banner, the realm descended into chaos. Twelve regions established their own governments and declared themselves kings, with Helian Xuan commanding the greatest power among them.","The Crown Prince died in July. Helian Xuan rebelled in September. By the beginning of November, thirteen rebel kings had emerged across the realm.","The capital, Shengjing, was tense. The prices of rice and coal rose day after day.","“You’re about to give birth, aren’t you?” Cheng Chao came to the Zhou family residence with his second elder brother and sister-in-law to deliver a gift for the coming birth. The siblings chatted together.","“About half a month from now,” Cheng Zhao said.","“What has Yuanshen been busy with lately?”","“He spends every day at the government office, making preparations to suppress the rebellion,” Cheng Zhao replied.","Cheng Chao then brought up Helian Xuan.","“I never thought he would rebel,” Cheng Chao said.","Cheng Zhao was not surprised. “Prince An died suddenly. The father and son must have been plotting for a long time. Didn’t they try to win over the Cheng family because they wanted Grandfather to lend them his influence?”","“I thought he really was in love with you,” Cheng Chao said.","Cheng Zhao said, “Don’t disgust me. Why are you bringing that up again? You’re the only fool here. I never once thought he had any affection for me.”","“I’m an honest man. I believe whatever people tell me,” Cheng Chao said.","“Don’t flatter yourself. You simply can’t tell good from bad...”","The second sister-in-law laughed and tried to smooth things over. “All right, all right. The two of you quarrel every time you meet. You’re about to become a mother and an uncle—aren’t you afraid the children will laugh at you?”","Cheng Zhao gave a snort and ignored Cheng Chao.","Whenever Cheng Chao saw her looking like a peacock with its tail raised—proud and flamboyant—he felt an urge to tease her. At the same time, he had to admit that her “tail” was indeed magnificent and beautiful.","How irritating!","He hoped she would not give birth to another daughter who looked just like her. Otherwise, as her uncle, he would be driven to death by the child.","Zhou Yuanshen returned rather early that day.","The Duke’s residence had dinner prepared, and he kept his two brothers-in-law for drinks. Cheng Zhao ate separately with her second sister-in-law.","“When will you set out for the campaign?”","“We’re still preparing the provisions. Probably by the end of the twelfth lunar month,” Zhou Yuanshen said. “That’s already considered very quick.”","“When rebellion breaks out in a particular region, the imperial court first seals off the news, for fear that others will follow suit. Helian Xuan openly proclaimed himself king and rebelled, and even used his connections to spread the news throughout the realm. Otherwise, the other twelve regions would never have risen in revolt as well,” Cheng Yan said.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, “He had been plotting this for a long time.”","“It has nothing to do with anyone or anything else. He simply wants to seize the empire. He tried to assassinate the emperor and the Crown Prince. When that plan failed, he resorted to proclaiming himself king in Qinzhou,” Cheng Yan continued.","Zhou Yuanshen nodded.","Cheng Chao looked at him. “I’m familiar with Qinzhou. Take me with you when you go to put down the rebellion. Perhaps I can be of some help.”","The imperial army would attack Qinzhou first. It had the greatest number of rebel troops and prefectures, and its influence was the most extensive.","In the other regions, there were no shortage of scattered troops and defeated stragglers.","“All right. Follow me when the time comes—if your family agrees,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","“My parents and grandfather will certainly agree,” Cheng Chao replied.","“Aren’t you getting married soon?”","“Our wedding is set for April next year. The fighting should be over by April, shouldn’t it?” Cheng Chao asked.","Zhou Yuanshen fell silent.","“You expect to finish in three or four months? If it ends in three or four years, that would already count as good fortune and a favorable year,” Cheng Yan said.","Cheng Chao replied, “We can give it a try.”","As preparations for the campaign proceeded in haste, curfew was imposed throughout Shengjing.","Cheng Zhao was nearing the end of her pregnancy, yet she personally inspected the family’s cellar and storehouses to make sure there was enough coal and rice to feed everyone for two years.","The Second Master would also be going to war.","On the seventh day of the eleventh lunar month, Cheng Zhao gave birth to a son. She had remained active throughout her pregnancy, taking walks whenever the weather was neither too cold nor too hot, and the delivery went relatively smoothly.","Despite it being her first child, she gave birth in less than twelve hours.","Everyone praised how quickly she had delivered, but she had still suffered terribly.","Zhou Yuanshen held her hand and was unable to utter a word for a long while.","Cheng Zhao knew he was moved and that his heart ached for her. She smiled and said, “When peace has been restored, I’m going to the Guanyin Bodhisattva’s temple to fulfill my vow.”","She had burned incense at the small Buddhist shrine in the Nonghua Court, and the Bodhisattva had not punished her by condemning her to a lifetime without children. Cheng Zhao therefore believed that the Bodhisattva possessed a broad and compassionate heart and offered salvation to all beneath Heaven.","As befitted a deity who received incense from the entire realm, the Bodhisattva did not quibble with an ordinary woman like her.","“When peace has been restored, I’ll go with you,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","And so the husband and wife made their promise to each other.","Of all those in the family, the Second Madam was the happiest about Cheng Zhao giving birth. She searched through the genealogy and, together with the Second Master, chose names for the child. In one breath, she wrote down ten names for Cheng Zhao to select from.","Names such as Jing’an and Shiyong expressed the wish for “peace in all four directions and a prosperous, dignified age”—the hopes most cherished in those times.","Cheng Zhao said that both of those names were excellent.","“Those two were chosen by Yuanqi,” the Second Madam said.","Cheng Zhao thought of how Zhou Yuanqi, despite being so young, would have to endure such turmoil. Then she thought of her own newborn child, born into such troubled times, and felt a sudden ache of tenderness in her heart.","“We should ask the Duke when he returns,” Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen was in the outer residence, busy making arrangements for the baby’s third-day ceremony.","He was about to depart for the campaign and had been spending these days at home only when he could find a spare moment.","He thought Jing’an was a fine name.","Thus, Cheng Zhao’s eldest son was named Zhou Jing’an.","After that, Zhou Yuanshen was rarely home. He spent two years in Qinzhou, battling Helian Xuan’s army of five hundred thousand men. In the end, both sides were exhausted, their men and horses worn to the bone.","Cheng Zhao’s fourth brother stayed at Zhou Yuanshen’s side.","His wedding date with Guo Hanzhang could not possibly be honored. Just as they were preparing to postpone it, Guo Hanzhang brought more than a dozen people—including maids and senior household servants—and traveled south to find Cheng Chao.","It was a bold and audacious move, and one that heartened many people at the time.","She and Cheng Chao were married in the south. Since Cheng Chao could not return, neither did she. The fighting on the front lines was complicated, and the Guo family was deeply worried about her, yet they could not overcome her stubborn determination.","Cheng Zhao received a letter saying that Guo Hanzhang was organizing village women to grow grain and raise silkworms and mulberry trees on the front lines. She had earned even more respect from the soldiers than Cheng Chao himself.","“...I’m a little envious of her,” Cheng Zhao said to her mother-in-law. “She’s incredibly brave and has such tremendous drive.”","The Second Madam was likewise astonished when she heard this. “I knew she was no ordinary woman.”","The more chaotic the times, the more clearly a person’s worth became apparent.","Cheng Chao had truly struck gold by marrying such a fine wife.","“You’re managing such a large household all on your own. You’re remarkable too. There’s no need to envy her,” the Second Madam added.","The Second Master also went off to put down the rebellion.","At present, the household depended on the Second Madam and Cheng Zhao to support each other.","More than half of the servants had been dismissed. Only twenty people remained, including the stewards, maids, older female servants, and footmen. There were also the household guards and deputy generals, who could not be discharged—more than forty people in all—as well as Cheng Zhao’s personal retainers.","Cheng Zhao had not dismissed any of her retainers. No matter how difficult things became, she was determined to support them. Peace would return one day, and she would need them then.","Her mother had carefully cultivated and selected them for her.","There were more than a hundred people in the household altogether. In such chaotic times, feeding so many people was no easy task, and Cheng Zhao had to calculate every expense with painstaking care each day.","Fortunately, the Zhou family’s storehouses were well stocked.","Among Cheng Zhao’s relatives by marriage, the father-in-law of her third elder sister—Prince Jingnan—had also gone to suppress the rebellion, heading northwest, where rebel forces and ferocious bandits ran rampant.","When Cheng Zhao’s son was eight months old, just after the end of the hottest part of summer, she heard the tragic news that Prince Jingnan had died in battle. Her heart lurched.","She went to Prince Jingnan’s residence.","After curfew had been imposed in Shengjing, the streets had become far more desolate than before. Even in broad daylight, there were few pedestrians, and doors and gates were shut everywhere.","Cheng Zhao went to see the Princess Consort and her third elder sister.","The Princess Consort’s eyes were swollen from crying.","Her son and daughter-in-law were at her side.","In private, Cheng Ying told Cheng Zhao, “They still haven’t found Father-in-law’s body. There’s still hope.”","“If you need anything, just come to me. Whatever I have, I’ll give you,” Cheng Zhao said.","“For now, we don’t lack anything,” Cheng Ying replied.","Then she added, “Your eldest brother-in-law also went to suppress the rebellion. My eldest sister has moved back to her parents’ home.”","“I heard.”","“If you’re afraid, you can bring your child, your mother-in-law, and your younger brother-in-law back home as well,” Cheng Ying said.","“I’m not afraid. The Chen Duke’s residence has household guards, as well as the deputy generals and others whom Yuanshen left behind.”","Then Cheng Zhao asked, “If the news truly is bad, what will you do?”","Cheng Ying’s marriage had been forced through solely because the two families were evenly matched in power. She and Zhang Yunqi hardly ever saw each other.","If the Zhang family fell, what would become of Cheng Ying?","“Zhaozhao, if Father-in-law truly died in battle, I would remain with the Zhang family for the rest of my life. A daughter of the Cheng family would never abandon someone in their time of misfortune,” Cheng Ying said.","Cheng Zhao tightened her grip on her hand. “Let us hope there’s a turn for the better.”","She secretly slipped Cheng Ying a large purse filled with gold beans. It was heavy in her hand.","After autumn began, Cheng Zhao heard that both of Prince Jingnan’s daughters-in-law had returned to their parents’ homes.","“That’s far too heartless. The Princess Consort has always treated her daughters-in-law well, and they both have children. How could they leave at a time like this?” the Second Madam said angrily.","Cheng Zhao replied, “When a tree falls, the monkeys scatter. I told my third elder sister last time that marriages between two clans exist so they can stand together through thick and thin. Now that the prince has died in battle and the princely residence has fallen, there’s little meaning left in that family tie. Husband and wife are merely birds in the same forest; when disaster comes, each flies in a different direction.”","The Second Madam’s eyes grew moist. “Only troubled times reveal a person’s true character.”","She asked again, “What about your third sister? She’s the one who truly ought to leave. Zhang Yunqi has subjected her to humiliation and contempt throughout the capital.”","“She won’t leave. The Cheng family cannot raise anyone heartless or ungrateful,” Cheng Zhao said.","The Second Madam sighed deeply.","The prestige of an aristocratic family was built up little by little in precisely this way; every one of the children took pride in the family and would never bring it shame."]},{"number":252,"title":"Chapter 252: The Grand Finale (Part 2)","paragraphs":["When Cheng Zhao’s son reached his first-month celebration, no news of victory had yet arrived from Qinzhou. But good news came from Prince Jingnan’s residence: Prince Jingnan had ambushed and captured two rebel princes alive.","It turned out that the whole thing had been a ruse.","For a time, the entire capital was filled with excitement. With a victory secured, there was hope that the war might soon end. At last, everyone could see a way forward.","The Emperor was delighted as well and rewarded the Zhang family.","The families of the Zhang household’s two young madams sent them back once more.","Princess Consort Jingnan ought to have put on airs and refused to let them enter. But remembering that both women had children, she magnanimously chose not to hold their past against them.","As a result, Princess Consort Jingnan earned a reputation for being broad-minded.","By contrast, Cheng Ying was showered with praise for her righteousness.","“...I still think she’s been wronged,” Second Madam said to Cheng Zhao again. “She’s so beautiful, and so loyal. Yet she’ll still have to remain in the Zhang family’s inner household from now on. No one will forget what Zhang Yunqi did back then.”","“Mother, my third sister has a mind of her own. It isn’t our place to say anything about her affairs,” Cheng Zhao replied.","Second Madam still felt that Cheng Ying was wasting her life.","Another year passed.","It was a year filled with constant reports from the front. The great households tightened their belts, the smaller ones went hungry, and ordinary people were forced to sell their children.","The Zhou family ate one meal of dry rice and one meal of thin gruel each day.","Only the wet nurse and the children were allowed to eat their fill.","Everyone else, Cheng Zhao included, lived frugally. There was no alternative. The war had destroyed the farmland, and even those with money could not buy grain.","The Zhou family’s storehouses held plenty of provisions, but Cheng Zhao had to prepare not only for relatives who might come seeking grain, but also for the possibility that the war would drag on.","Many things had to be planned for in advance.","Second Madam had always been very supportive of her.","Zhou Yuanqi grew older by the day as well. With no one left at the clan school and the academies closed, he had no choice but to shut himself away and study alone.","In addition to reading, he practiced spearwork with his mother every day. He trained to keep himself strong—and to protect his mother and sister-in-law.","He had shot up in height that year. At a glance, he already looked like a grown boy.","In his second year stationed far away in Qinzhou, Zhou Yuanshen was already considering an assassination attempt on Helian Xuan. Helian Xuan, however, was highly wary of him, and the plan might well have ended with Zhou Yuanshen walking into a trap.","In the end, it was Cheng Chao who severely wounded Helian Xuan.","Several times, Helian Xuan’s spies sent people to approach Cheng Chao, hoping to persuade him to change sides.","“You and Cheng Zhao are twins, both children of the Commandery Princess Zhaoyang and the Emperor. The Cheng family of Wu Commandery is immensely powerful, and its servants are fiercely loyal. Yet all these secrets were kept hidden.","“The Cheng family’s First Madam once lost a child. You happened to fill that vacancy. Your younger sister was born undersized, so her wet nurse secretly raised her until she was a year old. The Cheng family’s scheme of replacing one child with another was passed off as the First Madam having given birth to her herself.”","That was what the spy sent to recruit Cheng Chao told him.","Cheng Chao seemed stunned.","After half a year of secret contact, Cheng Chao decided to meet Helian Xuan.","Helian Xuan was on his guard when they met, but he never expected Cheng Chao to be prepared to die. Cheng Chao suddenly wrapped his arms around him and leaped down the mountainside, intending for them both to perish.","He did not even have time to deliver a few stirring words about laying down his life for righteousness.","His actions alone made his meaning clear: he had never cared whose blood ran through his veins. No son of the Cheng family was a coward.","Helian Xuan had sparked the war. His rebellion had inspired rebels in other provinces to follow suit, throwing the entire realm into chaos.","Countless innocent people had died in the fighting.","As long as Helian Xuan died, Cheng Chao would have gained something. His own life was worth little.","The mountain was not especially high, and neither man died. Cheng Chao broke one leg and several bones, but none of his injuries were fatal.","Helian Xuan, however, was badly wounded.","Cheng Chao had broken his fall. Helian Xuan’s spine was shattered, and he might be paralyzed for the rest of his life.","His grand ambitions were destroyed in an instant. He had become a cripple, something he found more terrifying than death itself. With him so seriously injured, the rebel army’s morale plummeted, and suppressing the rebellion became much easier.","When Cheng Zhao’s son turned two, she received a secret report from Qinzhou: after three months of effort, Zhou Yuanshen had finally captured Helian Xuan.","The war might be over in another two months.","Cheng Zhao was ecstatic.","She was just about to send a reply when someone quietly arrived at the Chen State Duke’s residence.","Cheng Zhao never could have imagined that the next time she saw Xian Si would be under such circumstances.","It was the eleventh month of winter, with the cold biting to the bone. Xian Si, who was a Jieyu, had fled the palace. Cheng Zhao was so stunned that she stood frozen in place.","“The Emperor died suddenly. He was found dead in Lijing Palace. Consort Wu sent someone to escort me out of the palace. Now, no one knows who will succeed him or what the situation will become. You are the only person we could think of,” Xian Si said.","Cheng Zhao’s heart turned cold.","All her earlier excitement vanished.","The Emperor was dead.","He had died at the very moment when victory in the campaign to suppress the rebellion was close at hand.","His death would deal a tremendous blow to the army’s morale. The generals fighting the rebels would likely be left at a loss as well.","The Emperor had no adult sons left. Of the two sons still alive, one was seven and the other five. Both were mere children.","Their mothers were both of humble birth, each having been made a Jieyu only because she had borne a son.","The court relied on the great clans and aristocratic families.","What would happen from this point on? Who could say whom they should support?","As a Jieyu, Xian Si had been placed in the palace by Zhou Yuanshen, as had Consort Wu. The two women had to make plans not only for themselves, but also on Zhou Yuanshen’s behalf.","That was why she had risked coming to see Cheng Zhao.","“Return to the palace first, Your Ladyship. Don’t alert anyone. I’ll go tell my grandfather at once,” Cheng Zhao said.","Xian Si nodded and urged her repeatedly, “Quickly. Every moment we can buy matters. Eunuch Sheng is waiting to assist us in the palace.”","Cheng Zhao agreed.","After Xian Si left, Cheng Zhao entrusted her child to her mother-in-law. Taking Suyue and Qiubai with her, she followed a back route to avoid the patrols enforcing the curfew and went to the Cheng family residence.","She knocked on the door late at night, frightening her parents half to death.","When they learned what had happened, their expressions grew even graver, and it took them a long while to recover.","“Tell Grandfather to enter the palace immediately! He must join forces with Prince Rong and Grand Preceptor Guo to stabilize the situation,” Cheng Zhao said.","Prince Rong and Grand Preceptor Guo had to be guarded against. But first, the situation had to be stabilized and the heir apparent placed upon the throne.","Whoever supported the heir apparent’s accession would be the one who controlled him.","The night was bitterly cold. Cheng Zhao’s father immediately went knocking at his grandfather’s door. Her grandfather then took her father with him to the palace gates.","Eunuch Sheng was there to receive them.","The Cheng family’s chief steward went to inform Prince Rong and Grand Preceptor Guo.","Prince Rong was a prince of the blood, while Grand Preceptor Guo was the father of Empress Guo. Both had positions and influence, but neither had the means to act independently. They could only follow Cheng Zhao’s grandfather’s instructions.","When the funeral bells rang one hundred and eight times, they awakened the entire city of Shengjing.","The former Emperor had passed away, and the seven-year-old heir ascended the throne.","Every lantern and celebratory couplet outside the Chen State Duke’s residence was removed and replaced with white mourning cloth.","Cheng Zhao gave a bitter laugh. “If Helian Xuan hadn’t tried to recruit Cheng Chao, and had held out for a few more months, he might have turned the tables by now.”","With the former Emperor dead, Zhou Yuanshen’s army would suffer a decline in morale. Helian Xuan’s side, on the other hand, had been on the verge of victory. He might even have reached the capital.","Even if he could not conquer it, he would have had many more supporters for establishing a rival court.","He simply had not been blessed with that fate.","The former Emperor’s funeral and the new Emperor’s accession were handled entirely by Cheng Zhao’s grandfather, her father, and Prince Rong. Grand Preceptor Guo was somewhat overwhelmed by the responsibility.","That day, the price of rice in Shengjing doubled, and the people became increasingly uneasy.","It was in the third year, in the third month, that Zhou Yuanshen finally crushed Helian Xuan’s rebel army.","He returned to court with his troops.","After presenting the captured rebels and returning to his residence, he found Cheng Zhao waiting at the gate with his mother, Zhou Yuanqi, and their two-and-a-half-year-old child.","This time, Cheng Zhao did not cry.","She had endured too much. All she felt was that being alive was itself a blessing.","“Jing’an, call your father,” Cheng Zhao said as she held their child.","The child seemed to have been born with an instinctive affection for him. He called out warmly, “Father.”","His words were perfectly clear.","Zhou Yuanshen had always kept his emotions tightly controlled, but now his eyes were red. He gave a muffled reply, unable to say anything more.","“You’re not even as quick-witted as a child,” Second Madam said.","As she spoke, tears spilled down her own cheeks as well.","The whole family was reunited, and the entire household enjoyed a hearty meal together. Afterward, Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen returned to Chengming Hall, while the child remained at Jiangyun Courtyard.","After being reunited, husband and wife barely slept that night. The spring weather was warm, and Cheng Zhao was drenched in sweat. She took three baths in succession.","“So your grandfather is now regent, with Prince Rong and Grand Preceptor Guo assisting him?” Zhou Yuanshen asked.","Cheng Zhao nodded. “Yes.”","“I never would have imagined that the late emperor would meet his end like that. What illness did he have?”","“He was always half-mad. Perhaps he had a little of every illness,” Cheng Zhao said. “Fortunately, the two Dowager Consorts Wu reacted quickly, allowing us to seize the initiative.”","“The two Dowager Consorts Wu?”","“Xian Si said she couldn’t remember her family surname, so Consort Wu told her to take the Wu surname. All the ladies of the imperial palace moved to the imperial mausoleum to mourn. Only Dowager Empress Guo and the two Dowager Consorts Wu, who had rendered meritorious service, remained behind,” Cheng Zhao explained.","Zhou Yuanshen nodded. “The two of them were indeed perceptive.”","“Yuanshen, what do we do from here?” Cheng Zhao asked.","“I heard about your family’s secret while I was in Qinzhou.”","Cheng Zhao knew what he meant.","“Cheng Chao and I are both descendants of the Cheng clan of Wu Commandery,” Cheng Zhao said. “As for everything else, it was all a misunderstanding.”","Whatever grudges there had been in the past were matters between the adults. Cheng Zhao had a clan, parents, and biological brothers and sisters.","That was her life.","She had already made her choice, and she would never change it.","“Fourth Brother...”","“He doesn’t want to become emperor, and he isn’t suited to be emperor,” Cheng Zhao said firmly.","She was certain that Cheng Chao had made the same choice as she had. Otherwise, he would never have tried to die together with Helian Xuan.","Zhou Yuanshen pulled her tightly into his arms.","Zhou Yuanshen rendered great service in quelling the rebellion in Qinzhou. He was subsequently appointed Grand Marshal of the Armies, placed in command of all the empire’s military forces.","By the time all the rebels had submitted, and even the small kingdoms in the southwest had surrendered, more than three years had passed. Cheng Zhao’s son was nearly six years old.","During those three-plus years, Zhou Yuanshen was hardly ever home.","Cheng Zhao and he kept in touch through regular letters.","Six years had passed since Helian Xuan’s rebellion began, and many things had happened during that time.","Cheng Zhao’s father-in-law had been wounded on the battlefield and returned to the capital to recuperate.","Her mother-in-law could only sigh and say, “At least he came back alive.”","His right leg had been permanently injured, leaving him with a limp.","Both her parents-in-law took it in stride. They said that preserving his life was what mattered most, and a bad leg was nothing. At their age, aches and injuries were inevitable.","Cheng Zhao continued to manage the entire household.","There had been tragedies as well. The Fan family’s general—the younger brother of Cheng Zhao’s mother-in-law—had died in battle. His wife fainted from grief when she heard the news.","Cheng Zhao’s mother-in-law accompanied her and shed many tears of her own.","The Grand Lady stepped forward to take charge, and the Fan household remained orderly. Fan Xiao shouldered the burden of the entire family and often looked after the Duke of Chen’s residence as well.","“Yuanshen and Yuanjin are both on the battlefield,” Second Madam sometimes told Cheng Zhao. “I wish I could go too.”","Cheng Zhao comforted her. “Mother, what would become of us if you went? Father still needs someone to care for him, and his leg makes it difficult for him to move around.”","“...It’s giving me such a headache,” Second Madam said. “When will peace finally come?”","Cheng Zhao did not know either.","She could only change the subject, mentioning that Jing’an would turn six in another two months.","That was a major occasion.","“Yuanqi has prepared quite a few birthday gifts for him,” Cheng Zhao told her mother-in-law with a smile.","Second Madam said, “As his uncle, he ought to put in more effort. If there were no war, Yuanqi should be discussing marriage by now.”","Zhou Yuanqi was fifteen years old and very tall, though thin.","Cheng Zhao did not know whether he was naturally slender or whether all the food he ate had gone toward making him taller. He looked like a stalk of bamboo—long, narrow, and fragile.","“If there had been no war, perhaps he wouldn’t be so thin,” Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam replied, “You’ve watched him grow up, so you’re even more worried about him than I am. But don’t spoil him. What’s wrong with being thin while he’s growing?”","Cheng Zhao laughed.","“So many people have starved to death in these years,” Second Madam added.","Cheng Zhao’s smile faded.","Her heart sank at once.","Seeing that she had said the wrong thing, Second Madam took Cheng Zhao’s hand. “Things will get better.”","Cheng Zhao squeezed her hand in return. “Yes, they will, Mother!”","She felt incredibly fortunate.","Cheng Zhao had never asked her own mother about the truth of her birth. She did not care, because she had two mothers.","Second Madam treated her as if she were her own daughter.","Not long after the mother and daughter-in-law finished speaking, news arrived that the entire realm had surrendered.","Second Madam was overjoyed.","“After another three years of recovery, if Heaven is kind, the granaries should be full again,” she said.","Cheng Zhao echoed her wish, though she was not optimistic at heart.","The rebellions had ended, but what of the government? At present, Cheng Zhao’s grandfather was holding the entire imperial court together, with Prince Rong assisting him.","The young emperor disliked studying and had no interest in state affairs.","He had never been aware that he was a monarch. Whenever he attended court, he acted as though he were going to school.","Cheng Zhao waited for Zhou Yuanshen to return.","That winter, Zhou Yuanshen came home in triumph.","This time, Cheng Zhao and the child went to the city gates to watch him present the captives. Seated upright atop his tall horse, he looked imposing and majestic.","“Mother, that’s Father,” Zhou Jing’an said.","Cheng Zhao nodded.","Suddenly, she remembered the beginning of their arranged marriage, when her second brother had taken her to a teahouse to look at Zhou Yuanshen.","He had been even more handsome and dashing back then.","At the time, she had thought, “This man is my husband.”","Her tone had been very similar to Zhou Jing’an’s now: perfectly satisfied.","Mother and son returned home first.","Zhou Yuanshen came back rather late this time because he had been granted a banquet at the palace.","He drank very little, and the banquet ended quickly, according to his wishes.","Cheng Zhao, her parents-in-law, Zhou Yuanqi, and the child were waiting for him at the entrance.","His eyes went first to Cheng Zhao and remained fixed on her for a long while before he finally forced himself to look away. Then he looked at his mother, his father’s injured leg, the child, and Zhou Yuanqi.","“Come inside quickly,” Second Madam said. “Yuanshen, you’ve returned safely once again.”","“Yes.”","As he crossed the threshold, he took Cheng Zhao’s hand without the slightest concern for the others watching.","Cheng Zhao had cared deeply about propriety since childhood. Over the years, she had held the entire household together and considered herself extraordinarily strong.","Yet before she had even stepped over the threshold, tears were already rolling down her cheeks.","His hand was so warm in the bitter cold of winter.","The following April, Zhou Yuanshen ascended the throne.","It was the request of the court officials.","Cheng Zhao’s grandfather had been acting as regent, placing a distance between the officials and the young emperor. None of them had developed any true bond of loyalty with him. The young emperor had been neglected since childhood and did not even realize that he was a ruler. Every time he attended court, he behaved as though he were going to school.","Zhou Yuanshen’s prestige had shaken the empire. It was only a matter of time before he replaced the young emperor.","The unrest had continued for six years. The great clans had been worn to exhaustion, as had the court officials.","They longed for peace.","Those who opposed Zhou Yuanshen’s accession would merely prolong the chaos for several more years.","Everyone acted for their own interests.","After six years, those who had intended to profit from the turmoil had already filled their coffers. Those who had gained nothing were unwilling to let anyone else profit further.","The young emperor abdicated, Zhou Yuanshen ascended the throne, and the dynasty changed hands.","Cheng Zhao was made Empress, and Zhou Jing’an was made Crown Prince. The Second Master and Second Madam were granted the titles of Retired Emperor and Empress Dowager. Zhou Yuanqi was made Prince Yong, while Zhou Yuanjin, who was still stationed at the frontier, was made Prince Zhong.","Dowager Empress Guo, who had remained in the palace from the former dynasty, was moved elsewhere. This was arranged through discussions between the court officials and Grand Preceptor Guo.","The two Dowager Consorts Wu had rendered great service, so Zhou Yuanshen specially had a magnificent temple built for them. He also bestowed generous gifts of land upon them, providing for the two women as they cultivated themselves in religious seclusion while retaining their hair.","“I only want to be a dowager of leisure,” Cheng Zhao told Zhou Yuanshen.","“Are you afraid?” Zhou Yuanshen asked her.","“Not at all!” Cheng Zhao replied.","What she had wanted might not have come to her, but Heaven had given her something even better in compensation.","She had gained so much.","She would make an excellent dowager of leisure. As empress—or even as empress dowager—she would only be better. Cheng Zhao had that confidence."]},{"number":253,"title":"Chapter 253: The Grand Finale (Part 2) 02","paragraphs":["The new emperor ascended the throne, and the following year changed the era name to Taikang, granting a general amnesty throughout the realm.","In the first month of the first year of Taikang, Cheng Zhao was pregnant again and already seven months along.","She insisted on leaving the palace because her mother-in-law had gone out early that morning.","“Your Majesty, Your Majesty!” Nanny Li was frantic. “Your belly is already so big. What if you trip or bump into something? It simply isn’t worth the risk.”","“I’ll be careful,” Cheng Zhao said.","“You can’t just leave the palace whenever you please. If the censors hear of it, they’ll lecture you about failing to uphold the dignity of the Empress,” Nanny Li said again.","Nanny Li was the senior matron who had accompanied Cheng Zhao when she married, and she had remained by her side ever since.","Suyue and Qiubai had both become palace ladies, while the other maids who had come with Cheng Zhao had entered the palace with her as well.","“I’ll sneak out. Mother has gone too,” Cheng Zhao said. “The censors won’t find out.”","Nanny Li: “...”","She could not dissuade the Empress, and she certainly could not dissuade the empress dowager.","Qiubai could not help saying, “We’d better hurry. If we wait any longer, we truly won’t be able to get out. The carriage is ready, and His Majesty has given his permission.”","Nanny Li was utterly helpless.","Cheng Zhao changed into a simple everyday outfit and, taking Qiubai and two guards with her, quietly made her way to Prince Zhong’s residence.","Prince Zhong’s residence belonged to Zhou Yuanjin, Zhou Yuanshen’s fourth younger brother. It was not far from Prince Yong’s residence. As for Zhou Yuanqi’s residence, it was the former Duke of Chen’s estate.","When Cheng Zhao married into the Duke of Chen’s household, Zhou Yuanjin was stationed on the frontier. After something happened to his maternal uncle, the realm descended into chaos, and he continued guarding the border.","After Zhou Yuanshen ascended the throne, Zhou Yuanjin remained occupied with affairs along the frontier and had not returned home.","The empress dowager had been hoping he could come back for the New Year.","Then a minor matter delayed him, and he did not return until the first month of the year.","The empress dowager had mentioned him to Cheng Zhao several times. “I haven’t seen him in nearly ten years. I don’t even know what he looks like now. All I can remember is how he looked when he was seven or eight.”","He had arrived only yesterday, and the empress dowager had slipped out early that morning.","Cheng Zhao had risen early to pay her respects at the Palace of Longevity and Blessings. When she heard from the palace maids that the empress dowager had left the palace first thing in the morning, she too grew eager to see what was going on.","When they reached Prince Zhong’s residence, the guards standing watch at the entrance were still the ones the empress dowager had brought from the palace.","Seeing Cheng Zhao, one of them hurriedly bowed. “Her Majesty the empress dowager instructed us to wait here for you.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","Prince Zhong’s residence had little more than a newly hung plaque. Since Prince Zhong had only just returned to the capital, the household consisted of a few old retainers and aging gatekeepers, as well as his deputy general.","Cheng Zhao was led to the training grounds.","“The empress dowager came to see His Highness, and went straight to the training grounds?” Cheng Zhao asked.","The guard replied, “Yes. When Her Majesty entered the residence, there was already a young lady here.”","Cheng Zhao quickened her pace.","Qiubai did not try to stop her. She followed close behind, knowing that Cheng Zhao had been dreadfully bored these days and was eager for some excitement.","After the new emperor ascended the throne, Cheng Zhao moved into the Palace of Earthly Tranquility, expecting to have plenty to do.","Instead, she discovered that there was almost nothing.","The inner palace was far less complicated than the Duke of Chen’s residence had been when she first married into it. There were fewer matters to manage, and Cheng Zhao’s talent for running a household had no opportunity to shine.","Zhou Yuanshen seemed to notice how bored she was. He often brought memorials back with him, and the two of them would secretly read them and discuss them together.","Cheng Zhao loved reading histories. Ever since she was a child, she had studied maps of the realm in her grandfather’s private library and had developed a deep understanding of politics and statecraft.","These days, Zhou Yuanshen had been attending lessons with his tutors, making up for all the knowledge an emperor was expected to possess. He had studied formally at the Zhou clan school for only two years; everything else, he had learned through his own efforts and insight.","Because of his reserved nature, steady bearing, and handsome appearance, he possessed such an air of an aristocratic gentleman that people often forgot he had risen through the military ranks.","Whenever he failed to understand something his tutors taught him, he would memorize it first and then look it up in books.","But he had discovered that Cheng Zhao understood those things.","Not only did Cheng Zhao help him review his lessons, she also discussed the memorials with him. It was as though he had gained himself an assistant.","These activities were interesting and made Cheng Zhao feel somewhat more fulfilled.","And yet, she was still bored.","Perhaps the six years she had spent amid warfare had left her constantly tense. She simply could not bear to sit idle.","She wanted to see all kinds of excitement.","Following the guards, she arrived at the training grounds and saw her mother-in-law dressed in a short martial tunic, sparring with a woman wielding a spear.","Her mother-in-law had never neglected her spear practice over the years. The other woman’s technique was even more polished; unlike Cheng Zhao, she was no mere showy amateur.","The two of them fought for quite some time without either gaining the upper hand. It was Zhou Yuanjin who noticed Cheng Zhao first.","He strode over.","“Your Majesty.” He dropped to one knee and performed a formal bow.","Cheng Zhao hurriedly told him to rise. “Fourth Brother, I slipped out secretly. Don’t announce my arrival.”","Zhou Yuanjin stood.","He did not dare look at Cheng Zhao, while Cheng Zhao openly studied him.","He had spent too many years on the frontier and had not inherited his mother’s fair complexion, so his skin was rather dark. His features closely resembled Zhou Yuanqi’s.","Meanwhile, the second lady had won her match.","“Your Majesty has an impressive spear technique,” the woman said with a smile, cupping her fists.","Her mother-in-law was delighted. “You were only being generous.”","Cheng Zhao was looking at the woman.","She had a fine figure—tall, slender, and well-proportioned. Her wheat-colored skin was firm, and her eyes were especially bright. Her hair was tied high, giving her a bold and heroic air.","Cheng Zhao was accustomed to seeing refined young ladies. This was the first time she had encountered someone like this, and she could not help staring.","The woman came over to greet her.","Her mother-in-law walked over with a smile and said to Cheng Zhao, “Her name is Xie Yun. Her grandfather once served under your maternal grandfather.”","“So there’s such a connection between you?” Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","Her mother-in-law wiped away her sweat. “Why did you leave the palace too?”","“I was worried about you. And you didn’t even wait for me,” Cheng Zhao replied.","Her mother-in-law smiled. “I only came to take a look, then I was going back.”","“It’s already nearly midday,” Cheng Zhao pointed out.","Her mother-in-law: “...”","As they were talking, a deputy general came over. “General, the imperial edict has arrived at the relay station. They’ve been looking everywhere for you.”","Her mother-in-law was slightly taken aback. “His Highness is right here in the residence. What sort of edict would be sent to the relay station?”","Zhou Yuanjin said, “Mother, it isn’t for me...”","“Your Majesty the empress dowager, it is for this subordinate,” Xie Yun said.","Her mother-in-law: “...”","That day, the mother and daughter-in-law left Prince Zhong’s residence and stopped by Prince Yong’s residence as well, inspecting it from top to bottom. They also discussed choosing a princess consort for Prince Yong in a few days’ time.","Zhou Yuanqi saw the two of them completely ignoring him and complained several times in displeasure.","In the days that followed, her mother-in-law would occasionally discuss Xie Yun with Cheng Zhao.","“She has been appointed General Ningyuan and granted a residence.”","“If A-Shen had not ascended the throne, Yuanjin would probably have been made no more than a general. She is actually no less accomplished than him.”","“A-Shen has agreed to arrange their marriage. They’ll wed at the end of the year.”","Cheng Zhao listened with a smile.","She said, “Mother, every daughter-in-law who enters the family has to spar with you first.”","Xie Yun had sparred with her mother-in-law the very first time they met.","Remembering how Cheng Zhao had kicked open the gates on their first meeting, her mother-in-law could not help laughing. “That’s true.”","Then she added, “Why don’t we find Yuanqi a military family’s daughter as well? Once you’ve given birth, the four of us mothers-in-law and daughters-in-law can play polo together.”","“Wouldn’t that leave me as the only loser?” Cheng Zhao laughed. “My riding skills are only so-so. How could I possibly compete with you and General Xie?”","“Then let’s find Yuanqi a girl from a scholarly family. That way, the two of us can form one team, and the other two can form the opposing team,” her mother-in-law suggested.","The more she thought about it, the better the idea seemed. “Those two princess consorts will understand a little about social etiquette, won’t they? Surely they wouldn’t dare beat the empress dowager and the Empress. Zhao-zhao, we’re guaranteed to win.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","Her mother-in-law had never been one for strong opinions. Whatever Cheng Zhao said was fine with her, so long as Cheng Zhao was happy.","Naturally, she also did not care what Zhou Yuanqi thought.","“Very well, Mother. You choose,” Cheng Zhao said, happy to play along.","Although she said that, she secretly sent Zhou Yuanqi a letter to warn him to be prepared: if there was a young lady he fancied, he should say so early, lest the empress dowager make a match for him on a whim.","Zhou Yuanqi wrote back, saying that a scholar observed proper etiquette and never exchanged private correspondence with young ladies. He did not know anyone at all, so Her Majesty the Empress should not sully his good name.","Cheng Zhao was so exasperated that she laughed.","In mid-March of that year, Cheng Zhao gave birth to a princess.","Her mother-in-law was overjoyed.","“I’ve been hoping for a granddaughter for so long, and now we finally have one.” Her mother-in-law’s eyes reddened as she spoke. “It hasn’t been easy.”","It was not only the granddaughter who had come with such difficulty.","During those years of war, Cheng Zhao had given birth only to Zhou Jing’an. Then, for six long years, everyone had lived amid turmoil and unrest.","Her mother-in-law had barely had enough to eat or wear, yet she and Cheng Zhao had held the family together.","Cheng Zhao still remembered that when she had first married into the Zhou family, she had made a fuss over the smallest matter and threatened to divorce. Her grandfather had told her, “You’ve never gone hungry. That’s why you think every little thing is the end of the world.”","She had not understood him then.","During the war, Cheng Zhao had gone hungry too, and only then did she grasp what her grandfather meant. When one was starving, everything else was a minor matter.","Now that Cheng Zhao was the Empress, she often felt bored. That was because all the people she could rely on had entered the palace, leaving her with an abundance of fiercely loyal servants.","During the war, Cheng Zhao had not only protected them but also kept them from starving to death. The hardships she had endured for them had earned her their unwavering loyalty.","All those years of toil had been worth it.","Even so, looking back still made her break out in a cold sweat.","The birth of the little princess seemed to tell her mother-in-law that the hardships of the past were finally over and that an era of peace and prosperity had begun.","Though all things were still recovering, and life remained somewhat difficult.","Zhou Yuanshen was delighted as well. During the princess’s third-day bathing ceremony, he named her Zhou Yonghua, granted her the title of Princess Shengning, and bestowed a princess’s residence upon her.","Her parents-in-law also prepared gifts for the little princess.","Her father-in-law’s leg ailment had improved considerably under the careful treatment of the palace physicians. He now limped only slightly, which did not hinder him from walking, practicing with his spear, or holding the baby.","The inner palace was filled with joy.","Cheng Zhao did not feel that she was living in the inner palace at all.","The former Chen State Duke’s residence had been nearly as large. The distance between the two palace compounds was about the same as that between Chengming Hall and Jiangyun Court had once been.","It felt much like living at home. In fact, many of the servants attending them had come from the Chen State Duke’s residence. They were still simply a family living together.","While Cheng Zhao was in confinement after giving birth, she heard some news: Prince Jingnan had taken Cheng Ying as his adopted daughter, and the prince’s residence had issued a divorce certificate. Cheng Ying and Zhang Yunqi had divorced.","It was her mother-in-law who told her that Cheng Ying had divorced.","“...Madam Sheng requested permission to enter the palace to visit me and brought it up. Otherwise, I wouldn’t have known,” her mother-in-law said.","General Sheng had died in the campaign to quell the rebellion. After Zhou Yuanshen ascended the throne, he rewarded those who had distinguished themselves, and the Sheng family received many honors and gifts. Madam Sheng was granted the rank of First-Rank Lady.","She and the empress dowager had been close friends since their girlhood. Both were candid and unreserved by nature, and Madam Sheng often requested permission to enter the palace, visiting just as she had in the past.","Many of the latest stories from outside the palace came from Madam Sheng. Cheng Zhao’s family, however, was too cautious to bring such things to her.","“My third sister was once famous throughout the capital. She was the most outstanding and accomplished daughter in the Cheng family. Zhang Yunqi’s elopement destroyed her entire reputation.","“If Princess Consort Jingnan hadn’t gone to such lengths to support her, and if every member of the Cheng family hadn’t remained so steady, who knows how badly people would have trampled her. Every now and then, when I think of it, I feel wronged on my third sister’s behalf,” Cheng Zhao said.","There were five sisters in their family, and the third sister had the greatest talent.","Their mother occasionally said that Cheng Zhao was the cleverest and most beautiful, but in Cheng Zhao’s eyes, her third sister was the one who excelled in every way. Cheng Zhao felt she was far inferior to her.","“The Third Young Lady’s situation truly was unfortunate,” her mother-in-law said.","Cheng Zhao continued, “Now that they’re divorced, I suspect it was my third sister’s own choice. Otherwise, the Prince Jingnan’s residence would never have agreed to it.”","The Zhang family would never have dared force Cheng Ying into a divorce.","Zhou Yuanshen was the emperor, and the Wu Commandery Cheng clan had produced its first Empress. The Cheng family’s status had risen dramatically. Besides, with every new emperor came a new group of trusted ministers. Although Prince Jingnan had rendered outstanding military service, he was ultimately a general of the previous dynasty, while Zhou Yuanshen had no shortage of capable men at his disposal.","At a time like this, provoking the Cheng family would have been sheer suicide for the Zhang family. There was only one possibility: Cheng Ying herself had wanted the divorce.","“She lived a quiet, carefree life in a small courtyard at the prince’s residence and cared little for fame or wealth. Why would she suddenly want a divorce?” Cheng Zhao asked.","Her mother-in-law replied, “No matter how comfortable her life was, she was still someone else’s daughter-in-law, not their daughter. Whatever freedom she enjoyed, she was still living within another family’s inner court. If it were me, I’d divorce and leave no matter what.”","“Mother, that’s because you value your freedom above all else,” Cheng Zhao said. “My third sister may not think the same way.”","She then asked, “Does His Majesty intend to deal with Prince Jingnan? Prince Jingnan rendered great service in quelling the rebellion. If he were touched now, it could shake people’s confidence.”","Her mother-in-law already found family matters troublesome enough; political affairs were even more overwhelming.","“How about I go out and make some inquiries for you?” she suggested. “I can go straight to the Cheng family and ask your mother.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","That would frighten her family half to death.","Cheng Zhao told her mother-in-law to wait and see. She sent an eunuch to the Sheng residence instead, asking Madam Sheng to make inquiries. A few days later, Madam Sheng could return to the palace and share the news during a casual visit.","Madam Sheng failed to discover anything. Cheng Ying herself requested permission to enter the palace.","Cheng Zhao hurriedly sent someone to receive her.","The sisters had not seen each other in quite some time, so Cheng Zhao began with a few polite greetings.","Knowing that her sister was anxious, Cheng Ying asked with a smile, “Have you heard that I’ve divorced?”","“Tell me everything!” Cheng Zhao urged.","Cheng Ying could not help laughing.","“There’s no other reason. Dongbai wants to live with me,” Cheng Ying said.","He had finally developed genuine feelings for Cheng Ying.","Those feelings had disrupted Cheng Ying’s peaceful life.","“...To avoid him, I returned to my parents’ home and even stayed for a while at a temple. Mother told me that I was someone else’s wife, and there were certain duties I had to fulfill. I couldn’t have every advantage without giving anything in return.","“Mother told me to divorce. Given the Cheng family’s current status, it wouldn’t be difficult for me to marry again. Even if I chose not to, my family could establish a separate household for me as a single woman, return all my dowry, and give me additional money, land, and estates.","“Zhang Yunqi treated me poorly in the past, but circumstances have changed so greatly now. Who would dare criticize the Cheng family?” Cheng Ying said with a smile.","There was one more reason she did not mention: back then, she had refused to divorce not only because she enjoyed her comfortable life, but also because she feared that the gossip would affect her younger siblings’ marriages.","At that time, neither Cheng Zhao nor Cheng Chao was married.","Cheng Ying had quietly gone about her duties and never flaunted her contributions. She did not want Cheng Zhao to feel that she had suffered for their sake.","“‘Reputation’ is a matter of luck. When the Grand Madam and Huan-shi died, the Chen State Duke’s residence lost all its prestige. Back then, people mocked us behind our backs.","“I told my mother-in-law that our children would probably have to marry beneath them in the future—or else we would have to arrange marriages with families related to the Chengs by marriage.","“But not long afterward, war broke out. And now, what need does the Zhou family have for the reputation they once possessed? Third Sister, as long as this is what you want, that’s enough,” Cheng Zhao said.","Cheng Ying smiled. “I want to live a quieter life.”","Zhang Yunqi had pressed her too hard. She could hardly breathe.","“I discussed it with my parents-in-law, and naturally they agreed at once. They were worried that I would find life difficult after leaving the Zhang family, so they adopted me as their daughter.","“They returned the betrothal gifts from back then and gave me back my dowry as well. My mother-in-law even gave me an additional twenty thousand taels of silver,” Cheng Ying said.","“That was very generous of them,” Cheng Zhao replied.","Cheng Ying nodded. “They’re good people. If Dongbai never came back and chose to live his own life out there, I wouldn’t have thought of leaving the Zhang family.”","“Sometimes you have to break before you can build anew. Perhaps better days lie ahead,” Cheng Zhao said.","Cheng Ying merely replied, “I’ll be the same wherever I am.”","“Have you finished settling into your residence? Has your independent woman’s household been established?” Cheng Zhao asked.","“The household registration is all sorted out. Mother had the residence arranged before I divorced. Everything was taken care of down to the smallest detail. She had Second Brother handle it—he’s always been the most meticulous.” Cheng Ying smiled.","Back then, it had also been Second Brother who had purchased and furnished Eldest Sister’s residence. He truly had seen to everything.","Raised by their grandfather from childhood, Second Brother possessed an excellent eye for such things. The courtyards he arranged were not only comfortable but elegant as well.","“Oh, by the way, Chao and his wife will be returning to the capital soon,” Cheng Ying added.","“At last.” Cheng Zhao smiled. “I heard His Majesty say that Fourth Brother will be made a duke of the state, and Fourth Sister-in-law will receive the rank of a first-rank noblewoman.”","“They deserve it,” Cheng Ying said.","Cheng Chao had dealt Helian Xuan a grievous wound—the greatest achievement of all.","During the war, Cheng Chao had been trapped in Qinzhou and had nearly missed his wedding to Guo Hanzhang. Guo Hanzhang had taken her dowry and gone to Qinzhou on her own.","The fighting continued for three years. Guo Hanzhang organized the village women in farming and sericulture, providing supplies for the army. After the war ended, Cheng Chao remained there to recover from his injuries, while Guo Hanzhang helped the prefect and the general restore agriculture.","She had earned immense prestige among the local people. With a single call, everyone answered; she had practically become a living goddess of mercy.","For the past several years, she and Cheng Chao had stayed behind to stabilize Qinzhou.","Qinzhou was the fastest region to recover.","The couple’s contributions had been invaluable.","Zhou Yuanshen received memorial after memorial and would show them to Cheng Zhao.","He had said he would reward Guo Hanzhang handsomely.","He intended to grant her the title Lady of Sericulture—not as an appendage to her husband or his family, but as an honor bestowed upon her in her own right.","Cheng Zhao thought the title suited her perfectly.","“...Back then, everyone said Fourth Sister-in-law was fierce and sharp-tongued, that anyone who crossed her would be subjected to her biting sarcasm. Yet they all overlooked how decisive and formidable she truly was.” Cheng Ying smiled.","Then she added, “The Guo family has fallen on hard times these past few years.”","After the Crown Prince’s death and the change of dynasty, the Guo family had already begun to decline during the war.","Guo Hanzhang had relied entirely on herself to carve out a path of her own.","After Cheng Zhao had completed her postpartum confinement, Cheng Chao and Guo Hanzhang returned to the capital, and she summoned them both.","When the siblings saw each other again, their eyes grew slightly damp.","Cheng Zhao had nearly lost Cheng Chao forever. At the time, he had intended to die together with Helian Xuan.","What a fool.","But it was better for him to be a fool.","Compared with a madman, Cheng Zhao was far more relieved that her brother was merely foolish.","Cheng Zhao had the Crown Prince and the little princess brought in so that their uncle and aunt could meet them.","When Cheng Chao saw Cheng Zhao’s two children, he secretly let out a sigh of relief. “They both look like His Majesty.”","His Majesty was handsome, and both children were beautiful.","“What a pity they don’t look like me.”","“What’s there to regret?” Cheng Chao immediately retorted. “You’re annoying enough as it is.”","Cheng Zhao flew into a rage. “That’s slander! I’m perfectly well-behaved and obedient!”","Cheng Chao: “...”","The two of them quarreled at the slightest disagreement, then made peace and clasped hands moments later, leaving Guo Hanzhang utterly stunned.","Their mother-in-law even made a special trip to Kunning Palace to see Guo Hanzhang.","“That unruly Miss Guo from years ago has become such an impressive woman.” The empress dowager sighed.","Cheng Zhao smiled. “She’s still ‘unruly.’ It’s just that when a temperament like hers is put to good use, it benefits both the country and its people.”","“Indeed.” The empress dowager smiled. “Your temperament, too, is perfectly suited to being the Empress.”","Cheng Zhao could not help laughing.","The empress dowager was just as she had always been, convinced that Cheng Zhao was the finest of them all.","In the second year of the Taikang era, sea bandits arose in the east. The trouble dragged on for nearly half a year without any progress.","Afraid that the hard-won stability of the court might be shaken again, and concerned that both the government and the people might lose confidence, Zhou Yuanshen decided to lead the campaign himself.","Before departing, he placed the Crown Prince in charge of the government, with the Empress and the Chancellor assisting him.","The empress dowager was stunned. “He wants you to attend court and listen to state affairs?”","“Yes.”","“Isn’t that reckless? If you make even one mistake, the ministers will attack you!” the empress dowager said.","Cheng Zhao replied, “Mother, I can learn. Maintaining the people’s confidence is what matters most right now. He must lead the campaign himself. This is the first disturbance since His Majesty ascended the throne. If it cannot be suppressed quickly, others may follow its example.”","For a moment, the empress dowager did not know what to say.","“If those old ministers bully you, tell me. I’ll make a scene in court. I may be old, but I’m still the empress dowager. What can they do to me?” she said.","Cheng Zhao laughed and hurriedly agreed.","This period of court attendance lasted four months.","Cheng Zhao’s understanding of state affairs and her insight into governance astonished the ministers. Her grandfather also supported her at every turn.","The Crown Prince was only eight years old and merely sat nearby to learn. Prince Yong, Zhou Yuanqi, attended court as well. Every opinion Cheng Zhao offered, he would explain further and elevate with his own commentary.","In court, Zhou Yuanqi and her grandfather were worth a hundred men together. Their wholehearted support established Cheng Zhao’s authority without a word being said.","No matter what Cheng Zhao said, Zhou Yuanqi could always smooth it over and make it sound soundly reasoned.","Within the palace, meanwhile, her parents-in-law supported her to the utmost. She did not need to worry about anything else.","After returning victorious from the campaign, Zhou Yuanshen held Cheng Zhao in his arms beneath the bed curtains and asked, “From now on, will you attend court and listen to state affairs with me?”","“The ministers won’t agree,” Cheng Zhao said.","“It would merely be a return to the practices of antiquity. It was only the Helian clan that forbade the Empress and the empress dowager from attending court. In every other dynasty, which Empress or empress dowager did not sit in court?” Zhou Yuanshen replied.","Cheng Zhao: “...”","Beginning in the third year of the Taikang era, Cheng Zhao attended court alongside Zhou Yuanshen.","She was very busy.","Even so, she was happy every time she returned to the inner palace. Her daughter resembled the empress dowager in every way—bright, lively, and sweet-tongued. She worshiped Cheng Zhao and was forever praising her.","Whenever Cheng Zhao was troubled, she only had to sit with the empress dowager and listen to her daughter say a few words before her mood lifted completely.","“...I heard that Fan Xiao asked to marry your Third Sister, but she turned him down,” the empress dowager said to Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao had known for a long time that Fan Xiao loved her Third Sister.","But...","Cheng Zhao felt a little regretful. “Not everyone is suited to marriage. Third Sister has grown accustomed to her freedom. She probably doesn’t want to marry again.”","Because of this, Cheng Zhao had even summoned her Third Sister to ask her about it.","By then, it had been two years since Third Sister’s divorce.","In those two years, had Fan Xiao managed to move her?","Cheng Ying smiled. “Your Majesty, grant me a noble title.”","As the Empress’s elder sister, she was entitled to receive an honor.","“Of course, Third Sister. But you...” Cheng Zhao began.","“I’ve already told Fan Xiao. It isn’t that he’s lacking in any way; I simply don’t wish to fall into the mortal world again. Marriage is not meant for me,” Cheng Ying said. “I hope he finds a suitable match soon.”","However, Fan Xiao never sought another wife, and Cheng Ying never changed her mind. She remained unmarried for the rest of her life.","In private, Cheng Zhao said to the empress dowager, “The saying that ‘no daughter of the Cheng clan of Wu Commandery remarries’—I don’t know whether it has trapped Third Sister.”","“Not necessarily. Your Third Sister has always been like a celestial maiden, untouched by worldly concerns. Whoever she married would have made her suffer.","“When she was a maiden, she didn’t know that. After marrying once, she understood—and she didn’t want to hold anyone else back. She explained herself openly and honestly. That’s a good thing.” The empress dowager replied.","As a daughter and as a daughter-in-law, Third Sister had fulfilled every duty expected of her. Perhaps, for the rest of her life, she simply wanted to live as herself.","The empress dowager was fair-minded rather than blindly partial.","Of course, she was also trying to comfort Cheng Zhao.","Her words eased Cheng Zhao’s heart, and she stopped dwelling on the matter.","As long as it was her own choice, whether Third Sister married or remained single, she could be happy either way.","For many years afterward, whenever a rebellion broke out, Zhou Yuanshen would personally lead the campaign. As his mother-in-law put it, “He’d rather go out and fight than sit in court.”","Zhou Yuanshen was capable of handling state affairs—very capable, in fact—but he was not especially fond of them.","Cheng Zhao agreed completely.","Several years later, the people had recovered and prospered, ushering in an era of peace and abundance. There were no civil wars, resources were plentiful, and the population grew rapidly. By the twentieth year of Taikang’s reign, prosperity had reached its peak.","In the blink of an eye, Cheng Zhao turned fifty. By then, the realm had expanded farther than ever before. Zhou Yuanshen had entrusted the government to Cheng Zhao and the Crown Prince, then conquered the surrounding kingdoms one after another in a series of northern and southern campaigns.","Cheng Zhao had only two children: the Crown Prince and Princess Shengning. But the Crown Prince and the princess each had children of their own, and Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen were surrounded by grandchildren.","Their love for each other remained as strong as ever.","Zhou Yuanshen no longer went on campaigns, but he had lost interest in court affairs as well. In his free time, he practiced with his spear, chatted with officials from the Ministry of War, and often visited the capital garrison.","Cheng Zhao and the Crown Prince presided over court together. Mother and son were remarkably alike. Not only did they enjoy managing the affairs of the realm, they also loved matching wits with the ministers.","They even divided the roles between them: Cheng Zhao played the villain, decisive and ruthless, while the Crown Prince played the good cop, dispensing favors and winning people over.","Maintaining an established kingdom was no easy task.","Both Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen wanted to pave the way for the Crown Prince. The Crown Prince, wise and precocious, had understood his parents’ intentions from an early age and cooperated with them skillfully.","His first teacher, meanwhile, had been his uncle, Zhou Yuanqi, who personally taught him to read and write, guiding his hand as he practiced his characters.","There was no scholar in the realm more learned than Zhou Yuanqi. The Crown Prince benefited enormously from his instruction.","At the founding of the dynasty, the reason there had been no rivers of blood was that the dynasty’s most illustrious “great general” had been the Emperor himself.","Whenever Cheng Zhao and the Crown Prince could not resolve a matter, he would step in. Once he did, bloodshed and death were inevitable. At such times, Cheng Zhao and the Crown Prince would help plead for mercy.","The three members of the imperial family kept the court firmly under control in both civil and military affairs, and the political situation remained stable.","At fifty, Cheng Zhao had no desire to celebrate her birthday.","“With Father Emperor and Mother Empress still in good health, how could it be my turn to celebrate?” Cheng Zhao said with a laugh.","Zhou Yuanshen was adamant. “Bring out that golden pig.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","The golden pig was the birthday gift Zhou Yuanqi had given Cheng Zhao when he was eight years old.","Even in his forties, Zhou Yuanqi had not mellowed much. He was still proud and sharp-tongued, and he often found opportunities to make a few sarcastic remarks at Zhou Yuanshen’s expense.","He had even earned a reputation for incorruptibility and fearlessness before imperial authority.","Sometimes, when Cheng Zhao became too overbearing and crushed the ministers too thoroughly, she would be subjected to his mockery as well.","He was the only person he never insulted: the Crown Prince.","The ministers loved watching the imperial family’s antics. It was one of the few pleasures of attending court.","Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen could not trade insults with him. Mainly because they could never win.","They had to get some of their dignity back!","To put that golden pig on display and let Prince Yong see how mischievous he had been as a child, Cheng Zhao decided to celebrate her birthday after all.","“Mother Empress, where did this golden pig come from?”","“Grandmother, who made this golden pig?”","“What a large golden pig! Why was it made in the shape of a pig? What is it for?”","Amid the chorus of questions, Prince Yong—now the father of four and a great Confucian scholar who could speak eloquently in court—nearly revealed the fury he had felt as a child.","Zhou Yuanqi’s old face flushed red with anger.","Revenge between elder brother and sister-in-law was never too late—even after thirty years.","He hated those two so much!"]}]);
